(N'ea39bf95-a88b-5229-9dd0-cd78dbfa6675',N'17d55305-328d-5a8e-bf21-e58482d15cd5',0,3,19,N'<p> Employees should be kept informed about business development and performance </p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms: kept informed = get an update (được cập nhật)</p><p>+ Interpretation: Nhân viên nên được cập nhật về sự phát triển và hiệu suất của doanh nghiệp.</p><p>+ Answer: Stephen Harper cập nhật thông tin về công ty cho nhân viên hai tuần một lần khi họ nhận lương</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là B</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,19,NULL,0,1985),
(N'607e82d3-b008-5198-9bb5-4d8b85db454f',N'17d55305-328d-5a8e-bf21-e58482d15cd5',0,3,19,N'<p> Work output increases when employees have a good balance between company and family  responsibilities </p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms: more productive (năng suất hơn) = work output increases (sản lượng công việc tăng lên)</p><p>+ Interpretation: Sản lượng công việc tăng khi nhân viên cân bằng tốt giữa trách nhiệm công ty và gia đình.</p><p>+ Answer: Victor Davies cho biết chính sách cân bằng giữa công việc và gia đình dẫn đến lực lượng lao động năng suất và ổn định hơn</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là D</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,20,NULL,0,1985),
(N'4ad7bbf0-ae10-57ce-b450-d357c70d92d3',N'17d55305-328d-5a8e-bf21-e58482d15cd5',0,3,19,N'<p> It is critical to business success that all company members recognise that they  matter</p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms: recognize that they matter = realize that they count</p><p>+ Interpretation: Rất quan trọng cho thành công kinh doanh rằng tất cả thành viên công ty nhận ra họ có giá trị.</p><p>+ Answer: Hazel Gibbs làm việc cật lực để thuyết phục mọi người rằng tất cả đều quan trọng và là thành viên của cùng một đội</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là E</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,21,NULL,0,1985),
(N'b841e9bb-6dee-5ff7-ac47-10ec6e15ae8a',N'6e9f0c7e-c568-5fe2-a3e7-b6f383cf4c39',0,2,18,N'<p>Complete the summary. </p><p>Write <span>ONE WORD ONLY</span> from the text for each answer. </p>',N'',N'',N'',N'Family-friendly practices at Plastic Solutions and the Margaret Mills Corporation',11,0,3,NULL,0,1985),
(N'a714e3e7-c85b-51f2-9733-4dc17cc7e106',N'b841e9bb-6dee-5ff7-ac47-10ec6e15ae8a',0,3,19,N'<h3>Family-friendly practices at Plastic Solutions and the Margaret Mills Corporation</h3><p>At Plastic Solutions, a bi-weekly update is issued to workers at the same time as their pay. This  includes a section dealing with problems such as  }{SPACE}{ in communal areas of the workplace.</p><p>The CEO also arranges a regular }{SPACE}{ for selected employees for whom places are in great demand.</p><p>Finally, employees’ families are invited to company open days, when they are allowed to try out the }{SPACE}{ .</p><p>The Margaret Mills Corporation allows employees a great deal of flexibility with their children,  who can be brought to the office once  }{SPACE}{ has finished.</p><p>Mills likes to reward employees for company performance with a party or even a }{SPACE}{ for families. There is considerable evidence that these practices are having the desired effect.</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Các vấn đề như ____ ở khu vực chung của nơi làm việc.</p><p>+ Answer: Phần huấn luyện giải quyết các vấn đề như tin đồn và chuyện phiếm của các nhân viên</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là gossip</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,22,NULL,0,1985),
(N'79b07bd4-a365-5f19-95ff-615f6d2edf93',N'b841e9bb-6dee-5ff7-ac47-10ec6e15ae8a',0,3,19,N'Question number 23',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Giám đốc cũng tổ chức một ____ thường xuyên cho nhân viên được chọn.</p><p>+ Answer: Hội thảo Business Pragmatics diễn ra hàng tháng, chỉ dành cho người được mời, rất được ưa chuộng.</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là seminar</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,23,NULL,0,1985),
(N'3d699b29-ef81-594c-b51d-aecf373f938a',N'b841e9bb-6dee-5ff7-ac47-10ec6e15ae8a',0,3,19,N'Question number 24',N'<p>+ Synonym: try out (thử) = experiment with… (thử nghiệm với)</p><p>+ Interpretation: Gia đình nhân viên được mời đến ngày mở cửa, khi họ được phép thử ____.</p><p>+ Answer: Công ty Plastic Solutions tổ chức 1 ngày Open House cho gia đình của nhân viên, nơi trẻ em có thể được thử nghiệm với máy móc của công ty</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là machines</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,24,NULL,0,1985),
(N'a77e7e28-383e-579a-aed3-2fa7533e88b0',N'b841e9bb-6dee-5ff7-ac47-10ec6e15ae8a',0,3,19,N'Question number 25',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Con cái có thể được đưa đến văn phòng sau khi ____ kết thúc.</p><p>+ Answer: Nhân viên ở Margaret Mills được phép đón con sau giờ tan trường</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là school</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,25,NULL,0,1985),
(N'0ed845f0-327a-5ff8-859b-8a226ebd0cd1',N'b841e9bb-6dee-5ff7-ac47-10ec6e15ae8a',0,3,19,N'Question number 26',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Phần thưởng cho nhân viên có thể là một bữa tiệc hoặc thậm chí một ____ cho gia đình.</p><p>+ Answer: Để ăn mừng thành tích, công ty Margaret Mills đã đưa nhân viên và gia đình của họ đi một chuyến 2 ngày ở Montreal, Canada</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là trip</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,26,NULL,0,1985),
(N'778ff78e-f2b6-542b-a322-c09cc42b0b3a',N'f02f9deb-a3e9-57d4-b01e-4613191e63a3',0,1,15,(CAST(N'<p><span><span>Child’s Play in Medieval England</span></span></p><p><em>Professor Nicholas Orme investigates childhood in the Middle Ages</em></p><p></p><p><span><span>A</span></span> ‘Play up! Play up! And play the game!’ The ringing chorus of Sir Henry Newbolt’s celebrated cricket poem “Vitaï Lampada” (1908) sums up views about play in 19th- and early 20th-century Britain. Children’s play was important, and adults should regulate and direct it. Games promoted endurance, self-discipline and team spirit – qualities needed for the health of society and government. Newbolt was one in a long line of people who thought in this way. The notion that children’s play should be used for educational and social purposes goes back at least to the ancient Greeks and the toys and games of medieval England tell us much about how adults then saw childhood. But they also reveal a good deal about children themselves, and cast light on what has recently become a controversial issue.</p><p></p><p></p><p><span><span>B</span></span> Forty years ago, the French historian Philippe Ariès argued, in Centuries of Childhood, that childhood in the Middle Ages did not exist in its modern sense. Children were regarded by adults with relatively little affection and followed a way of life not very different from that of their elders. More recent historians have disputed this, pointing to plentiful signs of parental affection and arguing that childhood, by its very nature, must always have been much the same.</p><p></p><p></p><p><span><span>C</span></span> In this debate play is crucial. Did adults encourage it? If so, did they see it as recreational (by providing toys, for example) or as educational (making children play in particular ways)? Did children play as their elders told them, or did they invent their own games, away from adults and even against their wishes? These questions can be answered from a rich body of evidence including actual toys of the period, pictures of children’s activities in contemporary manuscripts and literary sources such as religious works and dictionaries. We know not only how medieval English children played but what their elders thought on the subject.</p><p></p><p></p><p><span><span>D </span></span>We know, for example, that adults gave children toys from infancy onwards. In 1398 the writer John Trevisa describes babies playing with ‘a child’s brooch’, an object similar in function to the bright plastic toys given to babies today to bite and handle. Willi' AS nvarchar(max))+N'am Horman, 16th-century author of a Latin textbook, talks of buying a rattle to stop a baby crying. Indeed, by 1300 it appears there was a toy industry in England. Boys’ toys often took military forms, such as the two metal soldiers of that date, found in London, and made from a mould. Girls had dolls, known before the 17th century as ‘poppets’ or puppets, commercially manufactured, imported and, in 1582, taxed at a halfpenny each. Not that children were by any means dependent on things that were bought for them. Gerald of Wales recalls how he and his brothers built towns, palaces, churches, and monasteries from sand at Manorbiere Castle in about 1150 (perhaps on the nearby beach).</p><p></p><p><span><span>E</span></span> Active games were universal. In his English-to-Latin dictionary of 1440, a mysterious recluse known as Geoffrey mentions children playing ‘tennis’ and swinging on what he calls a ‘totter’ or ‘merrytotter’. Children chased each other, swam and played ball games. Boys in the later Middle Ages shot arrows with bows, and archery is an example of a sport encouraged by adults, who wanted boys to grow up to play their part in what was, for most men, a warrior society.</p><p></p><p><span><span>F</span></span> However, by no means all children’s military activity was directed by adults. In 1400, six months after King Richard II had been overthrown by Henry IV, the children of London gathered together and chose themselves kings. Adam of Usk tells us they congregated ‘in thousands … and made war upon each other… whereby many died’. The new king had to order their parents and masters to stop them.</p><p></p><p><span><span>G</span></span> This willingness of children to take the initiative in play, not just to wait for adults to direct them, is evident in the way they observed the calendar. Medieval life was regulated by light, weather, crops and the Church’s cycle of fasts and festivals. Children shared in the adult round of religious festivals, but had their own observances as well, semidetached from their elders. In the 1200s, the priest Thomas Docking remarked that in spring a child ‘follows the ploughman; in autumn he accompanies the grape-gatherers’. In 1518, the poet Alexander Barclay records children playing with tops in March, looking for fruit in summer and making footballs by filling pigs’ bladders with dried peas in autumn.</p><p></p><p><span><span>H</span></span> It is clear from this evidence that the relationship between adults and chil'+N'dren in medieval society was, in major respects, a modern one. Parents took an indulgent interest in their children, providing them with toys and giving them time to play. Children played in a wide variety of ways – imaginatively, skilfully, athletically and violently – developing their minds, bodies and social skills. Adults tried at times to direct play – partly to keep children in order, partly to give them skills for adult life – but children gravitated to one another and formed a culture of their own. We can answer Ariès''s thesis, then, with a resounding ''No!! Childhood has always been much the same.</p>'),NULL,NULL,N'',NULL,1,0,3,NULL,0,1985),
(N'ba2a9d4f-f59a-5a25-903f-bd3c963a4328',N'778ff78e-f2b6-542b-a322-c09cc42b0b3a',0,2,18,N'<p>Which paragraph contains the following information? </p><p>Write the correct letter<span> A–H</span> in boxes 27–31. </p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',12,0,1,NULL,0,1985),
(N'687c0fe3-5285-515f-8cf3-33e095db9aee',N'ba2a9d4f-f59a-5a25-903f-bd3c963a4328',0,3,19,N'<p>economic evidence for play in medieval England </p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Bằng chứng kinh tế về trò chơi ở Anh thời Trung cổ.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn D nói về tồn tại của ngành công nghiệp đồ chơi việc búp bê được sản xuất một cách thương mại, được nhập khẩu và đánh thuế</p><p>-&gt; chính bằng chứng về mặt kinh tế</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là D</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,27,NULL,0,1985),
(N'49884520-8157-5737-9297-d4d87c1da2c4',N'ba2a9d4f-f59a-5a25-903f-bd3c963a4328',0,3,19,N'<p>an example of how children created their own toys  </p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Ví dụ về cách trẻ em tự tạo ra đồ chơi.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn G trích dẫn vào năm 1518, Alexander Barclay ghi lại rằng trẻ con vào mùa thu đã tự làm những quả bóng đá bằng cách lấp đầy những bong bóng lợn bằng đậu khô</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là G</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,28,NULL,0,1985),
(N'2f4914f7-a745-591a-b356-cacf902af332',N'ba2a9d4f-f59a-5a25-903f-bd3c963a4328',0,3,19,N'<p>an example of warlike play approved by grown-ups </p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Ví dụ về trò chơi có tính chiến tranh được người lớn chấp thuận.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn E nói rằng bắn cung là môn thể thao được người lớn ủng hộ cho trẻ em trai để chuẩn bị cho xã hội chiến binh</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là E</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,29,NULL,0,1985),
(N'ad459739-9f05-5282-8289-d1c574bc727c',N'ba2a9d4f-f59a-5a25-903f-bd3c963a4328',0,3,19,N'<p>a political event mirrored in children’s play </p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Một sự kiện chính trị được phản ánh trong trò chơi của trẻ em.</p><p>+ Answer: Sau khi vua Richard II bị lật đổ (một sự kiện chính trị), trẻ em London tự chọn vua và đánh lẫn nhau</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là F</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,30,NULL,0,1985),
(N'867f3313-9f12-555b-94ef-689238c2a572',N'ba2a9d4f-f59a-5a25-903f-bd3c963a4328',0,3,19,N'<p>the origin of an academic debate about medieval life </p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Nguồn gốc của một cuộc tranh luận học thuật về cuộc sống thời Trung cổ.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn B nói về cuộc tranh luận về sự tồn tại của tuổi thơ thời Trung cổ bắt đầu từ Ariès, trong khi các nhà sử học hiện đại để chỉ ra dấu hiệu của tình yêu thương của cha mẹ thời bấy giờ</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là B</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,31,NULL,0,1985),
(N'6497eab2-f9f8-5d3f-b1de-e888daa7e4e4',N'778ff78e-f2b6-542b-a322-c09cc42b0b3a',0,2,18,N'<p>Look at the following dates (Questions 32-35) and the list of events below. </p><p>Match each date with the correct event, <span>A-J</span>. </p><p>Write the correct letter, <span>A-J</span>, in boxes 32-35 on your answer sheet. </p>',N'',N'',N'',N'Answer choices',10,0,2,NULL,0,1985),
(N'145f5313-59f8-5b6b-b621-b555e7d9a577',N'6497eab2-f9f8-5d3f-b1de-e888daa7e4e4',0,3,19,N'<p>1400 </p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Năm 1400, sự kiện trẻ em đánh nhau theo băng nhóm.</p><p>+ Answer: Vào năm 1400, trẻ em London tụ tập hàng nghìn người và gây chiến với nhau</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là I</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,32,NULL,0,1985),
(N'3ea71b49-f586-52b4-bc27-1c98ffc96632',N'6497eab2-f9f8-5d3f-b1de-e888daa7e4e4',0,3,19,N'<p>1518 </p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Năm 1518, mô tả các hoạt động theo mùa của trẻ em.</p><p>+ Answer: Vào năm 1518, Barclay ghi lại trẻ em chơi cù vào tháng Ba, hái quả vào mùa hè và làm bóng đá vào mùa thu</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là J</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,33,NULL,0,1985),
(N'dfc7aa45-c5f0-5abe-bcaf-372dc907069a',N'6497eab2-f9f8-5d3f-b1de-e888daa7e4e4',0,3,19,N'<p>1582 </p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Năm 1582, búp bê bị đánh thuế ở Anh.</p><p>+ Answer: Mỗi con búp bê bị đánh thuế nửa xu vào năm 1582</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là F</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,34,NULL,0,1985),
(N'57f88ee2-2ce5-5c7f-a2bc-56af2edab558',N'6497eab2-f9f8-5d3f-b1de-e888daa7e4e4',0,3,19,N'<p> 1908</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Năm 1908, bài thơ về giá trị của trò chơi.</p><p>+ Answer: Bài thơ "Vitaï Lampada" của Newbolt xuất bản năm 1908, ca ngợi tinh thần thể thao</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là C</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,35,NULL,0,1985),
(N'1fa83062-6bec-57ad-8b13-c836ae5e92c7',N'778ff78e-f2b6-542b-a322-c09cc42b0b3a',0,2,18,N'<p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3? </span></p><p><span>In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write  </span></p><p><span><span>TRUE</span> if the statement agrees with the information </span></p><p><span><span>FALSE</span> if the statement contradicts the information </span></p><p><span><span>NOT GIVEN</span> if there is no information on this </span></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',1,0,3,NULL,0,1985),
(N'8b3ecdc8-ced1-5a60-a376-532ca10ef9af',N'1fa83062-6bec-57ad-8b13-c836ae5e92c7',0,3,19,N'<p>Little is known about adult attitudes to children’s play in the Middle Ages.</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Có rất ít thông tin về thái độ của người lớn đối với trò chơi trẻ em thời Trung cổ.</p><p>+Answer: Tác giả khẳng định chúng ta biết rõ suy nghĩ của người lớn về vấn đề này</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,36,NULL,0,1985),
(N'e4b31c59-e487-5246-85fc-cf711bdc1bc0',N'1fa83062-6bec-57ad-8b13-c836ae5e92c7',0,3,19,N'<p>Most toys were imported into England before 1300.  </p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Phần lớn đồ chơi được nhập khẩu vào Anh trước năm 1300</p><p>+ Answer: Bài đọc nói rằng búp bê đã được sản xuất và nhập khẩu vào Anh, nhưng không cho biết đa số là nhập khẩu</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là Not given</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,37,NULL,0,1985),
(N'e879f547-c01f-573a-b418-e029974069c5',N'1fa83062-6bec-57ad-8b13-c836ae5e92c7',0,3,19,N'<p>Medieval children celebrated the seasons in their own ways. </p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms: “celebrate in their own ways” (ăn mừng theo cách của chúng) = “had their own observances”</p><p>+ Interpretation: Trẻ em thời Trung cổ ăn mừng các mùa theo cách riêng của chúng.</p><p>+ Answer: Trẻ em có các hoạt động theo mùa riêng, không hoàn toàn phụ thuộc vào người lớn</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là True</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,38,NULL,0,1985),
(N'c9f7f475-c7ae-5a16-91e2-2da709a21610',N'1fa83062-6bec-57ad-8b13-c836ae5e92c7',0,3,19,N'<p>Medieval children made presents for their parents on special occasions. </p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Trẻ em thời Trung cổ làm quà cho cha mẹ trong các dịp đặc biệt.</p><p>+ Answer: Bài đọc có nói đến mối quan hệ giữa cha mẹ và con cái vào thời Trung cổ, nhưng không nói gì đến việc trẻ em có tặng quà cho cha mẹ hay không</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là Not given</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,39,NULL,0,1985),
(N'da5bb560-aa7c-599a-a68c-5981d579beb7',N'1fa83062-6bec-57ad-8b13-c836ae5e92c7',0,3,19,N'<p>Parents and children in the Middle Ages behaved much as they do today.</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Cha mẹ và con cái thời Trung cổ cư xử khá giống như ngày nay.</p><p>+ Answer: Tác giả kết luận rằng tuổi thơ về bản chất đều giống nhau qua các thời đại</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là True</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,40,NULL,0,1985),
(N'bca3bc6a-858f-5b47-8c2a-ead40f2a1f9f',NULL,0,0,11,NULL,NULL,NULL,N'',N'Vol 6 READING FULL TEST 2',0,7,1,NULL,1,1984),
(N'19c1fc35-b217-5fc7-9485-9b382173f58b',N'bca3bc6a-858f-5b47-8c2a-ead40f2a1f9f',0,1,13,(CAST(N'<p><span>The history of colours and the meanings people have given  them  </span></p><p>The use of colours has a long history in human development. Prehistoric paintings in caves  were found to contain yellow and red earth, white chalk, and a black made from the soot of  burned animal fat. Over time, new colours were invented, using a wide range of materials and  processes; for example, Chinese yellow was made from the resin of the gamboge tree, and  saffron yellow in India from a flower, the Crocus sativus. Archaeological evidence tells us that  these societies did not operate in the production of these yellows. In Europe in the Middle Ages  (470–1500 AD), red was made from kermes insects, but when the Spanish explorers returned  from the Americas in the 15th century, they brought not only gold, silver, and new bookshelves,  but also a new shade of red. What was different about this new shade was that it was the result  of a process involving a species of beetle.  </p><p></p><p>Such colours were expensive. In ancient times, more than 10,000 murex shellfish had to be  crushed to make a single gram of purple. As a result, purple became the colour of kings and  emperors in ancient Persia and Rome, and was also worn by priests on ceremonial occasions.  In Europe, during the Renaissance (1300–1600 AD), patrons would state in contracts that  painters were required to use expensive pigments to add value to the works they  commissioned. For instance, they might ask that the artist use gold paint or ultramarine, which  was made from the semi-precious gem called lapis lazuli. This had to be imported from ‘beyond  the sea’, which is what ‘ultramarine’ means in Latin.  </p><p></p><p>In the early 1800s, chemists began to develop synthetic paints, often from metals such as cobalt  (cobalt blue), zinc (zinc white), etc. Without these new colours, Impressionism and other  aspects of modern art development would not have been possible. By the mid-1800s, another  development was the use of portable tubes to contain the paint and keep it fresh. Today, still  more pigments are being invented, many of synthetic organic origin, adding new colours,  greater transparency for mixing or glazing, greater lightfastness, and so on. Colour printing  techniques, colour film, and video also continue to improve, and modern software is, of course,  the newest colour resource. Photo editing software makes the colour manipulation of  photographic images widely available. Word processing sof' AS nvarchar(max))+N'tware allows colour to be added to  documents, which were once just black and white. The number of colours companies can  produce has risen from 16 shades of grey to millions of colours – more than anyone could  possibly need.  </p><p></p><p>There are many different meanings that people have given to colours. This is a process that has  gone on for much of human history and has not yet come to an end. Green being associated  with environmental protection is a good example of this. In Europe, the colour black has been  used to express a variety of meanings, for example, formality and elegance, among many  others. However, black is not the only colour that represents death. In China and some other  Asian countries, the colour of sickness and death is white, whereas it is red which is traditionally  used for weddings. The same colour represents danger in many European countries. There is  always a reason why a given colour becomes associated with certain feelings or ideas, but that  does not mean the association is universal.  </p><p></p><p>Throughout history, specific colours have been used in specific social contexts, and these uses  have been established and controlled. A clear example of this can be seen in the products  developed and marketed for children. </p><p></p><p>Many contemporary children’s toys are made of brightly  coloured plastic, and these sell well. Books for very young children also tend to feature bright  primary colours (red, yellow, and blue) because young children find these appealing. The  reason for this attraction was explained by colour psychologists. Jonas Cohn, for instance,  writing in the 1890s, said that preference for strong, pure colours is a basic human instinct, and  therefore this preference is strongly present in children.  Educators, designers, and manufacturers adopted Cohn’s idea as part of developing a new  culture of childhood with its own dress code, its own literature – and its own colour schemes.  Lately, ideas have altered, and children are introduced to adult culture much earlier.  Consequently, bright reds, yellows, and blues have to some degree been replaced by mixed  colours such as pinks, mauves, and oranges.   </p>'),NULL,NULL,N'',NULL,1,0,1,NULL,0,1984),
(N'161b1052-28ba-590e-bbc7-1c9847a26b36',N'19c1fc35-b217-5fc7-9485-9b382173f58b',0,2,18,N'<p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? </span></p><p><span>In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write: </span></p><p><span><span>TRUE</span> if the statement agrees with the information </span></p><p><span><span>FALSE</span> if the statement contradicts the information </span></p><p><span><span>NOT GIVEN</span> if there is no information on this </span></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',1,0,1,NULL,0,1984),
(N'4f1f3ad7-5ed7-5bc7-9184-340c7ae4f8b7',N'161b1052-28ba-590e-bbc7-1c9847a26b36',0,3,19,N'<p>The shade of red brought back by 15th-century explorers was more popular with the public  than the red made from kermes insects.  </p>',N'<p>- Interpretation: Sắc đỏ do các nhà thám hiểm thế kỷ 15 mang về phổ biến hơn với công chúng so với màu đỏ làm từ côn trùng kermes.</p><p> - Answer: Đoạn văn chỉ mô tả sự khác biệt về nguồn gốc, không so sánh mức độ phổ biến.</p><p> -&gt; Đáp án là Not given </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,1,NULL,0,1984),
(N'6b9a5ea3-58d4-5584-b95e-b9a39a410e92',N'161b1052-28ba-590e-bbc7-1c9847a26b36',0,3,19,N'<p>During the Renaissance, some European artists were obliged to use low cost materials.  </p>',N'<p>- Interpretation: Trong thời Phục hưng, một số họa sĩ châu Âu bị bắt buộc sử dụng vật liệu giá rẻ. </p><p>- Answer: Các nhà bảo trợ yêu cầu họa sĩ sử dụng bột màu đắt tiền, để tăng thêm giá trị cho tác phẩm họ đặt hàng </p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là False   </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,2,NULL,0,1984),
(N'3732f7d5-6939-55e1-b19c-10eec83dba30',N'161b1052-28ba-590e-bbc7-1c9847a26b36',0,3,19,N'<p>The colours invented by chemists in the 1800s led to major new art movements. </p>',N'<p>- Interpretation: Các màu sắc do nhà hóa học phát minh vào những năm 1800 đã dẫn đến các phong trào nghệ thuật mới  </p><p>- Answer: Đoạn văn nói rằng nếu không có màu tổng hợp, trường phái Ấn tượng và các thành tựu nghệ thuật hiện đại khác đã không thể xảy ra. </p><p>\-&gt; Đáp án là True   </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,3,NULL,0,1984),
(N'05fcef6a-0ea2-5672-8912-b3977c143827',N'161b1052-28ba-590e-bbc7-1c9847a26b36',0,3,19,N'<p>People today continue to give new meanings to colours.  </p>',N'<p>- Interpretation:) Ngày nay mọi người vẫn tiếp tục tạo ra những ý nghĩa mới cho màu sắc.</p><p>- Answer: • Quá trình gán ý nghĩa cho màu sắc vẫn chưa kết thúc, ví dụ như màu xanh lá gắn với bảo vệ môi trường. </p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là True  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,4,NULL,0,1984),
(N'0679dfa6-2fab-55f6-b2c8-a913a67b142a',N'161b1052-28ba-590e-bbc7-1c9847a26b36',0,3,19,N'<p>In Europe, there are an equal number of positive meanings of black as there are negative ones.  </p>',N'<p>- Interpretation: Ở châu Âu, số lượng ý nghĩa tích cực của màu đen bằng với số lượng ý nghĩa tiêu cực. </p><p>- Answer: Đoạn văn liệt kê một số ý nghĩa của màu đen nhưng không so sánh số lượng</p><p> -&gt; Đáp án là Not given  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,5,NULL,0,1984),
(N'14ab3d12-cc81-5ae8-8cdc-ade53c81ff69',N'161b1052-28ba-590e-bbc7-1c9847a26b36',0,3,19,N'<p>Jonas Cohn believed children naturally like dark colours.  </p>',N'<p>- Interpretation: Jonas Cohn tin rằng trẻ em thích màu tối một cách tự nhiên. </p><p>- Answer: Cohn viết rằng bản năng con người là ưa chuộng những màu mạnh và trong sáng, và vì vậy những đặc điểm này thì nổi bật ở trẻ em </p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là False   </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,6,NULL,0,1984),
(N'382e82ac-c3a4-553b-95de-983435513928',N'19c1fc35-b217-5fc7-9485-9b382173f58b',0,2,18,N'<p>Complete the notes below. </p><p>Choose <span>ONE WORD ONLY </span>from the passage for each answer. </p><p>Write your answers in boxes 7-13 on your answer sheet. </p>',N'',N'',N'',N'Making and Using Colours',11,0,2,NULL,0,1984),
(N'df2e78eb-be4c-58be-a149-380b52485277',N'382e82ac-c3a4-553b-95de-983435513928',0,3,19,N'<h3>Making and Using Colours</h3><p><span>Making paints</span></p><p><span>Purple was:</span></p><p>• made from shellfish </p><p>• The earliest paints discovered in  }{SPACE}{ were made from animal products, chalk or  different soils.   </p><p>• expensive </p><p>• In the Middle Ages, red was made from either kermes insects or a kind of }{SPACE}{ </p><p>• used mostly by rulers and }{SPACE}{ </p><p>• In the Renaissance, ultramarine was made out of a type of }{SPACE}{ </p><p>• In the 1800s, chemists started to make colours by using different  }{SPACE}{ </p><p><span>Colours and different countries </span></p><p>• In the mid 1800s, colours were put into  }{SPACE}{ which made them easy to transport.   </p><p>• Red is worn at }{SPACE}{  in some countries but is also used to warn people of danger.   </p>',N'<p>- Interpretation: Những loại sơn sớm nhất được phát hiện trong ____ được làm từ sản phẩm động vật, phấn trắng hoặc các loại đất khác nhau. </p><p>- Answer: Các bức tranh thời tiền sử trong hang động chứa các chất màu từ đất, phấn và mỡ động vật </p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là caves  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,7,NULL,0,1984),
(N'91700d68-cd5e-550b-a60d-7fafb183ac33',N'382e82ac-c3a4-553b-95de-983435513928',0,3,19,N'Question number 8',N'<p>- Interpretation: Vào thời Trung cổ, màu đỏ được làm từ côn trùng kermes hoặc một loại ____. </p><p>- Answer: Màu đỏ mới được các nhà thám hiểm Tây Ban Nha mang về từ châu Mỹ được làm từ bọ cánh cứng </p><p> -&gt; Đáp án là beetle  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,8,NULL,0,1984),
(N'479817a8-24eb-57b7-b2e5-96bc0a2df487',N'382e82ac-c3a4-553b-95de-983435513928',0,3,19,N'Question number 9',N'<p>- Interpretation: Màu tím được sử dụng chủ yếu bởi những người cai trị và ____. </p><p>- Answer: Màu tím đã trở thành màu của các bậc quân chủ ở Ba Tư và Hy Lạp cổ đại, và cũng được mặc bởi thầy tu trong những buổi lễ </p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là priests  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,9,NULL,0,1984),
(N'cd32ceb7-22ae-5a38-ade3-fdc7628bdfb1',N'382e82ac-c3a4-553b-95de-983435513928',0,3,19,N'Question number 10',N'<p>- Interpretation: Trong thời Phục hưng, ultramarine được làm từ một loại ____.</p><p> - Answer: Ultramarine được làm từ một loại đá quý tên là lapis lazuli</p><p> -&gt; Đáp án là gem  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,10,NULL,0,1984),
(N'2770367f-1b8e-58f8-a13b-f71407acb5f8',N'382e82ac-c3a4-553b-95de-983435513928',0,3,19,N'Question number 11',N'<p>- Interpretation: Vào những năm 1800, các nhà hóa học bắt đầu tạo ra màu sắc bằng cách sử dụng các ____ khác nhau. </p><p>- Answer: Màu tổng hợp được làm từ kim loại như coban, kẽm </p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là metals   </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,11,NULL,0,1984),
(N'bea09122-8b9d-5110-99c2-280faafe2bb6',N'382e82ac-c3a4-553b-95de-983435513928',0,3,19,N'Question number 12',N'<p>- Interpretation: Vào giữa những năm 1800, màu sắc được cho vào ____ giúp dễ vận chuyển. </p><p>- Answer:  Các ống (tubes) sơn di động giúp bảo quản và vận chuyển dễ dàng</p><p> -&gt; Đáp án là tubes  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,12,NULL,0,1984),
(N'6ce7b658-7be4-5e70-8389-e2748ce48355',N'382e82ac-c3a4-553b-95de-983435513928',0,3,19,N'Question number 13',N'<p>- Interpretation: Màu đỏ được mặc trong ____ ở một số quốc gia nhưng cũng được dùng để cảnh báo nguy hiểm. </p><p>- Answer: • Ở Trung Quốc và một số nước châu Á, màu đỏ truyền thống được dùng trong đám cưới  </p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là weddings  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,13,NULL,0,1984),
(N'8af3d2dc-fdcd-50d5-ab58-62e12cef128f',N'bca3bc6a-858f-5b47-8c2a-ead40f2a1f9f',0,1,14,(CAST(N'<p><span>The Future of Food Packaging </span>  </p><p><span>A }{HEADING}{ </span> Food companies spend a lot of time thinking about packaging as a way to represent  their brand and make consumers love their products. More than cosmetic details like  labels or logos, a food’s container can suggest playfulness, environmental  consciousness, or high technology. Packaging provides consumers’ first and last  impressions of a product.  </p><p></p><p><span>B }{HEADING}{ </span> Fortunately for consumers, advances in food packaging technology promise to make  food storage and preparation simpler. Consumers are growing ever more obsessed with  sleek technology, reducing food waste, and minimizing health risks to themselves and  the environment, and in response, food packaging is undergoing some interesting  developments. Food-packaging designers are hard at work to make groceries  environmentally friendly, compact, and functional. </p><p></p><p><span> C  }{HEADING}{ </span>Edible packaging has been proposed as one solution to consumers’ environmental  concerns because it leaves no waste. The fried chicken chain KFC, for example, is  experimenting with an edible coffee-cup. Made from a hard cookie lined with heat resistant white chocolate, the cup is KFC’s attempt to reduce its landfill waste and  satisfy customers who are concerned that businesses produce products that support  food-system sustainability and innovation. Another company, Stonyfield Organic,  introduced frozen yogurt ‘pearls’ using edible food wrappers. The skin has no flavor and  can be rinsed and eaten with the yogurt (much like a grape), eliminating the need for  plastic spoons or wrappers for those on the go. It seems that people still want a layer of  sanitary protection, though, because the spherical yogurts are still sold in containers.  Similarly, a company called Loliware has sold gelatin-based edible drinking cups for two  years, in flavors like Madagascar vanilla and tart cherry. And last year, the company  introduced edible cupcake wrappers made from potato starch. Even with these new  advances, one decade-old edible invention continues to see great success — the clear  paper used to wrap Japanese Bolan Rice Candy. </p><p></p><p><span> D }{HEADING}{ </span> Another development has been nonstick packaging, which can eliminate the 3 to 15  percent of sauces left inside traditional bottles, like those last trails of ketchup and  mayonnaise that won’t come out no matter how hard you shake or ' AS nvarchar(max))+N'squeeze. Liquiglide  — which refers to both a company and the product it makes — is a permanently wet  slippery surface that allows viscous matter to slide off easily. Liquiglide estimates that its  coating could prevent 1 million tons of food waste each year. The coating is made from  components approved by the US government, and, according to the company, does not  affect the taste or smell of food. Another benefit of Liquiglide is that it prevents  carbonated beverages from going flat. </p><p></p><p><span> E }{HEADING}{ </span> New safety-enhancing packaging is now addressing the issue of food spoilage. It  might seem this was solved long ago with the advent of the ‘Sell-By’ date stamp, which  was meant to warn customers of when the food would no longer be considered suitable  for consumption. But after a Harvard report revealed that sell-by dates are often  inaccurate because of variances in transportation and grocery store policies, and that  they also contribute to America’s food-waste problem, the stamps have lost credibility in  the food industry. In response, scientists are working on food packaging — like plastic  wrap — that is ‘active and intelligent’ with tiny embedded sensors to first detect and  later prevent food from spoiling. This advancement in food packaging draws upon  nanotechnology, which is dedicated to making electronic sensors tiny and inexpensive.  Of course, one could also rely on what has saved humankind from food poisoning for  millennia — the senses. If it smells bad, throw it away. </p><p></p><p><span> F  }{HEADING}{ </span>Another emerging technology is packaging that disappears. MonoSol, LLC creates  food-grade water-soluble bags for pre-portioned oatmeal or rice. When boiled, the bag  dissolves, leaving only the food, ready to eat. MonoSol, LLC is marketing this to  professional kitchens as well as consumers, as a way to pre-measure meal ingredients  and ensure consistency regardless of who is cooking. Tomorrow Machine, a Swedish  design firm, has plans for three disappearing packages: an oil bottle made from  hardened sugar that cracks open like an egg; a fruit juice container made from seaweed  that ‘will wither at the same rate as its content’; and a peelable beeswax package for  rice or other dry goods.    </p><p></p><p><span>G }{HEADING}{ </span> Super-compressed packaging serves the increasing number of city dwellers who  generally have tiny kitchens and no storage room. Additionally, many people living in  urban ar'+N'eas walk home from grocery stores, and they need lighter and smaller  packages. Tomorrow Machine is also working on a compressed tiny package that  expands into a full-size bowl when hot water is added. </p>'),NULL,NULL,N'',NULL,4,0,2,NULL,0,1984),
(N'f2bdc598-6c41-541e-884c-4177af592f52',N'8af3d2dc-fdcd-50d5-ab58-62e12cef128f',0,2,18,N'<p>Reading Passage 2 has seven sections, <span>A–G. </span></p><p>Choose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below. </p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',4,0,1,NULL,0,1984),
(N'845d9396-d9b5-55dc-b5a9-d1c341cd9208',N'f2bdc598-6c41-541e-884c-4177af592f52',0,3,19,N'Paragraph A',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Sử dụng bao bì để truyền tải ý tưởng và thu hút khách hàng.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn A nói rằng bao bì không chỉ là những chi tiết thẩm mỹ mà còn thể hiện các giá trị được liệt kê, tạo nên ấn tượng đầu tiên và cuối cùng của người tiêu dùng về sản phẩm</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là ix</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,14,NULL,0,1984),
(N'dcf4a872-bc5a-56be-b35a-908f21332951',N'f2bdc598-6c41-541e-884c-4177af592f52',0,3,19,N'Paragraph B',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Nhiều lý do cho sự thay đổi trong bao bì.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn B nói rằng người tiêu dùng ngày càng quan tâm đến công nghệ, lãng phí, rủi ro sức khỏe và môi trường, thúc đẩy thay đổi bao bì</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là ii</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,15,NULL,0,1984),
(N'9e5b2f3a-cf3b-5368-b32d-f1942dd6f9ca',N'f2bdc598-6c41-541e-884c-4177af592f52',0,3,19,N'Paragraph C',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Bao bì có thể ăn được cùng với thực phẩm bên trong.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn C giới thiệu về các loại bao bì có thể ăn được như cốc cà phê của KFC (làm từ bánh quy) và bao bì sữa chua ăn được</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là iv</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,16,NULL,0,1984),
(N'170f2241-0283-5beb-bfab-b117a1e83ac3',N'f2bdc598-6c41-541e-884c-4177af592f52',0,3,19,N'Paragraph D',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Bao bì cho phép người tiêu dùng sử dụng nhiều sản phẩm hơn.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn D nói rằng lớp bao bì chống dính có thể loại bỏ từ 3 đến 15 phần trăm các loại sốt còn lại trong các chai lọ truyền thống</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là i</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,17,NULL,0,1984),
(N'dd495868-d546-5296-a6db-bf7ab53066a3',N'f2bdc598-6c41-541e-884c-4177af592f52',0,3,19,N'Paragraph E',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Bao bì báo hiệu khi thực phẩm bắt đầu thối rữa.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn E nói về các nhà khoa học nghiên cứu về bao bì thực phẩm với cảm biến phát hiện và ngăn ngừa thực phẩm bị hỏng</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là vii</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,18,NULL,0,1984),
(N'25a7db0e-3ab3-5c75-a3ca-557074cb039d',N'f2bdc598-6c41-541e-884c-4177af592f52',0,3,19,N'Paragraph F',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Bao bì biến mất hoặc phân hủy nhanh chóng.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn F nhắc đến một loại công nghệ đang lên chính là các loại bao bì có thể biến mất, sau đó liệt kê ví dụ về các loại bao bì có thể tự phân hủy</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là x</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,19,NULL,0,1984),
(N'3a0e36a9-80f6-5bf2-8dc3-1cfc734d8b01',N'f2bdc598-6c41-541e-884c-4177af592f52',0,3,19,N'Paragraph G',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Bao bì không chiếm nhiều diện tích.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn G nói rằng bao bì siêu nén phù hợp với cư dân thành phố có nhà bếp nhỏ, không có nhà kho và thường đi bộ về từ siêu thị (cần đến bao bì nhẹ và nhỏ hơn)</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là v</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,20,NULL,0,1984),
(N'7fd1177e-cae2-5f86-afc0-f38f38987dc8',N'8af3d2dc-fdcd-50d5-ab58-62e12cef128f',0,2,18,N'<p><span>Look at the following companies (Questions 21–23) and the list of packaging developments below. </span></p><p><span>Match each company with the correct packaging development, <span>A–F</span>. </span></p><p><span>Write the correct letter, <span>A–F</span>, in boxes 21–23 on your answer sheet. </span></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'Answer choices',10,0,2,NULL,0,1984),
(N'eaf6fb05-a005-5336-960b-dbcfacfa1faa',N'7fd1177e-cae2-5f86-afc0-f38f38987dc8',0,3,19,N'<p>KFC </p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms: "a sweet container for hot drinks" (sweet container = cup made with hard cookie, hot drinks = coffee_ Interpretation: Một vật chứa ngọt cho đồ uống nóng.</p><p>+ Answer: Cốc cà phê ăn được của KFC làm từ bánh quy cứng với lớp sô cô la trắng chịu nhiệt.</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là E</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,21,NULL,0,1984),
(N'99c9b062-99b0-50c8-a848-f460ea9f2f35',N'7fd1177e-cae2-5f86-afc0-f38f38987dc8',0,3,19,N'<p>Loliware </p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms: "packaging made from a vegetable product" (edible cupcake wrappers = packaging, vegetable product - sản phẩm từ rau củ = potato starch)</p><p>+ Interpretation: Bao bì làm từ sản phẩm thực vật.</p><p>+ Answer Loliware sử dụng tinh bột khoai tây (nguồn gốc thực vật) để làm vỏ bánh cupcake ăn được.</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là D</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,22,NULL,0,1984),
(N'b5b95777-f199-5019-a293-3c8300d99e40',N'7fd1177e-cae2-5f86-afc0-f38f38987dc8',0,3,19,N'<p> Tomorrow Machine </p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms: "a container that gets bigger under certain conditions" (container = package, under certain conditions - với điều kiện nhất định = when hot water is added - khi thêm nước nóng vào)</p><p>+ Interpretation: Một vật chứa phình to ra trong điều kiện nhất định.</p><p>+ Answer: Gói nén siêu nhỏ sẽ được mở rộng thành bát cỡ lớn khi thêm nước nóng</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là A</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,23,NULL,0,1984),
(N'4d6f8897-b0ad-5e93-817a-32fff2f8a8fd',N'8af3d2dc-fdcd-50d5-ab58-62e12cef128f',0,2,18,N'<p>Complete the sentences below. </p><p>Choose <span>ONE WORD ONLY </span>from the passage for each answer. </p><p>Write your answers in boxes 24–26 on your answer sheet. </p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',11,0,3,NULL,0,1984),
(N'41a6153e-d74d-576c-a608-0756431206aa',N'4d6f8897-b0ad-5e93-817a-32fff2f8a8fd',0,3,19,N'<p>In Japan, }{SPACE}{ has been used as edible packaging for years.</p><p>Liquiglide reduces food waste, especially in bottles containing various }{SPACE}{ </p><p>Tomorrow Machine is planning to use solid }{SPACE}{ as a container for oil.</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Ở Nhật Bản, ____ đã được sử dụng làm bao bì ăn được trong nhiều năm.</p><p>+ Answer: Một phát minh ăn được có từ nhiều thập kỷ là giấy trong (rice paper) dùng để gói kẹo gạo Nhật Bản </p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là paper</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,24,NULL,0,1984),
(N'89647451-cafb-5514-a974-fe21a0f6c4c2',N'4d6f8897-b0ad-5e93-817a-32fff2f8a8fd',0,3,19,N'Question number 25',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Liquiglide giảm lãng phí thực phẩm, đặc biệt trong chai chứa các ____ khác nhau.</p><p>+ Answer: Các loại sốt (sauces) đặc như tương cà, sốt mayonnaise thường bị sót lại trong chai, nên Liquiglide cho phép vật chất dạng sệt chảy ra 1 cách dễ dàng, có thể phòng tránh 1 tỉ tấn thức ăn khỏi bị lãng phí mỗi năm </p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là sauces</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,25,NULL,0,1984),
(N'1ef60808-ccd3-5ab0-b2df-a3c47f0ef72b',N'4d6f8897-b0ad-5e93-817a-32fff2f8a8fd',0,3,19,N'Question number 26',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Tomorrow Machine đang lên kế hoạch sử dụng ____ rắn làm vật chứa dầu.</p><p>+ Answer: Chai dầu của Tomorrow Machine được làm từ đường cứng có thể được tách ra như quả trứng </p><p>- &gt; Đáp án là sugar</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,26,NULL,0,1984),
(N'd496fb27-7ebf-5a1f-9eac-334fbe0cba07',N'bca3bc6a-858f-5b47-8c2a-ead40f2a1f9f',0,1,15,(CAST(N'<p><span>All in the family </span></p><p> A person''s brothers and sisters can have a powerful effect on their adult behaviour  We can choose our friends, the saying goes, but we cannot choose our family of origin. Our  parents provide the genetic material and make powerful early role models, but even more  influential in determining what kind of adult we will become are our brothers and sisters — our  siblings. They occupy a position of unique intimacy in our lives and cast a longer shadow than  many recognise or are prepared to acknowledge. By turns, enraging and lovable, familiar and  mysterious, our brothers and sisters are the human beings who people our first social  relationships. And a sibling relationship is the most enduring relationship many of us will ever  have — no less emotionally intense than the bonds we form with our spouses and our own  children — if only because they started when we were so young.  </p><p></p><p>Surprising new research by Dr Gene Brody found that having older children who do well in  school and are well liked by other children leads to parental ‘basking’ — increasing mothers''  self-esteem. It is clear that in turn this is associated with more positive parenting of younger  children, who display fewer behavioural problems as a result. Conversely, parents who get a  difficult first child may in turn experience a negative spiral of household tension.  </p><p></p><p>International sports star Piri Weepu is a rugby hard man, but at least some of his tough  temperament was forged long ago in the family home. His older brother Billy started rugby — tackling little Piri when he was just four — to ‘harden him up’. It seemed to work: Piri followed  his brother in playing for the under-sevens league before he even started school. There are as  many such stories as there are families: in the formative hothouse of the family, siblings interact  in complex ways with the powerful forcefields of parents, genetics and personality already at  work. It starts with birth order, which determines play roles: the firstborn leader, the middle-child  mediator and the rebellious youngest. These are roles that can stick for life. </p><p></p><p> Clinical psychologist Claire Cartwright says she has clients who believe, and it might not have  been true, that they were treated differently from their siblings, that one child in the family was  preferred over others. They are quite convinced that the parental judgements on them all those  years ago were ' AS nvarchar(max))+N'harsher, and that they were the ones who always got into trouble. Later, in the  workplace, such a person might be particularly defensive, and so behave in a way more prone  to attracting harsh judgements.  </p><p></p><p>However, the research shows that being Mummy or Daddy''s favourite has its own traps. If you  were the easy-going, co-operative child at home, you probably excelled at pleasing parents and,  later, bosses. But you might, as an adult, find it hard to be assertive with authority figures and  lack direction. On the other hand, the sibling who is disruptive and annoying as a child may be  able to reinterpret that role later, turning those attention-seeking characteristics into strengths  like determination and leadership. </p><p></p><p>How is it that full siblings, despite sharing DNA, can turn out so differently? One answer is that,  in fact, each sibling grows up in a different family, a unique micro-culture. For example, the  firstborn is, for a while, an only child, and therefore has a completely different experience of the  parents than those born later. The parents themselves are growing up too, weathering hardship  or good fortune, so one sibling might experience stability and closeness while another might be  raised in the midst of crisis. </p><p></p><p> Of course, there are many positive aspects of sibling relationships. Annette Henderson, a  lecturer in psychology, says firstborn children learn vocabulary more quickly than their siblings  because they are not competing to spend one-on-one time with parents. But younger children in  turn benefit from unintentional instruction from their bigger brothers and sisters, acquiring entire  phrases and an understanding of social concepts such as politeness. Similarly, a Cambridge  University study of 140 children found that even when there is a great deal of conflict, siblings  will still create a rich world of play and make-believe that extends them developmentally. Love hate relationships were common among the children, but even those who fought the most had  as many positive interactions as the other sibling pairs. It is also true that children compete for  parental attention by making themselves different from their brothers and sisters, particularly if  they are close in age. A 2003 research paper studied adolescents from 185 families over two  years, finding that those who changed, to differentiate themselves from their siblings, increased  the amount of warmth they gained from parents, '+N'and also developed stronger personalities and  a better sense of their own identity.  </p><p></p><p>Another consideration is that many families today are smaller and more intimate than their  historical counterparts. This may be advantageous because siblings tend to know each other  better and remain lifelong friends compared to children from bigger or more widely spaced  families, who perhaps lose touch with one another after leaving home. Then there was a 2010  American study which found that having a sister, whether younger or older, meant that 10- to  14-year-olds were less likely to feel lonely, unloved, self-conscious or fearful. The same study  found that having a loving sibling of either gender promoted good deeds, such as helping a  neighbour around the house or helping other children at school.  </p>'),NULL,NULL,N'',NULL,1,0,3,NULL,0,1984),
(N'd4bfbafc-b188-58e5-b612-8455bb396509',N'd496fb27-7ebf-5a1f-9eac-334fbe0cba07',0,2,18,N'<p><span>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3? </span></p><p><span>In boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet, write: </span></p><p><span><span>YES</span> if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer </span></p><p><span><span>NO</span> if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer </span></p><p><span><span>NOT GIVEN</span> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this </span></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',1,0,1,NULL,0,1984),
(N'c67ea8f9-98ed-59c5-a886-69f1c3f474cb',N'd4bfbafc-b188-58e5-b612-8455bb396509',0,3,19,N'<p> Parents and siblings play equal roles in shaping people''s adult personalities.</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Cha mẹ và anh chị em có vai trò ngang nhau trong việc hình thành tính cách người lớn.</p><p>+ Answer: Tác giả nói anh chị em có ảnh hưởng lớn hơn cha mẹ, không phải ngang bằng.</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là No</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,27,NULL,0,1984),
(N'647b62e7-922c-52b7-8f42-9e4cdd6b4236',N'd4bfbafc-b188-58e5-b612-8455bb396509',0,3,19,N'<p> People''s first social relationships tend to be with siblings of their own gender. </p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Mối quan hệ xã hội đầu tiên của con người có xu hướng là với anh chị em cùng giới.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn văn không đề cập đến giới tính của anh chị em trong mối quan hệ xã hội đầu tiên.</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là Not given</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,28,NULL,0,1984),
(N'c899bc84-2508-511a-8a00-cecbce1c33db',N'd4bfbafc-b188-58e5-b612-8455bb396509',0,3,19,N'<p>People''s relationships with their siblings tend to receive less attention when they marry.</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Mối quan hệ của mọi người với anh chị em có xu hướng nhận được ít sự chú ý hơn khi họ kết hôn.</p><p>+ Answer: Bài đọc không nói về sự thay đổi trong mối quan hệ anh chị em sau khi kết hôn.</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là Not given</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,29,NULL,0,1984),
(N'7b028db0-1f7e-561e-ae0c-11009aca2d6d',N'd4bfbafc-b188-58e5-b612-8455bb396509',0,3,19,N'<p>Parental ‘basking’ is advantageous for later siblings.  </p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Sự ''hãnh diện'' của cha mẹ có lợi cho những đứa con sau.</p><p>+ Answer: Khi cha mẹ hãnh diện về đứa con cả, họ nuôi dạy con sau tích cực hơn, giúp con sau ít gặp vấn đề về hành vi</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là Yes</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,30,NULL,0,1984),
(N'f9e4eda7-3cd8-5169-ae7f-e3a6e0f0878f',N'd496fb27-7ebf-5a1f-9eac-334fbe0cba07',0,2,18,N'<p>Choose the correct letter <span>A, B, C or D </span></p><p>Write the correct letter in boxes 31-34 on your answer sheet. </p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',1,0,2,NULL,0,1984),
(N'747545bf-6cc5-5685-9cda-c758c1c8368c',N'f9e4eda7-3cd8-5169-ae7f-e3a6e0f0878f',0,3,19,N'<p>What point does the writer make about birth order in the third paragraph? </p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation : Tác giả nói gì về thứ tự sinh trong đoạn ba?</p><p>+ Answer: Thứ tự sinh xác định vai trò trong gia đình và những vai trò này có thể gắn bó suốt đời, định hình tính cách khi trưởng thành.</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là B</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,31,NULL,0,1984),
(N'eb500ad6-4bcc-5f35-8d39-8be07a56121f',N'f9e4eda7-3cd8-5169-ae7f-e3a6e0f0878f',0,3,19,N'<p>What are we told about some of Claire Cartwright''s clients? </p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Điều gì được nói về một số khách hàng của Claire Cartwright?</p><p>+ Answer: Khách hàng tin rằng họ được đối xử khác với các anh chị em của mình, và họ tin rằng cha mẹ họ khắc nghiệt hơn rất nhiều vào khoảng thời gian đó</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là C</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,32,NULL,0,1984),
(N'fb60da92-c307-577c-baae-08982493dff6',N'f9e4eda7-3cd8-5169-ae7f-e3a6e0f0878f',0,3,19,N'<p>What is the writer''s main point about siblings in the fifth paragraph? </p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Luận điểm chính của tác giả về anh chị em trong đoạn năm là gì?</p><p>+ Answer: Những đứa trẻ nghịch ngợm, gây rối có thể chuyển đặc điểm đó thành điểm mạnh như sự quyết tâm và khả năng lãnh đạo khi trưởng thành</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là C</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,33,NULL,0,1984),
(N'd1a52bbe-46cb-5781-ba78-fbfbf0415cc6',N'f9e4eda7-3cd8-5169-ae7f-e3a6e0f0878f',0,3,19,N'<p> Which of the following best summarises the writer''s argument in the sixth paragraph?</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Điều nào sau đây tóm tắt đúng nhất lập luận của tác giả trong đoạn sáu?</p><p>+ Answer: Mỗi đứa trẻ lớn lên trong môi trường gia đình khác nhau vì cha mẹ thay đổi theo thời gian và hoàn cảnh sống khác nhau.</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là D</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,34,NULL,0,1984),
(N'2e3f66c2-a3f1-5a8e-af58-2a88b999f073',N'd496fb27-7ebf-5a1f-9eac-334fbe0cba07',0,2,18,N'<p>Complete the summary using the list of phrases below.</p><p>Drag the correct word or phrase from the list into each gap.</p>',N'',N'',N'',N'The positive aspects of sibling relationships',13,0,3,NULL,0,1984),
(N'2561b70c-524b-5144-a49c-fbb5709f474d',N'2e3f66c2-a3f1-5a8e-af58-2a88b999f073',0,3,19,N'<h3>The positive aspects of sibling relationships</h3><p>Annette Henderson suggests that young children''s interactions with older siblings involve }{SPACE}{ .</p><p>Also, a Cambridge study found that siblings still enjoy }{SPACE}{ even when they have a tendency to fight.</p><p>Research conducted in 2003 suggests that children develop }{SPACE}{ as a result of seeking attention.</p><p>Another factor is the trend for smaller families, which may mean today''s siblings enjoy }{SPACE}{ as adults.</p><p>A 2010 American study linked having a sister with }{SPACE}{ among children aged 10-14.</p><p>Finally, having a sibling may promote }{SPACE}{ according to the same study.  </p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Annette Henderson gợi ý rằng tương tác của trẻ nhỏ với anh chị lớn hơn liên quan đến ____.</p><p>+ Answer: Trẻ nhỏ học hỏi từ anh chị lớn, tiếp thu các cụm từ và khái niệm xã hội</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là G</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,35,NULL,0,1984),
(N'0dee252d-9ef4-59bc-8ff9-3072e0905d10',N'2e3f66c2-a3f1-5a8e-af58-2a88b999f073',0,3,19,N'Question number 36',N'<p>+ Synonyms: "imaginative games" = "play and make-believe".</p><p>+ Interpretation: Nghiên cứu của Cambridge cho thấy anh chị em vẫn thích ____ ngay cả khi có xu hướng cãi nhau.</p><p>+ Answer: Nghiên cứu cho thấy rằng các anh chị em vẵn tạo ra một thế giới chơi đùa phong phú và trí tưởng tượng mà giúp chúng phát triển</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là B</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,36,NULL,0,1984),
(N'f11fed1e-783a-5943-9931-49237072a96c',N'2e3f66c2-a3f1-5a8e-af58-2a88b999f073',0,3,19,N'Question number 37',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Nghiên cứu năm 2003 cho thấy trẻ em phát triển ____ do tìm kiếm sự chú ý.</p><p>+ Answer: Khi trẻ cố gắng tỏ ra khác biệt với anh chị em, chúng phát triển cá tính mạnh mẽ hơn và ý thức về bản thân tốt hơn.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,37,NULL,0,1984),
(N'dbf94901-6bfe-5345-b339-edd23b1e0ae7',N'2e3f66c2-a3f1-5a8e-af58-2a88b999f073',0,3,19,N'Question number 38',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Xu hướng gia đình nhỏ hơn có thể có nghĩa là anh chị em ngày nay có ____ khi trưởng thành.</p><p>+ Answer: Gia đình ngày nay thì nhỏ hơn và thân mật hơn, giúp anh chị em gần gũi và giữ tình bạn suốt đời</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là I</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,38,NULL,0,1984),
(N'c007ba38-2494-572a-8d58-e587e0ed89f6',N'2e3f66c2-a3f1-5a8e-af58-2a88b999f073',0,3,19,N'Question number 39',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Một nghiên cứu của Mỹ năm 2010 đã liên kết việc có chị/em gái với ____ ở trẻ 10-14 tuổi.</p><p>+ Answer: Có chị/em gái giúp trẻ trong độ tuổi 10 đến 14 ít cảm thấy cô đơn, không được yêu thương, tự ti hoặc sợ hãi</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là K</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,39,NULL,0,1984),
(N'57f46935-376b-5cb8-b18c-851e9f9e1379',N'2e3f66c2-a3f1-5a8e-af58-2a88b999f073',0,3,19,N'Question number 40',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Cuối cùng, có anh chị em có thể thúc đẩy ____ theo cùng nghiên cứu đó.</p><p>+ Answer: Anh chị em yêu thương khuyến khích hành vi tốt như giúp đỡ hàng xóm hoặc bạn học</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là D</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,40,NULL,0,1984),
(N'5e997e1a-b52b-5984-9975-67550f4ca0d7',NULL,0,0,11,NULL,NULL,NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-6/iL.VOL6.10.S1982.mp3',N'Vol 6 LISTENING FULL TEST 10',0,7,1,NULL,1,1982),
(N'4ce94a14-c4a2-5dd6-9cbd-e6ac789a3b7a',N'5e997e1a-b52b-5984-9975-67550f4ca0d7',0,1,13,(CAST(N'<h2>Health and Fitness Centre</h2><p>Speaker A: Good morning, Health and Fitness Center.<br>Speaker B: Oh, good morning. I was thinking of joining the center, but I''d like to find out a bit more about your facilities first. For example, what are your opening hours?<br>Speaker A: We open every day at 7 a.m. and close at 11 p.m. during the week, and 9.30 at weekends.<br>Speaker B: Right. And how much does membership cost?<br>Speaker A: Was this for yourself?<br>Speaker B: Well, probably for my wife as well, and maybe the children.<br>Speaker A: It depends. Well, for one adult, the charge is 154 pounds a year, but for family membership, that''s two adults and up to two children, it''s 285 pounds.<br>Speaker B: Okay, well that doesn''t sound too bad. Right. Now, we actually live quite near, but with the children, I expect we''d be driving there, so what''s the situation about parking?<br>Speaker A: That''s free for our members, and there''s always plenty of space.<br>Speaker B: Okay, well that''s certainly something to think about. We''ve been thinking of joining a fitness center for a bit, but we''ve never got round to it.<br>Speaker A: Well, these membership charges are fixed until August, but in September, they could go up, so I''d recommend that if you are interested, you join straight away.<br>Speaker B: Well, it does depend a bit on what facilities you have. One thing we''re all very keen on is swimming, for example, right?<br>Speaker A: Well, there are two pools. The main pool''s lovely. It''s 25 meters, and the roof is all made of glass, so you get lots of natural light. And there''s a separate pool for children.<br>Speaker B: And what about the gym?<br>Speaker A: Well, if you become a member, you get a session for orientation on the cardio and weights equipment in the gym, given by one of our qualified staff. That normally costs 15 pounds per person, so it''s a very good deal. And one thing that''s very popular is there''s TV installed on some of the equipment, so you can watch as you work out.<br>Speaker B: Okay.<br>Speaker A: Now, we do also have a program of evening classes. I don''t know if you''d like me to give you any information about them at this stage.<br>Speaker B: Sure.<br>Speaker A: Well, I''ll just give you a few examples now, but do ask if there''s anything in particular you''re interested in. For example, our Monday squash class is very popular.<br>Speaker B: I''ve never played it, but I like to learn. So is it aimed at beginners?<br>Speaker A: Yes, that''s ri' AS nvarchar(max))+N'ght.<br>Speaker B: Okay. Well, I might well be interested.<br>Speaker A: On Tuesdays, we do judo. We have different classes suitable for all levels. The only requirement is that you''re over 16, I''m afraid. We can''t cater for anyone younger than that at present.<br>Speaker B: No problem. What about yoga? I know my wife''s keen to take that up again.<br>Speaker A: We have a class on Wednesdays. I take it she''s not a beginner.<br>Speaker B: No. In fact, she used to be at advanced level, but she''s probably a bit rusty, as she hasn''t done any for a few years now.<br>Speaker A: Well, the Wednesday class is for intermediate students, so it might be okay for her. She can try it out for one lesson to see, and then sign up if she thinks it''s going to suit her.<br>Speaker B: Thanks. I''ll let her know.<br>Speaker A: And I don''t know if either you or your wife would be interested, but we do have classes on Thursday evenings for people interested in improving their diet as a way of staying healthy.<br>Speaker B: Hmm. Well, I suppose we both might be, but it would depend what time.<br>Speaker A: Well, there''s one class at 6.30 p.m., but it''s full up, so we''re opening a new one at 8:30 the same evening.<br>Speaker B: Right. Well, that would be better for us, actually. I''ll talk to my wife, so if we want to join.<br></p>'),(CAST(N'<p>Spea