eaker B: Okay.<br>Speaker A: Now, we do also have a program of evening classes. I don''t know if you''d like me to give you any information about them at this stage.<br>Speaker B: Sure.<br>Speaker A: Well, I''ll just give you a few examples now, but do ask if there''s anything in particular you''re interested in. For example, our Monday squash class is very popular.<br>Speaker B: I''ve never played it, but I like to learn. So is it aimed at beginners?<br>Speaker A: Yes, that''s right.<br>Speaker B: Okay. Well, I m' AS nvarchar(max))+N'ight well be interested.<br>Speaker A: On Tuesdays, we do judo. We have different classes suitable for all levels. The only requirement is that you''re over 16, I''m afraid. We can''t cater for anyone younger than that at present.<br>Speaker B: No problem. What about yoga? I know my wife''s keen to take that up again.<br>Speaker A: We have a class on Wednesdays. I take it she''s not a beginner.<br>Speaker B: No. In fact, she used to be at advanced level, but she''s probably a bit rusty, as she hasn''t done any for a few years now.<br>Speaker A: Well, the Wednesday class is for intermediate students, so it might be okay for her. She can try it out for one lesson to see, and then sign up if she thinks it''s going to suit her.<br>Speaker B: Thanks. I''ll let her know.<br>Speaker A: And I don''t know if either you or your wife would be interested, but we do have classes on Thursday evenings for people interested in improving their diet as a way of staying healthy.<br>Speaker B: Hmm. Well, I suppose we both might be, but it would depend what time.<br>Speaker A: Well, there''s one class at 6.30 p.m., but it''s full up, so we''re opening a new one at 8:30 the same evening.<br>Speaker B: Right. Well, that would be better for us, actually. I''ll talk to my wife, so if we want to join.<br></p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-6/iL.VOL6.10.S1982.PART1.mp3',NULL,1,0,1,NULL,0,1982),
