Speaker B: Oh yes, it''s my first time visiting the Skipping Islands. Can you recommend any good spots to visit or stay nearby?<br>
Speaker A: Sure, just for your information, this time of year is the best in terms of temperature. It will be colder a month later, so you have a lot of things to do in the warm weather. And let me just give you a brief introduction of the highlights you can visit here. First, there''s a place called Hardy Shore. It''s amazing. Don''t forget to try the local cheese once you are there. It''s made from milk of local goats, so it''s very special.<br>
Speaker B: Okay, I think I''ll have to write all these down in case I forget.<br>
Speaker A: Yes, you should. And do you play any sand sports?<br>
Speaker B: Yes, I do. I heard we can play beach football there. The sand is very soft.<br>
Speaker A: Well, we have great sand here, but we call that beach soccer.<br>
Speaker B: Oh, thanks for correcting me. Can you recommend some good restaurants here?<br>
Speaker A: Oh yes, the places with great food are all very close to a market. There are all sorts of interesting food for you to try.<br>
Speaker B: That would be great. I also heard the sugar produced here is different from the common types.<br>
Speaker A: That''s true, and that''s because we grow a special type of sugar cane.<br>
Speaker B: I see. Hmm, are there any vehicles I can use to get around the island?<br>
Speaker A: Speaking of that, if you want to have a good view of the ocean and the whole island, there''s a helicopter tour. It''s a little expensive, but the view is fantastic, so it''s worth the money.<br>
Speaker B: Sounds like a lot of fun. I''ve always wanted to do that. I''ll note that down.<br>
Before you hear the rest of the conversation, you have some time to look at questions 6 to 10.<br>
Now listen and answer questions 6 to 10.<br>
Speaker A: By the way, each village has a hostel of a different theme. You can check out the themes in this brochure.<br>
Speaker B: Thanks.<br>
Speaker A: There are also many quieter activities if you just want to relax. We have a theme park nearby, which is a 10-minute drive from here. Currently, there are a dozen of giant pirate models under creation, but you can see a film of pirates in the theme park instead. From previous viewers'' feedback, the film is one of those must-see movies. I believe you will be surprised by the special effects of the movie.<br>
Speaker A: Or, if y' AS nvarchar(max))+N'ou want more outdoor activities, there''s also tree climbing available on the Tashika Island. If you are new to this, you can ask the coach for some quick training. And we''ve got a safety net below. No need to worry about injury or anything.<br>
Speaker B: Okay. Anywhere else I can go on that island?<br>
Speaker A: Well, let''s see. You can go to Fisherman''s Village.<br>
Speaker B: What''s special about it?<br>
Speaker A: It''s a great place for fishing, if you are interested. You can go on a boat tour with the local fishermen. After the tour, you can go to a seaside barbecue site, where you can cook the fish.<br>
Speaker B: Hmm. I haven''t done fishing for a long time. Not sure if I can still catch one fish or not.<br>
Speaker A: Oh, that wouldn''t be a problem. The fishermen will give you a hand during the tour.<br>
Speaker A: I wanted to recommend the Stone Mountains to you, as it''s very popular for its camping trips. But lately it''s under reconstruction, so camping is not allowed at the moment. Sorry about that.<br>
Speaker B: That''s okay. I''d like to try fishing. It must be pretty exciting.<br>
Speaker A: Yes, it is. One more thing is, we don''t provide towels on the island, so you have to bring your own just in case you get wet.<br>
Speaker B: That won''t be a problem. Thank you very much for your information.<br>
