(N'7e4ca3a7-2af5-5952-b42a-1dde0e102d3f',N'594e3577-1155-58af-89cd-c7dca227b95e',0,3,19,N'<p>Indigo Beach Turtle Centre is special because of</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là A - “hundreds of loggerhead turtles” → số lượng lớn rùa có thể thấy. </p><p>- B sai vì không nói là “best reservation point”.</p><p> - C sai vì tất cả rùa đều đẻ trứng trên bãi biển, không riêng ở đây.</p><p>- Key word:</p><p> + hundreds (n): hàng trăm</p><p> + nest (v): làm tổ</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,11,NULL,0,1981),
(N'44f43b91-d766-5013-b146-b77c5951a505',N'594e3577-1155-58af-89cd-c7dca227b95e',0,3,19,N'<p>The guide thinks that the best time to see nesting turtles is</p>',N'<p>Đáp án là A - Guide chọn “favorite time” → best time.</p><p> - B sai vì là cả mùa, không phải “best”.</p><p>- C sai vì không đúng khoảng.</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ nesting season (n): mùa đẻ trứng</p><p> + favorite (adj): ưa thích nhất</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,12,NULL,0,1981),
(N'381bcb4a-9900-5b17-84e7-9f5421ec3094',N'594e3577-1155-58af-89cd-c7dca227b95e',0,3,19,N'<p>The main risk to the turtles at Indigo Beach is currently from</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là C - “foxes, crabs and birds” → animals gây nguy hiểm. </p><p>- A sai vì fishing đã bị cấm. </p><p>- B sai vì không có phát triển nhà ở.</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ danger (n): nguy hiểm </p><p>+ animals (n): động vật</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,13,NULL,0,1981),
(N'654f4607-b9b5-5bcb-ad5c-ab78fda6a56b',N'594e3577-1155-58af-89cd-c7dca227b95e',0,3,19,N'<p>Once you arrive at the Indigo Beach Tune Centre, you can pay extra to get</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là B - “hire an audio guide” → trả thêm tiền để có audio commentary. </p><p>- A sai vì không còn personal tours. </p><p>- C sai vì không nhắc đến staff service riêng.</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ audio guide (n): hướng dẫn âm thanh </p><p>+ commentary (n): thuyết minh</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,14,NULL,0,1981),
(N'6ef55347-7c96-5279-9a09-3c2343149282',N'8c39c305-9cde-57bc-8073-92e9a4fc4f1f',0,2,18,N'<p>Write the correct letter, <span><span>A - I</span></span>, Next to Questions <span><span>15 - 20</span></span>.</p><p><img src="https://ieltsroom.com/upload/images/ieltsadvancedtest/1ed416862502af2685bd.jpg" alt="Question diagram"></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'The Indigo Beach Turtle Centre',12,0,2,NULL,0,1981),
(N'8203a039-3283-50ec-b70a-2d862031d8fd',N'6ef55347-7c96-5279-9a09-3c2343149282',0,3,19,N'<p>Turtle Research Zone</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là F - “right hand fork… in amongst the trees” → vị trí F trên bản đồ.</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ fork (n): ngã rẽ</p><p> + trees (n): cây</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,15,NULL,0,1981),
(N'4ea416b1-ba42-5523-a936-a802a764a49a',N'6ef55347-7c96-5279-9a09-3c2343149282',0,3,19,N'<p>Information Kiosk</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là C - “L-shaped building on your left” → vị trí kiosk.</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ L-shaped (adj): hình chữ L </p><p>+ across (prep): đối diện</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,16,NULL,0,1981),
(N'5a211e35-16c9-5b75-8e65-e2bea39600bc',N'6ef55347-7c96-5279-9a09-3c2343149282',0,3,19,N'<p>Children’s Activity Area</p>',N'<p>Đáp án là D - “next to the toilets” → vị trí D trên map. </p><p>- Key word: + next to (prep): bên cạnh + toilets (n): nhà vệ sinh</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,17,NULL,0,1981),
(N'34dd2e8d-8403-5f00-aa6a-ae0340bae535',N'6ef55347-7c96-5279-9a09-3c2343149282',0,3,19,N'<p>Baby Turtle Pools</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là E - “oval shaped area… surrounded by trees” → khu E.</p><p> - Key word: </p><p>+ oval (adj): hình bầu dục </p><p>+ surrounded (v): bao quanh</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,18,NULL,0,1981),
(N'3024aa01-aa0e-5f25-bbb2-e3110a7276a5',N'6ef55347-7c96-5279-9a09-3c2343149282',0,3,19,N'<p>Old Gift Shop</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là I </p><p>- Mô tả Gift Shop cũ nằm ở lối rẽ đầu tiên bên trái → vị trí I.</p><p>- Key word:</p><p>+ "used to be... but" (cấu trúc): tín hiệu chuyển từ vị trí cũ sang vị trí mới - đây là bẫy, cần nghe tiếp câu sau circular </p><p>+ shaped building (n): tòa nhà hình tròn - mô tả vị trí cũ, không phải I </p><p>+ expand (v): mở rộng</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,19,NULL,0,1981),
(N'3099900d-38d1-564d-bb8a-797f7a4d42f6',N'6ef55347-7c96-5279-9a09-3c2343149282',0,3,19,N'<p>Conference Hall</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là H - “second building… square… before amphitheater” → vị trí H.</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ square (adj): hình vuông </p><p>+ amphitheater (n): nhà hát ngoài trời</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,20,NULL,0,1981),
(N'dd0d5a2a-da9f-5757-a6a2-cffe5992e864',N'7bf8814a-29fe-5c88-8b45-6f223fd8417a',0,1,15,(CAST(N'<h2>The Painter David Cox</h2><p>Lily: Right Jack, let''s get started on this presentation about David Cox. I think if we divide the research it''ll be much more efficient.<br>
Jack: No problem Lily. Yeah, we should get our notes in order. I found quite a bit, but some of the details are a bit fuzzy. Let''s start from the beginning with his early career.<br>
Lily: Right. So, initially he was working for a theatre company in London.<br>
Jack: I was reading that he left that job. The reason seems a bit unclear.<br>
Lily: Well, I read that he initially took the job because it involved traveling around with the which he apparently enjoyed. So, it wasn''t the traveling he disliked.<br>
Jack: And I didn''t see anything that suggested he felt it was beneath him as a serious artist.<br>
Lily: The text I found implied the main issue was with the people he worked with. It said he had some personal disagreements with the other scene painters.<br>
Jack: Ah, yes, I remember that. Exactly. Now later on he took a teaching job in Hereford. I wonder why he accepted that. He was already an established painter in London.<br>
Lily: Hereford was in a beautiful part of the country, but I don''t think he had a prior connection to it. And while there were other artists there, I didn''t get the sense that was the reason. But the book mentioned he had a young family to support, and a teaching position offered a steady income, which was probably very appealing.<br>
Jack: That makes sense.<br>
Lily: Agreed. Let''s move on to what the critics and biographers said about his work.<br>
Jack: The art historian Greg Smith made an interesting point. He suggested that some of Cox''s finished oil paintings, even the final versions, retain the loose energetic quality of an initial sketch.<br>
Lily: Right, even though they are complete works. He didn''t say anything about Cox taking a long time for each painting.<br>
Jack: Precisely. And then there''s his biographer, Nathaniel Solley, who commented on Cox''s technique. He highlighted that Cox would often paint landscapes after he returned to his studio, rather than working directly at the scene.<br>
Lily: Yes, that was a key technique for him. It wasn''t about combining materials or using a single dramatic color.<br>
Jack: Now, what about the famous critic John Ruskin? His comments on Cox were a bit weird.<br>
Lily: At one point, he praised Cox''s ability to capture the truth of nature. But then in another review, he almost denied his later, more expressive ' AS nvarchar(max))+N'style.<br>
Jack: It''s not that they are easy to misinterpret. They just don''t seem consistent.<br>
Lily: Definitely.<br>
Before you hear the rest of the talk, you have some time to look at questions 26 to 30.<br>
Now listen and answer questions 26 to 30.<br>
Lily: Okay, finally, let''s talk about the specific paintings we must include. What about bathers disturbed by a bull?<br>
Jack: Oh, that one. It''s quite funny, isn''t it? The scene of people scrambling out of the water in a panic. It comes across as humorous.<br>
Lily: I''d agree with that. And sun, wind and rain.<br>
Jack: That''s the one that critics frequently related to a famous painting by Turner, rain, steam and speed. Yes, the composition and theme are very similar.<br>
Lily: And next crossing the sands.<br>
Jack: That''s a classic Cox subject. He loved painting scenes of travelers on foot. And this one perfectly shows people making their way across the sands.<br>
Lily: Yes, he captured a theme of humble human endeavor against the elements that he frequently returned to. And the girl in a pinnacle.<br>
Jack: That''s an interesting one because it''s a portrait, or at least a single figure study. Cox was primarily a landscape painter. So this is quite uncommon subject matter for him.<br>
Lily: Right? It''s rare in his work.<br>
Jack: Lastly, junction of the seven and the Y.<br>
Lily: Ah, that''s a powerful one. The way he''s captured the stormy sky and the light breaking through the clouds is incredible.<br>
Jack: Absolutely. It''s a fantastic work. Well, I think that covers everything we need.<br>
Lily: Yes, this has been really helpful. Let''s put the presentation together tomorrow.<br>
Jack: Perfect. See you then.<br>
