successful</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ in the films.</p><ul><li><p>Directors are able to use</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ to create an atmosphere.</p><ul><li><p>Directors lack the ability to focus on what is important.</p></li></ul><p><span>Dramatic impact of Bergman''s films</span></p><ul><li><p>He had a unique ability to portray</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p><ul><li><p>Every image has a</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ and contributes to the overall meaning.</p><ul><li><p>A character''s gestures or facial expressions can be as important as his or her</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p><ul><li><p>His stories work at two levels, as drama and as</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p><p><span>Common themes in </span><em><span>Wild Strawberries</span></em></p><ul><li><p>The connection between journeys and</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p><ul><li><p></p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ relationships</p><ul><li><p>The need to</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ all that life offers</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là depth - Trong script nói rõ “they simply don''t have the depth that a work of art has” → thiếu “độ sâu” nên không đạt đến mức nghệ thuật. </p><p>- Câu hỏi paraphrase “lack the … necessary for great art” = thiếu yếu tố cần thiết → chính là “depth”. - Key word: </p><p>+ depth (n): chiều sâu </p><p>+ work of art (n): tác phẩm nghệ thuật</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,31,NULL,0,1978),
(N'dc4acf8f-f4b7-51cb-bbcb-01d1d698d318',N'a2932e34-21b9-5fb4-8643-b1e25db886fc',0,3,19,N'Question number 32',N'<p>- Đáp án là actors - Script: “vehicles for actors” → phim chỉ là “công cụ cho diễn viên nổi tiếng”. </p><p>- Đề: “using successful ___ in the films” → từ “successful” ám chỉ “box office successes” → actors.</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ actors (n): diễn viên </p><p>+ box office success (n): thành công phòng vé</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,32,NULL,0,1978),
(N'27f8e2c4-8939-5ccc-a46a-e21f9113e037',N'a2932e34-21b9-5fb4-8643-b1e25db886fc',0,3,19,N'Question number 33',N'<p>- Đáp án là light - Script: “play with light” → sử dụng ánh sáng để tạo không khí. </p><p>- Đề: “use ___ to create an atmosphere” → paraphrase trực tiếp.</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ light (n): ánh sáng </p><p>+ atmosphere (n): bầu không khí</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,33,NULL,0,1978),
(N'2b913833-cc49-5a89-9512-ff59b5f8f901',N'a2932e34-21b9-5fb4-8643-b1e25db886fc',0,3,19,N'Question number 34',N'<p>- Đáp án là emotion - Script: “ability to convey emotion” → khả năng truyền tải cảm xúc. - Đề: “portray ___” = convey → emotion.</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ convey (v): truyền tải</p><p> + emotion (n): cảm xúc</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,34,NULL,0,1978),
(N'edfc92b6-217f-5cc6-9f1e-38f3b6af3d9b',N'a2932e34-21b9-5fb4-8643-b1e25db886fc',0,3,19,N'Question number 35',N'<p>- Đáp án là purpose - Script: “each image… for a purpose” → mỗi hình ảnh đều có mục đích. - Đề: “has a ___ and contributes…” → khớp hoàn toàn.</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ purpose (n): mục đích </p><p>+ significant (adj): có ý nghĩa</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,35,NULL,0,1978),
(N'2652bcd7-4612-515e-8d20-f8e169054458',N'a2932e34-21b9-5fb4-8643-b1e25db886fc',0,3,19,N'Question number 36',N'<p>- Đáp án là words - Script: “as much as the words uttered” → cử chỉ quan trọng như lời nói. - Đề paraphrase: gestures as important as his or her ___ → words. </p><p>- Key word: + gesture (n): cử chỉ + utter (v): thốt ra</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,36,NULL,0,1978),
(N'44571ff4-30b0-5df9-b94b-fb088affca46',N'a2932e34-21b9-5fb4-8643-b1e25db886fc',0,3,19,N'Question number 37',N'<p>- Đáp án là myth - Script nói rõ 2 cấp độ: “dramatic narrative” và “myth”. - Đề: “as drama and as ___” → drama = narrative → còn lại là myth.</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ narrative (n): cốt truyện</p><p> + myth (n): huyền thoại</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,37,NULL,0,1978),
(N'fe808518-a79e-59c8-b6ac-46f0e09d84ba',N'a2932e34-21b9-5fb4-8643-b1e25db886fc',0,3,19,N'Question number 38',N'<p>- Đáp án là dreams - Script: journey gắn với “dreams”. - Đề: “connection between journeys and ___” → chính là dreams. </p><p>- Key word: + journey (n): hành trình + dreams (n): giấc mơ</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,38,NULL,0,1978),
(N'ad6519f2-99bd-52c7-b00c-ec3d94162fd7',N'a2932e34-21b9-5fb4-8643-b1e25db886fc',0,3,19,N'Question number 39',N'<p>- Đáp án là family - Script: “members of a family” → mối quan hệ gia đình. </p><p>- Đề: “___ relationships” → family relationships. </p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ relationships (n): mối quan hệ </p><p>+ family (n): gia đình</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,39,NULL,0,1978),
(N'b4507ca8-b419-5807-89c0-f837f8bbf4ba',N'a2932e34-21b9-5fb4-8643-b1e25db886fc',0,3,19,N'Question number 40',N'<p>- Đáp án là accept - Script: “we have to accept everything that life can give”. </p><p>- Đề: “need to ___ all that life offers” → paraphrase hoàn toàn.</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ accept (v): chấp nhận </p><p>+ philosophy (n): triết lý</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,40,NULL,0,1978),
(N'481b0680-a0d8-5650-aaa5-1cf3b8c93550',NULL,0,0,11,NULL,NULL,NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-6/iL.VOL6.5.S1977.mp3',N'Vol 6 LISTENING FULL TEST 5',0,7,1,NULL,1,1977),
(N'4da7f0e8-4eb8-5e0a-bc96-168785ac7fc7',N'481b0680-a0d8-5650-aaa5-1cf3b8c93550',0,1,13,(CAST(N'<h2>Homecare cleaning agency</h2><p>Speaker A: Good morning, Home Care Cleaning Agency.<br>Speaker B: Oh, hello. I''d like to arrange to have some cleaning done, please.<br>Speaker A: Certainly. Have you used our services before?<br>Speaker B: No, I haven''t, but a friend of mine has often used your company and suggested I phone you.<br>Speaker A: Oh, that''s great. I''ll just take some details from you and then you can let me know exactly what you would like done.<br>Speaker B: Okay.<br>Speaker A: First of all, what area are you in?<br>Speaker B: I''m in the Southwest.<br>Speaker A: Okay, and are you interested in having a regular cleaner or is this a one-off clean?<br>Speaker B: No, I''d like to arrange to have someone come in once a week.<br>Speaker A: Right. Now, let''s just get a bit of information about the house. How many bedrooms does it have?<br>Speaker B: Three.<br>Speaker A: Are they all double bedrooms?<br>Speaker B: Well, one of the bedrooms is quite small, so it''s probably really two double rooms.<br>Speaker B: We have the small bedroom set up as an office.<br>Speaker A: Okay. And just a standard kitchen, lounge, dining room and bathroom?<br>Speaker B: Well, actually, we don''t have a separate dining room. It''s a kitchen-diner. Then there''s the lounge and as well as that we have a family room. Oh, and two bathrooms.<br>Speaker A: Okay.<br>Before you hear the rest of the conversation, you have some time to look at questions five to ten. Now listen and answer questions five to ten.<br>Speaker A: Right. That''s all I need to know about the house itself. Now, what we do is we offer a basic cleaning service and then you let us know about anything extra you''d like cleaned.<br>Speaker B: Right. And what does the basic service include?<br>Speaker A: We clean all the floors and surfaces and do a basic clean in the kitchen and bathroom.<br>Speaker B: Okay, that sounds good. And do you clean windows?<br>Speaker A: Well, I''m afraid we don''t do that. Health and safety regulations. But we do offer other special services. We can put clean sheets on the beds, for example. Or we can clean out your fridge. A lot of people like that done.<br>Speaker B: I''m not so worried about that, but I would like the sheets changed.<br>Speaker A: That''s no problem. We can do that.<br>Speaker B: What about the carpet?<br>Speaker A: As well as the standard vacuum, we can shampoo it if you want.<br>Speaker B: Right. We''ve got young children, so it gets pretty dirty. I haven''t had it don' AS nvarchar(max))+N'e for six months. It really needs doing more often than that.<br>Speaker A: You can have it done every month if you like, but three months is what we usually recommend.<br>Speaker B: That sounds good. The only other thing is the washing. Do you do laundry work?<br>Speaker A: Yes, we do. That''s no problem. What exactly would you like done?<br>Speaker B: Well, it''s no problem to put a load of washing in the machine. I can do that, but I would like to have the ironing done.<br>Speaker A: That''s fine. And would you like the washing put away in drawers or wardrobes?<br>Speaker B: No, it''s OK. You can just leave everything out and fold it up.<br>Speaker A: OK, right. Now, I''ll just set up an account for you and I''ll take down some of your details. First of all, what''s your full name?<br>Speaker B: It''s Rose Killey.<br>Speaker A: And could I have your home address, please, Mrs Kelly?<br>Speaker B: Yes, it''s 48 Amyes Road. That''s A-M-Y-E-S. And that''s in Mount Eden.<br>Speaker A: OK. Now, what day of the week would you like the property cleaned?<br>Speaker B: It doesn''t really matter. Not Monday, but any other day.<br>Speaker A: OK, let''s see. We have a cleaner in your area later on Thursday, so shall we go for that day?<br>Speaker A: We could have someone there by about 9.30 in the morning. Does that suit you?<br>Speaker B: Yes, that''s fine. And do you charge an hourly rate or a total for the whole job?<br>Speaker A: No, we charge by the hour. It will work out to about $25 per hour.<br>Speaker B: Oh, that''s quite reasonable. I thought it might be closer to $30.<br>Speaker A: And how long do you expect it to take?<br>Speaker A: Well, you said the house isn''t large, so I''d guess no more than three hours at the most. We can occasionally finish a three-bedroom in two and a half, but that''s probably not too realistic.<br>Speaker B: Right. That sounds good.<br>Speaker A: OK, that''s lovely. Thank you very much. And we''ll have someone there next week.<br>Speaker B: Thank you.<br></p>'),(CAST(N'<p>Speaker A: Good morning, Home Care Cleaning Agency.<br>Speaker B: Oh, hello. I''d like to arrange to have some cleaning done, please.<br>Speaker A: Certainly. Have you used our services before?<br>Speaker B: No, I haven''t, but a friend of mine has often used your company and suggested I phone you.<br>Speaker A: Oh, that''s great. I''ll just take some details from you and then you can let me know exactly what you would like done.<br>Speaker B: Okay.<br>Speaker A: First of all, what area are you in?<br>Speaker B: I''m in the Southwest.<br>Speaker A: Okay, and are you interested in having a regular cleaner or is this a one-off clean?<br>Speaker B: No, I''d like to arrange to have someone come in once a week.<br>Speaker A: Right. Now, let''s just get a bit of information about the house. How many bedrooms does it have?<br>Speaker B: Three.<br>Speaker A: Are they all double bedrooms?<br>Speaker B: Well, one of the bedrooms is quite small, so it''s probably really two double rooms.<br>Speaker B: We have the small bedroom set up as an office.<br>Speaker A: Okay. And just a standard kitchen, lounge, dining room and bathroom?<br>Speaker B: Well, actually, we don''t have a separate dining room. It''s a kitchen-diner. Then there''s the lounge and as well as that we have a family room. Oh, and two bathrooms.<br>Spea