(N'02210b63-7017-5913-bdf6-02aa92c3875c',N'48661f59-f98e-5f02-85f7-9f82f43b6c4e',0,3,19,N'<p>The Performing Arts centre</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là B - “top… centre… past tennis courts” → vị trí B</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ centre (n): trung tâm </p><p>+ tennis courts (n): sân tennis</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,16,NULL,0,1977),
(N'e90c63b5-8468-5f0d-9898-8e5416db71c6',N'48661f59-f98e-5f02-85f7-9f82f43b6c4e',0,3,19,N'<p>School drop-off area</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là F - “first bay near the classrooms” → vị trí gần classroom (D)</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ bay (n): khu đỗ xe </p><p>+ classrooms (n): lớp học</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,17,NULL,0,1977),
(N'e792cef4-9549-5de2-b76d-1b7e7820caed',N'48661f59-f98e-5f02-85f7-9f82f43b6c4e',0,3,19,N'<p>The fire evacuation point</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là C - “oval shape… top right-hand corner” → điểm C</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ oval (adj): hình bầu dục </p><p>+ assemble (v): tập trung</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,18,NULL,0,1977),
(N'18428f00-6dff-5a84-8643-e6129ed98974',N'48661f59-f98e-5f02-85f7-9f82f43b6c4e',0,3,19,N'<p>The canteen</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là A </p><p>- “L-shaped building… from Sports Hall” → vị trí A</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ L-shaped (adj): hình chữ L </p><p>+ accessed (v): tiếp cận</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,19,NULL,0,1977),
(N'462e61c3-f783-5c6b-9eca-f4d98f48d9a8',N'48661f59-f98e-5f02-85f7-9f82f43b6c4e',0,3,19,N'<p>The IT centre</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là H </p><p>- “left of administration building… near art block” → vị trí H</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ left (n): bên trái </p><p>+ walkway (n): lối đi</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,20,NULL,0,1977),
(N'7c4e6c2e-b798-512c-981e-bc29964f70f3',N'481b0680-a0d8-5650-aaa5-1cf3b8c93550',0,1,15,(CAST(N'<h2>[VOL 6] Test 5-Section 3</h2><p>Narrator: You will hear two students called Mona and Tom discussing the essay for their management course. </p><p>Narrator: First, you have some time to look at questions 21 to 26. </p><p>Narrator: Now, listen carefully and answer questions 21 to 26. </p><p>Mona: Hello Tom, sorry I''m late. </p><p>Tom: Hi Mona, no problem. </p><p>Tom: I heard you finished the essay for the management course. </p><p>Tom: Which company did you focus on?</p><p>Mona: It was finished last week. </p><p>Mona: I chose the hotel where I interned last summer, and mainly concentrated on my work experience there. </p><p>Tom: Could you give me some details? I''m interested. </p><p>Mona: Well, during my three-month internship, I observed every part of the hotel carefully each day, and also talked with some of my colleagues. Mona: I found some problems in different parts of the hotel, and made a conclusion in the essay.</p><p>Mona: Let me start from the reception desk.</p><p>Mona: I noticed the staff there kept doing the same thing every day, like answering the phone, helping guests with check-in and check-out, etc. Mona: There was nothing special for them. </p><p>Tom: It must be very boring. </p><p>Mona: Yeah, I think so. </p><p>Mona: And in the restaurant, the employees told me that they must obey the rules exactly. </p><p>Mona: For example, if they don''t wear uniforms during working hours, 20% of their daily wages will be deducted. </p><p>Mona: And then, about the coffee bar. </p><p>Mona: During peak hours, I was asked to help in the coffee bar several times, as a shortage of hands always made many customers wait long for ordering, eating or paying the bills. </p><p>Mona: Their own staff could not control customer flow.</p><p>Tom: Oh, that seems a little messy.</p><p>Mona: Yes, definitely. </p><p>Mona: And the place where I worked was a shop selling towels and pajamas, as well as souvenirs. </p><p>Mona: Every day, I had to be there from 9:00 a.m. to 6:00 p.m. </p><p>Mona: My duty was to set up the window display and serve the customers. </p><p>Mona: At first, it seemed interesting, but later, I found this work was a bit tough. </p><p>Mona: Every night when I got off work, I was nearly exhausted. </p><p>Mona: What I wanted was just a good rest and sleep. </p><p>Tom: Doesn''t sound like an easy job. </p><p>Mona: It definitely wasn''t. </p><p>Mona: Then, there was the personnel office. </p><p>Mona: I went there on the first day when I arrived at the hotel,' AS nvarchar(max))+N' as I was not unfamiliar with everything. </p><p>Mona: I asked the staff several questions, but the employee of the personnel office seemed a bit annoyed and started complaining, which gave me a very bad impression. </p><p>Mona: Lastly, as regards cleaning, it wasn''t too bad compared with other parts of the hotel, except the vacuum cleaners, which were probably bought such a long time ago that the sound seemed too loud when they were working. </p><p>Mona: But fortunately, the hotel hasn''t received any complaint from the customers so far. </p><p>Narrator: Before you hear the rest of the discussion, you have some time to look at questions 27 to 30. </p><p>Narrator: Now, listen and answer questions 27 to 30. </p><p>Tom: I think you''ve benefited a lot from the internship. </p><p>Mona: Yeah, absolutely. </p><p>Mona: In the beginning, I just wanted to complete the essay for the course, but in the end, I found it has given me some practical examples which are helpful to what I intend to do after graduation. </p><p>Mona: As you know, I''ve always wanted to do something related to hotel management. </p><p>Mona: Due to the time limitation, I still haven''t got a clear idea of some specific work positions. </p><p>Tom: Well, I heard you''re going to give us a presentation of your essay next time in class. </p><p>Mona: Yes. Actually, I''m not so good at giving a presentation, but the tutor says that''s just what he wants me to do. </p><p>Mona: To know what is important when giving a presentation, like how to attract the audience, make eye contact, and make gestures, etc. </p><p>Mona: And other students can learn from my presentation. </p><p>Tom: I''m looking forward to it. </p><p>Tom: You know, now I''m only in the second year of the course, and I have to write an essay next semester, but I have no idea about where I can do an internship.</p><p>Tom: There are several hotels which I''m interested in. Do you think I should call their managers? </p><p>Mona: Well, I suggest you''d better not, because you''re more likely to be rejected by them. </p><p>Mona: There is a career office on campus that has got a list of companies offering internship opportunities to students. </p><p>Mona: The office will help you contact where you want to go. </p><p>Mona: You just have to prepare your personal information, like the CV.</p><p>Mona: Oh, don''t forget to provide a reference from the tutor. </p><p>Tom: Great. I''ve got it. </p><p>Tom: So, have you got any plans for your essay? </p><p>Tom: I''ve n'+N'oticed that the hotel industry is developing at a high speed. </p><p>Tom: People are more and more concerned about the quality of accommodation. </p><p>Tom: What I''m struck by is the numerous statistics showing the ever-increasing number of five-star hotels. </p><p>Tom: So, I intend to carry out extensive research on this aspect. </p><p>Tom: I''m thinking about using videos as a research method, but I haven''t decided yet. </p><p>Mona: I think it''s an interesting topic. </p><p>Mona: Anyway, if you have any questions later, I will be happy to help. </p><p>Tom: Thanks a lot, Mona. </p><p>Mona: You''re welcome. </p><p>Narrator: That is the end of part three. </p><p>Narrator: You now have 30 seconds to check your answers to part three</p>'),(CAST(N'<p>Narrator: You will hear two students called Mona and Tom discussing the essay for their managemen