(N'4a25686a-54f0-5809-bebb-b030716c4146',N'f2be2dd6-785e-5107-a3cb-8f2547214066',0,3,19,N'<h3>The History of Umbrellas</h3><p><span>Symbolism and Status</span></p><p>• Umbrellas symbolized }{SPACE}{ for rulers, showcasing authority.</p><p>• Only wealthy Roman }{SPACE}{ could own umbrellas, as a status symbol.</p><p><span>Materials and Construction</span></p><p>• In India, umbrellas were made from local }{SPACE}{ ,and in China from silk.</p><p>• Umbrellas were treated with }{SPACE}{ to make them waterproof, improving their usefulness. </p><p><span>Practical Enhancements</span></p><p>• Originally, umbrellas were designed to protect the }{SPACE}{ from various elements.</p><p>• Early umbrellas resembled big }{SPACE}{ ,providing extensive coverage.</p><p>• Umbrellas were often used with }{SPACE}{ , especially in cold or wet climates.</p><p>• The introduction of }{SPACE}{ in the 1850s made umbrellas lighter and more durable. </p><p>• In England, umbrella frames began to be made with }{SPACE}{  ,enhancing their durability.</p><p>• In Germany, the shift to using }{SPACE}{  for umbrellas improved their functionality and popularity.</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là power - “power icon of authority” → biểu tượng quyền lực</p><p>- Khớp với “symbolized ___ for rulers” - Key word: </p><p>+ power (n): quyền lực </p><p>+ authority (n): quyền uy</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,31,NULL,0,1962),
