Speaker B: Oh, hello. Yes, I''m calling from London. My husband has just got a new job in Australia, and his company recommended you to help us.<br>
Speaker A: Great. I''ll get some details from you. Let''s start with your name, shall we?<br>
Speaker B: Oh, yes. It''s Helen Green.<br>
Speaker A: Thank you. And what''s your current address?<br>
Speaker B: It''s a London address, 42 Station Road, Kew. It''s just near the Botanical Gardens.<br>
Speaker A: Oh, that sounds nice. And in case I need to contact you, could I have a telephone number?<br>
Speaker B: Yes, it''s 0207 9460 385.<br>
Speaker A: Got it. Now, Helen, whereabouts in Australia are you relocating to?<br>
Speaker B: Brisbane.<br>
Speaker A: And is your husband''s company paying for the move?<br>
Speaker B: Yes. It''s a company called Kirkby Technology.<br>
Speaker A: I think we''ve worked with them before. And how soon do you need to move?<br>
Speaker B: Well, they want my husband to start work in two weeks, at the start of the month. But school doesn''t finish here until the end of July, so we can''t possibly move until then.<br>
Speaker A: Shall we say the beginning of August then?<br>
Speaker B: That sounds more realistic. June is nearly over and I have so much to do before we move.<br>
Speaker A: Let''s start with the accommodation you need. Would you prefer a house or an apartment?<br>
Speaker B: Well, we live in a big house with a garden now, which we love. But I think that initially we''d be happy with an apartment that''s fairly central, just until we get to know the city a little better and can find a house we love.<br>
Speaker A: Sounds like a good idea. And what about location?<br>
Speaker A: There are some beautiful developments along the Brisbane River. It runs right through the city. The views are spectacular and you wouldn''t need to worry about transport.<br>
Speaker B: Well, actually, as we won''t have our own garden, I''d prefer something close to a park. That''s more important than a view for us.<br>
Speaker A: OK, I''ll make a note of that. Brisbane''s a lovely green city, so that won''t be hard.<br>
Speaker A: Is there anything else I can organise?<br>
Speaker B: Oh yes, furniture. We were planning to ship our own, but we''ve decided it isn''t really worth it.<br>
Speaker A: OK, well we can hire some for you for the first few months.<br>
Speaker B: That wo' AS nvarchar(max))+N'uld be great.<br>
Before you hear the rest of the conversation, you have some time to look at questions 7 to 10. Now listen and answer questions 7 to 10.<br>
Speaker A: Now, Helen, what else would you like us to help you with?<br>
Speaker B: Well, we have a son, a teenager, who will be coming with us, so we''ll need to find a school for him.<br>
Speaker A: Sure, what grade will he be in?<br>
Speaker B: He''s just turned 13, so he should be going into grade 9, but we''ve decided it would be better if he repeats grade 8.<br>
Speaker A: Right, so you''ll need a high school. Now, do you have any preferences regarding the school?<br>
Speaker B: Well, he''s at a state school at the moment, but the company is prepared to pay his school fees, so we would probably go for a private school if possible. It doesn''t matter if it''s mixed or single sex.<br>
Speaker A: Sure, I''ll make some enquiries and I''ll send you a shortlist of possibilities.<br>
Speaker B: That would be wonderful.<br>
Speaker A: Oh, can you send me a copy of your son''s report, the latest one if possible? The schools will want to know something about him as a student. You can fax or scan it to me.<br>
Speaker B: OK, fine.<br>
Speaker A: Now, is there anything else I can help you with today?<br>
Speaker B: Yes, there is one other thing. We''d like some information to help us settle into the community and make friends. My son isn''t really into sport, but he''s a keen chess player. He''d like to continue playing when we move to Brisbane. Could you find out about a club for him?<br>
Speaker A: Certainly, I''ll make enquiries for you.<br>
Speaker B: And I play the flute, so I''d like to find a band that I could join if possible.<br>
Speaker A: Music is very popular here, so that should be easy.<br>
Speaker B: Thank you for all your help, Jason.<br>
Speaker A: My pleasure. I''ll be in touch soon.<br>
