.<br>Speaker B: Sounds interesting.<br>Before you hear the rest of the conversation, you have some time to look at questions 8 to 10 on page 2.<br>Now listen and answer questions 8 to 10.<br>Speaker B: But let me find out about one more place. I''ve always wanted to go to Korea, but not on this trip. And I''ve been to Thailand, which I loved, but what about your Japan package?<br>Speaker A: Good choice. Well, that tour includes a terrific trip to a museum of traditional costume. The exhibits are gorgeous. They''ve got an absolutely priceless collection.<br>Speaker B: And I think the website says you take your clients to a market, don''t you? A crafts market, I think.<br>Speaker A: Well, we do go to a market, but it''s one that sells fish, and it''s one of the largest in the world. And you have the chance to sample the wares in a little restaurant nearby.<br>Speaker A: We also give you plenty of free time to wander around the city with our guides if you want.<br>Speaker B: And what''s the cost of all that?<br>Speaker A: £1,800.<br>Speaker B: Well, you''ve been ever so helpful. I''ve noted all the details down, and I''ll get back to you when I''ve made up my mind.<br>Speaker A: If we can give you any more help, do ring back.<br>Speaker B: Thanks, I will.<br></p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-6/iL.VOL6.2.S1881.PART1.mp3',NULL,1,0,1,NULL,0,1881),
(N'141c22ff-fa56-5afe-8293-886254625aca',N'dcdd4f30-5ff3-58d8-b20a-8e9c84f037fa',0,2,18,N'<p><em>Complete the table below.
Write <span>ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER</span> for each answer.</em></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'Asia-Pacific Tours Activity Holidays',11,0,1,NULL,0,1881),
(N'20039004-476e-52e3-80d3-bded05c26f17',N'141c22ff-fa56-5afe-8293-886254625aca',0,3,19,N'<h3>Asia-Pacific Tours Activity Holidays</h3><table border="1"><tbody><tr><td><p><span>Tour</span></p></td><td><p><span>Details</span></p></td><td><p><span>Cost</span></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Vietnam</p></td><td><ul><li><p>a cookery course at a 5- star hotel either</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ lessons</p> <ul><li><p>or a one-day trek in the</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p> <ul><li><p>attend a</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ performance</p></td><td><p>£ }{SPACE}{ </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Hong Kong</p></td><td><ul><li><p>go to the hills to look at</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p> <p>in a country park, followed by }{SPACE}{ in a monastery</p> <ul><li><p>visit an</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ factory with the chance to shop</p></td><td><p>£1320</p></td></tr><tr><td> }{SPACE}{ </td><td><ul><li><p>visit a museum of traditional</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p> <ul><li><p>tour of a big</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ market</p></td><td><p>£1800</p></td></tr></tbody></table>',N'<p>- Đáp án là diving </p><p>- Cụm “instruction in diving”tương ứng với “lessons” trong đề → “diving lessons” </p><p>- Đây là paraphrase trực tiếp: instruction = lessons</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ instruction (n): sự hướng dẫn </p><p>+ diving (n): lặn</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,1,NULL,0,1881),
(N'bb78b0e4-1e25-596a-bfb5-163a869ab5fd',N'141c22ff-fa56-5afe-8293-886254625aca',0,3,19,N'Question number 2',N'<p>- Đáp án là jungle </p><p>- “trek through the jungle” khớp với “trek in the …” trong đề </p><p>- Không có từnào khác phù hợp hơn trong đoạn</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ trek (n): chuyến đi bộ dài </p><p>+ jungle (n): rừng rậm</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,2,NULL,0,1881),
(N'71c1913a-3cad-5ea9-a10b-665994a0fff3',N'141c22ff-fa56-5afe-8293-886254625aca',0,3,19,N'Question number 3',N'<p>- Đáp án là dance </p><p>- “dance show” tương ứng với “performance” trong đề </p><p>- Opera bị loại vì “used to” (không còn nữa)</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ dance show (n): buổi biểu diễn múa </p><p>+ performance (n): buổi biểu diễn</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,3,NULL,0,1881),
(N'0c2c08c9-9e91-55e0-9264-6579a4f08c1c',N'141c22ff-fa56-5afe-8293-886254625aca',0,3,19,N'Question number 4',N'<p>- Đáp án là 1450 </p><p>- Giá mới sau khi giảm từ £1600 xuống £1450 </p><p>- Đề yêu cầu điền số → không cần ký hiệu £</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ reduced (v): giảm xuống </p><p>+ special price (n): giá ưu đãi</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,4,NULL,0,1881),
(N'19c2e149-5452-54cd-974d-4197c411abd9',N'141c22ff-fa56-5afe-8293-886254625aca',0,3,19,N'Question number 5',N'<p>- Đáp án là birds </p><p>- “see birds of all sorts” khớp với “look at … in a country park” </p><p>- Không có lựa chọn khác</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ birds (n): chim </p><p>+ country park (n): công viên quốc gia</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,5,NULL,0,1881),
(N'1efd5aa0-00b3-5afb-8864-5b8ebb46c1ba',N'141c22ff-fa56-5afe-8293-886254625aca',0,3,19,N'Question number 6',N'<p>- Đáp án là dinner </p><p>- “includes dinner in a monastery” → khớp trực tiếp với chỗ trống </p><p>- Đây là chi tiết cụ thể sau hoạt động đi bộ</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ dinner (n): bữa tối</p><p> + monastery (n): tu viện</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,6,NULL,0,1881),
(N'813f18e1-fd34-5441-b0dd-ef02c43e908c',N'141c22ff-fa56-5afe-8293-886254625aca',0,3,19,N'Question number 7',N'<p>- Đáp án là electronics </p><p>- “electronics factory” khớp trực tiếp với đề </p><p>- “ceramics factory” chỉ là so sánh → không phải đáp án</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ electronics (n): đồ điện tử </p><p>+ factory (n): nhà máy</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,7,NULL,0,1881),
(N'52586bf1-d858-5d01-842e-fa3b0bdadd83',N'141c22ff-fa56-5afe-8293-886254625aca',0,3,19,N'Question number 8',N'<p>- Đáp án là Japan </p><p>- Người nói hỏi về “Japan package” → đây là tour thứ 3 </p><p>- Korea và Thailand bị loại vì không chọn</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ package (n): gói du lịch </p><p>+ Japan (n): Nhật Bản</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,8,NULL,0,1881),
(N'9c9aa5b6-3211-5fae-9849-2c4a221b9ffe',N'141c22ff-fa56-5afe-8293-886254625aca',0,3,19,N'Question number 9',N'<p>- Đáp án là costume </p><p>- “museum of traditional costume” khớp hoàn toàn với đề </p><p>- Không có từ thay thế</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ costume (n): trang phục </p><p>+ museum (n): bảo tàng</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,9,NULL,0,1881),
(N'10908d4d-ef80-5595-8cbf-c3e88f65b377',N'141c22ff-fa56-5afe-8293-886254625aca',0,3,19,N'Question number 10',N'<p>- Đáp án là fish </p><p>- “market that sells fish” → khớp với “big … market” </p><p>- “crafts market” bị sửa lại → bẫy đề</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ fish (n): cá </p><p>+ market (n): chợ</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,10,NULL,0,1881),
(N'd8ba0ec9-4c87-599e-800f-e399f4d2eb83',N'b614f55b-5505-54fe-b28e-0a43c89f4a9a',0,1,14,(CAST(N'<h2>[VOL 6] Test 2 - Section 2</h2><p>You''ll hear the organiser of a weekend dancing course for adults welcoming a group of participants to the community centre where the course is being held. First you have some time to look at questions 11 to 14 on page 3. Now listen carefully and answer questions 11 to 14. Hello everyone and welcome to this weekend dancing course. Nice that you''re here safely. Since you''ve all just arrived I''d like to tell you firstly a bit about today''s program and secondly how to get around this community centre. Firstly, straight after this talk you''ll go off to the office where you should check in at the registration desk. Make sure you''re wearing the name tags that we posted you out in the mail last week.</p><p>The staff there will give you each a cloth bag as a little present from us to keep your dancing shoes in for the weekend. Other things useful to take to class each day will be a bottle of water, hopefully you''ve all brought one with you, and a towel for your face if it''s hot and you feel you need one. Also at registration you can pick up a list for the level class that you''re in so you can start learning people''s names. After checking in, this first afternoon is free for everyone. You could use this time to start thinking about your costumes for the final show but we won''t be making them until tomorrow. For those of you who are interested, there''s a lecture this afternoon in the main hall on the history of dance or you could practice for Sunday''s concert in the music room. There is also an informal gathering planned for tonight consisting of mainly easy dances where you can get to know each other. The tests of different levels won''t be held until the final afternoon so there''s no need to worry about those yet. Before you hear the rest of the talk, you have some time to look at questions 15 to 20 on page 4. Now listen and answer questions 15 to 20. Now, I said I would tell you how to find your way around the community centre. Well, we''re standing at the south end of the site. I''ll tell you where the bathrooms are first. That''s the most important thing. Walk straight ahead from here past this first big block on your left and you''ll find the bathrooms on your left just after it. Now, equally important of course is where you''ll sleep. So the bunk rooms are just here on our left. You can see them beside where we''re standing now. Now, we also have a games room where you can entertain yourself during your free time. Well, you''ll ge' AS nvarchar(max))+N't there if you go straight ahead from where we''re standing now, take the first turning right and carry on to the second building. It''s on your right just before the bike racks. Games and books are in the cupboard there and there''s a ping pong table, air hockey, things like that. Good for a rainy day. OK, what else? The hall is where we''ll be for class photos. You can find that in the middle of the site just south of the music room. The medical room, in case any of you get injured while you''re dancing, can be found in the centre of the site also. </p><p>Go straight on from here past two pathways and it''s on your right beside the music room. The nurse there is very good with sports injuries so don''t hesitate to visit her if you need to. Any questions? Oh yes, the reception office, of course. You''ll need to go over there after this talk to register. That''s quite a long walk away from here. Go straight ahead and take the third turning on your right, then you will find that the office is the second building on your left. The staff there are very friendly and if you have any problems during the weekend, go to see them and they''ll help you out. That is the end of Section 2. You now have half a minute to check your answers. Now turn to Section 3 on page 5</p>'),(CAST(N'<p>You''ll hear the organiser of a weekend dancing course for adults welcoming a group of participants to the community centre where the course is being held. First you have some time to look at questions 11 to 14 on page 3. Now listen carefully and answer questions 11 to 14. Hello everyone and welcome to this weekend dancing course. Nice that you''re here safely. Since you''ve all just arrived I''d like to tell you firstly a bit about today''s program and secondly how to get around this community centre. Firstly, straight after this talk you''ll go off to the office where you should check in at the registration desk. Make sure you''re wearing the name tags that we posted you out in the mail last week.</p><p>The staff there will give you each a cloth bag as a little present from us to keep your dancing shoes in for the weekend. Other things useful to take to class each day will be a bottle of water, hopefully you''ve all brought one with you, and a towel for your face if it''s hot and you feel you need one. Also at registration you can pick up a list for the level class that you''re in so you can start learning people''s names. After checking in, this first afternoon is free for everyone. You could use this time to start thinking about your costumes for the final show but we won''t be making them until tomorrow. For those of you who are interested, there''s a lecture this afternoon in the main hall on the history of dance or you could practice for Sunday''s concert in the music room. There is also an informal gathering planned for tonight consisting of mainly easy dances where you can get to know each other. The tests of different levels won''t be held until the final afternoon so there''s no need to worry about those yet. Before you hear the rest of the talk, you have some time to look at questions 15 to 20 on page 4. Now listen and answer questions 15 to 20. Now, I said I would tell you how to find your way around the community centre. Well, we''re standing at the south end of the site. I''ll tell you where the bathrooms are first. That''s the most important thing. Walk straight ahead from here past this first big block on your left and you''ll find the bathrooms on your left just after it. Now, equally important of course is where you''ll sleep. So the bunk rooms are just here on our left. You can see them beside where we''re standing now. Now, we also have a games room where you can entertain yourself during your free time. Well, you''ll get there if you go straight ahead fr' AS nvarchar(max))+N'om where we''re standing now, take the first turning right and carry on to the second building. It''s on your right just before the bike racks. Games and books are in the cupboard there and there''s a ping pong table, air hockey, things like that. Good for a rainy day. OK, what else? The hall is where we''ll be for class photos. You can find that in the middle of the site just south of the music room. The medical room, in case any of you get injured while you''re dancing, can be found in the centre of the site also. </p><p>Go straight on from here past two pathways and it''s on your right beside the music room. The nurse there is very good with sports injuries so don''t hesitate to visit her if you need to. Any questions? Oh yes, the reception office, of course. You''ll need to go over there after this talk to register. That''s quite a long walk away from here. Go straight ahead and take the third turning on your right, then you will find that the office is the second building on your left. The staff there are very friendly and if you have any problems during the weekend, go to see them and they''ll help you out. That is the end of Section 2. You now have half a minute to check your answers. Now turn to Section 3 on page 5</p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-6/iL.VOL6.2.S1881.PART2.mp3',NULL,1,0,2,NULL,0,1881),
(N'3847766f-16e9-5048-baac-3bd640d2dc84',N'd8ba0ec9-4c87-599e-800f-e399f4d2eb83',0,2,18,N'<p>Choose<span> TWO</span> letters,<span> A-E.</span></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',5,0,1,NULL,0,1881),
(N'90ea43d9-e547-53e3-b4c6-99ca3bc72784',N'3847766f-16e9-5048-baac-3bd640d2dc84',0,3,19,N'<p>Which<span> TWO</span> items will participants on the dancing course receive when they check in?</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là D (a shoe bag) </p><p>- “cloth bag … to keep your dancing shoes” → chính là shoe bag </p><p>- B (face towel) sai vì chỉ là “useful to take”, không phải được phát - E (water bottle) sai vì “you’ve all brought one” → tự mang</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ cloth bag (n): túi vải </p><p>+ keep shoes (v): đựng giày</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,11,NULL,0,1881),
(N'25a41a32-e1e5-5dcb-a7db-8c4324b6496b',N'3847766f-16e9-5048-baac-3bd640d2dc84',0,3,19,N'<p>Which<span> TWO</span> items will participants on the dancing course receive when they check in?</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là A (a class list) </p><p>- “pick up a list for the level class” = nhận danh sách lớp </p><p>- C (name tag) sai vì đã “posted you out in the mail” → gửi trước</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ pick up (v): nhận </p><p>+ list (n): danh sách</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,12,NULL,0,1881),
(N'50dcc749-56f1-5a16-886e-16aaa7077532',N'd8ba0ec9-4c87-599e-800f-e399f4d2eb83',0,2,18,N'<p>Choose<span> TWO l</span>etters,<span> A-E.</span></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',5,0,2,NULL,0,1881),
(N'78f83c7f-f444-5966-addf-658cae7613a4',N'50dcc749-56f1-5a16-886e-16aaa7077532',0,3,19,N'<p>Which <span>TWO</span> activities will take place on the first afternoon and evening?</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là C (an informal dance) </p><p>- “informal gathering … easy dances” = buổi nhảy không chính thức </p><p>- Đây là hoạt động buổi tối (evening)</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ informal gathering (n): buổi gặp gỡ không chính thức </p><p>+ easy dances (n): các điệu nhảy đơn giản</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,13,NULL,0,1881),
(N'21562e26-ce7f-5c04-883d-103d8d4eb4c6',N'50dcc749-56f1-5a16-886e-16aaa7077532',0,3,19,N'<p>Which <span>TWO</span> activities will take place on the first afternoon and evening?</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là D (a talk on dance history) </p><p>- “lecture … on the history of dance” = talk on dance history - A (costume making) sai vì “won’t be making them until tomorrow” </p><p>- E (tests) sai vì “won’t be held until the final afternoon”</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ lecture (n): bài nói chuyện </p><p>+ history (n): lịch sử</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,14,NULL,0,1881),
(N'2ab9ef27-a24a-54e8-a161-a4aabbc2f708',N'd8ba0ec9-4c87-599e-800f-e399f4d2eb83',0,2,18,N'<p>Label the map below. Write the correct letter,<span> A-I</span>, next to Question 15-20</p><p><img src="https://ieltsroom.com/upload/images/ieltsadvancedtest/88b109d48768b22bbd1a.png" alt="Question diagram"></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',12,0,3,NULL,0,1881),
(N'345cf1e7-7347-5fd0-a9d1-6fa3970363e0',N'2ab9ef27-a24a-54e8-a161-a4aabbc2f708',0,3,19,N'<p>the bathrooms</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là A </p><p>- Đi thẳng, qua khối nhà lớn bên trái → bathrooms ở bên trái sau đó </p><p>- Trên map, vị trí này tương ứng điểm A</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ straight ahead (adv): đi thẳng </p><p>+ on your left (phr): bên trái</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,15,NULL,0,1881),
(N'af10d8db-54da-58cc-95d4-51bda9a96f9d',N'2ab9ef27-a24a-54e8-a161-a4aabbc2f708',0,3,19,N'<p>the bunkrooms</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là E - “just here on our left” </p><p>+ “beside where we''re standing” </p><p>- Trên bản đồ, vị trí sát chỗ đứng bên trái là E</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ bunk rooms (n): phòng ngủ tập thể </p><p>+ beside (prep): bên cạnh</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,16,NULL,0,1881),
(N'5163825b-2e9b-5f98-b040-dab63bb3249d',N'2ab9ef27-a24a-54e8-a161-a4aabbc2f708',0,3,19,N'<p>the games room</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là I </p><p>- “second building… on your right… before the bike racks”</p><p> - Trên map, vị trí ngay trước bike racks bên phải là I</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ turning (n): ngã rẽ </p><p>+ building (n): tòa nhà</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,17,NULL,0,1881),
(N'2f831fe3-bd3c-51ce-99a7-517eb235fb01',N'2ab9ef27-a24a-54e8-a161-a4aabbc2f708',0,3,19,N'<p>the hall</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là F - “middle of the site” + “just south of the music room” - Trên bản đồ, vị trí D nằm ngay dưới music room </p><p>- Key word: + south of (prep): phía nam của + middle (n): trung tâm</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,18,NULL,0,1881),
(N'fcbc3962-4eb1-589e-9681-4e317fdfd260',N'2ab9ef27-a24a-54e8-a161-a4aabbc2f708',0,3,19,N'<p>the medical room</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là D</p><p> - “on your right beside the music room” </p><p>- Trên map, F nằm bên phải gần music room</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ beside (prep): bên cạnh </p><p>+ medical room (n): phòng y tế</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,19,NULL,0,1881),
(N'6318650b-8af4-5c8d-8b5d-192f992cb3b6',N'2ab9ef27-a24a-54e8-a161-a4aabbc2f708',0,3,19,N'<p>the reception office</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là B </p><p>- “third turning right → second building on left” </p><p>- Trên map, vị trí phù hợp là B</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ turning (n): ngã rẽ </p><p>+ office (n): văn phòng</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,20,NULL,0,1881),
(N'78888bcc-35c1-5ab5-8a7e-9428c03a87cc',N'b614f55b-5505-54fe-b28e-0a43c89f4a9a',0,1,15,(CAST(N'<h2>Innovative Environmental Solutions</h2><p>Speaker A: Okay, everyone get into pairs and look at the innovative environmental solutions we''ve been reading about this week. Discuss some of the pros and cons of each one.<br>
Speaker A: You want to work together Ella?<br>
Speaker B: Sure Dominic. Which solution do you want to look at first?<br>
Speaker A: I think the supermarket garden project''s interesting.<br>
Speaker B: That''s where the supermarket grows fruit and vegetables in the store and sells them.<br>
Speaker A: Yes. Understandably only a few shops have decided to adopt this idea. It''s hard to set up.<br>
Speaker B: What''s the reaction from customers?<br>
Speaker A: Well, of course they love the idea. One thing I didn''t expect though.<br>
Speaker B: What was that?<br>
Speaker A: The idea is hugely popular with local chefs and many of them are finding new ways to use the plants and all their different stages of growth.<br>
Speaker B: I see. I found the solar car park idea to be really practical.<br>
Speaker A: I know what you mean. Putting solar panels on the roofs of car parks to generate electricity might be a cost-effective way to power a whole shopping centre.<br>
Speaker B: The difficulty could be finding space to put all the panels. Some smaller shopping centres probably don''t have covered car parks.<br>
Speaker A: That''s right. It''s a shame because the technology seems to be all there and ready to go if the conditions are right.<br>
Speaker B: What do you think of the wildlife crossing solution?<br>
Speaker B: You know, when a bridge or a tunnel is built over or under a major roadway so that animals can cross.<br>
Speaker A: That idea has become very popular and has so many benefits. A lot of research has been done hasn''t it?<br>
Speaker B: Yes. It''s not surprising that the data reveals a huge drop in the number of road accidents in areas where there are wildlife crossings.<br>
Speaker A: That''s one of the predicted outcomes.<br>
Speaker B: Something I read about in the research, which I''d never considered before, was how the animal populations in these areas are affected.<br>
Speaker B: Naturally more of them survive, but because their habitat is not interrupted too much by the roads, the genetic diversity of local species has improved.<br>
Speaker A: That''s true. It''s worth the huge cost of building them if the result is a win-win for people and animals.<br>
Speaker A: I found the 100% renewable energy campaign, like solar and wind energy, ' AS nvarchar(max))+N'to be really impressive.<br>
Speaker B: Yes, it''s not so much the size of the movement, I mean only a few countries are involved, as the amount of support offered once a community joins.<br>
Speaker B: Considering the sheer amount of time and planning it takes for a city to convert completely to renewables, the organisers of the movement would need to do that.<br>
Speaker A: Did you read about carrot mobbing as an environmental movement?<br>
Speaker B: What''s that?<br>
Speaker A: It''s where huge numbers of people learn through the internet about where to shop at stores that use the profits to support environmental projects.<br>
Speaker A: So they stop buying products that aren''t eco-friendly, like a boycott?<br>
Speaker B: No, actually, it''s the opposite of that. It allows businesses to fund initiatives to help protect the environment by boosting their profiles.<br>
Speaker A: It''s a pity that most participants don''t get to know each other personally. It''s all through online notices.<br>
Before you hear the rest of the discussion, you have some time to look at questions 26 to 30 on page 6. Now listen and answer questions 26 to 30.<br>
Speaker A: Now everyone, let''s look at one particular environmental innovation, aerial reforestation. With your partner, discuss the process involved in this idea.<br>
Speaker B: So, aerial reforestation is where they drop mixtures from plains to sow vegetables, grains or trees and so on in areas that might be hard to reach.<br>
Speaker A: Let''s see. What are the steps?<br>
Speaker B: Well, the first step is choosing the right area. Whatever size land you''re working on, ensuring there''s enough light is crucial.<br>
Speaker B: The next step, whatever you''re planting, is to make sure you have the right seeds. To give them a better chance against the competition from other plants, you need to use a lot.<br>
Speaker B: So then you make a mixture with decent quality, durable compost for nourishment.<br>
Speaker A: Then do they infuse it with insecticide?<br>
Speaker B: That''s not necessary in this model.<br>
Speaker B: The next step is pressing the whole thing into a small chunk of clay to make a ball. This may then be covered in an outer material such as paper.<br>
Speaker A: Right. That way, when it lands, it will add balanced nutrients to the mixture.<br>
Speaker B: Yes. And it may also protect it from insects and other plants.<br>
Speaker B: So a few days before they release it from the plain onto the land below, the final ste'+N'p is dipping it in water, just enough to get the germination process started.<br>
Speaker A: Yes. And after that...<br>
