(N'8a756c41-bd67-5dbd-9b85-31187a33e5b1',N'df2b44be-5609-5872-9d4f-2b640a069b64',0,3,19,N'<h3>Canadian maple syrup</h3><p><span>Description</span></p><ul><li><p>It is a sweet liquid poured over pancakes etc.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>The production of sap needs a climate where night and day temperatures are very </p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p><p><span>History</span></p><ul><li><p>Folk stories claim that maple syrup was first used to cook</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p><ul><li><p>Sap collection in spring developed into a First Nations</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p><ul><li><p>The sap was collected in buckets.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>The sap was concentrated into syrup by</p></li></ul><p>- using hot stones to produce }{SPACE}{ </p><p>- leaving it outside at night and then removing the layer of }{SPACE}{ on top.</p><p><span>Uses</span></p><ul><li><p>First Nations people drank the fresh sap to give them energy.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>European settlers put the syrup in various types of</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p><ul><li><p>They also used it for drinks and for candy.</p></li></ul><p><span>Threats</span></p><ul><li><p>Its use for making sugar declined after 1880, when the</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ on Caribbean sugar was removed. </p><ul><li><p>Natural</p></li></ul><p>- Harvests may be affected by storms and destructive }{SPACE}{ </p><p>- Climate change may also affect sap production.</p><ul><li><p>Social</p></li></ul><p>- Maple syrup is expensive and faces considerable }{SPACE}{ </p><p>- The obesity issue is affecting sales.</p><ul><li><p><span>Reasons for optimism</span></p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Maple syrup is an important export.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>It is quite</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ compared with other sweeteners.</p><ul><li><p>Its taste is the main reason for its popularity.</p></li></ul>',N'<p>- Đáp án là different </p><p>- “hugely different” → paraphrase của “very different” trong đề </p><p>- Nói về sự chênh lệch nhiệt độ ngày – đêm</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ different (adj): khác nhau </p><p>+ temperatures (n): nhiệt độ</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,31,NULL,0,1881),
(N'36d39504-a86f-5f35-ae61-d87f0e0eba1c',N'df2b44be-5609-5872-9d4f-2b640a069b64',0,3,19,N'Question number 32',N'<p>- Đáp án là meat - “used this sap to boil meat” → nấu thịt - Khớp trực tiếp với “used to cook …” </p><p>- Key word: + boil (v): đun sôi + meat (n): thịt</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,32,NULL,0,1881),
(N'6ded196d-9f52-5aea-acf5-93b1ddb17991',N'df2b44be-5609-5872-9d4f-2b640a069b64',0,3,19,N'Question number 33',N'<p>- Đáp án là tradition</p><p>- “developed into a First Nations …” = became a tradition </p><p>- Đây là paraphrase trực tiếp</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ tradition (n): truyền thống </p><p>+ collect (v): thu thập</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,33,NULL,0,1881),
(N'323b5591-4220-5bf4-92f6-a5032ad0a6c3',N'df2b44be-5609-5872-9d4f-2b640a069b64',0,3,19,N'Question number 34',N'<p>- Đáp án là steam </p><p>- “produce …” = create steam </p><p>- Hơi nước giúp làm bay hơi nước → cô đặc siro</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ steam (n): hơi nước </p><p>+ concentrate (v): cô đặc</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,34,NULL,0,1881),
(N'06e60c50-3ca0-5f13-b44f-9af5023d1578',N'df2b44be-5609-5872-9d4f-2b640a069b64',0,3,19,N'Question number 35',N'<p>Đáp án là ice - “layer of ice … on top” → lớp băng trên cùng </p><p>- Khớp trực tiếp với đề</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ ice (n): băng </p><p>+ layer (n): lớp</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,35,NULL,0,1881),
(N'c14b29fc-41cb-5bf2-8a2e-d86cf702e47d',N'df2b44be-5609-5872-9d4f-2b640a069b64',0,3,19,N'Question number 36',N'<p>- Đáp án là medicine </p><p>- “incorporated it into medicine” → dùng trong y học </p><p>- Khớp với “various types of …”</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ medicine (n): thuốc </p><p>+ incorporate (v): kết hợp</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,36,NULL,0,1881),
(N'8de124a6-6dd3-56a4-b3ee-ab21d3e7cd14',N'df2b44be-5609-5872-9d4f-2b640a069b64',0,3,19,N'Question number 37',N'<p>- Đáp án là tax </p><p>- “stop charging tax” → loại bỏ thuế </p><p>- Khớp với “removed” trong đề</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ tax (n): thuế </p><p>+ cheaper (adj): rẻ hơn</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,37,NULL,0,1881),
(N'ddd60bde-d85b-5c0c-8be3-64f4356cdb63',N'df2b44be-5609-5872-9d4f-2b640a069b64',0,3,19,N'Question number 38',N'<p>- Đáp án là insects </p><p>- “destructive …” = invasive insects </p><p>- Là yếu tố tự nhiên gây hại</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ insects (n): côn trùng </p><p>+ invasive (adj): xâm lấn</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,38,NULL,0,1881),
(N'c4f7bbe4-4e52-58dc-aa9e-dff811ceb493',N'df2b44be-5609-5872-9d4f-2b640a069b64',0,3,19,N'Question number 39',N'<p>- Đáp án là competition </p><p>- “faces considerable …” = a lot of competition </p><p>- Áp lực từ sản phẩm rẻ hơn</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ competition (n): cạnh tranh </p><p>+ cheaper (adj): rẻ hơn</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,39,NULL,0,1881),
(N'ce9ea261-2220-5a8b-854d-02bb013e6023',N'df2b44be-5609-5872-9d4f-2b640a069b64',0,3,19,N'Question number 40',N'<p>- Đáp án là healthy </p><p>- “relatively healthy compared with other sweeteners” </p><p>- Đây là điểm tích cực</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ healthy (adj): tốt cho sức khỏe </p><p>+ compare (v): so sánh</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,40,NULL,0,1881),
(N'97e01757-307b-5892-adfc-eaff9a3a0a6f',NULL,0,0,11,NULL,NULL,NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-6/iL.VOL6.1.S1878.mp3',N'Vol 6 LISTENING FULL TEST 1',0,7,1,NULL,1,1878),
(N'cad2bac0-f39a-5f05-8bb2-5dd385762e65',N'97e01757-307b-5892-adfc-eaff9a3a0a6f',0,1,13,(CAST(N'<h2>[VOL 6] The White House Restaurant Booking Information Event Details</h2><p>Speaker A: Hello, White House Restaurant. How can I help you?<br>Speaker B: Good afternoon. I''m ringing to make enquiries about holding a party at your restaurant. I understand you have a private function room I could book?<br>Speaker A: We certainly have. What kind of event have you got in mind?<br>Speaker B: I''ve been asked to organise this for a colleague''s leaving party. She''s going off to head our Shanghai office, and we''re giving her a bit of a send-off.<br>Speaker A: Right. Well, we''ve got three rooms. The Mayfair room – that''s the basement with a dance floor. Then we''ve also got the Blue Room on the first floor. The last one is the Garden Room, which has doors leading onto the terrace. That''s very nice for summer lunch parties.<br>Speaker B: That sounds best. We were thinking of an evening, and as it''s summer, it''ll be great to be able to go outside.<br>Speaker A: OK. But what about numbers? It''s quite a big room, and you don''t want it for just a small party.<br>Speaker B: There are 26 of us from the office, and a few partners are coming along as well. So we''re looking at 35 people, I''d say.<br>Speaker A: That sounds fine. And how do you want the room set up? You could have two long tables, for example.<br>Speaker B: Would it be possible to have lots of round tables, small ones?<br>Speaker B: Then people can choose who they sit with. And we want them to look nice, so could we have candles on the tables?<br>Speaker B: Oh, and some soft background music, not pop songs or anything.<br>Speaker A: Certainly. Now, I need to take down some of your details. First of all, can I have your name, please?<br>Speaker B: Sure. It''s Lisa Elliott.<br>Speaker A: Is that with one or two L''s?<br>Speaker B: It''s with two. E-double-L-I-O-double-T.<br>Speaker A: OK. And the name of the company?<br>Speaker B: Newman Construction.<br>Speaker A: Right. And if you give me the address, I can send you a letter of confirmation.<br>Speaker B: It''s Abbey House, Bridge Street.<br>Speaker B: And that''s in Dewsbury. Let me just get that down.<br>Speaker A: And what about the postcode?<br>Speaker B: W-F-13-4-H-H.<br>Before you hear the rest of the conversation, you have some time to look at questions 7 to 10.<br>Now listen and answer questions 7 to 10.<br>Speaker A: Now, have you got a contact number in case I need to get hold of you?<br>Speaker B: Yes, it''s 476-259.<br>Speaker A: Right. And can you tell ' AS nvarchar(max))+N'me what kind of food you had in mind?<br>Speaker B: Well, we''d prefer a cold buffet. We don''t really want a hot sit-down meal.<br>Speaker A: OK. We can do several different buffet deals. Our prices per head are £15, £20 or £30 for the luxury buffet.<br>Speaker B: Um, I think we''ll go with the middle one.<br>Speaker A: I''ll make a note of that then.<br>Speaker B: Oh, and I don''t know if this is possible, but could you organise a bunch of flowers for us? We''d like to give them to her at the end of the meal and it''s easier not to bring them with us.<br>Speaker A: Certainly we can do that. I''ll include it in the estimate we send.<br>Speaker A: Now, what about the date?<br>Speaker B: We want it for the first week in July. I think it was the third. Let me check my diary. No, the fourth. Is that OK for you?<br>Speaker A: Yes, that''s fine. A few weeks away still.<br>Speaker A: What time do you want to start?<br>Speaker B: Seven o''clock. Some people will want to come straight from work. And we expect to finish about ten.<br>Speaker A: Right. And the last thing is, we''d need to have a deposit.<br>Speaker B: OK. How much is that going to be?<br>Speaker A: We charge 25 percent of the total cost.<br>Speaker B: Fine. If you send me a letter confirming everything, I can let you have a company check by return of post.<br>Speaker A: Great. I''ll get that off to you straight away.<br></p>'),(CAST(N'<p>Speaker A: Hello, White House Restaurant. How can I help you?<br>Speaker B: Good afternoon. I''m ringing to make enquiries about holding a party at your restaurant. I understand you have a private function room I could book?<br>Speaker A: We certainly have. What kind of event have you got in mind?<br>Speaker B: I''ve been asked to organise this for a colleague''s leaving party. She''s going off to head our Shanghai office, and we''re giving her a bit of a send-off.<br>Speaker A: Right. Well, we''ve got three rooms. The Mayfair room – that''s the basement with a dance floor. Then we''ve also got the Blue Room on the first floor. The last one is the Garden Room, which has doors leading onto the terrace. That''s very nice for summer lunch parties.<br>Speaker B: That sounds best. We were thinking of an evening, and as it''s summer, it''ll be great to be able to go outside.<br>Speaker A: OK. But what about numbers? It''s quite a big room, and you don''t want it for just a small party.<br>Speaker B: There are 26 of us from the office, and a few partners are coming along as well. So we''re looking at 35 people, I''d say.<br>Speaker A: That sounds fine. And how do you want the room set up? You could have two long tables, for example.<br>Speaker B: Would it be possible to have lots of round tables, small ones?<br>Speaker B: Then people can choose who they sit with. And we want them to look nice, so could we have candles on the tables?<br>Speaker B: Oh, and some soft background music, not pop songs or anything.<br>Speaker A: Certainly. Now, I need to take down some of your details. First of all, can I have your name, please?<br>Speaker B: Sure. It''s Lisa Elliott.<br>Speaker A: Is that with one or two L''s?<br>Speaker B: It''s with two. E-double-L-I-O-double-T.<br>Speaker A: OK. And the name of the company?<br>Speaker B: Newman Construction.<br>Speaker A: Right. And if you give me the address, I can send you a letter of confirmation.<br>Speaker B: It''s Abbey House, Bridge Street.<br>Speaker B: And that''s in Dewsbury. Let me just get that down.<br>Speaker A: And what about the postcode?<br>Speaker B: W-F-13-4-H-H.<br>Before you hear the rest of the conversation, you have some time to look at questions 7 to 10.<br>Now listen and answer questions 7 to 10.<br>Speaker A: Now, have you got a contact number in case I need to get hold of you?<br>Speaker B: Yes, it''s 476-259.<br>Speaker A: Right. And can you tell me what kind of food you had in mind?<br>Speaker B: Well, we''d prefer a cold ' AS nvarchar(max))+N'buffet. We don''t really want a hot sit-down meal.<br>Speaker A: OK. We can do several different buffet deals. Our prices per head are £15, £20 or £30 for the luxury buffet.<br>Speaker B: Um, I think we''ll go with the middle one.<br>Speaker A: I''ll make a note of that then.<br>Speaker B: Oh, and I don''t know if this is possible, but could you organise a bunch of flowers for us? We''d like to give them to her at the end of the meal and it''s easier not to bring them with us.<br>Speaker A: Certainly we can do that. I''ll include it in the estimate we send.<br>Speaker A: Now, what about the date?<br>Speaker B: We want it for the first week in July. I think it was the third. Let me check my diary. No, the fourth. Is that OK for you?<br>Speaker A: Yes, that''s fine. A few weeks away still.<br>Speaker A: What time do you want to start?<br>Speaker B: Seven o''clock. Some people will want to come straight from work. And we expect to finish about ten.<br>Speaker A: Right. And the last thing is, we''d need to have a deposit.<br>Speaker B: OK. How much is that going to be?<br>Speaker A: We charge 25 percent of the total cost.<br>Speaker B: Fine. If you send me a letter confirming everything, I can let you have a company check by return of post.<br>Speaker A: Great. I''ll get that off to you straight away.<br></p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-6/iL.VOL6.1.S1878.PART1.mp3',NULL,1,0,1,NULL,0,1878),
(N'851c7410-13f0-5ad8-aa3a-fd1fbc8cf35d',N'cad2bac0-f39a-5f05-8bb2-5dd385762e65',0,2,18,N'<p><em>Complete the form below. </em></p><p><em>Write <span>NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER</span> for each answer.</em></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'The White House Restaurant Booking Information Event Details',11,0,1,NULL,0,1878),
(N'eeddc641-3812-576f-b9a0-16cc0d7e315d',N'851c7410-13f0-5ad8-aa3a-fd1fbc8cf35d',0,3,19,N'<h3>The White House Restaurant Booking Information Event Details</h3><table border="1"><tbody><tr><td><p><span>Event Details</span></p></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p>Type of Event:</p></td><td><p>Colleague''s Leaving Party</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Preferred Room:</p></td><td> }{SPACE}{ Room</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Start Time:</p></td><td><p>7:00 PM, Estimated End Time: 10:00 PM</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Expected Number of Guests:</p></td><td><p>35</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><span>Room Setup</span></p></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p>Table Arrangement:</p></td><td> }{SPACE}{ Tables</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Special Decorations:</p></td><td> }{SPACE}{ on Tables</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Type of Meal:</p></td><td><p>Cold Buffet</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Selected Buffet Package:</p></td><td><p>£20 per head</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><span>Client Details</span></p></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p>Name:</p></td><td><p>Lisa }{SPACE}{ </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Company:</p></td><td><p>Newman }{SPACE}{ </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Address:</p></td><td><p>Abbey House, Bridge Street, Dewsbury</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Postcode:</p></td><td> }{SPACE}{ </td></tr><tr><td><p>Contact Number:</p></td><td> }{SPACE}{ </td></tr><tr><td><p><span>Additional Requests</span></p></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p>Special Request:</p></td><td><p>A bunch of }{SPACE}{ to be presented at the end of the meal</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Preferred date:</p></td><td> }{SPACE}{ </td></tr><tr><td><p><span>Payment</span></p></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p>Deposit:</p></td><td> }{SPACE}{ of the full cost</p></td></tr></tbody></table>',N'<p>- Đáp án là Garden - Người nói chọn “that sounds best” ngay sau khi lễ tân giới thiệu Garden Room, cho thấy đây là phòng được chọn</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ Garden Room (n): phòng khu vườn </p><p>+ sounds best (phrase): nghe có vẻ phù hợp nhất</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,1,NULL,0,1878),
(N'4520b0de-d8ce-55fe-b7d6-85eb8fc2da93',N'851c7410-13f0-5ad8-aa3a-fd1fbc8cf35d',0,3,19,N'Question number 2',N'<p>- Đáp án là round - Người đặt tiệc yêu cầu “lots of round tables” → loại bàn là bàn tròn</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ round (adj): tròn </p><p>+ tables (n): bàn</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,2,NULL,0,1878),
(N'0fa39f88-3a2a-56cd-baaf-be4171e906be',N'851c7410-13f0-5ad8-aa3a-fd1fbc8cf35d',0,3,19,N'Question number 3',N'<p>- Đáp án là candles - “candles on the tables” → trang trí đặc biệt trên bàn là nến</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ candles (n): nến </p><p>+ look nice (phrase): trông đẹp</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,3,NULL,0,1878),
(N'34d8a330-9ab1-5f9c-aefa-e9be0c89f192',N'851c7410-13f0-5ad8-aa3a-fd1fbc8cf35d',0,3,19,N'Question number 4',N'<p>- Đáp án là Elliott - Tên đầy đủ được đánh vần rõ: Lisa Elliott → điền phần còn thiếu là họ </p><p>- Key word: + Elliott (n): họ người + name (n): tên</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,4,NULL,0,1878),
(N'3f776bfa-34d6-51df-a871-9265d8447cff',N'851c7410-13f0-5ad8-aa3a-fd1fbc8cf35d',0,3,19,N'Question number 5',N'<p>- Đáp án là Construction - Tên công ty được nói đầy đủ: Newman Construction → điền phần sau “Newman”</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ Construction (n): xây dựng </p><p>+ company (n): công ty</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,5,NULL,0,1878),
(N'322d8221-0a65-5694-9aef-b8201cff8194',N'851c7410-13f0-5ad8-aa3a-fd1fbc8cf35d',0,3,19,N'Question number 6',N'<p>- Đáp án là WF13 4HH - Người nói đánh vần từng ký tự → ghép lại thành postcode chuẩn</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ postcode (n): mã bưu điện </p><p>+ letters/numbers (n): chữ cái/số</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,6,NULL,0,1878),
(N'a7ebe5d8-902d-5729-bc87-f5cad8578a61',N'851c7410-13f0-5ad8-aa3a-fd1fbc8cf35d',0,3,19,N'Question number 7',N'<p>- Đáp án là 476-259 - Người nói cung cấp trực tiếp “contact number” → điền chính xác số này</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ contact number (n): số liên lạc</p><p>+ get hold of (v): liên lạc với</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,7,NULL,0,1878),
(N'9fdd27f3-3eda-505b-a047-0ca0f31dbe62',N'851c7410-13f0-5ad8-aa3a-fd1fbc8cf35d',0,3,19,N'Question number 8',N'<p>- Đáp án là flowers - Cụm “a bunch of flowers” khớp chính xác với đề bài “A bunch of ___” </p><p>- Key word: + bunch (n): bó + flowers (n): hoa</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,8,NULL,0,1878),
(N'0f53c2e5-78f3-51e1-96eb-bc24d9e7f946',N'851c7410-13f0-5ad8-aa3a-fd1fbc8cf35d',0,3,19,N'Question number 9',N'<p>- Đáp án là 4th July - Người nói sửa từ “third” thành “the fourth” và trước đó đã xác định là tháng July → ghép lại thành ngày đầy đủ</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ fourth (n): ngày mùng 4 </p><p>+ July (n): tháng 7</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,9,NULL,0,1878),
(N'6d2d5dfb-bfc2-541f-bc79-ecac187d9d92',N'851c7410-13f0-5ad8-aa3a-fd1fbc8cf35d',0,3,19,N'Question number 10',N'<p>- Đáp án là 25 percent - “deposit = 25 percent of the total cost” → điền chính xác tỷ lệ phần trăm </p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ deposit (n): tiền đặt cọc </p><p>+ total cost (n): tổng chi phí</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,10,NULL,0,1878),
(N'58166a48-580c-5ffc-ad83-ca4c2f2c70e2',N'97e01757-307b-5892-adfc-eaff9a3a0a6f',0,1,14,(CAST(N'<h2>[VOL 6] Test 1 - Section 2</h2><p>Good evening and thank you for coming to the Kenvale school fair volunteers meeting. As you know this is the biggest fundraising event in the school year and as usual we''re expecting lots of people to come which is why we''re starting to prepare now six months before the big day. I''ll begin tonight by talking about the different volunteer roles so you can decide what you''d like to do. </p><p>The entertainment coordinator position involves deciding what kinds of rides and activities will be at the fair and making sure there''s a good variety of things to do. From past experience this role involves a lot of liaising with other helpers and the entertainers which means that most of the work is done after office hours. We need an advertising and promotion coordinator to make sure that people hear about the fair and lots of people come. We know this is a big job so we''ve decided to have a couple of people doing it to share the load. The parent who did this role last year has just been offered a job which starts next month so she won''t be able to lend us the benefit of her experience sadly. The technical coordinator makes sure that there is a suitable stage for the performers and that there are enough speakers and people can hear them and so on. Now this may sound like a technical background is required but it''s not as you don''t actually have to set up or fix anything yourself. Having a car is essential though because in the week leading up to the event you''ll need to be able to get to the school early in the mornings and occasionally later at night. We also need a staffing coordinator. This person will be required to look after the many helpers on the day of the fair. This role has just been created based on our experience of last year''s event. We found that our volunteers felt a bit overworked and so we''re hoping that this role will make things easier. It will help to reduce stress if you organise the helpers about a month before the fair. Before you hear the rest of the talk you have some time to look at questions 15 to 20. Now listen and answer questions 15 to 20. Now moving on to the map of the school fair I''ll point out some of the more important areas that you''ll need to know about so you can help direct the visitors. You can see that we''ll be using the large grounds just behind the school and we''ll set up temporary areas and pathways there. The first thing I''ll show you are the fairground rights which are always popular' AS nvarchar(max))+N' with the children. If you look at the map you''ll see the fair entrance at the bottom. From there follow the main path in the direction of the river and it''s the third area on the left, the large rectangular area. The entertainment stage is a big feature of the fair and this is where everyone will be able to see all the performers. To find this go straight along the main path until you get to the river. Turn right and follow the path to the end and there it is. There''s not much shade here so we should remind parents to bring hats for their children. If anyone wants a cold drink or a snack then they''ll ask you where the cafe is. Originally we were going to put it opposite the toilets but we''ve decided to put it near the river to take advantage of the views and breezes. You can see it on the map it''s a circular area surrounded by trees near the playground. The first aid tent is always an important part of the fair. We wanted to put that in an area that was easily accessible and a bit separated from the other attractions but near the entrance. If you look at the map you''ll see it south of the toilets not far from the school fence line. </p><p>The market stools are where visitors will be able to pick up a bargain or some homemade produce. Last year these were located just south of the meeting area but the stool holders complained that it was too exposed and hot. So this year we''ve moved them to the north of the meeting area. Lots of good shelter provided by the trees here. Of course there''ll be the ever-popular pony rides. To reach these direct visitors to follow the main path from the entrance until they reach the L-shaped area on the left next to the playground. Now as always...</p>'),(CAST(N'<p>Good evening and thank you for coming to the Kenvale school fair volunteers meeting. As you know this is the biggest fundraising event in the school year and as usual we''re expecting lots of people to come which is why we''re starting to prepare now six months before the big day. I''ll begin tonight by talking about the different volunteer roles so you can decide what you''d like to do. </p><p>The entertainment coordinator position involves deciding what kinds of rides and activities will be at the fair and making sure there''s a good variety of things to do. From past experience this role involves a lot of liaising with other helpers and the entertainers which means that most of the work is done after office hours. We need an advertising and promotion coordinator to make sure that people hear about the fair and lots of people come. We know this is a big job so we''ve decided to have a couple of people doing it to share the load. The parent who did this role last year has just been offered a job which starts next month so she won''t be able to lend us the benefit of her experience sadly. The technical coordinator makes sure that there is a suitable stage for the performers and that there are enough speakers and people can hear them and so on. Now this may sound like a technical background is required but it''s not as you don''t actually have to set up or fix anything yourself. Having a car is essential though because in the week leading up to the event you''ll need to be able to get to the school early in the mornings and occasionally later at night. We also need a staffing coordinator. This person will be required to look after the many helpers on the day of the fair. This role has just been created based on our experience of last year''s event. We found that our volunteers felt a bit overworked and so we''re hoping that this role will make things easier. It will help to reduce stress if you organise the helpers about a month before the fair. Before you hear the rest of the talk you have some time to look at questions 15 to 20. Now listen and answer questions 15 to 20. Now moving on to the map of the school fair I''ll point out some of the more important areas that you''ll need to know about so you can help direct the visitors. You can see that we''ll be using the large grounds just behind the school and we''ll set up temporary areas and pathways there. The first thing I''ll show you are the fairground rights which are always popular with the children. If you look at ' AS nvarchar(max))+N'the map you''ll see the fair entrance at the bottom. From there follow the main path in the direction of the river and it''s the third area on the left, the large rectangular area. The entertainment stage is a big feature of the fair and this is where everyone will be able to see all the performers. To find this go straight along the main path until you get to the river. Turn right and follow the path to the end and there it is. There''s not much shade here so we should remind parents to bring hats for their children. If anyone wants a cold drink or a snack then they''ll ask you where the cafe is. Originally we were going to put it opposite the toilets but we''ve decided to put it near the river to take advantage of the views and breezes. You can see it on the map it''s a circular area surrounded by trees near the playground. The first aid tent is always an important part of the fair. We wanted to put that in an area that was easily accessible and a bit separated from the other attractions but near the entrance. If you look at the map you''ll see it south of the toilets not far from the school fence line. </p><p>The market stools are where visitors will be able to pick up a bargain or some homemade produce. Last year these were located just south of the meeting area but the stool holders complained that it was too exposed and hot. So this year we''ve moved them to the north of the meeting area. Lots of good shelter provided by the trees here. Of course there''ll be the ever-popular pony rides. To reach these direct visitors to follow the main path from the entrance until they reach the L-shaped area on the left next to the playground. Now as always...</p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-6/iL.VOL6.1.S1878.PART2.mp3',NULL,1,0,2,NULL,0,1878),
(N'b7f775db-6171-52e1-a3ed-d03bea14aa4b',N'58166a48-580c-5ffc-ad83-ca4c2f2c70e2',0,2,18,N'<p><em>What does the speaker say about each of the following volunteer roles at the school fair?
Choose <span>FOUR</span> correct answers, <span>A-F</span>, and write the correct letter next to questions 11-14.</em></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'Answer choices',15,0,1,NULL,0,1878),
(N'02777c85-73d8-5901-9c8e-ecf586320c35',N'b7f775db-6171-52e1-a3ed-d03bea14aa4b',0,3,19,N'<p>Entertainment coordinator</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là E </p><p>- Câu “most of the work is done after office hours” → làm việc ngoài giờ hành chính → tương đương với evening work</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ after office hours (phrase): sau giờ hành chính </p><p>+ evening work (n): làm việc buổi tối</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,11,NULL,0,1878),
(N'6e801712-0bb8-50f9-bd1d-6507f289e94f',N'b7f775db-6171-52e1-a3ed-d03bea14aa4b',0,3,19,N'<p>Advertising and promotion co-ordinator</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là B </p><p>- “a couple of people doing it” → cần nhiều hơn 1 người → khớp với đáp án B</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ a couple of people (phrase): vài người </p><p>+ share the load (phrase): chia sẻ công việc</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,12,NULL,0,1878),
(N'56df4472-153c-569a-b4db-20d39deb003b',N'b7f775db-6171-52e1-a3ed-d03bea14aa4b',0,3,19,N'<p>Technical coordinator</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là F </p><p>- “Having a car is essential” → cần phương tiện cá nhân → tương đương “need your own transport”</p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ essential (adj): cần thiết </p><p>+ car (n): xe ô tô</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,13,NULL,0,1878),
