(N'3ab3255a-5a73-5494-bc58-15529e3da93c',N'26a65e30-478a-5628-9916-07f62b123ad1',0,3,19,N'<h3>The study of animal learning behavior</h3><table border="1"><tbody><tr><td><p><span>Topic</span></p></td><td><p><span>Aim</span></p></td><td><p><span>Conclusions</span></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>The }{SPACE}{ between two species</p></td><td><p>• To see how species }{SPACE}{ in a desert</p> <p>• Sample: Lizards and mice</p></td><td><p>• They both feed on }{SPACE}{ </p> <p>• They }{SPACE}{ with each other for food sometimes</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>The }{SPACE}{ between two species</p></td><td><p>• To see how animals obtain extra }{SPACE}{ </p> <p>• Sample: Kangaroos and locusts</p></td><td><p>• Kangaroo''s }{SPACE}{ has increased</p> <p>• The }{SPACE}{ of locusts is enlarged</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>The cooperation
between two species</p></td><td><p>• To see if some plants provide }{SPACE}{ for ants</p> <p>• Sample: Fire ants and some plants</p></td><td><p>• Particular plants may be treated as</p>  }{SPACE}{ by some ants</p></td></tr></tbody></table>',N'<p>Question: Hỏi về chủ đề đầu tiên giữa hai loài → cần 1 danh từ chỉ mối quan hệ. Answer: Từ khóa là interaction. Key vocab: interaction = sự tương tác.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,31,NULL,0,1678),
(N'30c4630b-92cd-5dd4-852e-cc1837c57edb',N'26a65e30-478a-5628-9916-07f62b123ad1',0,3,19,N'Question number 32',N'<p>Question: Mục tiêu nghiên cứu là gì → động từ chỉ cách loài sống chung. Answer: coexist (cùng tồn tại). Key vocab: co-exist = sống chung, tồn tại cùng.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,32,NULL,0,1678),
(N'ee2241ad-6e6d-513b-b1fc-06e2941631af',N'26a65e30-478a-5628-9916-07f62b123ad1',0,3,19,N'Question number 33',N'<p>Question: Cả hai loài ăn gì? Answer: Đều ăn insects. Key vocab: food source = insects.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,33,NULL,0,1678),
(N'5716f3ef-6d7e-5a49-b118-7500f53d5bd0',N'26a65e30-478a-5628-9916-07f62b123ad1',0,3,19,N'Question number 34',N'<p>Question: Họ làm gì với nhau vì thức ăn? Answer: Họ cạnh tranh (compete). Key vocab: compete = tranh giành.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,34,NULL,0,1678),
(N'be9514fe-b9c6-528b-9e15-541581a36add',N'26a65e30-478a-5628-9916-07f62b123ad1',0,3,19,N'Question number 35',N'<p>Question: Chủ đề thứ hai là gì → so sánh. Answer: comparison. Key vocab: comparison = sự so sánh</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,35,NULL,0,1678),
(N'5fb6010a-6e6a-511d-a3b8-234b075cea25',N'26a65e30-478a-5628-9916-07f62b123ad1',0,3,19,N'Question number 36',N'<p>Question: Mục tiêu: tìm thêm gì trong môi trường khắc nghiệt? Answer: resources. Key vocab: resources = nguồn tài nguyên.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,36,NULL,0,1678),
(N'6754cf7c-9e12-576f-9ea2-42c23456057d',N'26a65e30-478a-5628-9916-07f62b123ad1',0,3,19,N'Question number 37',N'<p>Question: Cái gì của kangaroo đã tăng? Answer: population. Key vocab: population = số lượng cá thể.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,37,NULL,0,1678),
(N'36829867-fa08-572a-a7a7-d178b7344e3e',N'26a65e30-478a-5628-9916-07f62b123ad1',0,3,19,N'Question number 38',N'<p>Question: Đặc điểm nào của châu chấu tăng? Answer: size. Key vocab: size = kích thước.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,38,NULL,0,1678),
(N'7abcef61-d14f-5b4b-ad84-8f049b3985c1',N'26a65e30-478a-5628-9916-07f62b123ad1',0,3,19,N'Question number 39',N'<p>Question: Cây cung cấp gì cho kiến? Answer: protection.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,39,NULL,0,1678),
(N'fc13744f-eaa2-5878-830e-10f0dcaa6182',N'26a65e30-478a-5628-9916-07f62b123ad1',0,3,19,N'Question number 40',N'<p>Question: Một số loài kiến coi cây là gì? Answer: shelter. Key vocab: shelter = nơi ở.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,40,NULL,0,1678),
(N'17964a92-ef3f-532c-a00e-8933bae1af3b',NULL,0,0,11,NULL,NULL,NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-4/iL.VOL4.1.S1676.mp3',N'Vol 4 LISTENING FULL TEST 1',0,7,1,NULL,1,1676),
(N'b5eab2c9-e52e-5b12-a8b8-288826265b4b',N'17964a92-ef3f-532c-a00e-8933bae1af3b',0,1,13,(CAST(N'<h2>[VOL 4] Sailing Courses</h2><p>(1-6) Oh, good morning. I''m calling on behalf of my 13-year-old son, Jacob. He''s interested in learning to sail. Great!
Well, we have what we call a Taster day on the 22nd of June. I''m not sure he can make it, but we''ll see. Jacob''s really interested, though, so can you tell me about the courses?
OK. We have two types of courses for children under 16 – two days and five days.
Could you explain the difference?
Well, the two day one just covers basic techniques in sailing. And on this course, the kids always sail with the instructor they''ve been allocated.
Well, that''s good to know.
Yeah, and the cost is £65.
Oh, I thought it was more than that. I heard it was £125.
That''s for the five day course.
OK. I presume that course goes into much more detail?
Yes. And from the third day, the kids are given the choice to sail on their own if they want. We use the same types of boat, but we help them learn more techniques, in particular how to manage the boat in a variety of types of weather.
Hmm, I think Jacob would enjoy that course. Do you give them a certificate if they complete the course?
Absolutely! We give them out on the final day, which a lot of the kids really like.
Great! Could you tell me a bit more about what the children have to bring, and so forth?
Well, the most important thing is the clothing. It goes without saying that whatever the time of year they should have plenty of warm clothes, as it can be quite cool out on the water.
What about footwear? Do they have to wear anything special?
The only rule is that they''ve got to have shoes of some kind. They mustn''t have bare feet.
OK. And we suggest the kids pack an extra pair of trousers, you know, waterproof ones. They don''t have to wear them unless it starts to rain.
Fine.
So basically, it''s just using your common sense.
Yes.
Oh, and one other thing we do say is that the children mustn''t wear jeans because they get extremely heavy when they''re wet.
Oh, OK.
(7-10) One thing I forgot to ask is whether it''s possible to get a meal anywhere.

I''m afraid not, but we do have a shop called the Marina Stores where he can get a snack.

Okay, and before I forget, when I drop Jacob off, where can I park?

Good question. There are spaces near the entrance, but you have to pay for them. But there''s no charge for the car park just by the bridge. Do you know it?

Oh yes, I know where you mean.

Now we do need you to fill in a registration form. You should send that in a couple of week' AS nvarchar(max))+N's before the course starts. The form is on the website, but we ask you to print it off and add your signature.
Yes, of course! What sort of information do you need?
About your child''s swimming ability, any special requirements and so on.
Will you need to know who his doctor is?
Yes
We''ve just recently changed surgeries, so I''ll make a note to get that.
And one more thing. There''s a separate form on the website, which is optional, that asks whether you''re willing for photographs to be taken during the course.
Yes, of course. No problem.
Great! So I''ll send you…

