(N'bc2d0ee1-1d1b-5d06-9a83-056d8e3ef885',N'ed404198-880d-541d-a2fc-93e915a4b45f',0,1,13,(CAST(N'<h2>North Star Camping Equipment </h2><p><span>Now listen carefully and answer questions one to five. </span> </p><p>Hello, North Star Camping Equipment. This is Emma. Oh, hello.  I''ve been looking through your online catalogue. The problem is, um, I haven''t got time to come into the store this week. Is there any chance you can put some things aside for me? Sure.  Let me just get an order form. Okay. So, what''s your surname, please? Okay, Mr Greenaway. I''ll give you an order reference to write down. It''s a mixture of numbers and letters. The reference is 5174XCM.  Right. Got that. So, what were you looking for? Well, we''re going on a camping holiday. </p><p>Two adults, two children. So, the first thing would be a tent. We need something family size and I''d like to have a door at the front and one at the back.  Okay. And anything else? We all need sleeping bags as well.  So, what design do you need? Are you going to the mountains? Will there be snow? Oh, no. We''re going to the beach. It''ll be warm weather.  Okay. So, the design you need is what we call our summer sleeping bag. I''ll put four aside for you.  Then we''ll also need something to sleep on. Some camp beds, I guess. Camp beds, yeah. Or these days a lot of people are using, you know, air mattresses that you blow up.  That sounds good. Easier to pack away. And more comfortable. But how do we blow them up? You''ll need a pump. I''ll put one in for you. Okay.  </p><p>Now, what other things are you looking for? Well, thinking about the cooking equipment, we need a stove.  There are all sorts of camping stoves. It depends what fuel you want it to run on. There''s kerosene, charcoal. Oh, that sounds too messy. I think we want the fuel to be gas, if possible.  No problem. They''re a bit more expensive than the other options. That''s okay.  Then do you need any pots, a frying pan, anything like that? No, we''ll bring those from home. What we need to think about is water. We''ll need a large bottle for that.  All right. And how about knives and forks? No, we''ll be okay for those. But we''ll need something to eat off, you know, something unbreakable. Metal, maybe. Yeah, that''s best. So, plates, then. A set of four in metal. Shall I add that to your order? Yes, please. They''ll last a lifetime.  </p><p><span>Before you hear the rest of the conversation, you have some time to look at questions six to ten. Now listen and answer questions six to ten.  </span></p><p>Now, I''m just thinking what else we might need. We''ve got ' AS nvarchar(max))+N'raincoats, but we really need a couple of new torches. I''d rather not have plastic. The boys will just break them. We''ve got some good rubber ones. They''ll be perfect. I''ll organise two of those.  Then, I don''t know, do you want some games for your children to play? That''s not a bad idea. Even just a football or something? We''ve already got a ball. Let’s think. What we really need is something that young kids can use. Do you have a baseball set? They''d love that. Sure, I''ll put one in for you. Any other games? No, I think that''ll be enough. There''s lots of things to do up there.  </p><p>Where are you going, by the way? Up to the Bay of Islands. Oh, that''s a lovely region.  In fact, that reminds me, we need an up-to-date map of the area. Do you sell those? Mine is very old. No problem.  Great. Now, I''ve just thought, is there any chance you can deliver all these things? Absolutely. What''s the address? It''s 56 Taupo Street. I''ll spell that for you. T-A-U-P-O. That''s in Bayswater, isn''t it? Yes, that''s right.  And what would the charge be on that? The standard charge is $50. But hang on, your order will be over $500, so you get a discounted delivery charge of only $25.50. Great. Now, my wife and I will still be at work this week, so we won''t be at…  </p><p><span>That is the end of Part 1. You now have one minute to check your answers to Part 1. </span></p>'),(CAST(N'<p><span>Now listen carefully and answer questions one to five. </span> </p><p>Hello, North Star Camping Equipment. This is Emma. Oh, hello.  I''ve been looking through your online catalogue. The problem is, um, I haven''t got time to come into the store this week. Is there any chance you can put some things aside for me? Sure.  Let me just get an order form. Okay. So, what''s your surname, please? Okay, Mr Greenaway. I''ll give you an order reference to write down. It''s a mixture of numbers and letters. The reference is 5174XCM.  Right. Got that. So, what were you looking for? Well, we''re going on a camping holiday. </p><p>Two adults, two children. So, the first thing would be a tent. We need something family size and I''d like to have a door at the front and one at the back.  Okay. And anything else? We all need sleeping bags as well.  So, what design do you need? Are you going to the mountains? Will there be snow? Oh, no. We''re going to the beach. It''ll be warm weather.  Okay. So, the design you need is what we call our summer sleeping bag. I''ll put four aside for you.  Then we''ll also need something to sleep on. Some camp beds, I guess. Camp beds, yeah. Or these days a lot of people are using, you know, air mattresses that you blow up.  That sounds good. Easier to pack away. And more comfortable. But how do we blow them up? You''ll need a pump. I''ll put one in for you. Okay.  </p><p>Now, what other things are you looking for? Well, thinking about the cooking equipment, we need a stove.  There are all sorts of camping stoves. It depends what fuel you want it to run on. There''s kerosene, charcoal. Oh, that sounds too messy. I think we want the fuel to be gas, if possible.  No problem. They''re a bit more expensive than the other options. That''s okay.  Then do you need any pots, a frying pan, anything like that? No, we''ll bring those from home. What we need to think about is water. We''ll need a large bottle for that.  All right. And how about knives and forks? No, we''ll be okay for those. But we''ll need something to eat off, you know, something unbreakable. Metal, maybe. Yeah, that''s best. So, plates, then. A set of four in metal. Shall I add that to your order? Yes, please. They''ll last a lifetime.  </p><p><span>Before you hear the rest of the conversation, you have some time to look at questions six to ten. Now listen and answer questions six to ten.  </span></p><p>Now, I''m just thinking what else we might need. We''ve got raincoats, but we really need a couple' AS nvarchar(max))+N' of new torches. I''d rather not have plastic. The boys will just break them. We''ve got some good rubber ones. They''ll be perfect. I''ll organise two of those.  Then, I don''t know, do you want some games for your children to play? That''s not a bad idea. Even just a football or something? We''ve already got a ball. Let’s think. What we really need is something that young kids can use. Do you have a baseball set? They''d love that. Sure, I''ll put one in for you. Any other games? No, I think that''ll be enough. There''s lots of things to do up there.  </p><p>Where are you going, by the way? Up to the Bay of Islands. Oh, that''s a lovely region.  In fact, that reminds me, we need an up-to-date map of the area. Do you sell those? Mine is very old. No problem.  Great. Now, I''ve just thought, is there any chance you can deliver all these things? Absolutely. What''s the address? It''s 56 Taupo Street. I''ll spell that for you. T-A-U-P-O. That''s in Bayswater, isn''t it? Yes, that''s right.  And what would the charge be on that? The standard charge is $50. But hang on, your order will be over $500, so you get a discounted delivery charge of only $25.50. Great. Now, my wife and I will still be at work this week, so we won''t be at…  </p><p><span>That is the end of Part 1. You now have one minute to check your answers to Part 1. </span></p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-3/iL.VOL3.4.S1670.PART1.mp3',NULL,1,0,1,NULL,0,1670),
(N'2ae5d6e1-0953-53bb-863d-2fdf03079502',N'bc2d0ee1-1d1b-5d06-9a83-056d8e3ef885',0,2,18,N'<p>Complete the form below. </p><p>Write <span>ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER</span> for each answer. </p>',N'',N'',N'',N'North Star Camping Equipment',11,0,1,NULL,0,1670),
(N'526bd437-e993-54e5-968a-a053b0e68b6d',N'2ae5d6e1-0953-53bb-863d-2fdf03079502',0,3,19,N'<h3>North Star Camping Equipment</h3><table border="1"><tbody><tr><td><p><span>Customer surname:</span></p></td><td><p>Greenaway</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><span>Order reference:</span></p></td><td> }{SPACE}{ </td></tr><tr><td><p><span>Ordered items:</span></p></td><td><p><span>Tent</span></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><ul><li><p>family size</p></li></ul></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><ul><li><p>two doors</p></li></ul></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p><span>Sleeping bags</span></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><ul><li><p>the</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ design</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p><span>Beds</span></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><ul><li><p>four mattresses</p></li></ul></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><ul><li><p>a</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p><span>Cooking</span></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><ul><li><p>a gas stove</p></li></ul></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><ul><li><p>a suitable water</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><ul><li><p>a set of metal</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p><span>Other items</span></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><ul><li><p>two torches made of</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><ul><li><p>a</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ set suitable for children</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><ul><li><p>a recent</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><span>Delivery address:</span></p></td><td><p>56, }{SPACE}{ Street Bayswater </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Delivery charge:</p></td><td><p>$ }{SPACE}{ </p></td></tr></tbody></table>',N'<p>→ Đây là Order reference number – mã đơn hàng được nhân viên đọc chậm và đánh vần rõ ràng. Đề bài ghi “a mixture of numbers and letters”, nên cần chép đúng toàn bộ chuỗi, không bỏ chữ cái “XCM”. Nếu bỏ sót phần chữ, đáp án sai.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,1,NULL,0,1670),
(N'61c7ebf8-15fe-5bc8-ba38-7cf8f4388738',N'2ae5d6e1-0953-53bb-863d-2fdf03079502',0,3,19,N'Question number 2',N'<p>→ Câu hỏi: “the 2 ______ design.” Người nói hỏi “Will there be snow?” – “Oh, no, we’re going to the beach.” → Gợi ý khí hậu nóng. Do đó loại túi ngủ phù hợp là “summer design”. Nhiều thí sinh dễ nhầm với “warm” hoặc “beach”, nhưng từ chính xác được nhấn là “summer sleeping bag”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,2,NULL,0,1670),
(N'95832182-4913-5316-a0d4-55404d985350',N'2ae5d6e1-0953-53bb-863d-2fdf03079502',0,3,19,N'Question number 3',N'<p>→ “blow up” = bơm hơi → thiết bị dùng là “pump”. Nghe kỹ vì đây là đoạn hội thoại tự nhiên, dễ bị lướt qua do câu trả lời rất ngắn. Đáp án phải là pump, không phải “air pump” vì giới hạn “ONE WORD ONLY”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,3,NULL,0,1670),
(N'23b3aa4e-469f-5e0f-8ad4-e213a87f0c3e',N'2ae5d6e1-0953-53bb-863d-2fdf03079502',0,3,19,N'Question number 4',N'<p>→ Hỏi về “a suitable water ____”. Khách nói họ cần “a large bottle for water”, nên từ cần điền là “bottle”. Nhiều người có thể nghe nhầm “container” hoặc “tank”, nhưng trong transcript chỉ nhắc đến “bottle”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,4,NULL,0,1670),
(N'388fe058-0138-5edc-b348-d599ed176566',N'2ae5d6e1-0953-53bb-863d-2fdf03079502',0,3,19,N'Question number 5',N'<p>→ “a set of metal ____” → chính là “plates”. Khách muốn đồ không dễ vỡ, và “plates” là lựa chọn hợp lý vì dùng để ăn, khác với “pots” hoặc “pans”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,5,NULL,0,1670),
(N'c9de710a-75af-5f71-85a6-3e91f3a1a0c0',N'2ae5d6e1-0953-53bb-863d-2fdf03079502',0,3,19,N'Question number 6',N'<p>→ “two torches made of ____.” Khách không muốn loại “plastic” vì “the boys will just break them.” → Gợi ý rằng cần chất liệu bền hơn, và người bán gợi ý “rubber ones”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,6,NULL,0,1670),
(N'64323c4c-b558-5678-93b5-c27533fc41bf',N'2ae5d6e1-0953-53bb-863d-2fdf03079502',0,3,19,N'Question number 7',N'<p>→ “a ____ set suitable for children.” Khách muốn trò chơi cho trẻ nhỏ, gợi ý “football or something”, rồi quyết định chọn “baseball set”. Cần ghi đúng một từ, không viết “baseball set” vì form chỉ yêu cầu một từ.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,7,NULL,0,1670),
(N'dc02bdce-b3d9-5f7a-be4f-3e1d171106a8',N'2ae5d6e1-0953-53bb-863d-2fdf03079502',0,3,19,N'Question number 8',N'<p>→ “a recent ____.” “Up-to-date” = “recent”, nên “recent map” là diễn đạt tương đương. Dễ bị đánh lừa nếu nghe “guidebook” hoặc “brochure”, nhưng đáp án chính xác là “map”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,8,NULL,0,1670),
(N'fc76f7ad-9e82-5bb7-a3c8-3ce8bdc0accf',N'2ae5d6e1-0953-53bb-863d-2fdf03079502',0,3,19,N'Question number 9',N'<p>→ Địa chỉ giao hàng: “56, 9 ______ Street.” Người nói đánh vần rõ “T-A-U-P-O”, nên chỉ cần ghi “Taupo”. Lưu ý: viết sai chính tả (như “Toppo”) bị tính sai.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,9,NULL,0,1670),
(N'34147167-4796-5ec3-be66-cddbbe3713d4',N'2ae5d6e1-0953-53bb-863d-2fdf03079502',0,3,19,N'Question number 10',N'<p>→ “Delivery charge: 10 $ ______.” Từ “only” nhấn mạnh mức giảm giá từ $50 xuống $25.50. Phải ghi 25.50, không viết “$25.50” vì đề đã có ký hiệu $.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,10,NULL,0,1670),
(N'5fc43237-3106-5067-a253-b4aee4a20efa',N'ed404198-880d-541d-a2fc-93e915a4b45f',0,1,14,(CAST(N'<h2>The Frankston Connect Club</h2><p><span>Now listen carefully and answer questions 11 to 15. </span> </p><p>Hello, I''ve been asked to talk to you today about Connect. Connect is a club for people who have retired from full-time work. The first Connect club began back in 1960 in Brisbane, Australia.  Today I''ll concentrate on Frankston Connect, the club where I''m a member. It services the communities around the suburb of Frankston here in Melbourne.  Okay, so what are our club aims? We''re not a fitness club or anything like that. Some Connect branches do charity work, but that''s not for us. Our objective is to provide social contact with others who have similar interests and ideas.  Now, meetings. We have monthly club meetings where the usual club business is discussed. For example, at the last meeting we talked about how much money was spent that month. </p><p>Also at that meeting, someone had just returned from an overseas trip and he spoke about that. Then we looked at entries for our photography competition. The winner will be announced soon.  Up until now, we''ve used the school hall for our meetings, but that''s about to be renovated, so we needed to find an alternative. It''s been a great venue because of its size and it''s so easy to get to, but I''m sure historical Frankston Hall will suit us just fine.  Our social committee plans and organises club trips from time to time, and they''re always looking for suggestions from members for new places to go to. If you join, you should check the activities list that''s posted on our website each month and attend anything that interests you. Come and make friends. We''re just one big happy family.  So how do you join and what about membership fees? It''s simple. Just fill in the form and give it to me before you leave this morning. There are a few payment options. Some members prefer to make an annual payment, which is a slightly cheaper option, or you can pay monthly.  Why don''t you get a group together? It makes the activities more fun.  </p><p><span>Before you hear the rest of the talk, you have some time to look at questions 16 to 20. Now listen and answer questions 16 to 20.  </span></p><p>If you still haven''t decided whether to join or not, let me try to tempt you with some of our upcoming events.  Our Moonlight Wildlife Walk was previously available to members'' immediate families as well, but this wonderful activity has become so popular that it''s now limited to just members. Although it''s free, we do ask ' AS nvarchar(max))+N'our members to pay something to the Wildlife Fund so it can continue its good work. Everyone makes their way to the wildlife park independently, arriving at dusk, where a guide walks with the group and tells us about all the animals we encounter.  OK, theatre in the park. We see a different play every month. The park''s on the train line and easy to access, so we don''t organise buses or anything. Come along and recline on a blanket on the grass, although some members prefer to take along their own seat. No need to make a reservation, there''s plenty of space. </p><p>After the play, we all walk to a local cafe where you can purchase coffee and cake. It''s a really fun night out.  Birdwatching is a regular activity, and it''s organised by the keen birdwatchers in the club. This activity consists mainly of early morning and late afternoon walking trips to spot the birds when they''re most active. Birdwatching attracts only small numbers, so one of our ardent birdwatchers drives members in the club van to the best spots.  The City Botanical Gardens Walk is a popular activity that occurs a couple of times a year. </p><p>Members make their own way there and usually meet up outside the gates at 8.45am, setting off for the hours walk with the volunteer guide by 9am. Many members bring a friend or relative, and this is fine.  Now, the State Library. Our visits here in the past have always been great, because there''s something for everyone. You can easily spend a whole day in there. There''s a lovely restaurant, and you can take food into the small cinema there, where we''ll be watching a short film about the history of our local area.  So, what else can I tell you?  </p><p><span>That is the end of Part 2. You now have 30 seconds to check your answers to Part 2. </span></p>'),(CAST(N'<p><span>Now listen carefully and answer questions 11 to 15. </span> </p><p>Hello, I''ve been asked to talk to you today about Connect. Connect is a club for people who have retired from full-time work. The first Connect club began back in 1960 in Brisbane, Australia.  Today I''ll concentrate on Frankston Connect, the club where I''m a member. It services the communities around the suburb of Frankston here in Melbourne.  Okay, so what are our club aims? We''re not a fitness club or anything like that. Some Connect branches do charity work, but that''s not for us. Our objective is to provide social contact with others who have similar interests and ideas.  Now, meetings. We have monthly club meetings where the usual club business is discussed. For example, at the last meeting we talked about how much money was spent that month. </p><p>Also at that meeting, someone had just returned from an overseas trip and he spoke about that. Then we looked at entries for our photography competition. The winner will be announced soon.  Up until now, we''ve used the school hall for our meetings, but that''s about to be renovated, so we needed to find an alternative. It''s been a great venue because of its size and it''s so easy to get to, but I''m sure historical Frankston Hall will suit us just fine.  Our social committee plans and organises club trips from time to time, and they''re always looking for suggestions from members for new places to go to. If you join, you should check the activities list that''s posted on our website each month and attend anything that interests you. Come and make friends. We''re just one big happy family.  So how do you join and what about membership fees? It''s simple. Just fill in the form and give it to me before you leave this morning. There are a few payment options. Some members prefer to make an annual payment, which is a slightly cheaper option, or you can pay monthly.  Why don''t you get a group together? It makes the activities more fun.  </p><p><span>Before you hear the rest of the talk, you have some time to look at questions 16 to 20. Now listen and answer questions 16 to 20.  </span></p><p>If you still haven''t decided whether to join or not, let me try to tempt you with some of our upcoming events.  Our Moonlight Wildlife Walk was previously available to members'' immediate families as well, but this wonderful activity has become so popular that it''s now limited to just members. Although it''s free, we do ask our members to pay something to the' AS nvarchar(max))+N' Wildlife Fund so it can continue its good work. Everyone makes their way to the wildlife park independently, arriving at dusk, where a guide walks with the group and tells us about all the animals we encounter.  OK, theatre in the park. We see a different play every month. The park''s on the train line and easy to access, so we don''t organise buses or anything. Come along and recline on a blanket on the grass, although some members prefer to take along their own seat. No need to make a reservation, there''s plenty of space. </p><p>After the play, we all walk to a local cafe where you can purchase coffee and cake. It''s a really fun night out.  Birdwatching is a regular activity, and it''s organised by the keen birdwatchers in the club. This activity consists mainly of early morning and late afternoon walking trips to spot the birds when they''re most active. Birdwatching attracts only small numbers, so one of our ardent birdwatchers drives members in the club van to the best spots.  The City Botanical Gardens Walk is a popular activity that occurs a couple of times a year. </p><p>Members make their own way there and usually meet up outside the gates at 8.45am, setting off for the hours walk with the volunteer guide by 9am. Many members bring a friend or relative, and this is fine.  Now, the State Library. Our visits here in the past have always been great, because there''s something for everyone. You can easily spend a whole day in there. There''s a lovely restaurant, and you can take food into the small cinema there, where we''ll be watching a short film about the history of our local area.  So, what else can I tell you?  </p><p><span>That is the end of Part 2. You now have 30 seconds to check your answers to Part 2. </span></p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-3/iL.VOL3.4.S1670.PART2.mp3',NULL,1,0,2,NULL,0,1670),
(N'8e0902d2-8d15-5bd1-ae06-8e981cff5f70',N'5fc43237-3106-5067-a253-b4aee4a20efa',0,2,18,N'<p>Choose the correct letter, <span><span>A, B </span>or<span> C.</span></span></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'The Frankston Connect Club',1,0,1,NULL,0,1670),
(N'a21b795f-5401-5b10-863c-aa6a10168c10',N'8e0902d2-8d15-5bd1-ae06-8e981cff5f70',0,3,19,N'<p>The main aim of Frankston Connect is to</p>',N'<p>Câu hỏi: The main aim of Frankston Connect is to... </p><p>→ Người nói loại trừ fitness club và charity work, nhấn mạnh mục tiêu là social contact – kết nối người cùng chí hướng. </p><p>⇒ A. Help like-minded people to meet là chính xác.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,11,NULL,0,1670),
(N'a2caf8d9-70d9-5e10-bd32-57ace6af37fe',N'8e0902d2-8d15-5bd1-ae06-8e981cff5f70',0,3,19,N'<p>What happened at last month’s meeting?</p>',N'<p>Câu hỏi: What happened at last month’s meeting? </p><p>→ Có ba nội dung: bàn về tài chính, nghe thành viên kể về chuyến đi, và xem ảnh dự thi. Trong đó, phần “finances” được nhắc đầu tiên </p><p>→ đúng trọng tâm câu hỏi. </p><p>⇒ A. The club finances were discussed.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,12,NULL,0,1670),
(N'8039c855-b5c6-57f5-a32b-a1bc2f1f9d89',N'8e0902d2-8d15-5bd1-ae06-8e981cff5f70',0,3,19,N'<p>The venue for the monthly meetings will change because the school hall is</p>',N'<p>Hỏi lý do thay đổi địa điểm họp. </p><p>→ Không phải “not central” hay “too small”, mà là “under renovation”. </p><p>⇒ C. no longer available.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,13,NULL,0,1670),
(N'7781f5a3-a8c2-5126-b3ac-49979f7a444e',N'8e0902d2-8d15-5bd1-ae06-8e981cff5f70',0,3,19,N'<p>The Social Committee would like members to</p>',N'<p>Hỏi: The Social Committee would like members to... </p><p>→ Câu nói cho thấy họ muốn mọi người tham gia lên kế hoạch và đề xuất hoạt động. </p><p>⇒ A. Help organise activities.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,14,NULL,0,1670),
(N'457bd703-d27b-5ea9-8b0c-ce176a86f10e',N'8e0902d2-8d15-5bd1-ae06-8e981cff5f70',0,3,19,N'<p>How can you save money on members’ fees?</p>',N'<p>Hỏi: How can you save money on members’ fees? </p><p>→ Câu “annual payment = cheaper” </p><p>→ trả trước 1 năm tiết kiệm hơn. </p><p>⇒ B. Pay for one year.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,15,NULL,0,1670),
(N'e897db50-b2dc-5522-8c59-20fe6aa56b71',N'5fc43237-3106-5067-a253-b4aee4a20efa',0,2,18,N'<p>What information does the speaker give about each of the following future club events? </p><p>Choose <span>FIVE</span> answers from the box and write the correct letter, <span>A–H</span>, next to questions 16–20. </p>',N'',N'',N'',N'Answer choices',15,0,2,NULL,0,1670),
(N'62f412ef-eb6d-597a-8db3-eafd1cd06b3c',N'e897db50-b2dc-5522-8c59-20fe6aa56b71',0,3,19,N'<p>Moonlight Wildlife Walk</p>',N'<p>Hỏi: What info about Moonlight Wildlife Walk?</p><p>→ Họ kêu gọi đóng góp tài chính cho quỹ.</p><p>⇒ E. Donation of money requested.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,16,NULL,0,1670),
(N'24f79514-08fd-5f0c-a769-656694e9ed56',N'e897db50-b2dc-5522-8c59-20fe6aa56b71',0,3,19,N'<p>Theatre in the Park</p>',N'<p>Transport supplied by the club → thông tin phủ định: not organised. </p><p>→ Vậy không chọn G, chọn gì khác? Chưa có. Đọc tiếp: “...some members prefer to take along their own seat.” </p><p>→ đúng “chairs can be brought”. </p><p>⇒ F. Chairs can be brought.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,17,NULL,0,1670),
(N'164e1dfc-0a3c-50cc-a1ab-2c6eb79e2955',N'e897db50-b2dc-5522-8c59-20fe6aa56b71',0,3,19,N'<p>Bird-watching</p>',N'<p>Câu này mô tả việc có xe câu lạc bộ chở thành viên đi xem chim. </p><p>⇒ H. Transport supplied by the club.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,18,NULL,0,1670),
(N'4bcfcb3f-156d-57be-8aba-0dc898aa0608',N'e897db50-b2dc-5522-8c59-20fe6aa56b71',0,3,19,N'<p>Botanical Gardens Walk</p>',N'<p>Câu hỏi về Botanical Gardens Walk.</p><p>→ Nhấn mạnh việc non-members are welcome.</p><p>⇒ D. Non-members are welcome.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,19,NULL,0,1670),
(N'025594c5-8573-5d43-bf50-3c6f30cecfd7',N'e897db50-b2dc-5522-8c59-20fe6aa56b71',0,3,19,N'<p>State Library</p>',N'<p>Có phim tài liệu </p><p>→ “documentary shown”. </p><p>⇒ F. Documentary shown.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,20,NULL,0,1670),
(N'8366609b-dc4c-5ec2-8806-9d16a5f27406',N'ed404198-880d-541d-a2fc-93e915a4b45f',0,1,15,(CAST(N'<h2>Product development presentation: mosquito net</h2><p><span>Now listen carefully and answer questions 21 to 25. </span></p><p>
Hello Edward. Sit down. Thanks. I need some advice on my presentation about product development. Right. Have you decided what to focus on? Yes. The product I''ve chosen is a particular type of mosquito net. Any reason for choosing that? I spent last summer travelling round Africa with a friend. He''s studying medicine, so when we were in a region where mosquitoes cause malaria, we visited a medical centre. I chatted to an administrator while my friend talked to one of the doctors. And I found out they''ve had far fewer cases of malaria since these mosquito nets became available locally. That made me interested in them. OK. </p><p>
Mosquito nets have quite a long history, don''t they? I believe they''ve been used in Japan for centuries. That''s right. Though apparently Queen Cleopatra slept under one in ancient Egypt. That was probably where they were invented. And much later, nets were used in China, so perhaps they were invented there independently. Originally, they were made of silk, but later cotton was used, and nowadays they''re mainly synthetic. It wasn''t until the middle of the twentieth century that they developed nets treated with insecticides for use by the military, and that was a major step forward. They used an insecticide called DDT, but it was later found that this could be harmful to people as well as mosquitoes. Is that still a problem with modern nets? Oh no. The chemicals used nowadays are safe, even if people sleep under them every night. And the nets work and they''re odour-free. But they have to be treated fairly often with the chemical, which the owners need to do themselves. Presumably distribution of the chemical can be a problem in remote areas? I mean, people may not be able to get hold of it easily. That''s right. Hmm. </p><p>
OK, tell me about this net you''re going to talk about. Well, the brand name is Olliset, and the product was invented by a Japanese company. These nets are an improvement on the alternatives because the insecticide is contained inside the fibre and released gradually. It''s not coated on the outside as with ordinary nets. So the chemicals don''t have to be replaced? Right. And Olliset nets are also tougher and don''t tear as easily. They give protection for at least five years, compared with a year or two for other nets. Well, it sounds interesting. But for your seminar presentation, will y' AS nvarchar(max))+N'ou provide the bigger picture as well? Yes. It''ll be a case study of product development. </p><p>
