(N'ed497141-9cd2-50b3-b812-6f4e5dfd63f1',N'4c6e1a22-e4e3-544a-a2f1-a58502557ac6',0,3,19,N'<p>Online forum</p>',N'<p>Đáp án là A. Diễn đàn trực tuyến giúp sinh viên nhận phản hồi và hỗ trợ từ giảng viên. Key words: get support, faculty members

</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,28,NULL,0,1663),
(N'743ea05b-545b-5ef2-9ad9-1af3f1113453',N'4c6e1a22-e4e3-544a-a2f1-a58502557ac6',0,3,19,N'<p>placement tests</p>',N'<p>Đáp án là B. Người nói cho rằng việc đọc thêm tài liệu nền là cần thiết, đặc biệt sau kết quả không tốt ở bài kiểm tra. Key words: background reading, necessary

</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,29,NULL,0,1663),
(N'041de339-54a0-5b88-a6d4-8139bdb03b13',N'4c6e1a22-e4e3-544a-a2f1-a58502557ac6',0,3,19,N'<p>freshmen</p>',N'<p>Đáp án là H. Lời khuyên dành cho sinh viên năm nhất là không nên đặt mục tiêu phi thực tế để tránh căng thẳng quá mức. Key words: realistic goals, don''t push yourself</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,30,NULL,0,1663),
(N'c8bf88da-3374-5fc2-9b4a-ea8f4efc6732',N'10e149cb-8aec-53e8-91c4-57d8309b752f',0,1,15,(CAST(N'<h2>[VOL 2] Dinner Affects the Environment</h2><p>You now have half a minute to check your answers. You will hear a lecture about how carbon dioxide is produced from food and what are the effects of the emission problem. </p><p><span>First, you have some time to look at questions 31 to 40. Now listen carefully and answer questions 31 to 40. </span></p><p>Good afternoon, thanks for coming to today''s lecture. In the last few decades, the environmental impact of food production and consumption has become one of the greatest concerns.  When we look at what we eat and how we produce the food, we can find extensive evidence for how we damage our environment. Greenhouse gas emissions may come from livestock such as cows, agricultural soils and rice production. </p><p>According to statistics, the carbon dioxide emissions from the production of the food people consume every day are almost the same as the emissions we make when we are driving.  Let''s look at some more specific examples. The cultivation and processing of 100 grams of coffee beans are responsible for 140 grams of carbon dioxide. Now, some international organisations are training farmers in many countries to use sustainable agricultural methods as a way of reducing their carbon dioxide emissions.  </p><p>All agricultural practices have been found to have a variety of effects on the environment. Some of the environmental effects are associated with meat production. The popular red meat requires 28 times more land to produce than chicken, 11 times more water and results in 5 times more climate warming emissions.  </p><p>According to another research, cooking process also causes greenhouse gas emissions. Scientists now are working on how to best minimise its impact. Another problem that we cannot neglect is the packaging of food products, as packaging takes a lot of energy, water and other natural resources to produce.  So, a lot of natural resources are wasted when we throw the packaging materials away. </p><p>Furthermore, packaging waste produces a big amount of greenhouse gas. To make things even worse, the food we eat often comes from places far away.  Therefore, the transportation of our food across long distances contributes to air and water pollution. In recent decades, with the growing number of population, more food is in demand. So, more land has been used to produce food.  Hundreds and even thousands of forests have been cut down. It had a devastating effect on the climate because forests can a' AS nvarchar(max))+N'bsorb greenhouse gases. People in different parts of the world apply various kinds of farming practices.  </p><p>In most countries, cows and other livestock are kept on the farms, while in some countries they are kept in a restricted area on a mountain. But they all contribute to the carbon dioxide emissions. And for animal agriculture, the problem can be more serious because the livestock need food all the time.  In America, cows eat an overwhelming amount of corn and soybeans each year. In order to create a better world for us and our future generations, we should adopt sustainable agriculture. The goal of sustainable agriculture is to meet the world''s growing demand for food at the present without affecting future generations.  </p><p>Every person involved in the food system, growers, food processors, distributors, retailers, consumers and waste managers can play a role in ensuring a sustainable agricultural system. There are many practices commonly used by people working in sustainable agriculture and sustainable food systems. Crop growers may change their food production methods to prevent pollution, although some other areas of agriculture are very hard to change, such as fishing.  </p><p>Consumers and retailers concerned with sustainability can look for foods that are environmentally friendly. However, sustainable agriculture is more than a collection of practices, it is also a process of negotiation, a push and pull between the competing interests of an individual farmer or of people in a community as they work to solve complex problems about how we grow our food. In conclusion, I want to emphasize that we may not be able to go back to the old times and live a simpler lifestyle, but we can take an active role in preventing more environmental problems caused by carbon dioxide emissions.  In the next lecture, I will share some of the studies and effective solutions with you. </p><p><span>That is the end of section 4. You now have half a minute to check your answers. That is the end of the listening test.  </span></p>'),(CAST(N'<p>You now have half a minute to check your answers. You will hear a lecture about how carbon dioxide is produced from food and what are the effects of the emission problem. </p><p><span>First, you have some time to look at questions 31 to 40. Now listen carefully and answer questions 31 to 40. </span></p><p>Good afternoon, thanks for coming to today''s lecture. In the last few decades, the environmental impact of food production and consumption has become one of the greatest concerns.  When we look at what we eat and how we produce the food, we can find extensive evidence for how we damage our environment. Greenhouse gas emissions may come from livestock such as cows, agricultural soils and rice production. </p><p>According to statistics, the carbon dioxide emissions from the production of the food people consume every day are almost the same as the emissions we make when we are driving.  Let''s look at some more specific examples. The cultivation and processing of 100 grams of coffee beans are responsible for 140 grams of carbon dioxide. Now, some international organisations are training farmers in many countries to use sustainable agricultural methods as a way of reducing their carbon dioxide emissions.  </p><p>All agricultural practices have been found to have a variety of effects on the environment. Some of the environmental effects are associated with meat production. The popular red meat requires 28 times more land to produce than chicken, 11 times more water and results in 5 times more climate warming emissions.  </p><p>According to another research, cooking process also causes greenhouse gas emissions. Scientists now are working on how to best minimise its impact. Another problem that we cannot neglect is the packaging of food products, as packaging takes a lot of energy, water and other natural resources to produce.  So, a lot of natural resources are wasted when we throw the packaging materials away. </p><p>Furthermore, packaging waste produces a big amount of greenhouse gas. To make things even worse, the food we eat often comes from places far away.  Therefore, the transportation of our food across long distances contributes to air and water pollution. In recent decades, with the growing number of population, more food is in demand. So, more land has been used to produce food.  Hundreds and even thousands of forests have been cut down. It had a devastating effect on the climate because forests can absorb greenhouse gases. People in different par' AS nvarchar(max))+N'ts of the world apply various kinds of farming practices.  </p><p>In most countries, cows and other livestock are kept on the farms, while in some countries they are kept in a restricted area on a mountain. But they all contribute to the carbon dioxide emissions. And for animal agriculture, the problem can be more serious because the livestock need food all the time.  In America, cows eat an overwhelming amount of corn and soybeans each year. In order to create a better world for us and our future generations, we should adopt sustainable agriculture. The goal of sustainable agriculture is to meet the world''s growing demand for food at the present without affecting future generations.  </p><p>Every person involved in the food system, growers, food processors, distributors, retailers, consumers and waste managers can play a role in ensuring a sustainable agricultural system. There are many practices commonly used by people working in sustainable agriculture and sustainable food systems. Crop growers may change their food production methods to prevent pollution, although some other areas of agriculture are very hard to change, such as fishing.  </p><p>Consumers and retailers concerned with sustainability can look for foods that are environmentally friendly. However, sustainable agriculture is more than a collection of practices, it is also a process of negotiation, a push and pull between the competing interests of an individual farmer or of people in a community as they work to solve complex problems about how we grow our food. In conclusion, I want to emphasize that we may not be able to go back to the old times and live a simpler lifestyle, but we can take an active role in preventing more environmental problems caused by carbon dioxide emissions.  In the next lecture, I will share some of the studies and effective solutions with you. </p><p><span>That is the end of section 4. You now have half a minute to check your answers. That is the end of the listening test.  </span></p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-2/iL.VOL2.10.S1663.PART4.mp3',NULL,1,0,4,NULL,0,1663),
(N'3ebc08f7-06b1-5f5d-b8e8-508c1bacae7e',N'c8bf88da-3374-5fc2-9b4a-ea8f4efc6732',0,2,18,N'<p>Complete the notes below. </p><p>Write <span>ONE WORD ONLY</span> for each answer.</p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',11,0,1,NULL,0,1663),
(N'84413d76-2cd7-5e85-bd5d-3548522aa677',N'3ebc08f7-06b1-5f5d-b8e8-508c1bacae7e',0,3,19,N'<p><span>Food industry</span></p><ul><li><p>The amount of CO2 from producing our daily meals is the same as that from</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p><ul><li><p>The process of making 100g</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ beans can result in 140g CO2.</p><ul><li><p>The</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ production process contributes to climate &amp; warming emissions.</p><ul><li><p>Scientists are working on reducing the impact of</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ process.</p><ul><li><p>Packaging needs</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ as well as water and other resources for production.</p><ul><li><p>Long distance</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ leads to more pollution.</p><ul><li><p>Due to the damage of</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ the total amount of CO2 increases greatly</p><p><span>Agriculture</span></p><ul><li><p>Livestock are either kept on farms or on a</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ in different parts of the world.</p><ul><li><p>In animal agriculture,</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ required constantly</p><ul><li><p>Some agricultural activities like</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ are unlikely to be changed</p>',N'<p> Đáp án là driving </p><p>- Câu hỏi so sánh lượng CO2 từ bữa ăn hằng ngày với lượng CO2 từ một hoạt động khác </p><p>- Script nói trực tiếp “almost the same as the emissions we make when we are driving”, nên chỗ trống phải là “driving” </p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ emissions (n): khí thải </p><p>+ driving (n): việc lái xe</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,31,NULL,0,1663),
(N'c721c93b-da29-5ec3-bfd3-8babb126c515',N'3ebc08f7-06b1-5f5d-b8e8-508c1bacae7e',0,3,19,N'Question number 32',N'<p>Đáp án là coffee </p><p>- Câu hỏi nêu “100g ___ beans” và hỏi loại hạt nào </p><p>- Script khẳng định đúng cụm “100 grams of coffee beans” </p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ cultivation (n): sự canh tác </p><p>+ processing (n): sự chế biến</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,32,NULL,0,1663),
(N'60d87405-e9fd-5778-aaf0-a9bf53a7c483',N'3ebc08f7-06b1-5f5d-b8e8-508c1bacae7e',0,3,19,N'Question number 33',N'<p>Đáp án là meat </p><p>- Chỗ trống đứng trước “production process”, nên cần danh từ chỉ lĩnh vực sản xuất </p><p>- Script nêu rõ “associated with meat production”, trùng chính xác với ý câu hỏi </p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ associated with: liên quan tới </p><p>+ meat (n): thịt</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,33,NULL,0,1663),
(N'10c64a66-5b26-5477-8599-c4c116733dc5',N'3ebc08f7-06b1-5f5d-b8e8-508c1bacae7e',0,3,19,N'Question number 34',N'<p>Đáp án là cooking </p><p>- Câu hỏi hỏi “impact of ___ process” và ngay sau đó script nói về “cooking process” </p><p>- Câu tiếp theo nhấn mạnh scientists đang giảm tác động của “its impact”, quy chiếu về cooking process </p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ minimise (v): giảm thiểu </p><p>+ impact (n): tác động</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,34,NULL,0,1663),
(N'093314bb-9a64-53e4-8204-d1e77814b268',N'3ebc08f7-06b1-5f5d-b8e8-508c1bacae7e',0,3,19,N'Question number 35',N'<p>Đáp án là energy </p><p>- Câu hỏi nói “Packaging needs ___ as well as water…”, nên đáp án phải là thứ đứng trước “water” trong script </p><p>- Script liệt kê rõ “takes a lot of energy, water…” nên điền “energy” </p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ packaging (n): bao bì </p><p>+ neglect (v): bỏ qua/xao nhãng</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,35,NULL,0,1663),
(N'f33b23aa-7430-5c11-af1d-a651d1d347d6',N'3ebc08f7-06b1-5f5d-b8e8-508c1bacae7e',0,3,19,N'Question number 36',N'<p>Đáp án là transportation </p><p>- Câu hỏi nói “Long distance ___ leads to more pollution.” </p><p>- Script nêu nguyên nhân trực tiếp: “the transportation of our food across long distances contributes to… pollution” </p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ transportation (n): vận chuyển </p><p>+ contributes to: góp phần gây ra</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,36,NULL,0,1663),
(N'a8532f3f-4f86-55d4-a433-32103f80ad79',N'3ebc08f7-06b1-5f5d-b8e8-508c1bacae7e',0,3,19,N'Question number 37',N'<p>Đáp án là forests </p><p>- Câu hỏi nói “Due to the damage of ___”, nên cần danh từ chỉ đối tượng bị phá hủy </p><p>- Script nói rõ “forests have been cut down” và nhấn mạnh vai trò của forests trong hấp thụ khí nhà kính </p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ cut down (v): chặt phá </p><p>+ absorb (v): hấp thụ</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,37,NULL,0,1663),
(N'e68b2d33-a8af-5102-9ca6-aff6ca75d195',N'3ebc08f7-06b1-5f5d-b8e8-508c1bacae7e',0,3,19,N'Question number 38',N'<p>Đáp án là mountain </p><p>- Câu hỏi: “kept on farms or on a ___ in different parts…” </p><p>- Script nêu đúng cấu trúc đối lập: “on the farms” và “on a mountain” </p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ restricted area (n): khu vực hạn chế </p><p>+ livestock (n): gia súc</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,38,NULL,0,1663),
(N'0b0767b1-c55f-514c-8e33-f9efa311af96',N'3ebc08f7-06b1-5f5d-b8e8-508c1bacae7e',0,3,19,N'Question number 39',N'<p>Đáp án là food</p><p>- Câu hỏi: “In animal agriculture, ___ required constantly” </p><p>- Script nói thẳng “livestock need food all the time”, tương ứng trực tiếp với “required constantly” </p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ all the time: liên tục </p><p>+ livestock (n): gia súc</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,39,NULL,0,1663),
(N'57d600f7-7cb9-5293-8011-a0bb1fc17255',N'3ebc08f7-06b1-5f5d-b8e8-508c1bacae7e',0,3,19,N'Question number 40',N'<p>Đáp án là fishing </p><p>- Câu hỏi: “Some agricultural activities like ___ are unlikely to be changed” </p><p>- Script đưa ví dụ đúng dạng “very hard to change, such as fishing”, nên đáp án là fishing </p><p>- Key word: </p><p>+ hard to change: khó thay đổi </p><p>+ fishing (n): hoạt động đánh bắt cá</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,40,NULL,0,1663),
(N'1ef71a32-973c-58d7-b32b-b7ff2006fba9',NULL,0,0,11,NULL,NULL,NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-2/iL.VOL2.9.S1662.mp3',N'Vol 2 LISTENING FULL TEST 9',0,7,1,NULL,1,1662),
(N'0670869a-7ac9-547d-be65-a3044a01f66a',N'1ef71a32-973c-58d7-b32b-b7ff2006fba9',0,1,13,(CAST(N'<h2>Ohope Holiday Park: Accommodation</h2><p>Good morning, Ahopee Holiday Park. Oh, hello. We''re planning on coming to Ahopee for a couple of weeks during the summer holidays, and some friends of mine recommended your holiday park, particularly the wooden cabins you have. That''s good to hear. Well, we have different types of cabin available. Can you tell me about the most basic type? Yes. We have a couple of cabins still available which are right beside the pool. </p><p>That sounds great. Yes, they are in a good spot. They have one main living area, and there''s another room with the beds. If you want to do any cooking, there''s a communal kitchen that everyone uses. But otherwise, the kitchen in the cabin just has a fridge, a small one, and also a microwave for heating things up. I see. And what''s the cost of that? That''s $35 per night. Okay. And what other types of cabin do you have? Right, we have our standard cabins. These are near reception, so that''s handy if you want to come in and get us to book a trip or anything. The kitchen is fully equipped too, so you can do all your cooking there. What other facilities does it have? Is there a television? In the standard cabin, I''m afraid not. But it has a shower, which you don''t get in the basic cabin. Okay. And that''s $55 a night inclusive. And is there another cabin type? Yes, the standard plus. All of these cabins are directly opposite the lake, and they all come with a private spa as well. Sounds good.</p><p> I should tell you that these cabins are quite popular, so I''d advise you to book as soon as possible. I don''t suppose there''s a discount for booking for a longer period. There is actually, for the standard plus. Once you go up to 5 nights, there''s a 15% discount, and anything more than 10 nights, it''s 18%. I''ll give it some thought. I think we''ll probably go for the standard. Alright.  So for children, what kind of activities can they do at the holiday park? Do you have a trampoline or anything? No, but a lot of the kids who come here do tennis. It costs nothing to use our court, and they can come borrow the rackets from us as long as they bring them back, of course. Great. My kids would be into that. And we''re planning to bring our boat with us and get out on the water. Is it possible for an afternoon or something to hire some equipment? We''re hoping to go fishing, but we don''t have our own stuff. Yes. For a small charge, we can let you have some equipment. Fantastic. Is there anything else for kids ' AS nvarchar(max))+N'to do in the Ahope area? Well, on Saturday or Sunday, you might like to go to the farm. It''s only a short drive from the holiday park. You can go riding there and see how everything works. It''s quite a popular thing to do. </p><p>OK. I''ll just make a note of that. Actually, one thing I would recommend, depending on whether your children don''t mind a late night... I''m sure they wouldn''t. Well, it''s a guided tour, $20 for a family, every evening, and you go along with the guide into the forest. That''s when the native birds wake up, and it''s a great chance to see them in their natural habitat. My daughter would love that. Now, I just want to check all this with my wife. Will you still be there in 30 minutes? No, I''m going on my lunch break. But I''ll pass your details on to someone else who can confirm your reservation. Her name''s Arataki. That''s A-R-A-T-A-K-I. All right. Thank you. You''re welcome. That is the end of Part 1.</p>'),(CAST(N'<p>Good morning, Ahopee Holiday Park. Oh, hello. We''re planning on coming to Ahopee for a couple of weeks during the summer holidays, and some friends of mine recommended your holiday park, particularly the wooden cabins you have. That''s good to hear. Well, we have different types of cabin available. Can you tell me about the most basic type? Yes. We have a couple of cabins still available which are right beside the pool. </p><p>That sounds great. Yes, they are in a good spot. They have one main living area, and there''s another room with the beds. If you want to do any cooking, there''s a communal kitchen that everyone uses. But otherwise, the kitchen in the cabin just has a fridge, a small one, and also a microwave for heating things up. I see. And what''s the cost of that? That''s $35 per night. Okay. And what other types of cabin do you have? Right, we have our standard cabins. These are near reception, so that''s handy if you want to come in and get us to book a trip or anything. The kitchen is fully equipped too, so you can do all your cooking there. What other facilities does it have? Is there a television? In the standard cabin, I''m afraid not. But it has a shower, which you don''t get in the basic cabin. Okay. And that''s $55 a night inclusive. And is there another cabin type? Yes, the standard plus. All of these cabins are directly opposite the lake, and they all come with a private spa as well. Sounds good.</p><p> I should tell you that these cabins are quite popular, so I''d advise you to book as soon as possible. I don''t suppose there''s a discount for booking for a longer period. There is actually, for the standard plus. Once you go up to 5 nights, there''s a 15% discount, and anything more than 10 nights, it''s 18%. I''ll give it some thought. I think we''ll probably go for the standard. Alright.  So for children, what kind of activities can they do at the holiday park? Do you have a trampoline or anything? No, but a lot of the kids who come here do tennis. It costs nothing to use our court, and they can come borrow the rackets from us as long as they bring them back, of course. Great. My kids would be into that. And we''re planning to bring our boat with us and get out on the water. Is it possible for an afternoon or something to hire some equipment? We''re hoping to go fishing, but we don''t have our own stuff. Yes. For a small charge, we can let you have some equipment. Fantastic. Is there anything else for kids to do in the Ahope area? Well, on Saturday' AS nvarchar(max))+N' or Sunday, you might like to go to the farm. It''s only a short drive from the holiday park. You can go riding there and see how everything works. It''s quite a popular thing to do. </p><p>OK. I''ll just make a note of that. Actually, one thing I would recommend, depending on whether your children don''t mind a late night... I''m sure they wouldn''t. Well, it''s a guided tour, $20 for a family, every evening, and you go along with the guide into the forest. That''s when the native birds wake up, and it''s a great chance to see them in their natural habitat. My daughter would love that. Now, I just want to check all this with my wife. Will you still be there in 30 minutes? No, I''m going on my lunch break. But I''ll pass your details on to someone else who can confirm your reservation. Her name''s Arataki. That''s A-R-A-T-A-K-I. All right. Thank you. You''re welcome. That is the end of Part 1.</p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-2/iL.VOL2.9.S1662.PART1.mp3',NULL,1,0,1,NULL,0,1662),
(N'a907c2b9-632d-5f47-b066-e715ac3064e2',N'0670869a-7ac9-547d-be65-a3044a01f66a',0,2,18,N'<p>Complete the table below
