(N'5d461c44-363f-55dc-b73e-185ee7af9408',N'302764df-4b56-5ab7-800b-ebf509e2952c',0,3,19,N'<p>According to Ravi, in which<span> TWO </span>ways are children''s periods of outdoor play now different from a generation ago?</p>',N'<p>Đáp án là C. Ravi chỉ ra sự khác biệt chính là các buổi chơi ngoài trời hiện nay thường ngắn hơn so với trước đây. Key words: play sessions, shorter time.

</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,25,NULL,0,1662),
(N'5d46f79b-6016-535f-ba52-082cfe032411',N'302764df-4b56-5ab7-800b-ebf509e2952c',0,3,19,N'<p>According to Ravi, in which<span> TWO </span>ways are children''s periods of outdoor play now different from a generation ago?</p>',N'<p>Đáp án là D. Ravi cho biết số lượng trò chơi tự nghĩ ra của trẻ em đã giảm so với thế hệ trước. Key words: declined, improvised games.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,26,NULL,0,1662),
(N'b8512a9f-9cc8-568b-b9c9-d75caac421f4',N'a3c2a920-68c8-5429-8612-304150879132',0,2,18,N'<p>Choose the correct letter, <span>A, B or C.</span></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',1,0,4,NULL,0,1662),
(N'652cae43-6ce5-553e-afb2-974f80d34a3f',N'b8512a9f-9cc8-568b-b9c9-d75caac421f4',0,3,19,N'<p>Ravi thinks parents should be more concerned about the decline of outdoor
play because</p>',N'<p>Đáp án là B. </p><p>Cụm từ "physical problems when they''re adults" (vấn đề thể chất khi trưởng thành) trong bài nghe đồng nghĩa với cụm "health problems later in life" (vấn đề sức khỏe sau này trong cuộc đời) ở đáp án B.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,27,NULL,0,1662),
(N'ddb43991-7567-59f9-9424-6dfcbc7329e2',N'b8512a9f-9cc8-568b-b9c9-d75caac421f4',0,3,19,N'<p>What does Ravisay that schools should do with regard to outdoor play?</p>',N'<p>Đáp án là A. </p><p>Câu hỏi: Ravi nói các trường học nên làm gì đối với việc vui chơi ngoài trời?</p><p>Việc chuyển từ "chỉ nghĩ đến kết quả thi cử" sang "phát triển sự tự tin" chính là hành động thay đổi mục tiêu (revise their aims)</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,28,NULL,0,1662),
(N'145047c8-dadb-55c1-be6a-23d8759c9265',N'b8512a9f-9cc8-568b-b9c9-d75caac421f4',0,3,19,N'<p>What did Smith and Barker say about children in rural areas?</p>',N'<p>Đáp án là A.</p><p>Câu hỏi: Smith và Barker nói gì về trẻ em ở vùng nông thôn?</p><p>Cụm từ "keep off" (tránh xa/không được bước vào) đồng nghĩa với "not be allowed on", và "agricultural land" chính là "farmland".</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,29,NULL,0,1662),
(N'd8d5f674-b5a7-51a0-b984-366d75858ea2',N'b8512a9f-9cc8-568b-b9c9-d75caac421f4',0,3,19,N'<p>What problem does Dr Chang highlight about Smith and Barker''sresearch?</p>',N'<p>Đáp án là C. </p><p>Câu hỏi: Tiến sĩ Chang (Giảng viên) nhấn mạnh vấn đề gì về nghiên cứu của Smith và Barker?</p><p>Ravi chỉ ra vấn đề lớn trong nghiên cứu của Smith và Barker là phạm vi nghiên cứu hẹp và thiếu bằng chứng thuyết phục. </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,30,NULL,0,1662),
(N'0d028870-df8d-5bb5-9220-ea3b2ecd6b45',N'1ef71a32-973c-58d7-b32b-b7ff2006fba9',0,1,15,(CAST(N'<h2>Field trial - heat pump technology</h2><p>I''m going to talk about a field trial that was carried out on heat pumps. But first, some background. The UK has adopted a very ambitious target for reducing carbon emissions. 27% of British carbon dioxide emissions come from the energy used in homes, so around a quarter of all reductions must also come from that sector rather than industry. So it''s not surprising that the government, private companies and independent agencies have been looking into green energy alternatives. At present, the most popular green energy, from a range which includes wind, biomass heating and ground heat, is solar. This has been the most readily accepted by the public. </p><p>However, the field trial I''ve looked at researched heat pump technology. Heat pump technology is relatively new to the UK market and because there is such limited experience of this technology, people have been reluctant to invest in it. So a field trial was needed to monitor this in a sample of heat pumps in real situations. </p><p>Getty Images The heat pumps in this trial are used for the same reason you''d use a boiler, but rather than burning a fuel to produce heat, they move heat from a low-temperature heat source and pump it to a higher temperature where it can be used to provide central heating or domestic hot water. Most heat pumps take heat from either the ground or the air, but water from ponds or rivers may occasionally be used. The general advice in the UK is that the temperature of the hot water stored in a cylinder should be periodically put up to 60°C to kill off bacteria. It is sometimes necessary to use an electric immersion heater to achieve this temperature, as most heat pump installations will be designed to produce domestic hot water at temperatures between 50 and 55°C.  </p><p>For this field trial, 83 UK sites were monitored and they provided a wide spectrum of performance results, even in installations that seemed similar. Some installations performed as well as heat pumps studied in European field trials, but many failed to meet these levels. This field trial monitored two central heating systems, radiators and the increasingly popular underfloor systems. The observations of the field trial led to some key conclusions. One was that heat pumps are sensitive pieces of equipment. In some of the early installations there were problems because the engineers hadn''t fitted the heat pump correctly. </p><p>This observation emphasises the need for ' AS nvarchar(max))+N'better training for everyone involved in the installation. Many different systems were monitored in the field trial and it was found that in most cases designs which were simple were more efficient. So this is something which both pump manufacturers and installers should bear in mind. Many customers mistakenly came to the conclusion that their system wasn''t working as well as they''d expected. However, when this was further investigated, it was found that they had not realised how to regulate the controls properly. There had been a failure to explain this in sufficient detail to the householders. And it was often the case that for the installation all sorts of workmen might be involved. For example, a ground works contractor, a plumber, a heat pump installer and an electrician. It was obvious that a supervisor should be appointed to oversee and be responsible for the whole installation. So what are the implications of this technology? That is the end of part four.</p>'),(CAST(N'<p>I''m going to talk about a field trial that was carried out on heat pumps. But first, some background. The UK has adopted a very ambitious target for reducing carbon emissions. 27% of British carbon dioxide emissions come from the energy used in homes, so around a quarter of all reductions must also come from that sector rather than industry. So it''s not surprising that the government, private companies and independent agencies have been looking into green energy alternatives. At present, the most popular green energy, from a range which includes wind, biomass heating and ground heat, is solar. This has been the most readily accepted by the public. </p><p>However, the field trial I''ve looked at researched heat pump technology. Heat pump technology is relatively new to the UK market and because there is such limited experience of this technology, people have been reluctant to invest in it. So a field trial was needed to monitor this in a sample of heat pumps in real situations. </p><p>Getty Images The heat pumps in this trial are used for the same reason you''d use a boiler, but rather than burning a fuel to produce heat, they move heat from a low-temperature heat source and pump it to a higher temperature where it can be used to provide central heating or domestic hot water. Most heat pumps take heat from either the ground or the air, but water from ponds or rivers may occasionally be used. The general advice in the UK is that the temperature of the hot water stored in a cylinder should be periodically put up to 60°C to kill off bacteria. It is sometimes necessary to use an electric immersion heater to achieve this temperature, as most heat pump installations will be designed to produce domestic hot water at temperatures between 50 and 55°C.  </p><p>For this field trial, 83 UK sites were monitored and they provided a wide spectrum of performance results, even in installations that seemed similar. Some installations performed as well as heat pumps studied in European field trials, but many failed to meet these levels. This field trial monitored two central heating systems, radiators and the increasingly popular underfloor systems. The observations of the field trial led to some key conclusions. One was that heat pumps are sensitive pieces of equipment. In some of the early installations there were problems because the engineers hadn''t fitted the heat pump correctly. </p><p>This observation emphasises the need for better training for everyone involved in th' AS nvarchar(max))+N'e installation. Many different systems were monitored in the field trial and it was found that in most cases designs which were simple were more efficient. So this is something which both pump manufacturers and installers should bear in mind. Many customers mistakenly came to the conclusion that their system wasn''t working as well as they''d expected. However, when this was further investigated, it was found that they had not realised how to regulate the controls properly. There had been a failure to explain this in sufficient detail to the householders. And it was often the case that for the installation all sorts of workmen might be involved. For example, a ground works contractor, a plumber, a heat pump installer and an electrician. It was obvious that a supervisor should be appointed to oversee and be responsible for the whole installation. So what are the implications of this technology? That is the end of part four.</p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-2/iL.VOL2.9.S1662.PART4.mp3',NULL,1,0,4,NULL,0,1662),
(N'091a2974-ca8d-5f7d-91d0-566c0f939b76',N'0d028870-df8d-5bb5-9220-ea3b2ecd6b45',0,2,18,N'<p>Complete the notes below.
Write <span>ONE WORD ONLY</span> for each answer.</p>',N'',N'',N'',N'Field trial - heat pump technology',11,0,1,NULL,0,1662),
(N'a8c06c34-5a9b-5d17-a7f3-b3e0dbc74857',N'091a2974-ca8d-5f7d-91d0-566c0f939b76',0,3,19,N'<h3>Field trial - heat pump technology</h3><p><span>Background</span></p><p>Aim in UK isto reduce carbon emissions from energy consumed in }{SPACE}{ by approximately 25%</p><p>Most popular ''green'' energy: }{SPACE}{ </p><p>Little investment in heat pumps in UK due to lack of }{SPACE}{ in using them</p><p><span>What is a heat pump?</span></p><p>Heat pumpsserve the same purpose as a }{SPACE}{ </p><p>Most heat pumps get heat from the earth or the }{SPACE}{ </p><p>Water is heated to 60°C to destroy }{SPACE}{ </p><p><span>The field trial</span></p><p>83 sites acrossthe UK</p><p>Central heating systems monitored: }{SPACE}{ and under-floor heating</p><p>Key conclusions:</p><p>• installation: need to provide improved }{SPACE}{ in pump-fitting technique</p><ul><li><p></p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ designs performed best</p><ul><li><p>customers needed to be told about regulating the controls</p></li></ul><p>• need for a }{SPACE}{ to co-ordinate the installation</p>',N'<p>Đáp án là homes. Người nói nêu rõ phần lớn lượng CO₂ cần cắt giảm đến từ năng lượng tiêu thụ trong các hộ gia đình. Key words: emissions, energy used, homes.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,31,NULL,0,1662),
(N'f729a98b-cc7b-5621-af50-dcc18a28bdbf',N'091a2974-ca8d-5f7d-91d0-566c0f939b76',0,3,19,N'Question number 32',N'<p>Đáp án là solar. Người nói xác định năng lượng xanh được chấp nhận rộng rãi nhất hiện nay là năng lượng mặt trời. Key words: most popular, green energy, solar.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,32,NULL,0,1662),
(N'ecd970a3-0709-5503-9a98-9918cdc34c27',N'091a2974-ca8d-5f7d-91d0-566c0f939b76',0,3,19,N'Question number 33',N'<p>Đáp án là experience. Việc thiếu kinh nghiệm sử dụng công nghệ bơm nhiệt khiến người dân ngần ngại đầu tư. Key words: limited experience, reluctant, invest.
</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,33,NULL,0,1662),
(N'7aabe050-6835-59fd-b9e3-eace0436d0c9',N'091a2974-ca8d-5f7d-91d0-566c0f939b76',0,3,19,N'Question number 34',N'<p>Đáp án là boiler. Người nói so sánh chức năng của heat pump với nồi hơi truyền thống. Key words: same reason, use, boiler.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,34,NULL,0,1662),
(N'441ed599-69dd-5aa2-853f-643c8c359c3a',N'091a2974-ca8d-5f7d-91d0-566c0f939b76',0,3,19,N'Question number 35',N'<p>Đáp án là air. Người nói liệt kê nguồn lấy nhiệt phổ biến của heat pump, trong đó có không khí. Key words: take heat, ground, air</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,35,NULL,0,1662),
(N'36d7a822-0353-5b0e-9848-1a25778fb684',N'091a2974-ca8d-5f7d-91d0-566c0f939b76',0,3,19,N'Question number 36',N'<p>Đáp án là bacteria. Nước được đun đến 60°C nhằm tiêu diệt vi khuẩn. Key words: 60°C, kill off, bacteria.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,36,NULL,0,1662),
(N'4d2529b5-fbad-5492-8daf-62edc78e83cc',N'091a2974-ca8d-5f7d-91d0-566c0f939b76',0,3,19,N'Question number 37',N'<p>Đáp án là radiators. Thử nghiệm theo dõi hai hệ thống sưởi trung tâm gồm bộ tản nhiệt và sưởi sàn. Key words: monitored, central heating, radiators.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,37,NULL,0,1662),
(N'938106e9-9e2e-546d-a056-eea7b22f7453',N'091a2974-ca8d-5f7d-91d0-566c0f939b76',0,3,19,N'Question number 38',N'<p>Đáp án là training. Kết luận cho thấy cần cải thiện đào tạo trong quá trình lắp đặt heat pump. Key words: need, better, training.

</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,38,NULL,0,1662),
(N'731eb7a8-ca87-5f87-97a9-b35dc0106eda',N'091a2974-ca8d-5f7d-91d0-566c0f939b76',0,3,19,N'Question number 39',N'<p>Đáp án là simple. Các thiết kế đơn giản được chứng minh hoạt động hiệu quả hơn. Key words: designs, simple, efficient</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,39,NULL,0,1662),
(N'40ca800e-cf33-5191-93f8-95adfd3a58c8',N'091a2974-ca8d-5f7d-91d0-566c0f939b76',0,3,19,N'Question number 40',N'<p>Đáp án là supervisor. Người nói nhấn mạnh cần một người giám sát để điều phối toàn bộ quá trình lắp đặt. Key words: appointed, oversee, responsible.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,40,NULL,0,1662),
(N'96d6174b-866f-5a26-9a1c-e92343b2f4b6',NULL,0,0,11,NULL,NULL,NULL,N'',N'Vol 3 READING FULL TEST 11',0,7,1,NULL,1,1657),
(N'507ab998-ba7e-5f5a-96bb-7004bfd1dc12',N'96d6174b-866f-5a26-9a1c-e92343b2f4b6',0,1,13,(CAST(N'<p><span><span>The Development of Exploration and Scientific Research in Antarctica</span></span></p><p><span><span>The modern scientific age in Antarctica really began with the introduction of aircraft in the 1920s. Aircraft transformed the possibilities of exploring the frozen continent around the South Pole, because before that Antarctic travel had been limited to the use of dog-teams pulling sledges. A plane could survey thousands of square kilometres an hour, equivalent to a whole summer''s work using previous techniques. However, the first planes in Antarctica. such as the Lockheed Vega and the Ford Trimotor, were unreliable in freezing conditions. This made polar flying particularly hazardous, since there was little chance of rescue if a plane was forced down in a remote region. <br><br>It was in 1928 that Herbert Wilkins hoped to make the first flight in Antarctica, attempting to cross the continent. A further attempt in 1930 was also unsuccessful, but Wilkins'' aerial photographs seemed to show that the Antarctic Peninsula was in fact an island, not part of the continent as had previously been thought. This new theory caused some excitement among geographers and cartographers. However, the British Grahamland Expedition of 1934-37 proved conclusively that the Antarctic Peninsula was attached to the rest of the continent. <br><br>In 1929, the famous American pilot Richard Byrd flew over the South Pole, and another American, Lincoln Ellsworth, made a successful Antarctic flight in 1935. Although Ellsworth claimed a sector of the continent for the USA, the American government did not follow it up. In 1938, the German explorer, Alfred Ritscher, led an expedition south across the sea Once Antarctica was reached, the aircraft that had been stored in pieces on the ship''s deck was reconstructed. The aeroplane was then launched and used to stake a claim to one section of Antarctica by dropping thousands of tiny flags from the air. <br><br>A significant motivation behind many Antarctic expeditions right up to the 1940s was simply the spirit of adventure. Many of these expeditions had a large measure of private funding, and often the subsequent book about the expedition was a means of clearing debts ihcurred. The vast majority of Antarctic expeditions since 1940 have been funded by governments. usually for political reasons and scientific research.</span></span></p><p><span><span>The setting up of the Research and Development Committee in Britain was a signific' AS nvarchar(max))+N'ant development in the history of science in the Antarctic. The Committee''s report, published in 1920, focused particularly on the sea that circles the Antarctic continent. The report proposed detailed scientific investigations of the physiology and behaviour of the whales inhabiting the region. As a result, a shore station at Grytviken on the island of South Georgia near Antarctica was occupied by scientists for six years. In addition, three research ships were commissioned. They travelled through the Southern Ocean all year, esearching physical and chemical oceanography. The high quality of the </span></span>specimens and data collected by scientists produced nearly 40 large volumes of reports. This entire project came to be known as the Discovery Investigations. The costs of the Discovery. Investigations were completely covered by the proceeds of a tax that was placed on whaling businesses operating in the area.</p><p>It was in 1875 that the idea of international scientific collaboration at the poles was first proposed, with the aim of collecting valuable data. The result was the first Polar Year in 1882-83. A second Polar Year was organised 50 years later, involving 44 nations and scientific bodies. Both of these Polar Years had been timed to coincide with a period when the sun was at its lowest level of activity, in order to monitor the impact this had. So much interest was aroused by this process that a third Polar Year was organised 25 years later. In 1951 it was decided that this scientific programme should be expanded to cover the globe. This new project was renamed the International Geophysical Year (IGY). Antarctica was chosen as an area for particular attention because of its important influence on global weather. Throughout this period, politics were kept firmly in the background.</p><p>The IGY took place in 1957-58 and it was during this period that the last great Antarctic journey was accomplished. Dr Vivian Fuchs'' privately-funded Trans Antarctic Expedition finally achieved what the explorer Ernest Shackleton had first set out to do in 1914. Driving modified tractors, Fuchs'' team traversed Antarctica from coast to coast in 99 days and covered 2, 180 miles or roughly 3,500 kilometres. But there were scientific objectives as well. because the expedition''s measurements allowed the first estimates to be made of the volume of ice that existed across the whole continent. So successful was the IGY that it was extended for a further year in order t'+N'o promote Antarctic science. It also led directly to the signing of a treaty by members of the international community to regulate human conduct in Antarctica over the years ahead.</p><p></p><p></p><p><span><span>&nbsp;</span></span></p>'),NULL,NULL,N'',NULL,1,0,1,NULL,0,1657),
(N'52521450-d4dd-58d2-a8fd-695c26a6a358',N'507ab998-ba7e-5f5a-96bb-7004bfd1dc12',0,2,18,N'<p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? </p><p>In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write    </p><p><span>TRUE</span> if the statement agrees with the information </p><p><span>FALSE</span> if the statement contradicts the information </p><p><span>NOT GIVEN</span> if there is no information on this </p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',1,0,1,NULL,0,1657),
(N'4276bc85-0022-5dae-b428-38d7bc54a4c9',N'52521450-d4dd-58d2-a8fd-695c26a6a358',0,3,19,N'Until the 1920s, humans relied on animals to explore Antarctica. ',N'<p>+Question: Interpretation: Cho đến những năm 1920, con người dựa vào động vật để thám hiểm Nam Cực. </p><p>+Answer:  Dựa vào thông tin trong bài ta thấy trước đó việc đi lại ở Nam Cực chỉ giới hạn ở việc sử dụng chó kéo xe trượt tuyết =&gt; phải dựa vào chó kéo xe trượt tuyết.  </p><p>=&gt; Đáp án cần điền là TRUE  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,1,NULL,0,1657),
(N'3fde2baa-6835-504d-9e3a-011c536dd9d5',N'52521450-d4dd-58d2-a8fd-695c26a6a358',0,3,19,N'Herbert Wilkins failed to fly across the Antarctic continent in 1928.',N'<p>+Question:   Interpretation: Herbert Wilkins đã thất bại khi bay ngang qua lục địa Nam Cực vào năm 1928.  </p><p>+Answer: Bài đọc cho biết vào năm 1928, Herbert Wilkins đã cố gắng thực hiện chuyến bay đầu tiên vượt qua Nam Cực và một nỗ lực khác vào năm 1930 cũng không thành công =&gt; nghĩa là Wilkins cũng đã thất bại. </p><p>=&gt; Đáp án cần điền là TRUE  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,2,NULL,0,1657),
(N'f8de9f95-f6b0-546e-b5e4-e0049e331af6',N'52521450-d4dd-58d2-a8fd-695c26a6a358',0,3,19,N'The expedition of 1934-37 confirmed a new theory about the Antarctic Peninsula. ',N'<p>+Question:  Interpretation: Chuyến thám hiểm 1934-37 xác nhận giả thuyết mới về bán đảo Nam Cực. </p><p>+Answer:  Thông tin trong bài cho biết một giả thuyết mới cho rằng bán đảo Nam Cực là một hòn đảo chứ không phải một phần của lục địa, nhưng chuyến thám hiểm 1934-37 đã chứng minh bán đảo Nam Cực gắn liền với phần còn lại của lục địa </p><p>=&gt; chuyến thám hiểm chứng minh giả thuyết mới là sai.  </p><p>=&gt; Đáp án cần điền là FALSE  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,3,NULL,0,1657),
(N'52401d07-b7ea-5e0d-a85d-30c66f6b3860',N'52521450-d4dd-58d2-a8fd-695c26a6a358',0,3,19,N'Lincoln Ellsworth was influenced by the flight of Richard Byrd. ',N'<p>+Question:  Interpretation: Lincoln Ellsworth chịu ảnh hưởng từ chuyến bay của Richard Byrd. </p><p>+Answer:  Không có thông tin cho rằng Lincoln Ellsworth chịu ảnh hưởng từ chuyến bay. </p><p>=&gt; Đáp án cần điền là NOT GIVEN  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,4,NULL,0,1657),
(N'905f7df5-3bc3-53d9-9fe5-a79f2c10c80c',N'52521450-d4dd-58d2-a8fd-695c26a6a358',0,3,19,N'The govemment of the LISA claimed part of Antarctica in 1935.',N'<p>+Question:  Interpretation: Chính phủ Mĩ đã tuyên bố chủ quyền một phần Nam Cực vào năm 1935. </p><p>+Answer:  Theo thông tin trong bài thì Ellsworth đã tuyên bố một khu của lục địa này thuộc về Mĩ nhưng chính phủ không thực hiện điều đó =&gt; chính phủ Mĩ không tuyên bố chủ quyền lên Nam Cực.</p><p> =&gt; Đáp án cần điền là FALSE  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,5,NULL,0,1657),
(N'fafdb961-ca4f-5e41-98b7-41a52f1b1e3e',N'52521450-d4dd-58d2-a8fd-695c26a6a358',0,3,19,N'After 1940, nations rather than individuals paid for most Antarctic expeditions. ',N'<p>+Question:   Interpretation: Sau năm 1940, hầu hết các chuyến thám hiểm Nam Cực được các quốc gia chi trả hơn là cá nhân. </p><p>+Answer:  Thông tin trong bài cho biết, phần lớn các chuyến thám hiểm Nam Cực kể từ năm 1940 đều được chính phủ tài trợ =&gt; chính phủ tài trợ nhiều hơn cá nhân. </p><p>=&gt; đáp án là TRUE  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,6,NULL,0,1657),
(N'01d61d2c-ba99-5e2f-b7cf-a55a4b24d21d',N'507ab998-ba7e-5f5a-96bb-7004bfd1dc12',0,2,18,N'<p>Choose<span> ONE WORD ONLY</span> from the passage for each answer. </p><p>Write your answers in boxes 7-13 on your answer sheet. </p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',11,0,2,NULL,0,1657),
(N'41cac757-eebd-5a5e-b550-f2c7604390be',N'01d61d2c-ba99-5e2f-b7cf-a55a4b24d21d',0,3,19,N'A 1920 report called for research into the whales in the sea around Antarctica researchers worked from the station at Grytviken and also from several }{SPACE}{ Local companies paid a }{SPACE}{ which funded the Discovery Investigations The first two Polar Years researched the effects of the }{SPACE}{ Antarctica affects the worlds }{SPACE}{ so it was a focus for the IGY Vivian Fuchs'' expedition crossed Antarctica using special }{SPACE}{ The total amount of }{SPACE}{ in Antarctica was calculated by Fuchs'' expedition One result of the IGY was the establishment of a }{SPACE}{ to control aspects of Antarctica''s future ',N'<p>+Question:   Interpretation: Các nhà nghiên cứu làm việc từ trạm ở Grytviken và cũng từ vài ...... </p><p>+Answer:  Dựa vào thông tin trong bài ta có thể một trạm nghiên cứu ven biển tại Grytviken đã được các nhà khoa học sử dụng trong sáu năm và ba tàu nghiên cứu đã được đưa vào hoạt động =&gt; ngoài trạm Grytviken, các nhà nghiên cứu còn làm việc ở các con tàu. </p><p>=&gt; đáp án là ships  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,7,NULL,0,1657),
(N'd3913064-1d92-59bd-b9dc-cdc0e2afc0aa',N'01d61d2c-ba99-5e2f-b7cf-a55a4b24d21d',0,3,19,N'Question number 8',N'<p>+Question: Interpretation: Các công ty địa phương trả …… để tài trợ cho dự án Discovery Investigations. </p><p>+Answer:  Thông tin trong bài cho thấy chi phí của dự án được chi trả hoàn toàn bằng tiền thu được từ thuế đánh vào các doanh nghiệp săn bắt cá voi hoạt động trong khu vực =&gt; thuế được dùng để tài trợ cho dự án. </p><p>=&gt; từ cần điền là tax  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,8,NULL,0,1657),
(N'053e22bd-6d95-5251-8008-58144bbd8897',N'01d61d2c-ba99-5e2f-b7cf-a55a4b24d21d',0,3,19,N'Question number 9',N'<p>+Question: Interpretation: Hai năm cực đầu tiên đã nghiên cứu tác động của …… </p><p>+Answer:  Bài cho rằng hai năm cực đều được tính toán sao cho trùng với thời kỳ mặt trời hoạt động ở mức thấp nhất để theo dõi tác động của hiện tượng này =&gt; nghiên cứu tác động của mặt trời. </p><p>=&gt; Đáp án cần điền là sun  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,9,NULL,0,1657),
(N'1d7014e5-cbe7-5db0-9689-a75bc4f20dc7',N'01d61d2c-ba99-5e2f-b7cf-a55a4b24d21d',0,3,19,N'Question number 10',N'<p>+Question:  Interpretation: Nam Cực ảnh hưởng đến …… của thế giới. </p><p>+Answer: Thông tin trong bài cho thấy Nam Cực là khu vực cần đặc biệt chú ý vì ảnh hưởng quan trọng của nơi này đến thời tiết toàn cầu =&gt; nó ảnh hưởng đến thời tiết của thế giới. </p><p>=&gt; Đáp án cần điền là weather  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,10,NULL,0,1657),
(N'edeb6beb-b0e5-5261-82e2-eb3f42980495',N'01d61d2c-ba99-5e2f-b7cf-a55a4b24d21d',0,3,19,N'Question number 11',N'<p>+Question:  Interpretation: Chuyến thám hiểm của Vivian Fuchs băng qua Nam Cực bằng …… </p><p>+Answer:  Dựa vào thông tin trong bài ta thấy nhóm của Fuchs đã lái những chiếc máy kéo được cải tiến để đi qua Nam Cực. </p><p>=&gt; Từ cần điền là tractors  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,11,NULL,0,1657),
(N'6525cb8a-240a-586a-a2d6-781476fb56db',N'01d61d2c-ba99-5e2f-b7cf-a55a4b24d21d',0,3,19,N'Question number 12',N'<p>+Question:   Interpretation: Tổng lượng …… ở Nam Cực được tính toán bởi đoàn thám hiểm của Fuchs. </p><p>+Answer: Dựa vào thông tin trong bài ta thấy các phép đo của đoàn thám hiểm đã cho phép đưa ra những ước tính đầu tiên về khối lượng băng tồn tại trên toàn bộ lục địa =&gt; tổng lượng băng được tính toán bởi đoàn thám hiểm của Fuchs. </p><p>=&gt; từ cần điền là ice  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,12,NULL,0,1657),
(N'a1b862fa-4dc8-5879-bd6c-3f99ce4b7ed6',N'01d61d2c-ba99-5e2f-b7cf-a55a4b24d21d',0,3,19,N'Question number 13',N'<p>+ Question: Interpretation: Một kết quả của IGY là việc thành lập …… để kiểm soát các khía cạnh của Nam Cực. </p><p>+Answers: Dựa vào thông tin trong bài ta thấy nó dẫn đến việc các thành viên của cộng đồng quốc tế ký kết một hiệp ước nhằm điều chỉnh hành vi của con người ở Nam Cực trong những năm tiếp theo </p><p>=&gt; kết quả của IGY là thành lập một hiệp ước. =&gt; Câu trả lời sẽ là treaty  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,13,NULL,0,1657),
(N'73a7c6b5-10f7-567e-b809-b52ea90a8d9e',N'96d6174b-866f-5a26-9a1c-e92343b2f4b6',0,1,14,(CAST(N'<p><span><span>Effects of changes in world population</span></span></p><p><span><span>A }{HEADING}{ </span></span> Human fertility rates around the world are dropping for a variety of complex reasons. While the population itself continues to increase, the rate of increase is slowing, and sometime in the next 80 years, world population will peak in the vicinity of nine billion before contracting. That raises an important question: is population contraction a bad thing? Some think not. There is aschool of thought that argues that smaller populations are good. Population control proponents claim variously that (1) we do not have the food to sustain higher populations; (2) our planet already suffers from overcrowding; (3) the environmental impact of increased populations will bring catastrophe either through pollution or consumption of finite natural resources; or in contrast, they argue decreased populations will lead to higher wages and a better quality of life as available supplies exceed reduced demands. These arguments seem reasonable at first, but do not withstand scrutiny.</p><p><span><span>B }{HEADING}{ </span></span> Let''s start with food. The worry about mass starvation is a remnant of Paul Ehrlich''s 1968 book The Population Bomb. Ehrlich, Professor of Population Studies in the department of Biological Sciences at Stanford University in California, wrote that in the face of expanding populations, the world will undergo famines - hundreds of millions of people are going to starve to death." As Ehrlich himself now admits, this prediction proved faulty. Instead, the availability of food has greatly increased, even with a growing population. Demographer Philip Longman notes that food shortages have become ''a political problem, related to fair distribution, not an issue of inadequate supply''.</p><p>How did this happen? In 1965, Danish economist Ester Bose-rup proposed that population increase fosters agricultural innovation, which in turn increases production. Her theories have been borne out by events, which show that some areas of the world may lack supplies while the world has an overall surplus.</p><p><span><span>C }{HEADING}{ </span></span> What about overcrowding? Everywhere you go today, you find traffic jams and sprawl, with people packed into crowded places. But this is a problem of density, not population. There''s plenty of land available out there. The problem is that people who used to live in the rural areas have relocated to cities. This mas' AS nvarchar(max))+N'sive migration into cities has caused urbanization, which is different trom overpopulation, and the problems associated with this include air pollution, lower wages, limited access to healthcare and educational opportunities.</p><p><span><span>D }{HEADING}{ </span></span> Environmental concerns are more interesting, but such end-of-the-world warnings are not new. Global warming and the fact that the Earth has only finite amounts of natural resources that we will surely deplete, are the two main concerns of environmentalists. This, too, is an argument we have heard before. As Massimo Livi-Bacci, Professor Of Demography at the University Of Florence, Italy, explains in his Concise History of World Population, more than 100 years ago economists feared that coal supplies would he exhausted, and about 30 years ago the Club of Rome made similar predictions regarding other natural resources''. Instead, innovation stepped in to syovide greater efficiency. For instance, in the Arnerica of 1850, you needed an average of 4.6 tons of petroleum equivalent to produce $1,000 of goods and services. By 1950, you need only 1.8 tons, and by 1978, 1.5 tons.</p><p><span><span>E }{HEADING}{ </span></span> This leaves us with the econwny. In 1971, Simon Smith Kuznets won the Nobel Prize in Economics for his theory of ''tested knowledge''. Kuznets explained, ''More population means more creators and both of along established production patterns and of new knowledge and inventions.'' Kuznets was codifying what others had noticed before. Political economist Adam Srnlth remarked that the most decisive mark of the prosperity of any country is the increase of the number of its inhabitants.'' As Livi-Bacci observes, ''All things being equal, population increase is followed by increased per capita production.'' So the proposed ''benefits'' of population decline are, at the very least, suspect. In addition, there are worrying potential costs of population decline. Of course, this worry is theoretical because we''ve never seen population decline on the massive scale that''s coming our way. Or rather, we''ve never seen it in the modem world.</p><p><span><span>F }{HEADING}{ </span></span> There are, however, two historical examples. Between 400 BC and AD 1, world population increased from about 153 milhon to 252 million. For the next 200 years, growth slowed almost to a halt. Then, between AD 200 and AD 600, the population shrank from 257 million to 208 million. It took an additional 400 years for the p'+N'opulation to recover to the level it had attained in AD 1. The other drop in population occurred between 1340 and 1400, when the Black Death, one of the most deadly pandemics in human history, ravaged the world. Global population fell from 442 million to 375 million. Neither of these drops was a particularly pleasant period in human history. Or, as Canadian journalist Mark Steyn notes in America Alone, ''Them is no precedent in human history for economic growth on declining human capital.'' It is impossible to anticipate with certainty the effects of population decline. But there is good mason to it will be bad for us. Innovation will suffer as the demand for nearly everything slackens. Instead of producing windfalls of excess supply, economies will probably contract. As Livi-Bacci observes, ''Historically, areas depopulated or in the process of losing population have almost always been characterized by backward economies.'' The real question therefore is whether or not falling populations will lead to the demise of civilization as we know it.</p>'),NULL,NULL,N'',NULL,4,0,2,NULL,0,1657),
(N'713f4dd6-bb40-5411-beaf-68997f38ef73',N'73a7c6b5-10f7-567e-b809-b52ea90a8d9e',0,2,18,N'<p>You should spend about 20 minutes on questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2. </p><p>Questions 14-19 Reading Passage 2 has six sections, <span>A-F.</span> </p><p>Choose the correct heading for each section from the list of headings below. </p><p>Write the correct number, i-viii, in boxes on your answer sheet. </p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',4,0,1,NULL,0,1657),
(N'65065516-dc09-5d79-8365-a66f05021751',N'713f4dd6-bb40-5411-beaf-68997f38ef73',0,3,19,N'Paragraph A',N'<p>+Question: Interpretation: Đoạn A. </p><p>+Answer:  Đoạn A đặt ra câu hỏi liệu suy giảm dân số có phải là điều xấu không? Một số người cho rằng không, có một trường phái cho rằng dân số nhỏ hơn là tốt =&gt; phù hợp với tiêu đề ‘Liệu sự suy giảm dân số có mang lại lợi ích cho thế giới không?’. </p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là iii  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,14,NULL,0,1657),
(N'605beb9f-ee44-5cef-95c7-6cc8f7d9ea01',N'713f4dd6-bb40-5411-beaf-68997f38ef73',0,3,19,N'Paragraph B',N'<p>+Question:   Interpretation: Đoạn B.  </p><p>+Answer: Từ đoạn B ta biết nguồn cung lương thực đã tăng lên đáng kể, nhà nhân khẩu học Philip Longman lưu ý rằng tình trạng thiếu lương thực đã trở thành ''một vấn đề chính trị, liên quan đến việc phân phối công bằng, chứ không phải là vấn đề cung không đủ'' =&gt; nội dung tập trung vào nguồn cung cấp thực phẩm.  </p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là i  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,15,NULL,0,1657),
(N'f1810a24-6854-5318-86c6-f0e27756f630',N'713f4dd6-bb40-5411-beaf-68997f38ef73',0,3,19,N'Paragraph C',N'<p>+Question:  Interpretation: Đoạn C. </p><p>+Answer:  Dựa vào thông tin trong đoạn C ta thấy vấn đề là những người từng sống ở nông thôn đã di cư đến các thành phố gây ra quá trình đô thị hóa =&gt; đoạn này phân tích tác động của di chuyển dân cư.  </p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là vi  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,16,NULL,0,1657),
(N'f6d847e4-8b7e-5fee-b672-f279fdc5544e',N'713f4dd6-bb40-5411-beaf-68997f38ef73',0,3,19,N'Paragraph D',N'<p>+Question:  Interpretation: Đoạn D. </p><p>+Answer:  Theo thông tin trong đoạn D, Sự nóng lên toàn cầu và thực tế là Trái Đất chỉ có một lượng tài nguyên thiên nhiên hữu hạn mà chúng ta chắc chắn sẽ cạn kiệt =&gt; cho thấy phát triển tiềm năng của ông vẫn cần được nghiên cứu thêm. </p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là ii  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,17,NULL,0,1657),
(N'97caed41-fd91-59ed-8841-be85d90b9dc7',N'713f4dd6-bb40-5411-beaf-68997f38ef73',0,3,19,N'Paragraph E',N'<p>+Question:   Interpretation: Đoạn E. </p><p>+Answer:  Thông tin trong đoạn E cho biết dân số càng đông thì càng có nhiều người sản xuất và mọi thứ đều bình đẳng, sự gia tăng dân số sẽ kéo theo sự gia tăng sản lượng bình quân đầu người =&gt; chỉ ra liên hệ giữa dân số và năng suất. </p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là v  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,18,NULL,0,1657),
(N'681a4091-1d80-5bde-8d0d-0033df3c5efd',N'713f4dd6-bb40-5411-beaf-68997f38ef73',0,3,19,N'Paragraph F',N'<p>+Question:   Interpretation: Đoạn F. </p><p>+Answer:  Đoạn F đã liệt kê hai lần giảm dân số mạnh trong lịch sử, từ đó có nhận xét những khu vực có dân số giảm hoặc đang trong quá trình mất dân số hầu như luôn được đặc trưng bởi nền kinh tế lạc hậu =&gt; ta thấy được hậu quả của giảm dân số.  </p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là vii  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,19,NULL,0,1657),
(N'e7f5b5ec-8e26-5d10-bb9d-e9197c0fcd74',N'73a7c6b5-10f7-567e-b809-b52ea90a8d9e',0,2,18,N'<p>Complete the sentences below. </p><p>Choose <span>ONE WORD ONLY</span> from the passage for each answer. </p><p>Write your answers in boxes 20-22 on your answer sheet. </p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',11,0,2,NULL,0,1657),
(N'07fd01b7-196a-5253-9c06-bacc1bd26afb',N'e7f5b5ec-8e26-5d10-bb9d-e9197c0fcd74',0,3,19,N'Boserup''s ideas explain wy overall, the world can have a food }{SPACE}{ while some areas don''t have enough. In the last 100 years or so, }{SPACE}{ has led to a more efficient use of resources. Adam Smith argued that a country''s }{SPACE}{ is caused by a growth in population',N'<p>+Question:   Interpretation: Ý tưởng của Boserup giải thích tại sao nhìn chung, thế giới có thể có …… lương thực trong khi một số khu vực lại không có đủ. </p><p>+Answer:  Dựa vào thông tin trong bài ta có thể thấy các lý thuyết của bà đã được chứng minh một số khu vực trên thế giới có thể thiếu nguồn cung cấp trong khi thế giới lại có thặng dư chung =&gt; thế giới có thể có thặng dư lương thực trong khi một số khu vực lại thiếu thốn. </p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là surplus  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,20,NULL,0,1657),
(N'4d18f2ce-08bf-582f-b827-07bfcff898f1',N'e7f5b5ec-8e26-5d10-bb9d-e9197c0fcd74',0,3,19,N'Question number 21',N'<p>+Question: Interpretation: Trong 100 năm qua, …… đã giúp sử dụng tài nguyên hiệu quả hơn. </p><p>+Answer:  Dựa vào thông tin trong bài ta có thể thấy hơn 100 năm trước các nhà kinh tế lo ngại rằng nguồn cung than đá sẽ cạn kiệt nhưng sự đổi mới đã xuất hiện để mang lại hiệu quả cao hơn =&gt; sự đổi mới giúp sử dụng tài nguyên hiệu quả hơn. </p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là innovation  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,21,NULL,0,1657),
(N'37d376db-eb11-57c0-84e9-283bd45ba233',N'e7f5b5ec-8e26-5d10-bb9d-e9197c0fcd74',0,3,19,N'Question number 22',N'<p>+Question: Interpretation: Adam Smith cho rằng sự …… của một quốc gia phụ thuộc vào tăng dân số. </p><p>+Answer:  Dựa vào thông tin trong bài ta có thể thấy Adam Smith nhận xét rằng dấu hiệu quyết định của sự thịnh vượng của bất kỳ quốc gia nào là sự gia tăng số lượng cư dân =&gt; sự thịnh vượng của một quốc gia phụ thuộc vào tăng dân số. </p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là prosperity  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,22,NULL,0,1657),
(N'23ee426f-7e89-545d-9b36-b87e41152571',N'73a7c6b5-10f7-567e-b809-b52ea90a8d9e',0,2,18,N'<p>Choose <span><span>TWO</span></span> letters, A-E.</p><p>Write the correct letters in boxes 23 and 24 on your answer sheet.</p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',5,0,3,NULL,0,1657),
(N'9e72656b-2a44-5fc7-bb18-36ffaec99c9c',N'23ee426f-7e89-545d-9b36-b87e41152571',0,3,19,N'Which TWO of the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 2? ',N'<p>+Question:  Interpretation: Hai câu nào sau đây đồng tình với quan điểm của tác giả trong Đoạn đọc 2? </p><p>+Answer: Thông tin trong bài cho thấy nguồn cung thực phẩm đã tăng lên đáng kể =&gt; nghĩa là nguồn cung đã lớn hơn trước kia. </p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là A  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,23,NULL,0,1657),
(N'39ac6f2b-6194-54ac-82fe-128d8dd860a0',N'23ee426f-7e89-545d-9b36-b87e41152571',0,3,19,N'Which TWO of the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 2? ',N'<p>+Question:  Interpretation: Hai câu nào sau đây đồng tình với quan điểm của tác giả trong Đoạn đọc 2? </p><p>+Answer:  Theo bài đọc, những người từng sống ở vùng nông thôn đã chuyển đến thành phố =&gt; hoàn toàn trùng khớp với đáp án E. </p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là E  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,24,NULL,0,1657),
(N'3c8692b9-a03b-53d7-ae03-549e7502232c',N'73a7c6b5-10f7-567e-b809-b52ea90a8d9e',0,2,18,N'<p>Choose<span> TWO </span>letters, A-E. </p><p>Write the correct letters in boxes 23 and 24 on your answer sheet. </p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',5,0,4,NULL,0,1657),
(N'fd6ed3e8-0f15-5bd6-ba2e-66919022d1e8',N'3c8692b9-a03b-53d7-ae03-549e7502232c',0,3,19,N'Which TWO claims does the writer make about future population decline? ',N'<p>+Question:   Interpretation: Tác giả đưa ra hai khẳng định nào về sự suy giảm dân số trong tương lai? </p><p>+Answer: Dựa vào thông tin trong bài ta thấy có lý do chính đáng để tin rằng suy giảm dân số sẽ làm nhu cầu về hầu hết mọi thứ giảm sút, làm sự đổi mới bị ảnh hưởng =&gt; giảm sút về số lượng ý tưởng mới. </p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là C  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,25,NULL,0,1657),
(N'096c2305-22fb-5140-9c82-2a7ab122ff9a',N'3c8692b9-a03b-53d7-ae03-549e7502232c',0,3,19,N'Which TWO claims does the writer make about future population decline? ',N'<p>+ Question: Interpretation: Tác giả đưa ra hai khẳng định nào về sự suy giảm dân số trong tương lai? </p><p>+Answers: Bài cũng cho biết rằng thay vì tạo ra nguồn cung dư thừa, nền kinh tế có thể sẽ suy thoái =&gt; nền kinh tế ngày càng nhỏ hơn. </p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là E  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,26,NULL,0,1657),
(N'f3ea230e-9c5a-5ea3-b99f-b5ab195c6c4a',N'96d6174b-866f-5a26-9a1c-e92343b2f4b6',0,1,15,(CAST(N'<p><span><span><span>The lost animals of Australia</span></span></span></p><p></p><p>The history of Australia''s animals over the past 50,000 years has been largely one of extinction. The time has been too short for new species of large animals to evolve and, over this period, nearly one-third of Australia''s mammal species have become extinct, along with nearly all the large reptiles and many of the flightless birds. The cause of these extinctions is still hotly debated. One school of thought suggests that humans caused the extinctions, and another that they were due to changes in climate. The greatest problem in evaluating these theories is that we do not know exactly when these animals became extinct. Fossils from a number of well-dated cave and lakeside sites suggest that all the now-extinct species had already vanished 35,000 years ago, but a few other sites suggest that giant marsupials might have survived until 25,000 years ago, or even as late as 6,000 years ago. One certainty is that Australia''s climate has changed greatly over the past 40,000 years. Between 25,000 and 15,000 years ago, the sea level dropped by more than 100 metres and the continent experienced an extremely arid phase. Clearly, the timing of the extinctions is of critical importance. If they can be shown to coincide with the arrival of humans, about 50,000 years ago, then circumstantial evidence would point to humans as the cause. If, however, the giant marsupials survived until 25,000 years ago, the increased aridity would seem to be the more likely cause.</p><p></p><p>Before these extinctions, Australia was a very different place. Naturally occurring fires were probably less frequent than they are now, because large marsupial herbivores (of which there were about forty species) reduced the standing crop of vegetation.</p><p></p><p>Rainforest plants were widespread in the parts of Australia which are now very dry. The largest marsupial species was the diprotodon, which, like other Australian marsupial giants, was about one-third the weight of its ecological equivalent elsewhere. It probably weighed between 1,000 and 2,000 kilograms, while the elephant of Afro-Asia weighed about 5,000 kilograms. The relatively small size of the Australian marsupial giants has been attributed to Australia''s extraordinarily poor soils and erratic climate, both factors which typically limit plant growth.</p><p></p><p>Judging by the teeth of extinct species, there were many specialist grazers and browse' AS nvarchar(max))+N'rs, paralleling the great mammal communities of Africa today. But the Australian carnivores were very different from their African equivalents. For example, the Australian marsupial lion was only about the size of a leopard; there was no equivalent of the large group of cat- and dog-like carnivores of Africa. The marsupial lion was Australia''s only cat-like species; there was one dog-like species, the thylacine, which vanished from mainland Australia 3,000 years ago, but seems to have survived on the Australian island of Tasmania until the 1930s, and one scavenger/carnivore, the Tasmanian devil. The larger Australian carnivores were all reptiles. The largest of these, the gigantic snakes of the genus Wonambi, were more than 8 metres long, and together with the 7-metre goanna and the 3-metre land crocodile, were the main predators. There were never vast numbers of most species. Large, warm-blooded creatures were at a disadvantage, their prey being limited by the nature of the soil and climate. The cold-blooded reptilian carnivores, which required less energy, were therefore able to dominate.</p><p></p><p>There is strong evidence to support the theory that humans were responsible for the decline of large animals in Australia. In their Afro-Eurasian homeland, humans were medium-sized members of a very large community of carnivores and omnivores. But by 40,000 years ago, they were taking a very broad range of prey, including mammals much larger than themselves. Studies have shown that when humans or other predators arrive in areas where there have previously been no ecologically equivalent species, they invariably have a profound impact. For example, over the past 1,000 years, Polynesians in Hawaii have destroyed more than 70% of the bird species, and during the 1800s, hunters on islands close to Antarctica severely depleted many seal species.</p><p></p><p>Australian animals were particularly vulnerable to the impact of humans. Marsupial herbivores were adapted only to avoiding predation by large but relatively unintelligent reptiles, while humans are the most efficient predators that have ever existed. From the mountain rainforests to the desert centre, extinctions emptied landscape after landscape, until finally the largest surviving mammals were humans themselves. Medium-sized animal species weighing between 10 and 100 kilograms either also became extinct or became smaller over thousands of years. Grey kangaroos are now only half the size they once were, wh'+N'ile koalas and Tasmanian devils weigh, on average, one-third less than they once did.</p><p></p><p>In general, in Australia, the larger the species, the more it has reduced in size, with the exception of humans and wombats; the latter may have been protected by their burrowing habits. This shrinking may also be attributable to human hunting practices. If hunters claimed the largest individuals of these species, fast-maturing small specimens would have been more likely to survive to maturity. Increasingly, they would have produced smaller offspring. Only the smallest mammals, those weighing less than 10 kilograms, survived unaltered, although some may have been restricted to a smaller number of areas. This extinction pattern changed with the arrival of Europeans towards the end of the 18th century. As a result of this, a large number of smaller species also became extinct over the course of the following century, together with 21 medium-sized mammals and one large mammal species.</p>'),NULL,NULL,N'',NULL,1,0,3,NULL,0,1657),
(N'83f4b917-f9b4-529e-98e4-27b2251951e4',N'f3ea230e-9c5a-5ea3-b99f-b5ab195c6c4a',0,2,18,N'<p>Choose the correct letter <span>A, B, C or D.</span> </p><p>Write the correct letter in boxes 27-32 on your answer sheet. </p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',1,0,1,NULL,0,1657),
(N'942a3209-f6c4-58d2-be46-423c0faf847f',N'83f4b917-f9b4-529e-98e4-27b2251951e4',0,3,19,N'The writer states that it is difficult to decide why prehistoric Australian animals became extinct because ',N'<p>+Question: Interpretation: Tác giả nói rằng khó xác định lý do tuyệt chủng của các động vật cổ Australia vì. </p><p>+Answer:  Thông tin trong bài cho biết một số hóa thạch cho thấy tất cả các loài hiện đã tuyệt chủng đã biến mất 35,000 năm trước, nhưng các hóa thạch khác lại cho thấy thú có túi khổng lồ có thể đã sống sót lâu hơn </p><p>=&gt; các bằng chứng đang mâu thuẫn nhau. </p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là C  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,27,NULL,0,1657),
(N'048ca3cf-204e-5569-afa2-ffbd2c0b8849',N'83f4b917-f9b4-529e-98e4-27b2251951e4',0,3,19,N'The writer suggests that Australia''s larger mammals were smaller than those of Africa and Asia because ',N'<p>+Question:   Interpretation: Tác giả gợi ý rằng các loài thú có túi lớn ở Úc nhỏ hơn so với châu Phi và châu Á vì. </p><p>+Answer: Thông tin trong bài cho thấy kích thước nhỏ của loài thú có túi khổng lồ ở Úc được cho là do đất đai cực kỳ cằn cỗi và khí hậu thất thường của Úc, hạn chế sự phát triển của thực vật =&gt; dẫn đến việc hạn chế thức ăn </p><p>=&gt; vì thế mà chúng nhỏ hơn. =&gt; Đáp án là A.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,28,NULL,0,1657),
(N'4d5ea38c-69b9-5777-b268-7fdbf75dbd9c',N'83f4b917-f9b4-529e-98e4-27b2251951e4',0,3,19,N'According to the writer, large Australian carnivores were mostly reptiles because ',N'<p>+Question:  Interpretation: Theo tác giả, các loài động vật ăn thịt lớn ở Úc chủ yếu là bò sát vì. </p><p>+Answer:  Thông tin trong bài cho biết những loài động vật máu nóng gặp bất lợi vì con mồi bị giới hạn bởi đặc điểm đất đai và khí hậu nên các loài bò sát ăn thịt máu lạnh đã chiếm ưu thế =&gt; các loài động vật ăn thịt lớn ở Úc chủ yếu là bò sát vì chúng thích nghi hơn với môi trường.   </p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là C   </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,29,NULL,0,1657),
(N'ad6f8803-c8d6-522b-b25f-933eb07056a8',N'83f4b917-f9b4-529e-98e4-27b2251951e4',0,3,19,N'According to the writer, the effect of the first humans in Australia was particularly great because Australian animals ',N'<p>+Question:  Interpretation: Theo tác giả, tác động của con người đầu tiên ở Úc đặc biệt lớn vì các động vật Úc. </p><p>+Answer:  Thông tin trong bài cho biết động vật ở Úc đặc biệt dễ bị tổn thương trước tác động của con người vì chúng chỉ thích nghi để tránh các loài bò sát lớn và tương đối kém thông minh, trong khi con người là loài săn mồi hiệu quả nhất từng tồn tại =&gt; tác động của con người lên chúng lớn hơn. </p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là C  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,30,NULL,0,1657),
(N'47207401-c953-5e90-9c6e-08d91743339a',N'83f4b917-f9b4-529e-98e4-27b2251951e4',0,3,19,N'What, according to the writer, does the wombat have in common with humans? ',N'<p>+Question:  Interpretation: Theo tác giả, wombat giống con người ở điểm nào? </p><p>+Answer:  Thông tin trong bài cho thấy ở Úc, loài càng lớn thì kích thước càng bị thu hẹp, ngoại trừ con người và wombat =&gt; chỉ có con người và wombat giữ nguyên kích thước. </p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là A  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,31,NULL,0,1657),
(N'b0946fda-e853-516e-88c4-42ffd08a6856',N'83f4b917-f9b4-529e-98e4-27b2251951e4',0,3,19,N'The writer suggests that Australian mammals have become smaller because',N'<p>+Question:   Interpretation: Tác giả gợi ý rằng các loài thú Australia nhỏ đi là vì. </p><p>+Answer:  Thông tin trong bài cho biết nếu thợ săn bắt được những cá thể lớn nhất của loài này, những mẫu vật nhỏ trưởng thành nhanh sẽ có nhiều khả năng sống sót đến khi trưởng thành hơn =&gt; vì những con lớn bị săn nên chúng phải nhỏ đi để sinh tồn.</p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là C  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,32,NULL,0,1657),
(N'e2f4570f-cb4f-567b-a014-858648d66a8b',N'f3ea230e-9c5a-5ea3-b99f-b5ab195c6c4a',0,2,18,N'<p>Complete each sentence with the correct ending, <span>A-F</span>, below. </p><p>Write the correct letter, <span>A-F</span>, in boxes 33-36 on your answer sheet.  </p>',N'',N'',N'',N'Answer choices',10,0,2,NULL,0,1657),
(N'10279458-55ac-5e70-a6d1-899df17372b5',N'e2f4570f-cb4f-567b-a014-858648d66a8b',0,3,19,N'<p>The failure of a new species of large mammals to evolve</p>',N'<p>+Question:   Interpretation: Sự thất bại trong việc tiến hóa loài thú lớn mới. </p><p>+Answer:  Dựa vào thông tin trong bài ta thấy thời gian còn quá ngắn để các loài động vật lớn mới có thể tiến hóa =&gt; vậy nguyên nhân thất bại là do chưa có đủ thời gian trôi qua. </p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là A   </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,33,NULL,0,1657),
(N'f646340c-5e7b-5170-afc4-29fdbdd2e976',N'e2f4570f-cb4f-567b-a014-858648d66a8b',0,3,19,N'<p>The extinction date of the large Australian animals</p>',N'<p>+Question: Interpretation: Ngày tuyệt chủng của các loài lớn ở Úc. </p><p>+Answer:  Dựa vào thông tin trong bài ta thấy có một vấn đề lớn là chúng ta không biết chính xác khi nào những loài động vật này tuyệt chủng =&gt; vậy ngày chúng tuyệt chủng là một yếu tố quan trọng vẫn chưa được giải quyết.</p><p> =&gt; Đáp án là F  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,34,NULL,0,1657),
(N'746688ad-47a0-5f0f-bbea-e96fff31c9ed',N'e2f4570f-cb4f-567b-a014-858648d66a8b',0,3,19,N'<p>A reduction in the number of forest fires</p>',N'<p>+Question: Interpretation: Sự giảm số lượng các vụ cháy rừng. </p><p>+Answer:  Thông tin trong bài cho biết các vụ cháy tự nhiên có lẽ ít xảy ra hơn là vì các loài thú có túi ăn cỏ lớn đã làm giảm lượng thảm thực vật đang phát triển =&gt; vì giảm thực vật dẫn đến cháy rừng ít hơn =&gt; cháy rừng ít là do có nhiều thú ăn cỏ. </p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là E   </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,35,NULL,0,1657),
(N'ad527c48-6c6d-533d-ba7e-dbce450c5a86',N'e2f4570f-cb4f-567b-a014-858648d66a8b',0,3,19,N'<p>The arrival of humans in a previously uninhabited area</p>',N'<p>+Question:  Interpretation: Sự xuất hiện của con người ở vùng chưa có người. </p><p>+Answer: Theo bài đọc, các nghiên cứu đã chỉ ra rằng khi con người hoặc các loài săn mồi khác đến những khu vực trước đây không có loài nào có giá trị sinh thái tương đương, chúng chắc chắn sẽ gây ra tác động sâu sắc, ví dụ như việc người Polynesia đã tiêu diệt hơn 70% các loài chim, và những thợ săn trên các đảo gần Nam Cực đã làm suy giảm nghiêm trọng nhiều loài hải cẩu =&gt; sự xuất hiện của con người thường chịu trách nhiệm cho một số lượng lớn các vụ tuyệt chủng. </p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là D   </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,36,NULL,0,1657),
(N'87de61ba-f7a6-5cbc-a381-c1bcf303e560',N'f3ea230e-9c5a-5ea3-b99f-b5ab195c6c4a',0,2,18,N'<p>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3?<br>In boxes 37-40 on your answer sheet, write   <br><br><span>YES            </span>if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer<br><span>NO   </span>          if statement contradicts the claims of the writer<br><span>NOT GIVEN </span>   if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this </p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',1,0,3,NULL,0,1657),
(N'1d9786b7-8671-57cc-90ff-a9cabbccc6ae',N'87de61ba-f7a6-5cbc-a381-c1bcf303e560',0,3,19,N'Mass extinction in Australia was limited to giant mammals. ',N'<p>+Question:  Interpretation: Tuyệt chủng hàng loạt ở Australia chỉ giới hạn ở thú lớn. </p><p>+Answer:  Dựa vào thông tin trong bài ta có thể thấy gần một phần ba số loài động vật có vú ở Úc đã tuyệt chủng, cùng với hầu hết các loài bò sát lớn và nhiều loài chim không biết bay  =&gt; không chỉ thú lớn mà nhiều loài cũng đã tuyệt chủng.  </p><p>=&gt; Đáp án cần điền là NO  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,37,NULL,0,1657),
(N'141024e6-4390-55bf-9b05-2e5b39738ddf',N'87de61ba-f7a6-5cbc-a381-c1bcf303e560',0,3,19,N'Australia''s climate became cooler about 50.000 years ago. ',N'<p>+Question:   Interpretation: Khí hậu Úc trở nên lạnh hơn khoảng 50.000 năm trước. </p><p>+Answer: Không có thông tin cho rằng Úc bây giờ lạnh hơn 50.000 năm trước. </p><p>=&gt; Đáp án cần điền là NOT GIVEN  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,38,NULL,0,1657),
(N'0410ad68-95c2-59c4-b01a-a052f90c15ca',N'87de61ba-f7a6-5cbc-a381-c1bcf303e560',0,3,19,N'The Wonambi snake was the biggest Australian carnivore ',N'<p>+ Question: Interpretation: Rắn wonambi là loài ăn thịt lớn nhất của Úc. </p><p>+Answers: Thông tin trong bài cho biết các loài ăn thịt lớn hơn ở Úc đều là loài bò sát và loài lớn nhất trong số này là loài rắn khổng lồ thuộc chi Wonambi =&gt; rắn wonambi là loài ăn thịt lớn nhất của Úc. </p><p>=&gt; Câu trả lời sẽ là YES  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,39,NULL,0,1657),
(N'4198fa56-af91-5405-859b-3c69b677c786',N'87de61ba-f7a6-5cbc-a381-c1bcf303e560',0,3,19,N'Europeans the extinction of some smaller Australian mammals',N'<p>+ Question: Interpretation: Người châu Âu gây ra sự tuyệt chủng của một số loài thú nhỏ ở Úc. </p><p>+Answers: Từ bài đọc ta có thể thấy việc người châu Âu đến vào cuối thế kỷ 18 đã dẫn đến một số lượng lớn các loài nhỏ bị tuyệt chủng =&gt; người châu Âu là nguyên nhân của sự tuyệt chủng của thú nhỏ. </p><p>=&gt; Câu trả lời sẽ là YES  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,40,NULL,0,1657),
(N'75c446a9-ed9c-5cf2-a294-139b8667f167',NULL,0,0,11,NULL,NULL,NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-5/iL.VOL5.8.S1652.mp3',N'Vol 5 LISTENING FULL TEST 8',0,7,1,NULL,1,1652),
(N'0268e5c9-062f-5304-873e-53be61fc0f2f',N'75c446a9-ed9c-5cf2-a294-139b8667f167',0,1,13,(CAST(N'<h2>[VOL 5] Test 8 - Section 1</h2><p><span>Now turn to Section 1. Section 1. You will hear a tourist phoning a tourist information office about holiday accommodations. First, you have some time to look at questions 1 to 4.</span></p><p>You will see that there is an example that has been done for you. On this occasion only, the conversation relating to this will be played first. Hello, Tourist Association. Can I help you? Yes, I''m going on vacation and I''ve been looking at your website about accommodations on Po Shan Island.</p><p>I''m traveling on my own and noticed that there were several kinds of accommodations there. Can you give me some more information? Sure. Well, there''s a small hotel located near the bank. It''s convenient and quite comfortable. Yes, I saw that on the website. It looks very nice. The hotel is located near the bank, so bank has been written in the space. Now we shall begin. You should answer the questions as you listen because you will not hear the recording a second time.</p><p><span>Listen carefully and answer questions 1 to 4.</span></p><p>Hello, Tourist Association. Can I help you? Yes, I''m going on vacation and I''ve been looking at your website about accommodations on Po Shan Island. I''m traveling on my own and noticed that there were several kinds of accommodations there.</p><p>Can you give me some more information? Sure. Well, there''s a small hotel located near the bank. It''s convenient and quite comfortable. Yes, I saw that on the website. It looks very nice. Do they have any planned activities there? I think it mentioned that they have a lecture about the island every morning in the hotel. I want to make sure, but they do run a tour of the island every morning after breakfast. It goes all around the island and it''s free. And then in the afternoon, guests have a chance to go out sailing if they want. And what kind of things are nearby? Things I might enjoy seeing. Isn''t there a huge market of some sort? I seem to recall something like that, where they sell lots of fresh vegetables. It''s the fish market, actually. All straight off the boats. It''s not far from the hotel. Everyone enjoys that and I''m sure you would, too. Oh, and there''s also a pottery factory. Not very big, but they produce lovely items you can buy right there on the spot at a range of very reasonable prices. And is it correct that all the rooms have a balcony? Yes, they''re very small, but some have beautiful sea views. We''d have to check if those are available.' AS nvarchar(max))+N' They do get booked up quickly. Oh, I''m sure they do. And how much are the rooms at the hotel? Well, in the high season, they''re almost $400 per person a night. But you''re lucky. We''ve just entered the low season, so they''re $2.99. A good deal. Yes, it does seem reasonable. Before you hear the rest of the conversation, you have some time to look at questions 5 to 10. Now listen and answer questions 5 to 10. But what about other accommodations, like bed and breakfast? Is there anything close to the beach? I understand it''s quite beautiful.</p><p>Ah, that''s where the island''s only bed and breakfast is, and it makes it very popular indeed. The rooms are on the small side, but the location''s fabulous. And, of course, breakfast is included. And you''ll be interested to know that every day, the owner takes any guests that are interested on a walk around the island. He''s an expert on the birds you find on the island, so it can be fascinating. Is there anything in particular to do or to see? Well, it''s a little isolated, but people who stay there rave about a vegetarian restaurant only about a mile away. I haven''t been there myself, but even dedicated meat lovers seem to love it. Anything else about the accommodations? Ah, there isn''t a television, if you require one of those. But even though they''re a little off of the beaten track, every room has an Internet connection as part of the cost, so guests find that very convenient. And what''s the room cost? Ah, for one, that would be $249. I''m afraid they don''t have off-season rates. Still, it''s pretty good. What about the youth hostel? What if I wanted to stay there? It can be a little noisy, especially at weekends, because it''s very close to the park. And the local kids use that a lot during the day.</p><p>But in the hostel, you meet lots of young people. And as for activities, every morning they even have a cookery class anyone can go to. The guests seem to really like that. And then they can apply what they learn to the meals they make for themselves at the hostel. That sounds like fun, too. Yes. And for an afternoon activity, you can go cycling. There''s a shop nearby that rents everything you need at a very low rate. It''s a great way of seeing the island. Any chance of getting any other exercise, other than playing with the local kids?</p><p>Oh, there certainly is. There''s a well-equipped gym you are welcome to use. It was just finished a couple of months ago. The hostel staff can arrange for you to get a visitor'''+N's card. It''s a great facility. How much is a private room in the hostel, then? They''ve got a number of those for just $120 a night. But again, if you''re interested, I''d contact them as soon as possible.</p>'),(CAST(N'<p><span>Now turn to Section 1. Section 1. You will hear a tourist phoning a tourist information office about holiday accommodations. First, you have some time to look at questions 1 to 4.</span></p><p>You will see that there is an example that has been done for you. On this occasion only, the conversation relating to this will be played first. Hello, Tourist Association. Can I help you? Yes, I''m going on vacation and I''ve been looking at your website about accommodations on Po Shan Island.</p><p>I''m traveling on my own and noticed that there were several kinds of accommodations there. Can you give me som