igh season, they''re almost $400 per person a night. But you''re lucky. We''ve just entered the low season, so they''re $2.99. A good deal. Yes, it does seem reasonable. Before you hear the rest of the conversation, you have some time to look at questions 5 to 10. Now listen and answer questions 5 to 10. But what about other accommodations, like bed and breakfast? Is there anything close to the beach? I understand it''s quite beautiful.</p><p>Ah, that''s where the island''s only bed and breakfast is, and it makes it very popular indeed. The rooms are on the small side, but the location''s fabulous. And, of course, breakfast is included. And you''ll be interested to know that every day, the owner takes any guests that are interested on a walk around the island. He''s an expert on the birds you find on the island, so it can be fascinating. Is there anything in particular to do or to see? Well, it''s a little isolated, but people who stay there rave about a vegetarian restaurant only about a mile away. I haven''t been there myself, but even dedicated meat lovers seem to love it. Anything else about the accommodations? Ah, there isn''t a television, if you require one of those. But even though they''re a little off of the beaten track, every room has an Internet connection as part of the cost, so guests find that very convenient. And what''s the room cost? Ah, for one, that would be $249. I''m afraid they don''t have off-season rates. Still, it''s pretty good. What about the youth hostel? What if I wanted to stay there? It can be a little noisy, especially at weekends, because it''s very close to the park. And the local kids use that a lot during the day.</p><p>But in the hostel, you meet lots of young people. And as for activities, every morning they even have a cookery class anyone can go to. The guests seem to really like that. And then they can apply what they learn to the meals they make for themselves at the hostel. That sounds like fun, too. Yes. And for an afternoon activity, you can go cycling. There''s a shop nearby that rents everything you need at a very low rate. It''s a great way of seeing the island. Any chance of getting any other exercise, other than playing with the local kids?</p><p>Oh, there certainly is. There''s a well-equipped gym you are welcome to use. It was just finished a couple of months ago. The hostel staff can arrange for you to get a visitor''s card. It''s a great facility. How '+N'much is a private room in the hostel, then? They''ve got a number of those for just $120 a night. But again, if you''re interested, I''d contact them as soon as possible.</p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-5/iL.VOL5.8.S1652.PART1.mp3',NULL,1,0,1,NULL,0,1652),
(N'f49c4be1-0f15-5e72-90a7-b602905bdf68',N'0268e5c9-062f-5304-873e-53be61fc0f2f',0,2,18,N'<p>Complete the form below.
Write <span>ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER</span> for each answer.</p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',11,0,1,NULL,0,1652),
(N'bb52e3d0-0e2d-5fc6-8b65-fc2c2a56889d',N'f49c4be1-0f15-5e72-90a7-b602905bdf68',0,3,19,N'<table border="1"><tbody><tr><td><p><span>Hotel</span></p> <p>Activities included in:</p> <ul><li><p>a free</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ of the island after breakfast</p> <ul><li><p>a chance to go</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ in the afternoon</p> <p><span>Attractions:</span></p> <ul><li><p>a fish market near the hotel</p></li></ul> <ul><li><p>a small</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ Factory</p> <p><span>Facilities and Price:</span></p> <ul><li><p>each room is equipped with a tiny</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p> <p><span>Bed and Breakfast</span></p> <ul><li><p>free breakfast</p></li></ul> <ul><li><p>can watch local</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p> <ul><li><p>a vegetarian restaurant nearby</p></li></ul> <p><span>Facilities and Price:</span></p> <ul><li><p>nо</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p> <ul><li><p></p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ is provided</p> <ul><li><p>cost: $249</p></li></ul> <p><span>Youth Hostel</span></p> <p>Activities included in:</p> <ul><li><p>a</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ class for all guests in the morning</p> <ul><li><p>in the afternoon, guests can go</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p> <p><span>Facilities and Price:</span></p> <ul><li><p>It has an updated</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ for guests to use</p> <ul><li><p>cost: $120</p></li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table>',N'<p>- Đáp án là tour. </p><p>- Nhân viên thông tin du lịch xác nhận khách sạn có một tour tham quan đảo miễn phí sau bữa sáng. Cụm “run a tour of the island” khớp trực tiếp với cấu trúc “a free ... of the island”. </p><p>- Key words: free; tour; island </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,1,NULL,0,1652),
(N'b53d3494-0191-55fa-a76c-3432c5b5223c',N'f49c4be1-0f15-5e72-90a7-b602905bdf68',0,3,19,N'Question number 2',N'<p>- Đáp án là sailing. </p><p>- Hoạt động buổi chiều được nêu rõ là đi thuyền buồm, dưới dạng lựa chọn cho khách. </p><p>- Đề dùng cấu trúc “a chance to go ...”, nên động từ dạng -ing được giữ nguyên. </p><p>- Key words: in the afternoon; go out sailing </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,2,NULL,0,1652),
(N'35d83dc8-f715-5089-b599-d3f073fa6ae9',N'f49c4be1-0f15-5e72-90a7-b602905bdf68',0,3,19,N'Question number 3',N'<p>- Đáp án là pottery. </p><p>- Điểm tham quan gần khách sạn ngoài chợ cá là nhà máy gốm nhỏ. Từ “pottery factory” xuất hiện trực tiếp trong bài nghe.</p><p>- Key words: small factory; pottery </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,3,NULL,0,1652),
(N'ba96a297-a40c-59b9-b2b2-b7bd08f2ec91',N'f49c4be1-0f15-5e72-90a7-b602905bdf68',0,3,19,N'Question number 4',N'<p>- Đáp án là balcony. </p><p>- Khách hỏi xác nhận về tiện nghi trong phòng và nhân viên khẳng định tất cả các phòng đều có ban công, dù kích thước nhỏ. - Key words: each room; balcony </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,4,NULL,0,1652),
(N'f9be0c13-722a-5b72-865b-28f1e28ce7ea',N'f49c4be1-0f15-5e72-90a7-b602905bdf68',0,3,19,N'Question number 5',N'<p>- Đáp án là birds. </p><p>- Khách lưu trú tại B&amp;B có thể tham gia đi bộ cùng chủ nhà, người này là chuyên gia về chim trên đảo, nên khách có thể quan sát chim địa phương. </p><p>- Key words: expert; birds </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,5,NULL,0,1652),
(N'3b643f7e-e269-5921-bcac-1ea7853885d2',N'f49c4be1-0f15-5e72-90a7-b602905bdf68',0,3,19,N'Question number 6',N'<p>- Đáp án là television. </p><p>- Nhược điểm của B&amp;B là không có TV, dù có Internet miễn phí. Câu hỏi hỏi “no ...”, nên điền đúng danh từ bị thiếu. </p><p>- Key words: there isn''t; television </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,6,NULL,0,1652),
(N'59209382-7ac8-5697-92f3-4bc5857b5513',N'f49c4be1-0f15-5e72-90a7-b602905bdf68',0,3,19,N'Question number 7',N'<p>- Đáp án là internet. </p><p>- Dù không có TV, mỗi phòng vẫn được cung cấp Internet miễn phí, đã bao gồm trong giá phòng.</p><p> - Key words: provided; Internet connection </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,7,NULL,0,1652),
(N'045fa710-f6a1-5876-b4f1-f7893488fed5',N'f49c4be1-0f15-5e72-90a7-b602905bdf68',0,3,19,N'Question number 8',N'<p>- Đáp án là cookery. Youth hostel có lớp học nấu ăn vào buổi sáng, mở cho tất cả khách lưu trú. </p><p>- Cụm “cookery class” được nhắc rõ ràng. </p><p>- Key words: class; cookery </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,8,NULL,0,1652),
(N'2887113a-c004-5146-ab62-eb0337e18d84',N'f49c4be1-0f15-5e72-90a7-b602905bdf68',0,3,19,N'Question number 9',N'<p>- Đáp án là cycling. </p><p>- Hoạt động buổi chiều tại youth hostel là đi xe đạp, với cửa hàng cho thuê đồ gần đó. </p><p>- Key words: afternoon activity; cycling </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,9,NULL,0,1652),
(N'3c7740e6-cf24-5673-838e-2cf75c455127',N'f49c4be1-0f15-5e72-90a7-b602905bdf68',0,3,19,N'Question number 10',N'<p>- Đáp án là gym. </p><p>- Youth hostel có phòng tập thể dục hiện đại, mới được hoàn thành gần đây và khách có thể sử dụng. </p><p>- Key words: well-equipped; gym </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,10,NULL,0,1652),
(N'bb3c7538-0dcf-5a87-a8e0-66f8d380cc37',N'75c446a9-ed9c-5cf2-a294-139b8667f167',0,1,14,(CAST(N'<h2>Plan of the gym</h2><p><span><span>You will hear an employee of a gym giving a talk to new members about the gym. First, you have some time to look at questions 11 to 14. Now listen carefully and answer questions 11 to 14.</span></span></p><p>Welcome to the tour of our gym, nothing but fitness. No doubt you know a little of what our gym has to give in terms of fitness, but as you''ll discover, we have much more than just running machines and weights on offer. The gyms open from 5.30am, nice and early in the morning, to 10pm at night. So these hours give you plenty of time to fit in your workouts in our weights and cardio rooms or with your personal trainers. Now obviously, reception is open whenever the gym is. We have a childcare centre on site for mums and dads wanting to fit a workout into your busy day, but it''s only open in the mornings, so you''ll need to plan your workout around that. For those of you too busy to eat properly at home, there''s a cafe on site offering healthy and delicious meals that start serving as soon as the gym opens and doesn''t shut until we close at night. Of course, to work out comfortably, you need suitable clothing. </p><p>We have a shop here for those of you who''d like to pick up some new shoes or workout gear. The staff there will be happy to kit you out from midday onwards, so do have a look at what''s on offer. We''re a modern gym, and we''re always updating our facilities. Actually, the gym''s just replaced all our treadmills with the latest models, so if you''re a runner, try them out. After you finish your run, you might want to improve your flexibility by taking one of our yoga classes in the comfortable yoga studio or relax in the traditional sauna. </p><p>You''ll notice the change rooms when you enter the gym. They''ve just been renovated and are now very luxurious and spacious. As the gym''s in the centre of the city, parking''s always a problem, even with our free passes for members. You''ll be glad to hear that an overhaul of the car park''s planned for next year.</p><p><span><span>Before you hear the rest of the talk, you have some time to look at questions 15 to 20. Now listen and answer questions 15 to 20.</span></span></p><p>Now, let''s talk about where things are. We''re standing in the entrance to the building. Some of you have meetings with your personal trainers today. To find them, walk past the right side of reception and into the cardio studio. Their office is on the right, just after you go past the manager''s o' AS nvarchar(max))+N'ffice. It''s a warm day, so why not head to the pool? The easiest way to get there is from the entrance, go around the left side of reception and into the cardio studio, and then you''ll see that the third door on the left is the way into the shop. Go into the shop and you''ll see there are two more doors. You want the one opposite you as you walk in. Go through that door and you''ll see the pool, which runs along the west side of the building. </p><p>Stretching after exercise is essential, so you''ll need the stretch area. To find it, from the entrance, head to the back of the cardio studio. You''ll see two doors facing you, and it''s the one on the right. As we''ve only got men here today, I''ll point out only where your change rooms are. From the entrance, go up the left side of the cardio studio and you want the middle door. That''s the room just before you reach the shop. If you''re looking to bulk up, the weights room will be important. It''s easy to find. From the entrance, walk past the left side of reception and through the cardio studio to the back of the building. The weights room is through the door on the left. The first aid room is beside it, although hopefully you won''t need to go in there. After this, you might want to have a drink in our cafe. Go to the shop, and this time take the door to your right, not the one opposite, and this leads to the cafe with a nice view of the river.</p>'),(CAST(N'<p><span><span>You will hear an employee of a gym giving a talk to new members about the gym. First, you have some time to look at questions 11 to 14. Now listen carefully and answer questions 11 to 14.</span></span></p><p>Welcome to the tour of our gym, nothing but fitness. No doubt you know a little of what our gym has to give in terms of fitness, but as you''ll discover, we have much more than just running machines and weights on offer. The gyms open from 5.30am, nice and early in the morning, to 10pm at night. So these hours give you plenty of time to fit in your workouts in our weights and cardio rooms or with your personal trainers. Now obviously, reception is open whenever the gym is. We have a childcare centre on site for mums and dads wanting to fit a workout into your busy day, but it''s only open in the mornings, so you''ll need to plan your workout around that. For those of you too busy to eat properly at home, there''s a cafe on site offering healthy and delicious meals that start serving as soon as the gym opens and doesn''t shut until we close at night. Of course, to work out comfortably, you need suitable clothing. </p><p>We have a shop here for those of you who''d like to pick up some new shoes or workout gear. The staff there will be happy to kit you out from midday onwards, so do have a look at what''s on offer. We''re a modern gym, and we''re always updating our facilities. Actually, the gym''s just replaced all our treadmills with the latest models, so if you''re a runner, try them out. After you finish your run, you might want to improve your flexibility by taking one of our yoga classes in the comfortable yoga studio or relax in the traditional sauna. </p><p>You''ll notice the change rooms when you enter the gym. They''ve just been renovated and are now very luxurious and spacious. As the gym''s in the centre of the city, parking''s always a problem, even with our free passes for members. You''ll be glad to hear that an overhaul of the car park''s planned for next year.</p><p><span><span>Before you hear the rest of the talk, you have some time to look at questions 15 to 20. Now listen and answer questions 15 to 20.</span></span></p><p>Now, let''s talk about where things are. We''re standing in the entrance to the building. Some of you have meetings with your personal trainers today. To find them, walk past the right side of reception and into the cardio studio. Their office is on the right, just after you go past the manager''s office. It''s a warm day, ' AS nvarchar(max))+N'so why not head to the pool? The easiest way to get there is from the entrance, go around the left side of reception and into the cardio studio, and then you''ll see that the third door on the left is the way into the shop. Go into the shop and you''ll see there are two more doors. You want the one opposite you as you walk in. Go through that door and you''ll see the pool, which runs along the west side of the building. </p><p>Stretching after exercise is essential, so you''ll need the stretch area. To find it, from the entrance, head to the back of the cardio studio. You''ll see two doors facing you, and it''s the one on the right. As we''ve only got men here today, I''ll point out only where your change rooms are. From the entrance, go up the left side of the cardio studio and you want the middle door. That''s the room just before you reach the shop. If you''re looking to bulk up, the weights room will be important. It''s easy to find. From the entrance, walk past the left side of reception and through the cardio studio to the back of the building. The weights room is through the door on the left. The first aid room is beside it, although hopefully you won''t need to go in there. After this, you might want to have a drink in our cafe. Go to the shop, and this time take the door to your right, not the one opposite, and this leads to the cafe with a nice view of the river.</p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-5/iL.VOL5.8.S1652.PART2.mp3',NULL,1,0,2,NULL,0,1652),
(N'8eda6dbb-5641-5fd2-9d21-e0d7d1c32fe9',N'bb3c7538-0dcf-5a87-a8e0-66f8d380cc37',0,2,18,N'<p>Choose <span>TWO</span> letters, <span>A-E.</span></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',5,0,1,NULL,0,1652),
(N'078ba0e0-9c67-5f98-ab18-40549bfe40b5',N'8eda6dbb-5641-5fd2-9d21-e0d7d1c32fe9',0,3,19,N'<p>Which <span>TWO</span> parts of the gym are closed for part of the day?</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là D (the childcare centre). Bài nghe nói rõ childcare centre chỉ mở buổi sáng, tức là đóng cửa trong một phần của ngày. </p><p>- Các khu khác như cafe hay reception đều mở suốt giờ hoạt động của phòng gym. </p><p>- Key words: only open in the mornings; childcare centre </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,11,NULL,0,1652),
(N'6d5ff53d-2291-58da-9296-f22b3f73dd2a',N'8eda6dbb-5641-5fd2-9d21-e0d7d1c32fe9',0,3,19,N'<p>Which <span>TWO</span> parts of the gym are closed for part of the day?</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án thứ hai là E (the shop). </p><p>- Cửa hàng chỉ mở từ giữa trưa trở đi, nên cũng bị đóng trong một phần của ngày. Điều này khớp với yêu cầu câu hỏi về “closed for part of the day”. </p><p>- Key words: from midday onwards; shop </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,12,NULL,0,1652),
