(N'80b25384-c2cf-5cf8-9286-935c7f538bfc',N'36aa8db2-29e9-5098-a905-3f49a9cdb3ca',0,3,19,N'<h3>The New Zealand artist Will Burton</h3><p><span>General information</span></p><p>• makes art from pieces of rubbish</p><p>• started this technique in the 1950s when the art was traditional</p><p><span>Childhood in Moa Point, Wellington</span></p><p>• started with }{SPACE}{ but found it too limited</p><p>• began to experiment with using rubbish</p><p>• made sculptures from waste found in the home, e.g. glass and }{SPACE}{ </p><p>• used ''natural'' waste materials such as }{SPACE}{ </p><p>• collected things from the dump, especially }{SPACE}{ items</p><p>• his }{SPACE}{ of old light bulbs are in the Wellington Museum today</p><p><span>At Art School</span></p><p>• developed his formal skills, e.g. learning how to use a }{SPACE}{ </p><p>• making }{SPACE}{ could have been his alternative career</p><p>• began a lifelong interest in }{SPACE}{ </p><p><span>Other Themes of his Work</span></p><p>• interested in how appearances are affected by light</p><p>• a critical observer of modern society</p><p>• uses written words to express his }{SPACE}{ </p><p>• his work gets depth from the feeling of }{SPACE}{ he expresses</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là painting.
- Thời thơ ấu, Will Burton
bắt đầu bằng hội họa nhưng
sớm từ bỏ vì cảm thấy nó
hạn chế trí tưởng tượng.
- Điều này dẫn trực tiếp đến
việc ông thử nghiệm vật
liệu khác.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,31,NULL,0,1652),
(N'2ca041e8-1750-5946-a5c9-7f7facec188d',N'36aa8db2-29e9-5098-a905-3f49a9cdb3ca',0,3,19,N'Question number 32',N'<p>- Đáp án là plastic.
- Ngoài thủy tinh, Burton
