(N'd02558ec-1a09-5a73-b19b-bdd1030df360',NULL,0,0,11,NULL,NULL,NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-5/iL.VOL5.9.S1651.mp3',N'Vol 5 LISTENING FULL TEST 9',0,7,1,NULL,1,1651),
(N'aa9ddc70-3a31-5ef1-b34f-f2226f9c4b19',N'd02558ec-1a09-5a73-b19b-bdd1030df360',0,1,13,(CAST(N'<h2>Part-time work in a charity shop</h2><p><span>Part 1. You will hear a telephone conversation between the manager of a shop run for charity and a young woman who is interested in volunteering. First you have some time to look at questions 1 to 4. Now listen carefully and answer questions 1 to 4. </span></p><p>Good morning. Charity Links. Mark speaking. Oh, good morning. My name''s Joanne Richardson and I''m ringing about the advert I saw on your city centre shop window. Asking for part-time volunteers to help in our shops? That''s right. Well, I''m interested in helping and wonder if I could ask a few questions. Of course. I understand your charity helps local people with housing problems, is that right? Yes, though it now focuses exclusively on helping the homeless. Oh, right. And I was just wondering, I live in the north of the city, do you have any shops in this area? Yes, we have one on Roslyn Road. Is that near the museum? Yes, we''re in the large white building next door. I know it. Yes, and it''s within easy walking distance for me. And do you have any vacancies for volunteers in that store? Well, we certainly will have very soon. Two of our Roslyn Road volunteers, a couple, are moving from the area on the 28th of February, so we''ll definitely have a gap starting the week after on the 5th of March. Great. That would suit me really well. And do you need people every day of the week? Well, we don''t open on Sundays and Mondays. At the moment, most of our volunteers prefer to work on Saturdays, but the two people we''re losing worked on Wednesday, so that''s a key day we need to fill. Right. I''ve made a note of that. </p><p><span>Before you hear the rest of the conversation, you have some time to look at questions 5 to 10. Now listen and answer questions 5 to 10.</span></p><p>And what type of work do you need people to do? Well, there''s lots of different tasks that you might not think of. So, for example, all the different things for sale have to have the prices on. Yes, sure. And I imagine you also have a lot of stuff that''s been donated. Absolutely. And that all needs sorting, particularly the clothing. Oh, right. I guess that''s a big job. It varies, but sometimes we get 50 or 60 bags of donations a day. Gosh. And then another area we need help in is looking at all the toys that have been donated and making sure none of the bits are missing. Oh, that sounds like fun. And what about personal qualities? I suppose you will want volunteers who are very flexibl' AS nvarchar(max))+N'e. Well, not necessarily because, you know, you''ll be part of a team. More important is for people to be reliable. We''ve got to be sure that people will turn up and do the work we ask. Yes, I can see that that''s really important for you. Yes. And I suppose it''s good if you''re confident. Well, that''s certainly an added bonus when you''re meeting the public. Sounds great. Well, I''m certainly interested in giving it a go. Great. So we''ll need you to fill in a form. You can pick one up from one of our shops or download it from our website. What''s the address? It''s www.giving.org.uk. OK, I''ve got it. Good. And then when you''ve found the website, on the homepage, click on the tab called Applications. Right. Well, thanks ever so much. I''ll try to get the form sent to you in the next couple of days. Thanks. We look forward to hearing from you. </p><p><span>Turn to part two. Part two. </span></p>'),(CAST(N'<p><span>Part 1. You will hear a telephone conversation between the manager of a shop run for charity and a young woman who is interested in volunteering. First you have some time to look at questions 1 to 4. Now listen carefully and answer questions 1 to 4. </span></p><p>Good morning. Charity Links. Mark speaking. Oh, good morning. My name''s Joanne Richardson and I''m ringing about the advert I saw on your city centre shop window. Asking for part-time volunteers to help in our shops? That''s right. Well, I''m interested in helping and wonder if I could ask a few questions. Of course. I understand your charity helps local people with housing problems, is that right? Yes, though it now focuses exclusively on helping the homeless. Oh, right. And I was just wondering, I live in the north of the city, do you have any shops in this area? Yes, we have one on Roslyn Road. Is that near the museum? Yes, we''re in the large white building next door. I know it. Yes, and it''s within easy walking distance for me. And do you have any vacancies for volunteers in that store? Well, we certainly will have very soon. Two of our Roslyn Road volunteers, a couple, are moving from the area on the 28th of February, so we''ll definitely have a gap starting the week after on the 5th of March. Great. That would suit me really well. And do you need people every day of the week? Well, we don''t open on Sundays and Mondays. At the moment, most of our volunteers prefer to work on Saturdays, but the two people we''re losing worked on Wednesday, so that''s a key day we need to fill. Right. I''ve made a note of that. </p><p><span>Before you hear the rest of the conversation, you have some time to look at questions 5 to 10. Now listen and answer questions 5 to 10.</span></p><p>And what type of work do you need people to do? Well, there''s lots of different tasks that you might not think of. So, for example, all the different things for sale have to have the prices on. Yes, sure. And I imagine you also have a lot of stuff that''s been donated. Absolutely. And that all needs sorting, particularly the clothing. Oh, right. I guess that''s a big job. It varies, but sometimes we get 50 or 60 bags of donations a day. Gosh. And then another area we need help in is looking at all the toys that have been donated and making sure none of the bits are missing. Oh, that sounds like fun. And what about personal qualities? I suppose you will want volunteers who are very flexible. Well, not necessarily because, you kno' AS nvarchar(max))+N'w, you''ll be part of a team. More important is for people to be reliable. We''ve got to be sure that people will turn up and do the work we ask. Yes, I can see that that''s really important for you. Yes. And I suppose it''s good if you''re confident. Well, that''s certainly an added bonus when you''re meeting the public. Sounds great. Well, I''m certainly interested in giving it a go. Great. So we''ll need you to fill in a form. You can pick one up from one of our shops or download it from our website. What''s the address? It''s www.giving.org.uk. OK, I''ve got it. Good. And then when you''ve found the website, on the homepage, click on the tab called Applications. Right. Well, thanks ever so much. I''ll try to get the form sent to you in the next couple of days. Thanks. We look forward to hearing from you. </p><p><span>Turn to part two. Part two. </span></p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-5/iL.VOL5.9.S1651.PART1.mp3',NULL,1,0,1,NULL,0,1651),
(N'060e37ad-2448-5a9a-907f-ec3a228a5107',N'aa9ddc70-3a31-5ef1-b34f-f2226f9c4b19',0,2,18,N'<p>Complete the notes below. </p><p>Write <span>ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER </span>for each answer </p>',N'',N'',N'',N'Part-time work in a charity shop',11,0,1,NULL,0,1651),
(N'941a55f0-00bd-5ac7-8b0d-5eefa9281e4a',N'060e37ad-2448-5a9a-907f-ec3a228a5107',0,3,19,N'<h3>Part-time work in a charity shop</h3><table border="1"><tbody><tr><td><p>Manager''s name Mark</p> <p><span>General information</span></p> <ul><li><p>The charity supports people who are</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p> <ul><li><p>There is a shop next to the</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ (on Roslyn Rd)</p> <ul><li><p>New staff are needed from</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ March</p> <ul><li><p>Day of the week when new staff are needed:</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p> <p><span>Areas of work</span></p> <ul><li><p>Putting</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ on items</p> <ul><li><p>Sorting donations, especially</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p> <ul><li><p>Checking</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p> <p><span>Personal qualities</span></p> <ul><li><p>Most important - must be</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p> <p>Also prefer people who are }{SPACE}{ </p> <p><span>Website</span></p> <ul><li><p>www.giving.org.uk</p></li></ul> <ul><li><p>Can find the form on the website - click on</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ tab</p></td></tr></tbody></table>',N'<p>- Đáp án là homeless vì người quản lý nói rất rõ rằng tổ chức hiện chỉ tập trung giúp người vô gia cư.  </p><p>- Ban đầu cô gái nhắc đến “people with housing problems”, nhưng ngay sau đó người nói sửa lại và nhấn mạnh “focuses exclusively on helping the homeless”.  </p><p>- Từ khóa quan trọng là focuses exclusively và the homeless, cho thấy đây là thông tin chính xác cần điền.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,1,NULL,0,1651),
(N'2c83113f-59d6-5627-8d3f-b7e2fb10ecd0',N'060e37ad-2448-5a9a-907f-ec3a228a5107',0,3,19,N'Question number 2',N'<p>- Đáp án là museum.  </p><p>- Trước đó người hỏi hỏi rõ “Is that near the museum?”, và người quản lý xác nhận là ở ngay tòa nhà trắng bên cạnh.  </p><p>- Cụm “next door” cho thấy vị trí của cửa hàng nằm ngay cạnh bảo tàng.  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,2,NULL,0,1651),
(N'1dfb5592-a7bb-5c79-a3f6-b9803f803c3b',N'060e37ad-2448-5a9a-907f-ec3a228a5107',0,3,19,N'Question number 3',N'<p>- Đáp án là 5th (March).  </p><p>- Hai tình nguyện viên rời đi vào 28/2, nên vị trí trống bắt đầu từ tuần sau, tức ngày 5/3.  </p><p>- Từ khóa quan trọng là starting the week after và 5th of March.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,3,NULL,0,1651),
(N'5bc7ee11-446c-51a4-9413-b9a37e31d145',N'060e37ad-2448-5a9a-907f-ec3a228a5107',0,3,19,N'Question number 4',N'<p>- Đáp án là Wednesday.  </p><p>- Dù có người làm vào thứ Bảy, nhưng người quản lý nhấn mạnh thứ Tư là ngày đang thiếu người.  </p><p>- Từ khóa quan trọng: key day, worked on Wednesday.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,4,NULL,0,1651),
(N'53eea15b-e8a2-5bc7-8b92-007d1f8f4ec6',N'060e37ad-2448-5a9a-907f-ec3a228a5107',0,3,19,N'Question number 5',N'<p>- Đáp án là prices. </p><p>- Người nói giải thích một trong các công việc là dán giá cho đồ bán.  </p><p>- Cụm quan trọng là have to have the prices on, cho thấy đây là nhiệm vụ bắt buộc.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,5,NULL,0,1651),
(N'afa1c1cc-2108-5c2c-aa24-f15eba6c1ab5',N'060e37ad-2448-5a9a-907f-ec3a228a5107',0,3,19,N'Question number 6',N'<p>- Đáp án là clothing.  </p><p>- Khi nói về đồ quyên góp, người nói nhấn mạnh đặc biệt là quần áo cần được phân loại.  </p><p>- Từ khóa là particularly the clothing.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,6,NULL,0,1651),
(N'db97657b-4047-5af3-a3bc-c35d006faf65',N'060e37ad-2448-5a9a-907f-ec3a228a5107',0,3,19,N'Question number 7',N'<p>- Đáp án là toys.  </p><p>- Công việc ở đây là kiểm tra đồ chơi để chắc chắn không bị thiếu bộ phận.  </p><p>- Key word: toys, none of the bits are missing.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,7,NULL,0,1651),
(N'c3f2a65f-6ffe-5e06-b1be-d8fcf0fed49c',N'060e37ad-2448-5a9a-907f-ec3a228a5107',0,3,19,N'Question number 8',N'<p>- Đáp án là reliable.  </p><p>- Người quản lý nhấn mạnh đây là phẩm chất quan trọng nhất, còn quan trọng hơn cả sự linh hoạt.  </p><p>- Từ khóa: More important, reliable.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,8,NULL,0,1651),
(N'818883e3-2ed1-57df-bc49-88cb49d68942',N'060e37ad-2448-5a9a-907f-ec3a228a5107',0,3,19,N'Question number 9',N'<p>- Đáp án là confident.  </p><p>- Đây không phải yêu cầu bắt buộc mà là một điểm cộng, đặc biệt khi tiếp xúc với khách hàng.  </p><p>- Từ khóa: good if, confident.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,9,NULL,0,1651),
(N'2fad121b-cfb0-5cc1-858c-fdab79a1d23c',N'060e37ad-2448-5a9a-907f-ec3a228a5107',0,3,19,N'Question number 10',N'<p>- Đáp án là Applications.  </p><p>- Người nói hướng dẫn rất rõ: vào website và nhấn vào tab có tên này để tải form.  </p><p>- Đây là thông tin trực tiếp, không cần suy luận.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,10,NULL,0,1651),
(N'3084ca78-2e9b-5a60-a236-b036ca65e5ff',N'd02558ec-1a09-5a73-b19b-bdd1030df360',0,1,14,N'<h2>[VOL 5] Test 9 - Section 2</h2><p><span>Part 2. You will hear a tour leader giving information about a bus tour. First, you have some time to look at questions 11 to 15. Now listen and answer questions 11 to 15. </span></p><p>Thank you for choosing City Tours. The reason so many people choose our tours when visiting this city is because you can design your tour to suit your own interests. Your all-day pass entitles you to board our bus at any stop and stay as long as you like at each place. The all-day bus pass costs $18 for adults. Children between the ages of 5 and 12 pay half the adult fare and children under 5 ride for free. Our buses run every hour on the half-hour starting at 8:30 a.m. Our most popular tour is the Center City Tour, which goes to all the major attractions in the center of the city. </p><p>From the starting point here at the tour bus office, the bus goes to the first stop, Hill Park. As you may guess, this park is located at the top of a small hill. The next stop is the fishing docks. Following that, the bus goes on to the third stop, Bay Bridge, located at the foot of the bridge which crosses the bay. The fourth stop is in the shopping district, then the fifth and last stop is at Green Street. </p><p><span>Before you hear the rest of the talk, you have some time to look at questions 16 to 20. Now listen and answer questions 16 to 20. </span></p><p>There are many interesting things to do and see on the Center City Tour. At the first stop, you can enjoy a spectacular view of the bay, the city, and especially the fishing docks, which are located at the foot of the hill. At the second stop, you can walk around and look at the boats. Fresh fish from the bays are also for sale here since this is a place where the fishermen bring in their catch. The next stop here. You can eat fresh fish here, prepared in the traditional local way. The fourth stop is, of course, where you can do your shopping. Don''t miss the opportunity to purchase some of our city''s famous handmade baskets. You would want to take several home as souvenirs of your visit to our city. </p><p>Finally, the last stop on the tour. You can visit one of the oldest buildings in our city, the theater. This building was built over 400 years ago and is still used today as a place to see plays, musicals, and other performances, as well as our annual film festival. </p><p><span>That is the end of part two. You now have half a minute to check your answers.</span>
</p>',N'<p><span>Part 2. You will hear a tour leader giving information about a bus tour. First, you have some time to look at questions 11 to 15. Now listen and answer questions 11 to 15. </span></p><p>Thank you for choosing City Tours. The reason so many people choose our tours when visiting this city is because you can design your tour to suit your own interests. Your all-day pass entitles you to board our bus at any stop and stay as long as you like at each place. The all-day bus pass costs $18 for adults. Children between the ages of 5 and 12 pay half the adult fare and children under 5 ride for free. Our buses run every hour on the half-hour starting at 8:30 a.m. Our most popular tour is the Center City Tour, which goes to all the major attractions in the center of the city. </p><p>From the starting point here at the tour bus office, the bus goes to the first stop, Hill Park. As you may guess, this park is located at the top of a small hill. The next stop is the fishing docks. Following that, the bus goes on to the third stop, Bay Bridge, located at the foot of the bridge which crosses the bay. The fourth stop is in the shopping district, then the fifth and last stop is at Green Street. </p><p><span>Before you hear the rest of the talk, you have some time to look at questions 16 to 20. Now listen and answer questions 16 to 20. </span></p><p>There are many interesting things to do and see on the Center City Tour. At the first stop, you can enjoy a spectacular view of the bay, the city, and especially the fishing docks, which are located at the foot of the hill. At the second stop, you can walk around and look at the boats. Fresh fish from the bays are also for sale here since this is a place where the fishermen bring in their catch. The next stop here. You can eat fresh fish here, prepared in the traditional local way. The fourth stop is, of course, where you can do your shopping. Don''t miss the opportunity to purchase some of our city''s famous handmade baskets. You would want to take several home as souvenirs of your visit to our city. </p><p>Finally, the last stop on the tour. You can visit one of the oldest buildings in our city, the theater. This building was built over 400 years ago and is still used today as a place to see plays, musicals, and other performances, as well as our annual film festival. </p><p><span>That is the end of part two. You now have half a minute to check your answers.</span>
