(N'ab63c4ff-8565-5e16-8972-f80a62f3a8a3',N'abb3ecef-aae4-56b1-8e89-4d4abeeaf846',0,3,19,N'<h3>Research on A Chain Store in the UK</h3><p><span>Initial expansion</span></p><ul><li><p>The company expanded by opening more</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ to increase market share in England.</p><ul><li><p>They could raise capital by reducing the number of branches in southern</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p><p><span>Consultation</span></p><ul><li><p>They shut down the</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ of the convenience stores in Oxford.</p><ul><li><p>Over 200 staff had to be transferred and</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p><ul><li><p>A new brand image was established to focus on selling</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p><p><span>The future way</span></p><ul><li><p>A</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ was assigned to hold each discussion.</p><ul><li><p>Retail stores should be flexible in making</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p><ul><li><p>Changes should be introduced in</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ so that the staff can become accustomed the new rules.</p><p><span>Conclusion</span></p><ul><li><p>Be open-minded about the</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ for expansion they choose.</p><ul><li><p>Companies have saved costs by changing the structure of the</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ department.</p>',N'<p>Đáp án là petrol stations. Người nói mô tả chiến lược mở rộng ban đầu là mở thêm các trạm xăng trên khắp cả nước để tăng thị phần ở England. Key words: open: mở, petrol stations: trạm xăng, market share: thị phần. Scripts: “open petrol stations across the country” - “mở trạm xăng trên khắp cả nước”</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,31,NULL,0,1646),
(N'bc83f327-ee58-5dc0-b5a5-e9aed74f90a2',N'abb3ecef-aae4-56b1-8e89-4d4abeeaf846',0,3,19,N'Question number 32',N'<p>Đáp án là Scotland. Người nói nêu rõ họ tăng nguồn vốn bằng cách đóng các trạm kém lợi nhuận ở miền nam Scotland để dồn nguồn lực cho các trạm có lãi hơn. Key words: less profitable: kém lợi nhuận, closing: đóng, south: miền nam. Scripts: “south of Scotland” - “miền nam Scotland”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,32,NULL,0,1646),
(N'ddd11509-469b-5c10-b3be-d5ade90c7aa5',N'abb3ecef-aae4-56b1-8e89-4d4abeeaf846',0,3,19,N'Question number 33',N'<p>Đáp án là head office. Phần tư vấn nhắc trực tiếp việc công ty đóng trụ sở chính của hệ thống convenience stores ở Oxford theo khuyến nghị của consultants. Key words: consultants: tư vấn, closed: đóng, head office: trụ sở chính. Scripts: “closed the head office” - “đóng trụ sở chính”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,33,NULL,0,1646),
(N'00967fa5-cd01-5459-b6ee-c8bd7f13c567',N'abb3ecef-aae4-56b1-8e89-4d4abeeaf846',0,3,19,N'Question number 34',N'<p>Đáp án là retrained. Người nói giải thích để tránh sa thải, họ chuyển hơn 200 nhân viên sang nơi khác và đào tạo lại để làm nhiệm vụ mới. Key words: transferred: điều chuyển, retrained: đào tạo lại, new roles: vai trò mới. Scripts: “retrained them” - “đào tạo lại họ”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,34,NULL,0,1646),
(N'e3066459-5b80-5362-a732-5f4d3739a211',N'abb3ecef-aae4-56b1-8e89-4d4abeeaf846',0,3,19,N'Question number 35',N'<p>Đáp án là fresh produce. Người nói nhấn mạnh công ty xây dựng hình ảnh thương hiệu mới bằng cách tập trung bán nông sản tươi được trồng bởi nông dân địa phương, nhằm gắn kết cộng đồng. Key words: brand image: hình ảnh thương hiệu, focus on selling: tập trung bán, local farmers: nông dân địa phương. Scripts: “selling fresh produce” - “bán nông sản tươi”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,35,NULL,0,1646),
(N'4e3c94c9-4e75-5d5b-a099-096bc0c04270',N'abb3ecef-aae4-56b1-8e89-4d4abeeaf846',0,3,19,N'Question number 36',N'<p>Đáp án là manager. Người nói nêu rõ mỗi manager được giao nhiệm vụ tổ chức các buổi thảo luận để thu thập ý kiến và mối quan ngại của nhân viên. Key words: assigned: được giao, manager: quản lý, discussions: thảo luận. Scripts: “every manager” - “mỗi quản lý”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,36,NULL,0,1646),
(N'c594428d-6f44-5860-a083-a9cc38b4b632',N'abb3ecef-aae4-56b1-8e89-4d4abeeaf846',0,3,19,N'Question number 37',N'<p>Đáp án là profit-making strategies. Người nói đề xuất các cửa hàng bán lẻ cần linh hoạt trong chiến lược tạo lợi nhuận, từ đó giúp hoạt động thương mại hiệu quả hơn và tăng hài lòng của nhân viên. Key words: flexibility: linh hoạt, profit-making: tạo lợi nhuận, retail stores: cửa hàng bán lẻ. Scripts: “profit-making strategies” - “chiến lược tạo lợi nhuận”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,37,NULL,0,1646),
(N'3c60c6a8-8c5e-5cf8-a205-2d03a30f891e',N'abb3ecef-aae4-56b1-8e89-4d4abeeaf846',0,3,19,N'Question number 38',N'<p>Đáp án là stages. Người nói khẳng định thay đổi cần được triển khai theo từng giai đoạn để nhân viên quen dần với quy định mới, tránh sốc thay đổi. Key words: introduced: đưa vào áp dụng, stages: từng giai đoạn, familiarize: làm quen. Scripts: “in stages” - “theo từng giai đoạn”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,38,NULL,0,1646),
(N'033e7dac-2957-58bb-8e4a-2d73cff00a39',N'abb3ecef-aae4-56b1-8e89-4d4abeeaf846',0,3,19,N'Question number 39',N'<p>Đáp án là case studies. Ở phần kết, người nói khuyên nên cởi mở với các case studies phù hợp khi lựa chọn hướng mở rộng, vì chúng giúp rút kinh nghiệm và ra quyết định ít cảm tính hơn. Key words: open-minded: cởi mở, case studies: nghiên cứu tình huống, expansion: mở rộng. Scripts: “Research suitable case studies” - “nghiên cứu các case study phù hợp”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,39,NULL,0,1646),
(N'29c3f3d9-149c-502d-9b2f-43802ba95faf',N'abb3ecef-aae4-56b1-8e89-4d4abeeaf846',0,3,19,N'Question number 40',N'<p>Đáp án là sales. Trong đoạn nghe cậu gửi, phần “saved costs by changing the structure of the 40 ____ department” không được đọc trọn câu, nhưng nội dung có nhắc trực tiếp “sales staff”, nên t điền theo mạch hợp lý là sales department. Key words: sales staff: nhân viên bán hàng, structure: cấu trúc, department: phòng ban. Scripts: “sales staff” - “nhân viên bán hàng”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,40,NULL,0,1646),
(N'13fd5830-b62f-5aea-931d-4e3dd22f9dc1',NULL,0,0,11,NULL,NULL,NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-2/iL.VOL2.5.S1644.mp3',N'Vol 2 LISTENING FULL TEST 5',0,7,1,NULL,1,1644),
(N'f9f72c5b-2258-5ca5-923c-78189d04bcba',N'13fd5830-b62f-5aea-931d-4e3dd22f9dc1',0,1,13,(CAST(N'<h2>[VOL 2] Information about School Registration</h2><p>Part one.  You will hear a telephone conversation between a man looking for information on registering his child for school and a school district employee.  First, you have some time to look at questions one to six.  Now listen carefully and answer questions one to six.  Good afternoon, Lemon Grove School District.  Hi, I''m calling for information on school registration. I think my son should attend one of the schools in your district.  What grade will your son be entering?  He just turned five. He''ll be starting school this year.  Oh, okay. One moment, please.  I''ll get the information for kindergarten registration.  Okay, thank you.  Can you give me your address?  Yes, it''s 7418 DiMarino Street.  Okay, thanks. Yes, at that address, your child should attend Monterey Heights Elementary.  Can you spell that, please?  Yes, it''s M-O-N-T-E-R-E-Y Heights.  Great.  So how do I register him?  We have registration at each school site Monday through Thursday from 9 to 1. Oh, no, sorry, 1:30. You''ll need to pick up a kindergarten registration packet from the school beforehand, though.  It has all the forms you''ll need to fill out.  Can I pick up the packet any time?  Sure. The school office is usually open till 3:30 in the afternoons.  Oh, no. I can''t really get there that early.  Well, the school has late office hours until 4 on Thursdays, or I think you can pick up a packet in the school library any day before 5.  Oh, okay.  I''ll stop by there some day this week, then, before 5.  Can you tell me what forms we''ll need?  I''m sure you need his immunization records.  Yes, those, and we also need a general health history signed by your child''s doctor, a form filled out by the dentist, emergency contact information, and a residency verification form with proof of residence.  Oh, and an original birth certificate.  Okay, that shouldn''t be a problem.  Can I ask one more question?  Sure, go ahead.  I was wondering about before- and after-school care.  Do you provide transportation after school?  No, unfortunately, we don''t. Parents or caregivers need to pick up the children.  There is, however, an on-site licensed daycare for working parents who need after-school care for their children.  It''s housed within the school grounds, and someone from the daycare will walk to the main school building to pick up your child each day.  It''s run by the city youth council and comes highly recommended.  Can I get information about' AS nvarchar(max))+N' that as well?  Yes, flyers and contact information will be included with your packet.  Okay, thank you.  Before you hear the rest of the conversation, you have some time to look at questions 7 to 10.  Now listen and answer questions 7 to 10.  Oh, and one more thing.  I saw a flyer recently for an introduction event for new students and parents. An open house, I think it was called.  But I can''t remember the date. Was it August 3rd?  That must have been last year''s flyer. We haven''t put out information on this year''s open house yet, but it''ll probably be sometime in August.  Ah, no, actually, it will be in July this year, since schools start a little early this year.  Once your child is registered, you''ll get all that information in the mail, and it''ll be on the school website as well.  Great.  I''m assuming that during the open house, we get to tour the school and meet our child''s teacher?  Yes, and you will set up a time for kindergarten entrance testing as well.  Wow, testing already. That starts early.  Well, we want to make sure children are properly placed and qualified for special services, if necessary.  Okay, I guess that makes sense.  Oh, and the first day of school?  The first day will be August 19.  We start in the middle of the week to help with the adjustment.  And for kindergartners, the first three days are half days, from 8 to 12:30.  Oh, okay.  And then the next week, the regular schedule, 8 o''clock to 2:05, will be in force.  Yes, and you can access the full school calendar of holidays and breaks on the school website.  Oh, yeah, I''ve seen that. The website is very helpful.  Thank you so much for your time.  You''re welcome, sir.  That is the end of Part 1.</p>'),(CAST(N'<p>Part one.  You will hear a telephone conversation between a man looking for information on registering his child for school and a school district employee.  First, you have some time to look at questions one to six.  Now listen carefully and answer questions one to six.  Good afternoon, Lemon Grove School District.  Hi, I''m calling for information on school registration. I think my son should attend one of the schools in your district.  What grade will your son be entering?  He just turned five. He''ll be starting school this year.  Oh, okay. One moment, please.  I''ll get the information for kindergarten registration.  Okay, thank you.  Can you give me your address?  Yes, it''s 7418 DiMarino Street.  Okay, thanks. Yes, at that address, your child should attend Monterey Heights Elementary.  Can you spell that, please?  Yes, it''s M-O-N-T-E-R-E-Y Heights.  Great.  So how do I register him?  We have registration at each school site Monday through Thursday from 9 to 1. Oh, no, sorry, 1:30. You''ll need to pick up a kindergarten registration packet from the school beforehand, though.  It has all the forms you''ll need to fill out.  Can I pick up the packet any time?  Sure. The school office is usually open till 3:30 in the afternoons.  Oh, no. I can''t really get there that early.  Well, the school has late office hours until 4 on Thursdays, or I think you can pick up a packet in the school library any day before 5.  Oh, okay.  I''ll stop by there some day this week, then, before 5.  Can you tell me what forms we''ll need?  I''m sure you need his immunization records.  Yes, those, and we also need a general health history signed by your child''s doctor, a form filled out by the dentist, emergency contact information, and a residency verification form with proof of residence.  Oh, and an original birth certificate.  Okay, that shouldn''t be a problem.  Can I ask one more question?  Sure, go ahead.  I was wondering about before- and after-school care.  Do you provide transportation after school?  No, unfortunately, we don''t. Parents or caregivers need to pick up the children.  There is, however, an on-site licensed daycare for working parents who need after-school care for their children.  It''s housed within the school grounds, and someone from the daycare will walk to the main school building to pick up your child each day.  It''s run by the city youth council and comes highly recommended.  Can I get information about that as well?  Yes, flyers and contact information wi' AS nvarchar(max))+N'll be included with your packet.  Okay, thank you.  Before you hear the rest of the conversation, you have some time to look at questions 7 to 10.  Now listen and answer questions 7 to 10.  Oh, and one more thing.  I saw a flyer recently for an introduction event for new students and parents. An open house, I think it was called.  But I can''t remember the date. Was it August 3rd?  That must have been last year''s flyer. We haven''t put out information on this year''s open house yet, but it''ll probably be sometime in August.  Ah, no, actually, it will be in July this year, since schools start a little early this year.  Once your child is registered, you''ll get all that information in the mail, and it''ll be on the school website as well.  Great.  I''m assuming that during the open house, we get to tour the school and meet our child''s teacher?  Yes, and you will set up a time for kindergarten entrance testing as well.  Wow, testing already. That starts early.  Well, we want to make sure children are properly placed and qualified for special services, if necessary.  Okay, I guess that makes sense.  Oh, and the first day of school?  The first day will be August 19.  We start in the middle of the week to help with the adjustment.  And for kindergartners, the first three days are half days, from 8 to 12:30.  Oh, okay.  And then the next week, the regular schedule, 8 o''clock to 2:05, will be in force.  Yes, and you can access the full school calendar of holidays and breaks on the school website.  Oh, yeah, I''ve seen that. The website is very helpful.  Thank you so much for your time.  You''re welcome, sir.  That is the end of Part 1.</p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-2/iL.VOL2.5.S1644.PART1.mp3',NULL,1,0,1,NULL,0,1644),
