(N'2c417c5f-58c0-57fb-a141-9bda26916b9d',N'01a0e4eb-57a9-5a64-b34f-ea8658b0272e',0,3,19,N'<h3>Information about School Registration</h3><p><span>Grade Level:</span> kindergarten</p><p><span>School:</span> }{SPACE}{ Heights Elementary School</p><p><span>Registration:</span></p><ul><li><p>Monday to Thursday from 9.00 to 1.30</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Can pick up packet from the school</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ any afternoon up to 5.00</p><p><span>Forms:</span> Immunisation records</p><ul><li><p>Heal forms from doctor and</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p><ul><li><p>Emergency contact information</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Residency verification form</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Original birth certificate</p></li></ul><p><span>Childcare: </span>No }{SPACE}{ is provided</p><ul><li><p>There is on-site licensed daycare for working</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p><ul><li><p>This is organised by the City</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ Council</p><p><span>Orientation:</span></p><ul><li><p>Open house in July - details provided through the</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ and on the school''s website</p><ul><li><p>Will tour the school, meet the</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ and schedule entrance testing</p><p><span>Schedule:</span></p><ul><li><p>First day of school will be on</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p><ul><li><p>First week is 8.00 to 12.30</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Regular schedule is 8.00 to</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p>',N'<p>Đáp án là Monterey. Nhân viên trường xác nhận với địa chỉ đã cung cấp thì con của người gọi sẽ học tại Monterey Heights Elementary School. Key words: attend: theo học, elementary school: trường tiểu học. Scripts: “your child should attend Monterey Heights Elementary”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,1,NULL,0,1644),
(N'8ade4c31-8222-555a-a1d4-2ea6a0fb70df',N'01a0e4eb-57a9-5a64-b34f-ea8658b0272e',0,3,19,N'Question number 2',N'<p>Đáp án là library. Khi người cha không thể đến văn phòng trường sớm, nhân viên cho biết có thể lấy hồ sơ đăng ký tại thư viện trường trước 5 giờ chiều. Key words: pick up: lấy, library: thư viện. Scripts: “pick up a packet in the school library any day before 5”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,2,NULL,0,1644),
(N'f35e6ea4-757a-52bc-8400-8e4cdb0a0b6c',N'01a0e4eb-57a9-5a64-b34f-ea8658b0272e',0,3,19,N'Question number 3',N'<p>Đáp án là dentist. Ngoài hồ sơ tiêm chủng và giấy xác nhận từ bác sĩ, nhà trường còn yêu cầu mẫu đơn do nha sĩ điền. Key words: form: mẫu đơn, dentist: nha sĩ. Scripts: “a form filled out by the dentist”</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,3,NULL,0,1644),
(N'b116f237-aad0-5450-adfa-37762a42f25a',N'01a0e4eb-57a9-5a64-b34f-ea8658b0272e',0,3,19,N'Question number 4',N'<p>Đáp án là transportation. Nhân viên xác nhận rằng nhà trường không cung cấp dịch vụ đưa đón trẻ trước và sau giờ học. Key words: provide: cung cấp, transportation: phương tiện đưa đón. Scripts: “No, unfortunately, we don''t”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,4,NULL,0,1644),
(N'f380a114-69ca-59d0-8142-b544e120b689',N'01a0e4eb-57a9-5a64-b34f-ea8658b0272e',0,3,19,N'Question number 5',N'<p>Đáp án là parents. Dịch vụ trông trẻ tại trường được thiết kế dành cho các phụ huynh đang đi làm và cần hỗ trợ sau giờ học. Key words: working parents: phụ huynh đi làm, daycare: trông trẻ. Scripts: “on site licensed daycare for working parents”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,5,NULL,0,1644),
(N'726bd09b-e2d9-5896-b043-475551a579ed',N'01a0e4eb-57a9-5a64-b34f-ea8658b0272e',0,3,19,N'Question number 6',N'<p>Đáp án là youth. Dịch vụ trông trẻ được tổ chức và quản lý bởi Hội đồng Thanh thiếu niên của thành phố. Key words: council: hội đồng, youth: thanh thiếu niên. Scripts: “run by the city youth council”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,6,NULL,0,1644),
(N'e20b2609-6cfd-515b-abe7-82b73c68d45e',N'01a0e4eb-57a9-5a64-b34f-ea8658b0272e',0,3,19,N'Question number 7',N'<p>Đáp án là mail. Sau khi đăng ký, thông tin về buổi open house sẽ được gửi trực tiếp qua thư cho phụ huynh. Key words: information: thông tin, mail: thư. Scripts: “you''ll get all that information in the mail”</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,7,NULL,0,1644),
(N'3468d2a9-d5ba-5fa3-91fc-32d8067fc16f',N'01a0e4eb-57a9-5a64-b34f-ea8658b0272e',0,3,19,N'Question number 8',N'<p>Đáp án là teacher. Trong buổi open house, phụ huynh sẽ được tham quan trường và gặp giáo viên của con mình. Key words: meet: gặp, teacher: giáo viên. Scripts: “meet our child''s teacher”</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,8,NULL,0,1644),
(N'afc0d569-86e6-5104-a114-8385acd0e6e5',N'01a0e4eb-57a9-5a64-b34f-ea8658b0272e',0,3,19,N'Question number 9',N'<p>Đáp án là August 19. Nhân viên trường xác nhận ngày đầu tiên đi học của học sinh là ngày 19 tháng 8. Key words: first day: ngày đầu tiên, August: tháng Tám. Scripts: “The first day will be August 19”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,9,NULL,0,1644),
(N'b61345c9-6c0f-5ef6-a8be-9ed0e13f8b02',N'01a0e4eb-57a9-5a64-b34f-ea8658b0272e',0,3,19,N'Question number 10',N'<p>Đáp án là 2.05. Sau tuần đầu tiên học nửa ngày, thời khóa biểu chính thức sẽ kết thúc lúc 2 giờ 05 chiều. Key words: regular schedule: lịch học chính thức, finish: kết thúc. Scripts: “8 o''clock to 2.05”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,10,NULL,0,1644),
(N'53de5bbf-fa92-56fd-9afe-e54cd8dbd317',N'13fd5830-b62f-5aea-931d-4e3dd22f9dc1',0,1,14,(CAST(N'<h2>[VOL 2] Dinosaur Museum in Canada Foot</h2><p>Hello, everyone. I am Jo, your tour guide, and I welcome you to this wonderful place. As you must have seen outside, this place in Canada was built to preserve and showcase some of the most interesting landmarks in the world.

I am here to give you a brief introduction of what we have and where we would be going on this tour.

We will begin our tour by exploring the awe-inspiring display of the world''s largest dinosaur bones, which are truly magnificent in size. It is at the foot of the Rocky Mountains. These remarkable fossils have been excavated and date back over 100 million years to the Mesozoic era.

It''s worth noting that during this visit, you will have the opportunity to observe around 170 meticulously preserved dinosaur footprints. Furthermore, on our upcoming trip next year, you will be delighted to witness an even greater spectacle with 190 footprints in larger sizes. It is truly remarkable to imagine the immense size of these ancient creatures.

We highly recommend embarking on a night tour. This is because the true beauty of this place reveals itself under the cover of darkness. Rest assured, it is an experience unlike any other you have encountered. Prepare to be amazed by the breathtaking sight of the illuminated skyscrapers in the CBD area.

For our second location, you can have a chance to explore Stikine River Park. We have thoughtfully installed artificial lights that will make you forget it is nighttime and immerse yourself in the early past. Of course, we also offer a daytime tour as an alternative, but there may not be as much to see during the day.

The next stop is one of the places that displays Canada''s rich mineral deposits. We have a huge reservoir in this area, and you might see some workers working in the area. I can tell you that you can find one of the largest uranium deposits here in Canada. There is also an agricultural development site here. Plans are ongoing to expand it in the near future, and don''t miss out on checking out the nearby rest area by the highway. It''s the perfect spot to snap some awesome photos and soak in the stunning views. Trust me, you''ll have plenty of chances to capture jaw-dropping images that will totally blow your mind.

Perhaps the most special feature of this third stop is the presence of raccoons in the Science Centre Museum. Oh my, these are so beautiful, and their blue colour is just amazing and always makes them stand out. Raccoons are many ' AS nvarchar(max))+N'in the area, and they are quite intelligent and curious creatures, as you will see. You also get to see a river at this stop. Though it''s not the longest, it''s one of the cleanest in the world. So as you relax, you get a very great view at this third location. This river is devoid of a lot of contaminants usually seen in rivers, and the government has taken extra precautions to ensure that it remains so.

To embark on this wonderful tour, of course, we would need transportation, and this has been well catered for. You would have noticed a lot of horses in the area while coming in. Yes, you can ride on horseback as we go along, but this mode of transportation would require a permit from the authorities. So once you have it, you can go see any of the handlers as we move.

If you don''t have one, there is no problem. The primary mode of transportation here is by boat, and they have boats available for use.

As you may have been informed, exploring on foot is more enjoyable, but it can be easy to get lost in certain areas without proper road directions. It is advisable to have a tour guide or travel in groups.

In terms of the inner city bus, it is not accessible during this time of year. However, if you return in two months, it will offer a different experience.</p>'),(CAST(N'<p>Hello, everyone. I am Jo, your tour guide, and I welcome you to this wonderful place. As you must have seen outside, this place in Canada was built to preserve and showcase some of the most interesting landmarks in the world.

