(N'bc67fc15-c160-579d-aca7-308a2ff2210c',N'6b787ce6-6260-59ca-b348-8a4970c473cb',0,2,18,N'<p>Choose <span>FIVE</span> answers from the list below and write the correct letter (A- G) next to questions 21 - 25.</p>',N'',N'',N'',N'Answer choices',15,0,1,NULL,0,1644),
(N'600b91f9-e1ce-58d5-aba3-d1424fc6128b',N'bc67fc15-c160-579d-aca7-308a2ff2210c',0,3,19,N'<p>The Aerosol Spray</p>',N'<p>Đáp án là B. Aerosol spray được nhắc đến là có ảnh hưởng trực tiếp đến ngành sơn, vì ứng dụng hiện đại của phát minh này gắn chặt với việc phun sơn trong công nghiệp và nghệ thuật. Key words: aerosol spray: bình xịt, painting industry: ngành sơn. Scripts: “its influence on the painting industry”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,21,NULL,0,1644),
(N'd2927758-80a5-5b32-9b43-a5f9837f2599',N'bc67fc15-c160-579d-aca7-308a2ff2210c',0,3,19,N'<p>The Spinning Machine</p>',N'<p>Đáp án là F. Spinning machine được nói là đã cách mạng hóa ngành sản xuất quần áo, tức là tác động trực tiếp đến ngành may mặc và công nghiệp dệt. Key words: spinning machine: máy kéo sợi, garment: quần áo. Scripts: “revolutionised the garment manufacturing industry”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,22,NULL,0,1644),
(N'44b2bd72-fcfe-54d5-801d-f66741b3d885',N'bc67fc15-c160-579d-aca7-308a2ff2210c',0,3,19,N'<p>The Battery</p>',N'<p>Đáp án là A. Pin hóa học được liên hệ với sự phát triển của điện thoại di động, đặc biệt là việc thu nhỏ pin để thiết bị có thể mang theo. Key words: battery: pin, mobile phone: điện thoại di động. Scripts: “development of the mobile phone depended largely on getting a battery small enough”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,23,NULL,0,1644),
(N'a6072721-ecd1-579d-8bbb-a518f340f4e9',N'bc67fc15-c160-579d-aca7-308a2ff2210c',0,3,19,N'<p>The Sextant</p>',N'<p>Đáp án là G. Sextant giúp con người xác định vị trí địa lý trên biển thông qua các thiên thể, nên ảnh hưởng trực tiếp đến lĩnh vực hàng hải và định hướng. Key words: sextant: hải bàn góc, navigation: định vị hàng hải. Scripts: “work out their geographical position”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,24,NULL,0,1644),
(N'7e35e00e-178f-5f27-b3a9-1818c5e79a11',N'bc67fc15-c160-579d-aca7-308a2ff2210c',0,3,19,N'<p>Light Polarisers</p>',N'<p>Đáp án là E. Light polarisers được sử dụng trong những chiếc máy ảnh chụp lấy liền đầu tiên, nên tác động trực tiếp đến ngành nhiếp ảnh. Key words: light polarisers: kính phân cực, cameras: máy ảnh. Scripts: “used in the first instant cameras”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,25,NULL,0,1644),
(N'12774835-a19d-52bc-9fbf-1b8bc6741930',N'6b787ce6-6260-59ca-b348-8a4970c473cb',0,2,18,N'<p><em>Choose the correct letter <span>A, B, </span>or <span>C.</span></em></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',1,0,2,NULL,0,1644),
(N'16c7314b-d17f-526d-9311-dd1c7c9a1e98',N'12774835-a19d-52bc-9fbf-1b8bc6741930',0,3,19,N'<p>What was the problem with using quick dry ink in fountain pens?</p>',N'<p>Đáp án là A. Mực khô nhanh dùng trong in ấn không chảy tốt trong bút máy vì quá đặc, khiến mực không thể chảy qua ngòi bút. Key words: quick-drying ink: mực khô nhanh, too thick: quá đặc. Scripts: “it was too thick to pass through the nib”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,26,NULL,0,1644),
(N'bb059f23-80bc-5ae4-ab5e-bb9fde220a2f',N'12774835-a19d-52bc-9fbf-1b8bc6741930',0,3,19,N'<p>Who first produced a pen with a metal ball bearing at the end of a pen?</p>',N'<p>Đáp án là B. John Loud là người đầu tiên phát minh ra bút có viên bi kim loại ở đầu bút, dù phát minh của ông chưa được sản xuất thương mại. Key words: John Loud: John Loud, roller ball: viên bi lăn. Scripts: “the American John Loud patented a roller ball tip”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,27,NULL,0,1644),
(N'6ce694f5-140f-563d-9425-562d203b17a1',N'12774835-a19d-52bc-9fbf-1b8bc6741930',0,3,19,N'<p>In which country did Biro first manufacture his ball point pens?</p>',N'<p>Đáp án là B. Biro rời Hungary và bắt đầu sản xuất bút bi đầu tiên tại Argentina trước khi được cấp phép sản xuất ở các nước khác. Key words: Argentina: Argentina, manufacture: sản xuất. Scripts: “he created a new home for himself in Argentina”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,28,NULL,0,1644),
(N'9e91a1d7-f14a-586a-933d-a5484d2353c7',N'6b787ce6-6260-59ca-b348-8a4970c473cb',0,2,18,N'<p><em>Write </em><span><em><span>NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS</span></em></span><em> from the listening for each answer.</em></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',11,0,3,NULL,0,1644),
(N'5fb9fa21-9fd1-52cc-b3db-fd81aa59b3a4',N'9e91a1d7-f14a-586a-933d-a5484d2353c7',0,3,19,N'<p><img src="https://ieltsroom.com/upload/images/ieltsadvancedtest/3b3740a2720904685d2a.jpg" alt="Question diagram"></p> }{SPACE}{  }{SPACE}{ ',N'<p>Đáp án là central spring. Bộ phận này nằm trong ống mực và có vai trò điều chỉnh dòng mực khi bút được ấn xuống để viết. Key words: spring: lò xo, ink tube: ống mực. Scripts: “In the middle of the ink tube is a central spring”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,29,NULL,0,1644),
(N'af1fb91c-36c9-5463-9163-127ca62bf5d5',N'9e91a1d7-f14a-586a-933d-a5484d2353c7',0,3,19,N'Question number 30',N'<p>Đáp án là ink tank. Đây là bộ phận chứa mực, nằm phía trên lò xo và cung cấp mực cho viên bi khi viết. Key words: ink tank: ống chứa mực, above: phía trên. Scripts: “the ink tank, which is found above the spring”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,30,NULL,0,1644),
(N'52a7a2c0-fce5-583a-844f-6010ecfd6221',N'13fd5830-b62f-5aea-931d-4e3dd22f9dc1',0,1,15,(CAST(N'<h2>[VOL 2] Childhood Obesity &amp; Sugary Drinks</h2><p>Good afternoon, everyone, and thanks for coming to my presentation today, which is on the link between childhood obesity and sugary drinks.

Childhood obesity is a worrying phenomenon that affects many developed societies. Childhood obesity rates have doubled throughout the past 30 years in the United States for children aged 2 to 5 and 12 to 19, and tripled in the age group of 6 to 11. Many social and environmental pressures lead to greater obesity in children. Chief among these influences is the wide variety and availability of sugar-sweetened drinks that contain little to no nutritional value.

These beverages include soft drinks, sports drinks, fruit drinks, flavored teas and coffees, and energy drinks. Throughout the past 10 to 15 years, these drinks have exploded onto the consumer scene, flooding grocery stores, gas stations, convenience stores, and vending machines. Americans have doubled their consumption of soda pop in the last 25 years, a trend that closely follows the obesity epidemic.

The average American drinks 1.6 cans of soda pop a day, which is more than 500 cans a year. Soda drinking is particularly rampant among teenagers. Data indicates that soft drinks account for 13% of a teenager''s caloric intake, by far the largest source of calories in his or her diet.

For decades, milk was the most common beverage consumed by children, but by the mid-1990s, boys and girls were drinking twice as much soda pop as milk. One recent study has demonstrated a strong link between consumption of sugar-sweetened beverages and childhood obesity. Although some studies conflict regarding the causality between sugar-sweetened beverages and obesity, a number of research studies confirm the findings that increased soft drink and sugar-laden beverage consumption is a risk factor for obesity.

Not only do sugar-sweetened drinks likely lead to obesity, they are also associated with tooth decay and fragile bones. Soft drinks can also contain large amounts of caffeine. The amounts of caffeine found in such drinks are often about 10 grams per ounce.

With that in mind, take a look at the amount of caffeine found in other beverages. Most experts recommend that children consume well under 100 grams of caffeine per day. The pharmacological effects of caffeine are notable in children, most commonly seen as hyperactivity, sleep disturbances, and restlessness. Drinking large amounts of caffeine can also be associated ' AS nvarchar(max))+N'with high blood pressure and frequent headaches.

Researchers have reported that a new practice among college-age students is the simultaneous consumption of energy drinks and alcohol, which allows greater consumption of alcohol since alertness is perpetuated by the energy drink. In addition, the sugar content of energy drinks is comparable to or higher than most soft drinks, with, for example, a typical energy drink containing 27 grams of sugar.

Alcohol usually contains a lot of sugar, and this can lead to massive sugar intakes for people who mix energy drinks with alcohol.

So what can be done to limit the amount of the nutritionally poor liquid calories that children and adolescents are consuming? On an individual basis, the best approach is simply to replace soda and sports drinks with water or low-fat milk in children''s diets. Water is the best hydrator available. Low-fat milk not only hydrates but delivers calcium, protein, and vitamin D.

What happens at school may be out of the immediate control of a parent, but parents can petition the school to eliminate machines that sell soft drinks and energy drinks in favor of bottled water. Children should be watched at home regarding their choice of liquids. A glass of 100% fruit juice per day is fine, but excessive soda, sports drinks, or energy drinks is unhealthy.

Parents need to provide guidance to their children so that they know and understand this. Moderation in guiding children, of course, is appropriate. Children who are constantly deprived of treats are more likely to binge eat or drink. Studies suggest that children who are raised by parents who exert excessive dietary restraint may be more likely to become obese.

Also, the role models presented by parents are important. Children possess the ability to regulate their caloric intake. However, if they see their parents struggle with the effort to control food or drink intake and the conscious restriction of intake to control weight, they may pattern their own eating and drinking behavior after their parents instead of allowing their internal energy regulation to guide them. This in turn seems to lead to greater obesity in children.

In conclusion, parents should adopt healthy eating and drinking patterns, limiting the consumption of soft drinks and other sugar-sweetened drinks, and to do so without obsession. Helping children develop a love for the refreshing taste of water or a cold glass of milk will pay immediate health rewards for children a'+N's well as dividends for their future health and weight control. Careful education of today''s youth will be the key to them avoiding these destructive drinks.</p>'),(CAST(N'<p>Good afternoon, everyone, and thanks for coming to my presentation today, which is on the link between childhood obesity and sugary drinks.

