(N'23f4b118-722b-5491-8fe0-39e569b64b6d',N'9aa45abc-2fc5-5f8d-b192-50fd94eacaca',0,3,19,N'<p><span>Which two problems are caused by water hyacinth?</span></p>',N'<p>Đáp án là B.  </p><p>Script nói rõ nước bị phủ kín khiến nông dân không thể di chuyển bằng thuyền và không thể đánh cá.  </p><p>Key word:  </p><p><em>cannot fish (v) không thể đánh cá  </em></p><p><em>farmers (n) nông dân</em></p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,21,NULL,0,1641),
(N'fd985830-4bdf-5ab5-8a6f-cf3df26e6d25',N'9aa45abc-2fc5-5f8d-b192-50fd94eacaca',0,3,19,N'<p><span>Which two problems are caused by water hyacinth?</span></p>',N'<p>Đáp án là E.  </p><p>Việc đập không hoạt động dẫn đến hạn chế nghiêm trọng việc phát điện, đúng với “electricity production is affected”.  </p><p>Key word:  </p><p><em>electricity generation (n) sản xuất điện  </em></p><p><em>restrict (v) hạn chế</em></p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,22,NULL,0,1641),
(N'03ada5cd-e1f3-50a8-aaae-471b8455c6b3',N'781fbb98-633f-5e5e-b707-6d4c789e3e54',0,2,18,N'<p><span>Choose the correct letter, <span>A</span>, <span>B </span>or <span>C</span>.</span></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',1,0,2,NULL,0,1641),
(N'3685aef2-255e-566e-a6ed-5d5ce50bc9d5',N'03ada5cd-e1f3-50a8-aaae-471b8455c6b3',0,3,19,N'<p>Where was water hyacinth originally from?</p>',N'<p>Đáp án là A.  </p><p>Amazon Basin thuộc khu vực Mỹ Latinh, tương ứng với Latin America.  </p><p>Key word:  </p><p><em>native (adj) có nguồn gốc  </em></p><p><em>Amazon Basin (n) lưu vực Amazon</em></p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,23,NULL,0,1641),
(N'b3f97b50-e34b-59e8-b136-c2b81774d608',N'03ada5cd-e1f3-50a8-aaae-471b8455c6b3',0,3,19,N'<p>What is the primary cause of the decrease in nutrients from the soil?</p>',N'<p>Đáp án là C.  </p><p>Nguyên nhân chính được nêu trực tiếp là chặt phá rừng, không phải mưa hay xói mòn đơn lẻ.  </p><p>Key word:  </p><p><em>cut down trees (v) chặt cây  </em></p><p><em>deforestation (n) phá rừng</em></p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,24,NULL,0,1641),
(N'948b24eb-03a8-5031-b4ee-1dd0dc946568',N'03ada5cd-e1f3-50a8-aaae-471b8455c6b3',0,3,19,N'<p>When will the biological solution bring risks to the environment?</p>',N'<p>Đáp án là C.  </p><p>Rủi ro môi trường chỉ xuất hiện sau nhiều năm, không phải ngay lập tức hay sau 6 tháng. </p><p>Key word:  </p><p><em>side effects (n) tác động phụ  </em></p><p><em>for years (adv) trong nhiều năm</em></p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,25,NULL,0,1641),
(N'b5529c18-33ab-5a2e-be40-12d449bd9167',N'03ada5cd-e1f3-50a8-aaae-471b8455c6b3',0,3,19,N'<p>What does John say about the mechanical solution?</p>',N'<p>Đáp án là C. </p><p>John nhấn mạnh chi phí cao là nhược điểm chính của biện pháp cơ học.  </p><p>Key word:  </p><p><em>costly (adj) tốn kém  </em></p><p><em>mechanical removal (n) biện pháp cơ học</em></p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,26,NULL,0,1641),
(N'dca6bfde-d724-5fff-99f2-150a2c4db535',N'781fbb98-633f-5e5e-b707-6d4c789e3e54',0,2,18,N'<p><span>What is the benefit of the cut down water hyacinth to each of the following aspects? </span></p><p><span>Choose <span>FOUR </span>answers from the box an write the correct letter, <span>A-F </span>next to Questions 27-30</span></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'Benefits of the cut- down water hyacinth',15,0,3,NULL,0,1641),
(N'553659e2-139f-554c-84e3-81a1e828c083',N'dca6bfde-d724-5fff-99f2-150a2c4db535',0,3,19,N'<p>dried water hyacinth</p>',N'<p>Đáp án là D.  </p><p>Water hyacinth phơi khô được dùng làm vật liệu trồng cây, giúp cây phát triển tốt hơn.  </p><p>Key word:  </p><p><em>alternative soil (n) đất thay thế  </em></p><p><em>grow crops (v) trồng cây</em></p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,27,NULL,0,1641),
(N'5f966ee6-d5b2-578c-a40c-fed11a463d54',N'dca6bfde-d724-5fff-99f2-150a2c4db535',0,3,19,N'<p>mushroom farmers</p>',N'<p>Đáp án là C.  </p><p>Thu hoạch sớm giúp nông dân có lợi nhuận nhanh, đúng với “make quick profits”.  </p><p>Key word:  </p><p><em>harvest sooner (v) thu hoạch sớm  </em></p><p><em>profit (n) lợi nhuận</em></p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,28,NULL,0,1641),
(N'a680f645-531f-51b4-8eb8-9c09a94af74d',N'dca6bfde-d724-5fff-99f2-150a2c4db535',0,3,19,N'<p>oyster and straw mushrooms</p>',N'<p>Đáp án là E.  </p><p>Oyster và straw mushrooms mang lại lợi ích trực tiếp cho sức khỏe con người.  </p><p>Key word:  </p><p><em>nutritional values (n) giá trị dinh dưỡng  </em></p><p><em>human health (n) sức khỏe con người</em></p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,29,NULL,0,1641),
(N'2ff5106a-1c56-5f7a-9aea-d34ee2dd5c01',N'dca6bfde-d724-5fff-99f2-150a2c4db535',0,3,19,N'<p>cows</p>',N'<p>Đáp án là B.  </p><p>Khí methane được dùng làm nguồn năng lượng thay thế.  </p><p>Key word:  </p><p><em>methane gas (n) khí mê-tan  </em></p><p><em>alternative energy (n) năng lượng thay thế</em></p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,30,NULL,0,1641),
(N'6ef1dc5e-f67b-5fd0-9829-e7dd175a5d2f',N'd81544fd-4ada-52df-8e1f-67f0cff585c8',0,1,15,(CAST(N'<h2>[VOL 1] Bislama - The Pidgin English Language of Vanuatu</h2><p><span>You will hear part of a linguistics lecture about a language called "Bishlama" that is spoken in the Pacific Islands.</span></p><p><span><span>First, you have some time to look at questions 31-40 on page 7. You can find out more about the language in the description. Now listen carefully and answer questions 31-40.</span></span></p><p>Good morning and welcome back to this series of linguistics lectures. Today I will be talking about the language "Bishlama" which is a form of pigeon English.</p><p>Pigeon is used to describe new languages that are created by combining two or more existing languages, often in a simplified form. The study of pigeon languages is important because it provides us with information about language change and modification.</p><p>The pigeon English known as "Bishlama" is used in the South Pacific nation of Vanuatu, a group of islands where 81 first languages are still regularly used by the local people.</p><p>There are a further 17 local languages that are in danger of dying out and 8 that are being identified as extinct. This gives a total of 106 first languages in all, a very high number for a small country with a population of just 200,000 people.</p><p>Then thinking about foreign languages, English is the most important and has official status largely because it is the medium for all education purposes. However, it is "Bishlama" that is the most widely spoken language in the country, used regularly by more than 90% of the population.</p><p>We should note here that in earlier times some people had negative feelings towards the language. In fact, for many years it was commonly referred to as a "broken language" and its use was discouraged. But attitudes have changed dramatically and today the people of Vanuatu are very proud of this unique language. It is only when we understand the historical context that we can comprehend just why "Bishlama" developed in Vanuatu.</p><p>The first form of pigeon English in this region can be traced to around 1800 when foreign traders arrived and local people were recruited to work as sailors. On board multilingual ships, there was an obvious need for a common tongue and pigeon English was born. This early form of "Bishlama" continued to spread as trade in the Pacific developed in Sandalwood and other local commodities.</p><p>Then from about 1860 a lot of people from Vanuatu travelled to Australia to work on the new plantations' AS nvarchar(max))+N' as laborers. Again, because of the multilingual nature of these workplaces it was very important to have a common language.</p><p>Finally, in modern times there have been other pressures that have maintained the need for a common language.</p><p>Like many other parts of the world from about the 1950s, Vanuatu experienced a significant migration of its people from small villages into the city and it has been here that "Bishlama" has really established itself as the country''s first language.</p><p>So then, how can we describe the language itself? In general terms, pigeon languages can be defined as extremely simple versions of the original language. However, this is not a satisfactory definition in this case and linguists prefer to describe "Bishlama" as a "developed pigeon" because it has more rules and ideas than most simple pigeon languages found in other parts of the world. Let''s think first about the vocabulary.</p><p>Because Britain was the colonial power, the majority of "Bishlama"''s vocabulary is derived from English. However, some care needs to be taken here.</p><p>For example, the word "from" in "Bishlama" can also mean "because of", so we need to be aware that words can have a wider range of meanings in "Bishlama".</p><p>Indeed, there are numerous other potentially misleading terms and English is not the only contributor to the vocabulary.</p><p>Again, because of the region''s history there are some words, around 5-10% that are derived from French. Then, a relatively small number of words have been taken from local, specific languages. Usually, this is the case where there is no English equivalent for naturally occurring phenomena or to describe some aspect of the culture that is unique to the country. Finally, a word about grammar.</p><p>Although the vocabulary is based largely on English, it''s important to note that the grammatical structure of "Bishlama" is derived from patterns common in the local languages of "vanuatu".</p><p>So, for example, there are two distinct pronouns meaning "we". One means "I" and "you", and another means "I" and "some others, but not "you". Sounds confusing in English, but in the local languages such distinctions are common.</p><p>A different example concerns the word "long". It is almost the only preposition in "Bishlama" and may be used in place of a whole range of English words such as "at", "to", "with", "on", "in" and so on. Well, that is the end of the formal part of the lecture. If you have any questions now, '+N'I''ll be most happy to answer.</p><p><span><span>That is the end of section 4. You now have half a minute to check your answers. That is the end of the listening test. You now have 10 minutes to transfer your answers to the listening answer sheet.</span></span></p>'),(CAST(N'<p><span>You will hear part of a linguistics lecture about a language called "Bishlama" that is spoken in the Pacific Islands.</span></p><p><span><span>First, you have some time to look at questions 31-40 on page 7. You can find out more about the language in the description. Now listen carefully and answer questions 31-40.</span></span></p><p>Good morning and welcome back to this series of linguistics lectures. Today I will be talking about the language "Bishlama" which is a form of pigeon English.</p><p>Pigeon is used to describe new languages that are created by combining two or more existing languages, often in a simplified form. The study of pigeon languages is important because it provides us with information about language change and modification.</p><p>The pigeon English known as "Bishlama" is used in the South Pacific nation of Vanuatu, a group of islands where 81 first languages are still regularly used by the local people.</p><p>There are a further 17 local languages that are in danger of dying out and 8 that are being identified as extinct. This gives a total of 106 first languages in all, a very high number for a small country with a population of just 200,000 people.</p><p>Then thinking about foreign languages, English is the most important and has official status largely because it is the medium for all education purposes. However, it is "Bishlama" that is the most widely spoken language in the country, used regularly by more than 90% of the population.</p><p>We should note here that in earlier times some people had negative feelings towards the language. In fact, for many years it was commonly referred to as a "broken language" and its use was discouraged. But attitudes have changed dramatically and today the people of Vanuatu are very proud of this unique language. It is only when we understand the historical context that we can comprehend just why "Bishlama" developed in Vanuatu.</p><p>The first form of pigeon English in this region can be traced to around 1800 when foreign traders arrived and local people were recruited to work as sailors. On board multilingual ships, there was an obvious need for a common tongue and pigeon English was born. This early form of "Bishlama" continued to spread as trade in the Pacific developed in Sandalwood and other local commodities.</p><p>Then from about 1860 a lot of people from Vanuatu travelled to Australia to work on the new plantations as laborers. Again, because of the multilingual nature of these ' AS nvarchar(max))+N'workplaces it was very important to have a common language.</p><p>Finally, in modern times there have been other pressures that have maintained the need for a common language.</p><p>Like many other parts of the world from about the 1950s, Vanuatu experienced a significant migration of its people from small villages into the city and it has been here that "Bishlama" has really established itself as the country''s first language.</p><p>So then, how can we describe the language itself? In general terms, pigeon languages can be defined as extremely simple versions of the original language. However, this is not a satisfactory definition in this case and linguists prefer to describe "Bishlama" as a "developed pigeon" because it has more rules and ideas than most simple pigeon languages found in other parts of the world. Let''s think first about the vocabulary.</p><p>Because Britain was the colonial power, the majority of "Bishlama"''s vocabulary is derived from English. However, some care needs to be taken here.</p><p>For example, the word "from" in "Bishlama" can also mean "because of", so we need to be aware that words can have a wider range of meanings in "Bishlama".</p><p>Indeed, there are numerous other potentially misleading terms and English is not the only contributor to the vocabulary.</p><p>Again, because of the region''s history there are some words, around 5-10% that are derived from French. Then, a relatively small number of words have been taken from local, specific languages. Usually, this is the case where there is no English equivalent for naturally occurring phenomena or to describe some aspect of the culture that is unique to the country. Finally, a word about grammar.</p><p>Although the vocabulary is based largely on English, it''s important to note that the grammatical structure of "Bishlama" is derived from patterns common in the local languages of "vanuatu".</p><p>So, for example, there are two distinct pronouns meaning "we". One means "I" and "you", and another means "I" and "some others, but not "you". Sounds confusing in English, but in the local languages such distinctions are common.</p><p>A different example concerns the word "long". It is almost the only preposition in "Bishlama" and may be used in place of a whole range of English words such as "at", "to", "with", "on", "in" and so on. Well, that is the end of the formal part of the lecture. If you have any questions now, I''ll be most happy to answer.</p><p><span><span>That is the end o'+N'f section 4. You now have half a minute to check your answers. That is the end of the listening test. You now have 10 minutes to transfer your answers to the listening answer sheet.</span></span></p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-1/iL.VOL1.1.S1641.PART4.mp3',NULL,1,0,4,NULL,0,1641),
(N'9be2954b-c7c0-5b8a-b003-be3cdd045f3b',N'6ef1dc5e-f67b-5fd0-9829-e7dd175a5d2f',0,2,18,N'<p><span>Complete the notes below.</span></p><p><span>Write <span>ONE WORD ONLY</span> for each answer.</span></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'Bislama - The Pidgin English Language of Vanuatu',11,0,1,NULL,0,1641),
(N'95062603-685b-5932-9a34-d70d14f22661',N'9be2954b-c7c0-5b8a-b003-be3cdd045f3b',0,3,19,N'<h3>Bislama - The Pidgin English Language of Vanuatu</h3><p><span>Languages in Vanuatu</span></p><p><span>Local languages:</span></p><p>Actively spoken languages: 81</p><p>Declining languages: 17</p> }{SPACE}{ languages: 8</p><p>Total: 106</p><p><span>Foreign languages:</span></p><p>English is used in the }{SPACE}{ system</p><p><span>Bislama</span></p><ul><li><p>It is spoken by 90% of the population today.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>In the past this language was described as</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p><p><span>History of Bislama</span></p><ul><li><p>Around 1800 it was used as a common language on many ships.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>After 1860 Vanuatu people worked in Australian</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p><ul><li><p>After 1950 people move to the</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p><p><span>Description of Bislama</span></p><p><span><span>General</span></span></p><ul><li><p>Bislama should be called a</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ ‘pidgin</p><p><span>Vocabulary</span></p><ul><li><p>Most words come from English.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Words such as “from” may have more</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ in Bislama.</p><ul><li><p>Less than 10% of words are of</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ origin.</p><ul><li><p>Pacific words describe the natural world and also local</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p><p><span>Grammar</span></p><ul><li><p>It is based on Vanuatu languages.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>The word “long” acts as an important</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ in Bislama.</p>',N'<p> Đáp án là extinct.  </p><p>- Câu hỏi yêu cầu điền loại ngôn ngữ còn lại trong nhóm local languages, và con số 8 được xác định rõ là “extinct”.  </p><p>Key word:  </p><p><em>+ extinct (adj) tuyệt chủng  </em></p><p><em>+ local languages (n) ngôn ngữ địa phương</em></p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,31,NULL,0,1641),
(N'c110c02f-821b-52c6-a836-cc3d88f43016',N'9be2954b-c7c0-5b8a-b003-be3cdd045f3b',0,3,19,N'Question number 32',N'<p>Đáp án là education.  </p><p>- English được sử dụng trong hệ thống giáo dục, đúng với cấu trúc “used in the … system”.  </p><p>Key word:  </p><p><em>+ education (n) giáo dục  </em></p><p><em>+ medium (n) phương tiện</em></p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,32,NULL,0,1641),
(N'e4a53621-bd6b-541a-9567-14d2b3dfc1c0',N'9be2954b-c7c0-5b8a-b003-be3cdd045f3b',0,3,19,N'Question number 33',N'<p>Đáp án là broken.  </p><p>- Cụm “broken language” được dùng trực tiếp trong bài để mô tả Bishlama trong quá khứ.</p><p>Key word:  </p><p><em>+ broken (adj) bị coi là kém chuẩn  </em></p><p><em>+ discouraged (v) bị ngăn cản</em></p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,33,NULL,0,1641),
(N'fa3af96d-1a25-51c2-a905-85f1427770f8',N'9be2954b-c7c0-5b8a-b003-be3cdd045f3b',0,3,19,N'Question number 34',N'<p>Đáp án là plantations.  </p><p>- Sau năm 1860, người dân Vanuatu sang Úc làm việc tại các đồn điền, từ này xuất hiện nguyên văn trong script.  </p><p>Key word:  </p><p>+ plantations (n) đồn điền  </p><p>+ laborers (n) lao động</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,34,NULL,0,1641),
(N'178e70ce-17bc-5a1b-8356-6a8e32046ca7',N'9be2954b-c7c0-5b8a-b003-be3cdd045f3b',0,3,19,N'Question number 35',N'<p>Đáp án là city.  </p><p>- Câu nói rõ sự di cư từ làng nhỏ vào thành phố sau năm 1950.  </p><p>Key word:  </p><p><em>+ migration (n) di cư  </em></p><p><em>+ city (n) thành phố</em></p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,35,NULL,0,1641),
(N'f5181b04-5749-55db-8664-6155a27417dd',N'9be2954b-c7c0-5b8a-b003-be3cdd045f3b',0,3,19,N'Question number 36',N'<p>Đáp án là developed.  </p><p>- Bishlama được gọi là “developed pigeon”, không phải pigeon đơn giản.  </p><p>Key word:  </p><p><em>+ developed (adj) phát triển  </em></p><p><em>+ pigeon (n) ngôn ngữ pidgin</em></p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,36,NULL,0,1641),
(N'45e4dc13-1ee7-5a01-bdad-3a51ba7f7b57',N'9be2954b-c7c0-5b8a-b003-be3cdd045f3b',0,3,19,N'Question number 37',N'<p>Đáp án là meanings.  </p><p>- Từ “from” có nhiều nghĩa hơn trong Bishlama, nên chỗ trống yêu cầu danh từ số nhiều. </p><p>Key word:  </p><p><em>+ meanings (n) nghĩa  </em></p><p><em>+ wider range (n) phạm vi rộng hơn</em></p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,37,NULL,0,1641),
(N'0a3e63cf-6895-5b15-926d-7046841a358e',N'9be2954b-c7c0-5b8a-b003-be3cdd045f3b',0,3,19,N'Question number 38',N'<p>Đáp án là French.  </p><p>- Bài nói rõ 5-10% từ vựng có nguồn gốc từ tiếng Pháp.  </p><p>Key word:  </p><p><em>+ derived from (v) có nguồn gốc từ  </em></p><p><em>+ French (n) tiếng Pháp</em></p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,38,NULL,0,1641),
(N'eaa12433-8f53-5203-9f82-5335cda0e65c',N'9be2954b-c7c0-5b8a-b003-be3cdd045f3b',0,3,19,N'Question number 39',N'<p>Đáp án là culture.  </p><p>- Các từ địa phương dùng để mô tả hiện tượng tự nhiên hoặc khía cạnh văn hóa đặc thù. </p><p>Key word:  </p><p><em>+ culture (n) văn hóa  </em></p><p><em>+ unique (adj) độc đáo</em></p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,39,NULL,0,1641),
(N'74d6b07e-65f8-510b-8e6b-3a52bb230a66',N'9be2954b-c7c0-5b8a-b003-be3cdd045f3b',0,3,19,N'Question number 40',N'<p>-Đáp án là preposition.</p><p>-“Long” được mô tả là gần như giới từ duy nhất trong Bishlama.</p><p>+Key word:</p><p>+ preposition (n) giới từ</p><p>+ grammar (n) ngữ pháp</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,40,NULL,0,1641),
(N'0ee7ab27-69c8-5ca0-bf3c-c2d33afc5651',NULL,0,0,11,NULL,NULL,NULL,N'',N'Vol 5 READING FULL TEST 14',0,7,1,NULL,1,1639),
(N'8e1bdc63-81c9-5d5e-9f66-138c6a3d45a4',N'0ee7ab27-69c8-5ca0-bf3c-c2d33afc5651',0,1,13,(CAST(N'<p><span><span>Tunnelling under the Thames</span></span></p><p><br>The first tunnel ever to be built under a major river was the tunnel under London''s River Thames. At the beginning of the 19th century, the port of London was the busiest in the world. Cargoes that had travelled thousands of miles and survived all the hazards of the sea were unloaded on the banks of the Thames, only for their owners to discover that the most frustrating portion of their journey lay ahead. Consignments intended for the southern parts of Britain had to be lifted onto horse carts, pulled through the docks and across London Bridge, built in the 12th century and as impractical as its early date implies. By 1820, London Bridge had become the centre of the world''s largest traffic jam.</p><p></p><p><br>It was an intolerable situation, and it was clear that if private enterprise could build another crossing closer to the docks, there would be good money to be made in tolls paid by users. Another bridge was out of the question, as this would deny sailing ships access to the city centre and ambitious men turned their thoughts to tunnelling beneath the Thames instead. This was not such an obvious idea as it might appear. Although increasing demand for coal had meant a great many tunnels had been dug in mines in Britain, working methods remained primitive. Tunnels were dug by men with simple tools, by candlelight. However, in 1807, a group of businessmen set themselves up as the Thames Archway Company. Their ambition was to tunnel below the Thames, but there was little to guide them as there had been no previous attempt to do this. Their chief engineer was Richard Trevithick, designer of the world''s first high-pressure steam engine. His men made progress at the beginning, but then things began to go disastrously wrong, with muddy soil pouring into the tunnel. Eventually, the Thames Archway Company had had enough. Its funds were exhausted, Trevithick was sick from exposure to the river water, and its efforts had proved only that a passage under the river exceeded the limits of contemporary mining technology.</p><p></p><p><br>At that time, the only machines used in mines were pumps. It took a man of genius to recognise that a different sort of machine was needed, a machine that could prevent the roof and walls of a tunnel from collapsing. This man was Marc Brunel, a Frenchman who had become one of the most prominent engineers in Britain. Not long after the failure of the Thames Archway Co' AS nvarchar(max))+N'mpany, Brunel saw a rotten piece of wood lying on the riverbank. Examining the wood through a magnifying glass, he observed it was infested with something that looked like a worm. Brunel realised that as it tunnelled through the wood, it would push chewed wood into its mouth and digest it, then excrete a hard substance that lined the new tunnel. Brunel realised that the worm''s digging technique could be adapted to produce a new way of tunnelling. His realisation led him to invent a device that has been used in one form or another in most major tunnels built since – the tunnelling shield. It consisted of a heavy iron frame that could be pushed forward a few inches at a time. The front of the frame was made up of a series of iron frames that could be folded back to allow miners to dig the ground ahead. Behind these frames was a wall consisting of a series of iron plates pressed against the tunnel face and supported on a set of horizontal wooden planks, that would prevent the face from collapsing. It was a complex and rather cumbersome machine and not easy to use, but it seemed that it would protect the miners from the worst of the river''s water. Brunel''s team carefully examined earth samples taken from beneath the riverbed, and subsequently decided to dig the tunnel close to the muddy river bottom, where he could expect to find clay. This would be a more solid and safe substance to dig through than the sand that was found deeper down.</p><p></p><p><br>Brunel began work on his tunnel in 1825, but the problems of such an operation soon became apparent. Although the shield itself worked well, water began to drip into the tunnel. This was more of an annoyance than a danger while the pump was working, but this machine proved unreliable and sometimes failed altogether. When the pump broke down, work had to stop as the tunnel quickly flooded. There were occasions when the miners had to abandon their tools and flee for their lives. Even when Brunel''s men were able to work, they had to run the constant risk of the pumps failing. They also complained of frequent headaches and dizziness, caused by the poor air quality. The air underground was dirty and stale, contaminated due to the lack of an adequate ventilation system. There were lighting problems too. Illuminating the tunnels by candlelight was a constant challenge. Lamps give off only a very weak glow, and there were a number of accidents because the miners could not see what they were doing. Lastly, a number of B'+N'runel''s miners walked off the job because they could not tolerate the excessive temperatures that developed in the cramped conditions underground.</p><p></p><p><br>Despite all these setbacks, the tunnel finally emerged on the opposite river bank on August 12, 1841. Brunel''s triumph, however, was only partial. The small payment per person made by the thousands of visitors who flocked to see the marvel hardly paid even a penny per foot of the tunnel''s construction costs. Brunel had gone bankrupt long before the project was completed, and the government loan he had required to complete the project had to be paid back with interest. As a result, there was not enough funding to make it accessible to horse-drawn vehicles, as intended. Instead, the passageways were filled with souvenir sellers and entertainers. In the end, the tunnel was closed two years later, used at night, before it was finally closed entirely and fell into dereliction for decades.</p><p><br>It was only when the underground railway came to London in the 1880s that the Thames Tunnel found and achieved a measure of real usefulness. It was bought in 1869 by the East London Railway, who found it to be in such excellent condition that it was immediately pressed into service as a route for passenger trains heading east. The tunnel became, and remains, part of the London Underground network.<br></p>'),NULL,NULL,N'',NULL,1,0,1,NULL,0,1639),
(N'9c8d1573-decc-509a-8a6b-da3c357655ee',N'8e1bdc63-81c9-5d5e-9f66-138c6a3d45a4',0,2,18,N'<p>In boxes 1-8 on your answer sheet, write: <span>TRUE/ FALSE/ NOT GIVEN.</span></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',1,0,1,NULL,0,1639),
(N'83a02793-7d8f-503e-b783-5010fbe9908a',N'9c8d1573-decc-509a-8a6b-da3c357655ee',0,3,19,N'<p>In the early 19th century, the port of London was considered a safer destination than other ports.</p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms: <br>+ Question: Interpretation: Vào đầu thế kỷ 19, cảng London được xem là điểm đến an toàn hơn so với các cảng khác.<br>+ Answer: Trong bài chỉ nói cảng London là cảng bận rộn nhất, hàng hoá đến đây sau khi vượt qua nguy hiểm của biển mà không hề có thông tin so sánh London với các cảng khác về độ an toàn </p><p>⇒ đáp án là NOT GIVEN.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,1,NULL,0,1639),
(N'96e13243-2dfd-522c-a2a0-09ea83c77cc3',N'9c8d1573-decc-509a-8a6b-da3c357655ee',0,3,19,N'<p>London Bridge provided quick access for cargo being sent to southern Britain. </p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms: southern parts of Britain = southern Britain<br>+ Question: Interpretation: Cầu London giúp vận chuyển hàng xuống miền Nam nhanh chóng.<br>+ Answer: Bài cho thấy cầu London không hiệu quả cho người dùng, phải thông qua nhiều bước mới có thể vận chuyển hàng tới miền nam nước Anh, tức là không hề nhanh </p><p>⇒ đáp án là FALSE.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,2,NULL,0,1639),
(N'fb510fba-19d7-542a-b862-9adf139b943f',N'9c8d1573-decc-509a-8a6b-da3c357655ee',0,3,19,N'<p>It was generally believed that a new river crossing would be profitable. </p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms: profitable = good money to be made in tolls<br>+ Question: Interpretation: Người ta tin rằng làm thêm một chỗ bắc qua sông sẽ sinh lời.<br>+ Answer: Thông tin trong bài có nhắc việc xây thêm một lối băng qua sông sẽ thu được nhiều tiền, tức là sẽ sinh lời </p><p>⇒ đáp án là TRUE.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,3,NULL,0,1639),
(N'6e917215-ee2e-5bab-aad4-2d540effc7c6',N'9c8d1573-decc-509a-8a6b-da3c357655ee',0,3,19,N'<p>Building a second bridge crossing was initially considered to be the best solution.</p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms: best solution = out of the question +Question: Interpretation: Giải pháp đầu tiên được nghĩ tới là xây thêm cầu. + Answer: Bài khẳng định ngay rằng không thể xây thêm cầu, vì thế chuyển sang nghĩ đến đường hầm, trái với đề bài </p><p>⇒ đáp án là FALSE.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,4,NULL,0,1639),
(N'39b40c0f-b55a-579a-bc44-1fab0af23a61',N'9c8d1573-decc-509a-8a6b-da3c357655ee',0,3,19,N'<p>It was believed that coal could be found under the River Thames. </p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms:<br>+ Question: Interpretation: Người ta tin rằng có thể tìm thấy than dưới lòng sông Thames.<br>+ Answer: Đoạn văn chỉ nói đến việc nhiều hầm mỏ than được đào ở Anh vì nhu cầu dùng than tăng chứ không hề nói có than dưới sông Thames </p><p>⇒ đáp án là NOT GIVEN.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,5,NULL,0,1639),
(N'05892fb6-5f4f-51e9-a066-bda6be6cb16c',N'9c8d1573-decc-509a-8a6b-da3c357655ee',0,3,19,N'<p>The Thames Archway Company was the first group to try tunnelling below the Thames. </p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms: first group = no previous attempt<br>+ Question: Interpretation: Công ty Thames Archway là nhóm đầu tiên thử đào hầm dưới sông Thames.<br>+ Answer: Trong bài nói rõ trước đó chưa từng có ai thử khi mà công ty Thames Archway đào hầm </p><p>⇒ Đáp án là TRUE.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,6,NULL,0,1639),
(N'75f036f0-245f-5129-aa26-e8fc6cb86dcd',N'9c8d1573-decc-509a-8a6b-da3c357655ee',0,3,19,N'<p>Some of Trevithick''s men were injured during a mudslide at his tunnel.</p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms: muddy soil pouring into the tunnel = mudslide at his tunnel<br>+ Question: Interpretation: Một số công nhân của Trevithick bị thương do đất bùn sạt vào hầm.<br>+ Answer: Trong bài chỉ nói bùn tràn vào hầm, không hề đề cập đến việc công nhân bị thương </p><p>⇒ đáp án là NOT GIVEN</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,7,NULL,0,1639),
(N'ed071a39-d6aa-5fad-a8cd-83f266eed5ee',N'9c8d1573-decc-509a-8a6b-da3c357655ee',0,3,19,N'<p>The Thames Archway Company ran out of money to finance the tunnel project.</p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms: ran out of money = funds were exhausted<br>+ Question: Interpretation: Công ty Thames Archway đã hết tiền để chi trả cho dự án đào hầm.<br>+ Answer: Thông tin trong bài có nói rõ là công Archway đã cạn kiệt vốn”, tức là không còn tiền để tiếp tục dự án. </p><p>⇒ Đáp là TRUE</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,8,NULL,0,1639),
(N'9d51195f-6db9-58b5-b005-08b04a38caa4',N'8e1bdc63-81c9-5d5e-9f66-138c6a3d45a4',0,2,18,N'<p>Complete the notes below.
Choose <span>ONE WORD ONLY</span> from the passage for each answer.
