Interpretation: Cảnh sát có thể nhận biết các vụ vẽ bậy mới bằng chữ ký, được gọi là …… mà họ đã quen.
+Answer:
Thông tin trong bài cho biết các chữ ký hoặc biệt danh đặc trưng, ​​được gọi là ‘tag’ có thể giúp xác định thủ phạm tiềm năng mà cảnh sát địa phương có thể đã quen thuộc =&gt; chúng được gọi là tag.
=&gt; Đáp án là tags
</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,25,NULL,0,1612),
(N'027f077c-990a-59c0-925f-33b9a27f27b8',N'd756a1bf-b813-587d-9a6b-329dda2835d1',0,3,19,N'Question number 26',N'<p>+ Question: Interpretation: Người vận hành phải tuân thủ các quy định liên quan trong quá trình vận hành và trang bị …… phù hợp. </p><p>+ Answers: Thông tin trong bài cho biết người vận hành cần tuân thủ hướng dẫn sử dụng sản phẩm về cách dùng và cách tháo gỡ, đồng thời phải đeo các thiết bị bảo hộ phù hợp =&gt; họ phải trang bị thiết bị bảo hộ phù hợp. </p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là protective equipment</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,26,NULL,0,1612),
(N'e40f84e1-4e9f-5494-a410-433b60dff554',N'b55c79f9-8c04-5bd6-b3b3-7f33eef6880c',0,1,15,(CAST(N'<p><span><span>Star Performers</span></span></p><p><em>Most organisations are looking for talent. But what if they’ve got it wrong, asks Jeffrey Pfeffer</em></p><p></p><p><span><span><span>A</span></span></span> One widely held assumption about talent is that it is a reasonably fixed characteristic and it is therefore the job of organisations to identify, recruit and retain star performers. This belief affects the way people are managed in the workplace. Most recruitment decisions are influenced by the skills and abilities of an individual rather than their aptitude and attitude. In terms of career development, organisations invest in staff who have been selected to reach higher-level positions, while ignoring front-line employees and people with less perceived potential. This idea, that talent is a fixed, identifiable characteristic – and that those firms with the best people do the best – is both flawed and harmful to people and organisations. There is a lot of evidence on this point, and it is useful to highlight some of the most pertinent arguments.</p><p></p><p><span><span>B</span></span> First, are there stars? There is no question that in every field, from sports to computer programming to music, there are people who are better than the rest. As psychologist Dean Keith Simonton, who has spent his career studying greatness, has said, ‘Wherever you look, the same story can be told. Identify the ten per cent who have achieved the most in a certain endeavour. Count the accomplishments they have to their credit. Now tally the accomplishments of the remaining 90 per cent. The first tally will equal or surpass the second.’ For instance, in music, 16 individuals have produced about 50 per cent of the Western classical music that is performed and recorded today, while another 235 composers have produced the remaining half. The more interesting questions concern not the existence of stars, but whether these stars can be reliably identified and, even more importantly, whether their talent is a fixed aspect or can be altered.</p><p></p><p><span><span>C</span></span> Identifying the best people is tricky. Quality of performance changes over time and this is true whether we are talking about professors or footballers. If performance naturally varies, any measurement taken at a single point in time, such as when someone is being hired, will have error and imprecision. Therefore, single assessments of talent are likely to contain mistakes in their categorisation of' AS nvarchar(max))+N' people. Also, judgements about performance and ability depend on the standards used to judge what is good and bad. It should surprise no-one that for Bach to be considered a great musician, standards of music needed to change to embrace the qualities that his compositions possessed. Similarly, artists and art come in and out of fashion, which means that what is genius depends not only on a person’s ability, but on the prevailing standards used to evaluate output. 3 Turn over</p><p></p><p><span><span>D </span></span>Finally, it is difficult to evaluate people and their abilities with precision. In the domain of work, research shows that the best predictors of job performance tend to be measures of intelligence. But even these measures correlate only loosely with performance, which means that more than 80 per cent of the variation in performance is unexplained by even the best predictors. Even in the sports arena, where one would think natural ability would be readily assessed because sports teams spend lots of resources on identifying talent, mistakes get made. Basketball star Michael Jordan was dropped by his high-school basketball coach and a number of top American football quarterbacks were available early in their careers because they were not considered good enough by various teams.</p><p></p><p><span><span>E </span></span>This leads on to the next question: is talent born or made? Should organisations assume that almost anyone can become a star performer, which implies that there ought to be a greater emphasis on motivation and development, or do they just figure out who is good and who isn’t? Here the evidence is clear: talent is at least as much ‘created’ as inherent and, more importantly, the customary way companies think about identifying talent almost certainly works to destroy a lot of untapped potential. Decades of research by K Anders Ericsson, professor of psychology at Florida State University, show that exceptional performance doesn’t happen without around ten years of nearly daily, deliberate practice for about four hours a day, by people who with the assistance of their coaches have access to the best techniques. Once achieved, exceptional performance can’t be maintained without relentless effort. So performance may be as much a consequence of training as it is of innate ability, which suggests that performance can be altered by how people are managed.</p><p></p><p><span><span>F</span></span> Further research by Stanford psychology profe'+N'ssor Carol Dweck shows that the tendency of organisations to see performance results as an opportunity for an ‘assessment’ of ability, results in lower performance and poor motivation. Dweck identified two sets of goals that people bring to a performance context: ‘performance goals, where the purpose is to validate one’s ability or avoid demonstrating a lack of ability, and learning goals, where the aim is to acquire new knowledge and skills’. People with performance goals have been shown to be more prone to helpless behaviour and debilitation after a setback, while people with learning goals strive for higher performance. The implications for managing people and talent are clear. Seeing talent as fixed and job performance as a way of classifying people creates a self fulfilling prophecy in which ability and intelligence do become fixed. By contrast, seeing ability as malleable leads to a different sort of self-fulfilling prophecy, in which individuals and their employers may invest in ways to enhance</p>'),NULL,NULL,N'',NULL,1,0,3,NULL,0,1612),
(N'9ee8bcf8-77dc-5326-8139-4862289f13c5',N'e40f84e1-4e9f-5494-a410-433b60dff554',0,2,18,N'<p>Reading Passage 3 has six paragraphs, <span>A-F. </span></p><p>Which paragraph contains the following information? </p><p>Write the correct letter, <span>A-F,</span> in boxes 27-32 on your answer sheet. </p><p><span>NB</span> You may use any letter more than once. </p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',12,0,1,NULL,0,1612),
(N'25449a49-3e03-5a8f-8aab-be36c3afaa7c',N'9ee8bcf8-77dc-5326-8139-4862289f13c5',0,3,19,N'<p>disagreement with the view that employing talented people enables companies to achieve top performance. </p>',N'<p>+ Question: Interpretation: Sự phản đối quan điểm cho rằng tuyển người tài sẽ giúp công ty đạt thành tích cao nhất.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn A cho rằng quan điểm những công ty có nhân viên giỏi nhất sẽ hoạt động tốt nhất vừa sai lầm vừa gây hại cho cả cá nhân và tổ chức</p><p>=&gt; phản đối rõ ràng quan điểm được đưa ra.</p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là A</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,27,NULL,0,1612),
(N'4d92328d-3185-53c3-856d-17babc0283eb',N'9ee8bcf8-77dc-5326-8139-4862289f13c5',0,3,19,N'<p>a description of what individuals have to do on a regular basis to improve their performance. </p>',N'<p>+ Question: Interpretation: Mô tả những gì cá nhân phải làm thường xuyên để cải thiện hiệu suất.</p><p>+ Answer: Thông tin trong đoạn E cho biết để có được thành tích xuất sắc cần khoảng mười năm luyện tập gần như hàng ngày, có chủ đích, khoảng bốn giờ mỗi ngày, bởi những người được huấn luyện viên hướng dẫn và tiếp cận với những kỹ thuật tốt nhất</p><p>=&gt; nêu ra những gì cá nhân phải làm thường xuyên để cải thiện hiệu suất.</p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là E</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,28,NULL,0,1612),
(N'5ac57102-cde7-5487-ba3d-3496169f5b58',N'9ee8bcf8-77dc-5326-8139-4862289f13c5',0,3,19,N'<p>the evidence that exceptional talent exists in all areas of life.</p>',N'<p>+ Question: Interpretation: Bằng chứng cho thấy tài năng xuất chúng tồn tại trong mọi lĩnh vực của cuộc sống.</p><p>+ Answer: Theo thông tin trong đoạn B, trong mọi lĩnh vực, từ thể thao đến lập trình máy tính đến âm nhạc, đều có những người giỏi hơn những người khác =&gt; tài năng xuất chúng tồn tại trong mọi lĩnh vực.</p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là B</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,29,NULL,0,1612),
(N'd6a51797-f4de-52a9-b630-d34d84fb4b22',N'9ee8bcf8-77dc-5326-8139-4862289f13c5',0,3,19,N'<p>how different ways of evaluating achievement at work can cause different reactions in employees. </p>',N'<p>+ Question: Interpretation: Cách đánh giá thành tích công việc khác nhau có thể dẫn đến những phản ứng khác nhau ở nhân viên.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn F cho biết những người theo đuổi mục tiêu thành tích thường cảm thấy bất lực và suy nhược sau thất bại, trong khi những người theo đuổi mục tiêu học tập luôn phấn đấu để đạt được hiệu suất cao hơn</p><p>=&gt; cho thấy phản ứng khác nhau.</p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là F</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,30,NULL,0,1612),
(N'679e874c-aa81-59d5-81bb-4e5907da48dd',N'9ee8bcf8-77dc-5326-8139-4862289f13c5',0,3,19,N'<p>the belief that the time when an assessment is carried out affects its accuracy. </p>',N'<p>+ Question: Interpretation: Niềm tin rằng thời điểm tiến hành đánh giá ảnh hưởng đến độ chính xác của nó.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn C nêu rõ bất kỳ đánh giá được thực hiện tại một thời điểm duy nhất đều sẽ có sai số và thiếu chính xác.</p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là C</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,31,NULL,0,1612),
(N'86054ffa-1245-520d-872c-92e7d6c57e4e',N'9ee8bcf8-77dc-5326-8139-4862289f13c5',0,3,19,N'<p>the extent to which different talented individuals have contributed to their particular area of achievement. </p>',N'<p>+ Question: Interpretation: Mức độ đóng góp của các cá nhân tài năng khác nhau vào lĩnh vực thành tựu cụ thể của họ.</p><p>+ Answer: Thông tin trong đoạn B cho biết 16 cá nhân trong lĩnh vực âm nhạc đã sáng tác khoảng 50% số lượng nhạc cổ điển phương Tây được trình diễn và thu âm ngày nay</p><p>=&gt; cho thấy độ đóng góp rất lớn.</p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là B</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,32,NULL,0,1612),
(N'296445f5-d06a-5767-b216-60dd7bb47002',N'e40f84e1-4e9f-5494-a410-433b60dff554',0,2,18,N'<p>Answer the questions below. </p><p>Choose <span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER</span> from the passage for each answer. </p><p>Write your answers in boxes 33-35 on your answer sheet. </p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',11,0,2,NULL,0,1612),
(N'c6303fb9-ad13-50c8-96f0-99bf44618556',N'296445f5-d06a-5767-b216-60dd7bb47002',0,3,19,N'<p>How many Western classical composers are identified as exceptionally talented? }{SPACE}{ </p><p>Which composer initially received little recognition for his work? }{SPACE}{ </p><p>Who can help improve the performance of people practising daily? }{SPACE}{ </p>',N'<p>+ Question: Interpretation: Có bao nhiêu nhà soạn nhạc cổ điển phương Tây được đánh giá là tài năng xuất chúng?</p><p>+ Answer: Thông tin trong bài cho biết 16 cá nhân trong lĩnh vực âm nhạc đã sáng tác khoảng 50% số lượng nhạc cổ điển phương Tây được trình diễn và thu âm ngày nay</p><p>=&gt; nghĩa là có 16 nhà soạn nhạc cổ điển phương Tây được đánh giá là tài năng xuất chúng.</p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là 16</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,33,NULL,0,1612),
(N'aba97247-493c-5290-a045-c10e9cdb8bb2',N'296445f5-d06a-5767-b216-60dd7bb47002',0,3,19,N'Question number 34',N'<p>+Question: Interpretation: Nhà soạn nhạc nào ban đầu nhận được rất ít sự công nhận cho các tác phẩm của mình? </p><p>+Answer:  Thông tin trong bài cho biết để Bach được coi là một nhạc sĩ vĩ đại thì các tiêu chuẩn âm nhạc cần phải thay đổi để đón nhận những phẩm chất mà các tác phẩm của ông sở hữu </p><p>=&gt; vậy khi các tiêu chuẩn chưa thay đổi thì các tác phẩm của ông không được đón nhận. </p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là bach </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,34,NULL,0,1612),
(N'cb41a912-037d-5db2-8a59-17b5ce379780',N'296445f5-d06a-5767-b216-60dd7bb47002',0,3,19,N'Question number 35',N'<p>+ Question: Interpretation: Ai có thể giúp cải thiện hiệu quả luyện tập hàng ngày của mọi người?</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn văn cho thấy thành tích xuất sắc có thể đạt được nếu luyện tập thường xuyên và được hướng dẫn bởi những huấn luyện viên và tiếp cận với những kỹ thuật tốt nhất</p><p>=&gt; người có thể giúp cải thiện hiệu quả là những huấn luyện viên.</p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là coaches</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,35,NULL,0,1612),
(N'86df0c4e-5267-5cb3-8f92-8f9bc26fede9',N'e40f84e1-4e9f-5494-a410-433b60dff554',0,2,18,N'<p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3? </span></p><p><span>In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write </span></p><p><span><span>TRUE </span>if the statement agrees with the information </span></p><p><span><span>FALSE</span> if the statement contradicts the information </span></p><p><span><span>NOT GIVEN</span> if there is no information on this </span></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',1,0,3,NULL,0,1612),
(N'591ca570-c029-5910-86cb-1b147bca83dd',N'86df0c4e-5267-5cb3-8f92-8f9bc26fede9',0,3,19,N'<p>Companies usually hire people on the basis of their character.</p>',N'<p>+ Question: Interpretation: Các công ty thường tuyển dụng người dựa trên tính cách của họ.</p><p>+ Answer: Bài đọc cho biết hầu hết các quyết định tuyển dụng đều bị ảnh hưởng bởi kỹ năng và khả năng của cá nhân hơn là năng khiếu và thái độ của họ</p><p>=&gt; vậy nên quyết định không dựa trên tính cách.</p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là FALSE</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,36,NULL,0,1612),
(N'befa126f-8d78-5139-b5d0-ee75baa23f74',N'86df0c4e-5267-5cb3-8f92-8f9bc26fede9',0,3,19,N'<p>There are some areas of sport that have a greater proportion of talent than others.</p>',N'<p>+ Question: Interpretation: Có một số lĩnh vực thể thao có tỷ lệ tài năng cao hơn những lĩnh vực khác.</p><p>+ Answer: Bài chỉ nói mọi lĩnh vực đều có người giỏi, không so sánh tỷ lệ giữa lĩnh vực thể thao và những lĩnh vực khác.</p><p>=&gt; Đáp án cần điền là NOT GIVEN</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,37,NULL,0,1612),
(N'64e142ad-fd77-52ae-a7ac-b7ac9f47d0b5',N'86df0c4e-5267-5cb3-8f92-8f9bc26fede9',0,3,19,N'<p>Measures of intelligence accurately predict performance at work.</p>',N'<p>+ Question: Interpretation: Các chỉ số đo lường trí thông minh dự đoán chính xác hiệu suất làm việc.</p><p>+ Answer: Thông tin trong bài cho biết chỉ số về trí thông minh tương quan lỏng lẻo với hiệu suất, nghĩa là hơn 80% sự biến động về hiệu suất không được giải thích với ngay cả bởi các chỉ số dự đoán tốt nhất</p><p>=&gt; các chỉ số đo lường trí thông minh không thể dự đoán chính xác hiệu suất làm việc.</p><p>=&gt; Đáp án cần điền là FALSE</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,38,NULL,0,1612),
(N'59f69e29-7734-57ff-b3d4-88761106fd13',N'86df0c4e-5267-5cb3-8f92-8f9bc26fede9',0,3,19,N'<p>There are cases in which talented sportspeople have been overlooked.</p>',N'<p>+ Question: Interpretation: Có những trường hợp vận động viên tài năng bị bỏ qua.</p><p>+ Answers: Thông tin trong bài cho biết ngôi sao bóng rổ Michael Jordan từng bị huấn luyện viên bóng rổ thời trung học loại khỏi đội, và một số hậu vệ xuất sắc của đội bóng bầu dục Mỹ cũng từng bị các đội khác đánh giá thấp ngay từ đầu sự nghiệp</p><p>=&gt; ta thấy được những trường hợp vận động viên tài năng bị bỏ qua.</p><p>=&gt; Câu trả lời sẽ là TRUE</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,39,NULL,0,1612),
(N'3c8ad2a4-c0cd-5772-93c1-e5f9c05078bc',N'86df0c4e-5267-5cb3-8f92-8f9bc26fede9',0,3,19,N'<p>Newly formed organisations have the most highly motivated staff.</p>',N'<p>+ Question: Interpretation: Các tổ chức mới thành lập thường có đội ngũ nhân viên năng động nhất.</p><p>+ Answers: Không có thông tin nói về các tổ chức mới thành lập.</p><p>=&gt; Câu trả lời sẽ là NOT GIVEN</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,40,NULL,0,1612),
(N'9bdf3c34-cc78-5b9f-a28d-bb0805572394',NULL,0,0,11,NULL,NULL,NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-3/iL.VOL3.8.S1589.mp3',N'Vol 3 LISTENING FULL TEST 8',0,7,1,NULL,1,1589),
(N'663ab57b-8269-5d5e-b351-6c310d82b3be',N'9bdf3c34-cc78-5b9f-a28d-bb0805572394',0,1,13,(CAST(N'<h2>Art Show Registration Form</h2><p>Certainly, I''ll just need a few details. Can you provide your postcode to find your booking? Sure, it''s AF741T. Thank you. Ah yes, I''ve found your booking. Just to confirm, you''ve booked for the 25th of November, right? Yes, that''s correct. What time does the event begin? The doors open at 4pm, but the actual event starts at 4.30pm. However, we advise arriving early to avoid any delays. By the way, did you know there''s a discount for local residents? Yes, I think I already received it. I''m pretty sure I paid £16.50, right? Hmm, let me check. Ah yes, you''re right. You paid £16.50 instead of the standard £20. I''m glad I qualified for the discount. Will my family members be able to come for free, as I heard? That''s correct. </p><p>Family members of local residents can enter free of charge. Just make sure you bring some form of ID that shows your residency. Excellent. Do you know how many artworks will be on display this year? Oh, there will be more than 360 pieces from both local and international artists. Last year, we had 320 pieces, but we''ve expanded the exhibition. That''s impressive. And will there be any special performances this time? Yes, there''s a live sound show that''s generating a lot of excitement. It''s actually the first time we''re including this type of performance. Oh, a sound performance. I love unique events like that. Now, I also heard there will be live music, right? I believe I read it''s going to be guitar music. Actually, there was an initial plan for guitar music, but it''s been changed. Instead, we''ll have live piano music, which we think will create a better atmosphere for the event. That sounds lovely. Now, I''m curious about refreshments. Will there be any available? Yes, drinks will be sold at the venue, and each ticket holder gets a free drink, either alcoholic or non-alcoholic, depending on your preference. We''ll have a selection of beverages available, including water, juices and wine. </p><p>Nice. I''ll probably stick to non-alcoholic. I''m bringing my kids along. Are there any special activities for them? Certainly. We''re offering art workshops for children under 12, but please note that parents or guardians must accompany them at all times during the event. Understood. I''ll make sure to keep an eye on them. One last thing. What happens if the event is cancelled? Will we get our money back? Unfortunately, the tickets are non-refundable, but don''t worry. We''ve taken out an insurance policy for t' AS nvarchar(max))+N'he event. In the event of cancellation, the insurance will cover the cost of your tickets, so you''re safe there. That''s good to know. Thanks for all the information. You''re welcome. We look forward to seeing you at the event.</p>'),(CAST(N'<p>Certainly, I''ll just need a few details. Can you provide your postcode to find your booking? Sure, it''s AF741T. Thank you. Ah yes, I''ve found your booking. Just to confirm, you''ve booked for the 25th of November, right? Yes, that''s correct. What time does the event begin? The doors open at 4pm, but the actual event starts at 4.30pm. However, we advise arriving early to avoid any delays. By the way, did you know there''s a discount for local residents? Yes, I think I already received it. I''m pretty sure I paid £16.50, right? Hmm, let me check. Ah yes, you''re right. You paid £16.50 instead of the standard £20. I''m glad I qualified for the discount. Will my family members be able to come for free, as I heard? That''s correct. </p><p>Family members of local residents can enter free of charge. Just make sure you bring some form of ID that shows your residency. Excellent. Do you know how many artworks will be on display this year? Oh, there will be more than 360 pieces from both local and international artists. Last year, we had 320 pieces, but we''ve expanded the exhibition. That''s impressive. And will there be any special performances this time? Yes, there''s a live sound show that''s generating a lot of excitement. It''s actually the first time we''re including this type of performance. Oh, a sound performance. I love unique events like that. Now, I also heard there will be live music, right? I believe I read it''s going to be guitar music. Actually, there was an initial plan for guitar music, but it''s been changed. Instead, we''ll have live piano music, which we think will create a better atmosphere for the event. That sounds lovely. Now, I''m curious about refreshments. Will there be any available? Yes, drinks will be sold at the venue, and each ticket holder gets a free drink, either alcoholic or non-alcoholic, depending on your preference. We''ll have a selection of beverages available, including water, juices and wine. </p><p>Nice. I''ll probably stick to non-alcoholic. I''m bringing my kids along. Are there any special activities for them? Certainly. We''re offering art workshops for children under 12, but please note that parents or guardians must accompany them at all times during the event. Understood. I''ll make sure to keep an eye on them. One last thing. What happens if the event is cancelled? Will we get our money back? Unfortunately, the tickets are non-refundable, but don''t worry. We''ve taken out an insurance policy for the event. In the event of cancellat' AS nvarchar(max))+N'ion, the insurance will cover the cost of your tickets, so you''re safe there. That''s good to know. Thanks for all the information. You''re welcome. We look forward to seeing you at the event.</p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-3/iL.VOL3.8.S1589.PART1.mp3',NULL,1,0,1,NULL,0,1589),
(N'661ed823-214b-555c-b52c-b7e76fd45629',N'663ab57b-8269-5d5e-b351-6c310d82b3be',0,2,18,N'<p>Complete the form below.

Write ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER for each answer.</p>',N'',N'',N'',N'Art Show Registration Form',11,0,1,NULL,0,1589),
(N'7808be39-85f9-5fee-8ed9-95f5de4a7cef',N'661ed823-214b-555c-b52c-b7e76fd45629',0,3,19,N'<h3>Art Show Registration Form</h3><p><span>Event Name</span>: Annual Community Art Show</p><p><span>Visitor Details:</span></p><ul><li><p>Name: Alex Brown</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Postcode:</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p><p><span>Event Details:</span></p><ul><li><p>Date: 25th November</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Time</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p><ul><li><p>Standard Ticket Price: £20.00</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Discounted Ticket (for residents): £</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p><ul><li><p>Free entry for</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ members</p><ul><li><p>Over</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ artworks on display</p><ul><li><p>Special live performances include a</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ show</p><p><span>Additional Facilities:</span></p><ul><li><p>Live </p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ music</p><ul><li><p>Refreshments will be available for purchase, including a free</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ with each ticket.</p><p><span>Important Information:</span></p><ul><li><p>available for children under 12 (accompanied by</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{  )</p><ul><li><p>non-refundable but covered by</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ in case of event cancellation.</p>',N'<p>+Câu hỏi: Postcode: ______ </p><p>+Giải thích: Người nghe trực tiếp đọc mã bưu điện “AF741T”. </p><p>+Từ vựng: postcode = mã bưu điện.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,1,NULL,0,1589),
(N'396f6db6-e5c6-5f04-9bbb-4c5d3777606d',N'661ed823-214b-555c-b52c-b7e76fd45629',0,3,19,N'Question number 2',N'<p>+Câu hỏi: Time: ______ </p><p>+Giải thích: Giờ khai mạc chính thức là 4.30pm, không phải 4pm. </p><p>+Từ vựng: actual event starts at = sự kiện chính bắt đầu lúc.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,2,NULL,0,1589),
(N'be79ac8a-1d58-5436-b4d2-b1aceb2f0891',N'661ed823-214b-555c-b52c-b7e76fd45629',0,3,19,N'Question number 3',N'<p>+Câu hỏi: Discounted ticket (for residents): £______ </p><p>+Giải thích: Giá giảm cho cư dân địa phương là £16.50. </p><p>+Từ vựng: instead of = thay vì.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,3,NULL,0,1589),
(N'cb61bf83-f5e0-5c2d-80a0-8f58b464cbf2',N'661ed823-214b-555c-b52c-b7e76fd45629',0,3,19,N'Question number 4',N'<p>+Câu hỏi: Free entry for ______ members. </p><p>+Giải thích: Miễn phí cho các thành viên trong gia đình cư dân. </p><p>+Từ vựng: free of charge = miễn phí.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,4,NULL,0,1589),
(N'3375a57c-7b41-5f1e-9651-8cca44fef68e',N'661ed823-214b-555c-b52c-b7e76fd45629',0,3,19,N'Question number 5',N'<p>+Câu hỏi: Over ______ artworks on display. </p><p>+Giải thích: Số tác phẩm trưng bày hơn 360. </p><p>+Từ vựng: artworks on display = tác phẩm được trưng bày.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,5,NULL,0,1589),
(N'c6f9c018-be02-5bc8-be4f-45eec0f22781',N'661ed823-214b-555c-b52c-b7e76fd45629',0,3,19,N'Question number 6',N'<p>+Câu hỏi: Special live performances include a ______ show.
+Giải thích: Buổi biểu diễn đặc biệt là “sound show”.
+Từ vựng: live performance = trình diễn trực tiếp.
</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,6,NULL,0,1589),
(N'd6557242-80a6-5839-bca7-fa4267fd661e',N'661ed823-214b-555c-b52c-b7e76fd45629',0,3,19,N'Question number 7',N'<p>+Câu hỏi: Live ______ music. </p><p>+Giải thích: Âm nhạc trực tiếp là piano (không phải guitar như dự định). </p><p>+Từ vựng: live music = nhạc sống.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,7,NULL,0,1589),
(N'e74ac809-0099-5f96-ab68-498ac9a88d57',N'661ed823-214b-555c-b52c-b7e76fd45629',0,3,19,N'Question number 8',N'<p>+Câu hỏi: ... including a free ______ with each ticket.</p><p> +Giải thích: Mỗi vé đi kèm một đồ uống miễn phí.</p><p> +Từ vựng: ticket holder = người có vé.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,8,NULL,0,1589),
(N'30286048-999f-513b-863e-7c5dbd833a60',N'661ed823-214b-555c-b52c-b7e76fd45629',0,3,19,N'Question number 9',N'<p>+Câu hỏi: Available for children under 12 (accompanied by ______). </p><p>+Giải thích: Trẻ em dưới 12 tuổi phải đi cùng cha mẹ hoặc người giám hộ. </p><p>+Từ vựng: accompany = đi cùng, hộ tống.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,9,NULL,0,1589),
(N'e89c9952-76ec-5182-b883-f0317bcaf5cc',N'661ed823-214b-555c-b52c-b7e76fd45629',0,3,19,N'Question number 10',N'<p>+Câu hỏi: Non-refundable but covered by ______ in case of event cancellation. </p><p>+Giải thích: Dù không hoàn tiền, vé vẫn được bảo hiểm chi trả nếu hủy sự kiện. </p><p>+Từ vựng: covered by insurance = được bảo hiểm chi trả.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,10,NULL,0,1589),
(N'6fa821e9-4671-562c-86cd-2b8478d33ec4',N'9bdf3c34-cc78-5b9f-a28d-bb0805572394',0,1,14,(CAST(N'<h2>Burnside Fitness Centre</h2><p>Good morning everyone. We are gathered today for the unveiling of our new fitness centre. Our business started in 2006 when we recognised the need for a new, modern and affordable fitness centre for those living in the area. We pulled resources together and started a small centre just off this road to your left. We have been there over the years until we decided we needed more room and more facilities due to the increasing numbers. This new facility is estimated to contain at least 1,000 people at a time and is equipped with the latest state-of-the-art fitness facilities you can think of.  </p><p>From the entrance, just to your right, you would get to the meeting room where we hold team meetings sometimes. In the past, our customers usually came in through the west gate and went to the first room on their left to exercise. Well, this room used to be the gym room but now it''s the women''s fitting room.  Our female customers can change and try on clothes there. The gym room would be the big room on your right as you enter from the west gate. It houses state-of-the-art gym equipment as well as provides an arena for working out.  At the top right corner of the map, we have the men''s fitting room where men can change with some privacy. Some Squash members say they would like to have classes at the room between two fitting rooms as it would be more convenient to change after sweating. Well, we will have a discussion about it and inform you if any changes happen.  Now our Squash court is still at the other wing situated directly opposite the west gate. The larger building behind it is the largest in the state for skating courses. It provides adequate conditioning and the properly selected tracks for beginners.  Before you hear the rest of the talk, you have some time to look at questions 16 to 20. Now listen and answer questions 16 to 20. Why invest a lot in fitness and sports? Well, we have observed that in our society, the rate at which people develop preventable diseases is alarming.  Statistics show that there is a very strong link between sedentary lifestyle and these diseases. We have set up this centre to correct and combat it while making sure it is open accessible and affordable to all. To develop overall strength in the individual, the fitness machines are built to help those who always complain of muscle weakness, to overcome their challenges.  We also have rooms for mat exercises. </p><p>Many people always think that ' AS nvarchar(max))+N'such exercises are only good for limbs and shoulders. Well, actually for anyone who wants to have a flexible body, these exercises such as plank and crunches are a good choice.  You don''t need any high-end fitness equipment. We also have an expansive space just behind the building that we use for cycling exercises. This sport is good to help develop strength in the legs and it is equally a good way of freeing the mind.  Many members hope that such exercises will help them lose weight. I''m afraid they don''t work that way. We offer aerobics for those interested in raising their heart rate.  It is a great sport to train your mind and also makes blood flow more efficient and faster. Contrary to what most people think, weight training does little to help you lose weight but it does help you develop solid mental coordination and to stay focused without getting distracted so easily. So, as we unveil this centre today, we''re glad that you can also be a part of this step in the right direction.</p>'),(CAST(N'<p>Good morning everyone. We are gathered today for the unveiling of our new fitness centre. Our business started in 2006 when we recognised the need for a new, modern and affordable fitness centre for those living in the area. We pulled resources together and started a small centre just off this road to your left. We have been there over the years until we decided we needed more room and more facilities due to the increasing numbers. This new facility is estimated to contain at least 1,000 people at a time and is equipped with the latest state-of-the-art fitness facilities you can think of.  </p><p>From the entrance, just to your right, you would get to the meeting room where we hold team meetings sometimes. In the past, our customers usually came in through the west gate and went to the first room on their left to exercise. Well, this room used to be the gym room but now it''s the women''s fitting room.  Our female customers can change and try on clothes there. The gym room would be the big room on your right as you enter from the west gate. It houses state-of-the-art gym equipment as well as provides an arena for working out.  At the top right corner of the map, we have the men''s fitting room where men can change with some privacy. Some Squash members say they would like to have classes at the room between two fitting rooms as it would be more convenient to change after sweating. Well, we will have a discussion about it and inform you if any changes happen.  Now our Squash court is still at the other wing situated directly opposite the west gate. The larger building behind it is the largest in the state for skating courses. It provides adequate conditioning and the properly selected tracks for beginners.  Before you hear the rest of the talk, you have some time to look at questions 16 to 20. Now listen and answer questions 16 to 20. Why invest a lot in fitness and sports? Well, we have observed that in our society, the rate at which people develop preventable diseases is alarming.  Statistics show that there is a very strong link between sedentary lifestyle and these diseases. We have set up this centre to correct and combat it while making sure it is open accessible and affordable to all. To develop overall strength in the individual, the fitness machines are built to help those who always complain of muscle weakness, to overcome their challenges.  We also have rooms for mat exercises. </p><p>Many people always think that such exercises are only good for' AS nvarchar(max))+N' limbs and shoulders. Well, actually for anyone who wants to have a flexible body, these exercises such as plank and crunches are a good choice.  You don''t need any high-end fitness equipment. We also have an expansive space just behind the building that we use for cycling exercises. This sport is good to help develop strength in the legs and it is equally a good way of freeing the mind.  Many members hope that such exercises will help them lose weight. I''m afraid they don''t work that way. We offer aerobics for those interested in raising their heart rate.  It is a great sport to train your mind and also makes blood flow more efficient and faster. Contrary to what most people think, weight training does little to help you lose weight but it does help you develop solid mental coordination and to stay focused without getting distracted so easily. So, as we unveil this centre today, we''re glad that you can also be a part of this step in the right direction.</p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-3/iL.VOL3.8.S1589.PART2.mp3',NULL,1,0,2,NULL,0,1589),
(N'c71de41e-e354-5eef-9ef1-14a005c2f52e',N'6fa821e9-4671-562c-86cd-2b8478d33ec4',0,2,18,N'<p>Label the map below. </p><p>Write the correct letter, <span>A-H</span>, next to Question 11-15</p><p><img src="https://ieltsroom.com/upload/images/ieltsadvancedtest/7ca32d06822ddf8fbc5b.png" alt="Question diagram"></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'Burnside Fitness Centre',12,0,1,NULL,0,1589),
(N'1069632b-27b3-5c36-9a3a-fdb96221d836',N'c71de41e-e354-5eef-9ef1-14a005c2f52e',0,3,19,N'<p>meeting room</p>',N'<p>+Câu hỏi: Meeting room. </p><p>+Giải thích: Phòng họp nằm ngay bên phải entrance, ứng với G trên bản đồ. </p><p>+Từ vựng: meeting room = phòng họp. - entrance = lối vào - just to your right = ngay bên phải</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,11,NULL,0,1589),
(N'15bdbfa1-8792-52bc-ba7d-9e2892117866',N'c71de41e-e354-5eef-9ef1-14a005c2f52e',0,3,19,N'<p>women''s fitting room</p>',N'<p>+Câu hỏi: Women’s fitting room. </p><p>+Giải thích: Cửa west gate =&gt; rẽ trái =&gt; phòng đầu tiên là women’s fitting room, tương ứng H. - fitting room = phòng thay đồ - on the left = bên trái</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,12,NULL,0,1589),
(N'3953174c-1000-5065-8c31-ac2bb7e38c2f',N'c71de41e-e354-5eef-9ef1-14a005c2f52e',0,3,19,N'<p>fitness room</p>',N'<p>+Câu hỏi: Fitness room. Giải thích: Phòng tập (fitness room) nằm bên phải cổng tây, phòng lớn =&gt; C.
