(N'355f3030-8662-584e-9515-2c487d8e8761',N'a8fce4e1-a5a5-549c-8b74-8d06bbc1447d',0,3,19,N'<h3>Notes on New Jobs</h3><table border="1"><tbody><tr><td><p><span>Work details:</span></p> <ul><li><p>James enjoys the</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ of his work.</p> <ul><li><p>Annie does not enjoy all the</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ for her work.</p> <ul><li><p>Her job involves</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ and offering advice.</p> <ul><li><p>She works in the Council’s</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ Assessment division.</p> <ul><li><p>She proposes the</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ utilization of her clients’ land.</p> <p><span>Development application:</span></p> <ul><li><p>There are two difficult things for the farmer in her application, i.e.</p></li></ul> <p> }{SPACE}{ </p> <p>A new }{SPACE}{ </p> <p><span>Other information:</span></p> <ul><li><p>Annie thinks offspring</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ can control the land use.</p> <ul><li><p>A tram service ceased in James and Annie’s town in</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p> <ul><li><p>James studies</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ at university.</p></td></tr></tbody></table>',N'<p>Đáp án là location. James nói rõ điều anh ấy thích ở công việc của mình là vị trí làm việc, vì nó gần Central Library. Từ này xuất hiện trực tiếp trong lời nói và khớp hoàn toàn với cấu trúc câu trong đề.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,1,NULL,0,1563),
(N'37a953f3-d689-53bd-80c4-824dd138b458',N'a8fce4e1-a5a5-549c-8b74-8d06bbc1447d',0,3,19,N'Question number 2',N'<p>Đáp án là travelling. Annie cho biết điều cô không thích trong công việc là việc phải di chuyển quá nhiều, do khu vực làm việc rộng và phải đi lại bằng nhiều phương tiện khác nhau.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,2,NULL,0,1563),
(N'5d6170d8-1793-5a86-9e3f-25a3df16243a',N'a8fce4e1-a5a5-549c-8b74-8d06bbc1447d',0,3,19,N'Question number 3',N'<p>Đáp án là surveying. Khi được hỏi công việc cụ thể gồm những gì, Annie trả lời rằng phần lớn thời gian của cô dành cho việc khảo sát, sau đó mới đến tư vấn cho người sử dụng đất.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,3,NULL,0,1563),
(N'74eec47e-c62d-5ba3-8c5f-b87d2cc03c44',N'a8fce4e1-a5a5-549c-8b74-8d06bbc1447d',0,3,19,N'Question number 4',N'<p>Đáp án là Ecological. Annie làm việc trong bộ phận Ecological Assessment của Hội đồng, vì vậy chỉ cần điền từ đứng trước “Assessment” theo đúng form đề bài.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,4,NULL,0,1563),
(N'27bdf7b9-3689-5b8e-9ae4-8c81bf6b9f7b',N'a8fce4e1-a5a5-549c-8b74-8d06bbc1447d',0,3,19,N'Question number 5',N'<p>Đáp án là best. Annie nói nhiệm vụ của cô là đề xuất cách sử dụng đất tốt nhất cho khách hàng, đồng thời vẫn bảo vệ hoặc phục hồi hệ sinh thái.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,5,NULL,0,1563),
(N'81d1f907-a4d2-54f2-bf9b-ff6256ff1726',N'a8fce4e1-a5a5-549c-8b74-8d06bbc1447d',0,3,19,N'Question number 6',N'<p>Đáp án là wetland. Trong hồ sơ xin phát triển, khu đất ngập nước là phần khó xử lý nhất do đây là nơi sinh sống của một loài chim quý hiếm.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,6,NULL,0,1563),
(N'c4eb11b4-7d6b-5a10-8236-206a90e0144c',N'a8fce4e1-a5a5-549c-8b74-8d06bbc1447d',0,3,19,N'Question number 7',N'<p>Đáp án là road. Một trong những khó khăn khác là việc xây dựng đường, vì có thể phải làm đường vòng tránh khu đất ngập nước, gây tốn kém và hạn chế tiếp cận.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,7,NULL,0,1563),
(N'61cf7fb4-99ec-5d8b-b08f-731550edd03b',N'a8fce4e1-a5a5-549c-8b74-8d06bbc1447d',0,3,19,N'Question number 8',N'<p>Đáp án là generations. Annie cho rằng việc kiểm soát chặt chẽ sử dụng đất sẽ mang lại lợi ích lâu dài, và các thế hệ tương lai sẽ biết ơn điều đó.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,8,NULL,0,1563),
(N'824ae33f-93ae-585d-bb88-61c1fb0df617',N'a8fce4e1-a5a5-549c-8b74-8d06bbc1447d',0,3,19,N'Question number 9',N'<p>Đáp án là 1956. James cho biết dịch vụ xe điện kết thúc vào năm 1956, khi xe buýt hoàn toàn thay thế chúng trong thị trấn.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,9,NULL,0,1563),
(N'2dd35b48-6e83-59cf-b6ed-d1200e4e8710',N'a8fce4e1-a5a5-549c-8b74-8d06bbc1447d',0,3,19,N'Question number 10',N'<p>Đáp án là psychology. James xác nhận rằng anh từng học chuyên ngành tâm lý học ở đại học, dù công việc hiện tại tại City Archives khá khác với chuyên ngành này.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,10,NULL,0,1563),
(N'9eb6a5c2-ea9a-5be3-b1e3-233bed0575dd',N'78744c34-1803-50a6-8c6a-9ca5a9a187b9',0,1,14,(CAST(N'<h2>[VOL 2] Test 2 - Section 2</h2><p>Great to have you here today, Hamish. I''ve been a fan of yours for ages. The very first rock concert I went to when I was 13, your band was playing.

Gosh. I''d like to thank this station too. Juliet, if I remember rightly, Ray Rogers'' interest in Soundhole''s second album put us on the map.

Good old Ray. Alas, who could forget when Soundhole broke up and Ray wept live on his show?

But to set the record straight, Soundhole isn''t getting back together despite rumors on social networks. My performing days are over, even solo. Especially solo. Frankly, solo gigs were a nightmare. I was so anxious every time I went out onto a stage. Live audiences seriously scare me.

Yet you''ve got such a rapport with them. You look so relaxed in those clips on YouTube.

Yeah, well, one thing the social networks did get right is the reason I quit performing. Oh, I was manic when I was on the road with the band — crazy. I''d stay up days on end. Back home, I was horribly depressed. I''d sleep for a week. My life was a mess. My first wife left me and my second wife left me. I''ve got three children I hardly know. My son sent me a card just before Soundhole split up in which he''d written he''d seen more of me on TV than in the flesh.

Before you listen to the rest of the talk, you have 30 seconds to read Questions 15 to 20.

So how long have you been making acoustic guitars, Hamish?

Full time for about 3 years. My sister and I work together. She sources the materials and does the books. I build the instruments.

I checked on the internet last night, and it''s a long process to make a guitar.

You bet. There''s at least 15 steps. I won''t go into them all now, but sourcing the wood, the first step, is crucial. Cheap guitars use softer wood, which equates with poorer sound quality. But harder wood is scarce these days. For instance, the back of a great guitar historically was made from Brazilian rosewood, but the supply is minuscule now. I use East Indian rosewood, which will also disappear soon. Likewise, spruce was once preferred for the top of a guitar, but I use cedar, which is more plentiful.

I thought guitars were mainly mahogany.

Cheap guitars, yes, but only the necks of good ones. The neck must resist distortion when pulled by the strings, and it mustn''t swell or contract with changes in temperature and humidity. Mahogany''s perfect for the neck.

I like that wavy pattern you get on the tops and backs of guitars. How''s that done?

That patt' AS nvarchar(max))+N'ern is called book matching. A thickish block of wood, about half the size of the body, is sliced horizontally. The two pieces are laid together with the grain continuous before they''re glued.

Right. The next two steps are to saw the top of the guitar into that sensual shape and cut out the sound hole. What''s inside the guitar to control its vibration and improve its tone?

Braces — narrow little bits of wood glued in an X pattern. The process is known as strutting. The back also has strutting to reflect sound waves.

Interesting. How''s the neck made?

It''s carved from a single piece of mahogany, and a metal rod is driven up into it for reinforcement.

How''d you get those lovely curved sides?

Strips are cut, sanded, and soaked in water. They''re molded until they''re set in that shape. When everything''s been glued together — the back, the sides, the top, and the neck — the guitar is put into clamps for several days. There are some other reinforcements too, like end blocks and bindings.

I guess precision is the key to much of this work.

Absolutely. In fact, guitar making has improved my mental health because everything''s nice and slow and precise. I''m alone in my workshop, dealing with wood. It has a calming effect.

It seems as though you sound whole again.

Please, no more silly puns on the name of our band. I spent 14 years explaining that hole was spelt with a W.</p>'),(CAST(N'<p>Great to have you here today, Hamish. I''ve been a fan of yours for ages. The very first rock concert I went to when I was 13, your band was playing.

