(N'4c179c4a-f8ec-5605-bdf1-fcf4fe761fee',N'd682ae9e-fa39-5e78-a28f-fd84678a2a14',0,2,18,N'<p><em><span>Write <span>ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER</span></span></em></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'Joining Social Club Form',11,0,1,NULL,0,1555),
(N'549d6da4-64aa-5e4c-a22c-e87865a6e6f0',N'4c179c4a-f8ec-5605-bdf1-fcf4fe761fee',0,3,19,N'<h3>Joining Social Club Form</h3><table border="1"><tbody><tr><td><p><span>Name:</span> Jenny F.</p> <p><span>Nationality:</span> }{SPACE}{ </p> <p><span>Address:</span> }{SPACE}{ Rd., Bondi</p> <p><span>Mobile phone:</span> }{SPACE}{ </p> <p><span>Occupation:</span> }{SPACE}{ </p> <p><span>Free-time interests:</span> Singing and }{SPACE}{ </p></td></tr></tbody></table>',N'<p>Đáp án: Malaysian. Đây là câu xác nhận trực tiếp quốc tịch của Jenny. Từ/cụm: Malaysian = người Malaysia; “are you?” dùng để xác nhận thông tin.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,1,NULL,0,1555),
(N'c3122703-623a-55ef-885b-f90c6652d504',N'4c179c4a-f8ec-5605-bdf1-fcf4fe761fee',0,3,19,N'Question number 2',N'<p>Đáp án: Anglesey. Form đã có sẵn “___ Rd, Bondi”, nên chỉ điền tên đường. Script cho đúng tên và còn đánh vần rõ. Lưu ý: nếu ô trống chỉ 1 từ =&gt; điền Anglesey (không cần “Road”). </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,2,NULL,0,1555),
(N'2cb288ff-faa5-5c1a-8b69-1185c49a9335',N'4c179c4a-f8ec-5605-bdf1-fcf4fe761fee',0,3,19,N'Question number 3',N'<p>Đáp án: 0404229160. Đây là số điện thoại Jenny đọc ra. Lưu ý: viết liền hay có gạch nối đều thường được chấp nhận nếu đúng số; nhưng an toàn nhất khi điền đáp án là 0404229160 (chỉ số). </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,3,NULL,0,1555),
(N'1b56b170-bcb7-57b2-bb57-77b8bef7453f',N'4c179c4a-f8ec-5605-bdf1-fcf4fe761fee',0,3,19,N'Question number 4',N'<p>Đáp án: economist. Câu trả lời trực tiếp cho mục “Occupation”. Từ mới: temporary job = công việc tạm thời; in fact = thực ra. </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,4,NULL,0,1555),
(N'0318a9ef-792c-50ce-8646-4e9c0d9046d6',N'4c179c4a-f8ec-5605-bdf1-fcf4fe761fee',0,3,19,N'Question number 5',N'<p>Đáp án: dancing. Form ghi “Singing and ___”, Jenny nêu thêm sở thích nổi bật nhất là dancing. Từ/cụm: like best = thích nhất =&gt; thường là đáp án cần điền. </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,5,NULL,0,1555),
(N'a7357470-2729-5188-a4fb-0e0a9f87c681',N'd682ae9e-fa39-5e78-a28f-fd84678a2a14',0,2,18,N'<p><em><span>Choose the correct letters, <span>A, B</span> or <span>C.</span></span></em></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',1,0,2,NULL,0,1555),
(N'd8085413-53bf-5d82-ac0d-4871b6cf73e2',N'a7357470-2729-5188-a4fb-0e0a9f87c681',0,3,19,N'<p>According to Don, what might be a problem for Jenny?</p>',N'<p>Đáp án: A (understanding local people). “Australian slang… difficult to understand” = khó hiểu cách người bản địa nói (tiếng lóng), tức vấn đề là hiểu người địa phương. Từ mới: slang = tiếng lóng. </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,6,NULL,0,1555),
(N'd7a0659a-8185-5cf3-80e9-99dc3d69c8da',N'a7357470-2729-5188-a4fb-0e0a9f87c681',0,3,19,N'<p>How many members does the club have now?</p>',N'<p>Đáp án: B (fifty). Con số “currently about fifty” là số thành viên hiện tại. Lưu ý bẫy: có các mốc khác “thirty”, “eighteen”, “eighty” nhưng không phải “now”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,7,NULL,0,1555),
(N'ff0505c3-0b09-5130-9b0e-c2e08d1b7938',N'a7357470-2729-5188-a4fb-0e0a9f87c681',0,3,19,N'<p>How often does the club meet?</p>',N'<p>Đáp án: B (once every two weeks). “Every second Thursday” = mỗi thứ Năm cách tuần =&gt; 2 tuần/lần. Từ/cụm: every second = cách một (không phải “thứ hai”).</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,8,NULL,0,1555),
(N'674d4d3e-e4f6-597e-afe2-a03a38908096',N'a7357470-2729-5188-a4fb-0e0a9f87c681',0,3,19,N'<p>What is the club’s most frequent type of activity?</p>',N'<p>Đáp án: C (a talk). “presentation” trong ngữ cảnh CLB = một bài nói/buổi nói chuyện. Các hoạt động khác (visit/meal) chỉ “from time to time” = thỉnh thoảng.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,9,NULL,0,1555),
(N'13ca6e16-6910-5ff0-bb28-b7a7a989b6d3',N'a7357470-2729-5188-a4fb-0e0a9f87c681',0,3,19,N'<p>The main purpose of the club is to help members to</p>',N'<p>Đáp án: C (meet Australians). “people from this country” = người Úc; mục tiêu chính là tạo cơ hội giao lưu/gặp gỡ người Úc. Từ/cụm: main point = mục đích chính; mix in = hòa nhập/giao lưu.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,10,NULL,0,1555),
(N'99125d90-8515-5ae0-9c19-8dbc8ba97a97',N'c6f1b814-4f27-53b1-ae33-5d64f7d745fd',0,1,14,(CAST(N'<h2>[VOL 2] Test 1 - Section 2</h2><p>Part 2. You will hear the leader of a college camping club talking to members about a cycling holiday that they are going to have together. First, you have some time to look at questions 11 to 16 on page 4. </p><p><span>Now listen carefully and answer questions 11 to 16. </span></p><p>Right. Now let me bring you up to date with arrangements for our cycling tour next month. First of all, there''s the question of tents. As you know, the original idea was that I''d arrange to borrow some tents that belong to the college but it turns out that the mountaineering club will be using them at the same time. So I''m afraid you''ll have to bring your own. So could you let me know whether you''ll be using a single tent or sharing, please? I''ll need to know how many tents there''ll be for when I make the reservation at the various campsites. Last time, some of you said you''d like to hire bikes and pick them up when we arrive rather than taking your own with you. Well, I''ve enquired about bike hire in Westbury, the town where we''ll be arriving, and unfortunately there aren''t any shops that hire them out, so I''m afraid it means taking your own. I''ll book them on the train when I book the train tickets, which reminds me I''ll need to know the final number of people going so I can get a group discount on the train fare. Something else that''ll need to be booked is tickets for the football match we discussed last time. I''ve enquired about availability and there are only a few seats left, so anyone who wants to go will need to get tickets very soon, ideally today or tomorrow. At our next meeting, I''ll be able to give you all individual packs with the final programme and something about the area we''ll be cycling through and places we''ll be visiting. I''m afraid I haven''t had time to do that yet. </p><p><span>Before you hear the rest of the talk, you have some time to look at questions 17 to 20 on page 5. </span></p><p><span>Now listen and answer questions 17 to 20. </span></p><p>Now I''ll tell you briefly about some of the attractions in the places we''ll be staying at. As I said, we''ll be taking the train to Westbury, which has one or two very good restaurants. One thing that''s definitely worth visiting there is the site where the original town was constructed nearly 1,000 years ago. There''s not much of the original buildings left, but there''s still plenty to see. The site is being excavated and you''ll be able to help out if you want to. Our next o' AS nvarchar(max))+N'vernight stop will be in the village of Clooney. There are several old barns here that have been converted into a museum, showing the importance of sheep in the area over the centuries. The wool used to be sold for cloth and it made the district quite rich. There are plenty of photographs showing how agricultural workers used to live too. From there, we''ll go on to Pennerley. Pennerley is famous for its Museum of Village Life, but that''s being refurbished at the moment and isn''t likely to reopen by the time we go there. But there''s an open-air farmer''s market every day selling fruits, vegetables, cheese and meat, all grown or processed within a few miles of the town and sold by the farmers themselves. It''s definitely worth a visit. In Farlow, which is one of the oldest towns in the area, there''s a museum that shows how horses used to be the most common way of travelling around and how they were gradually replaced by steam trains and later, of course, diesel and electric trains, buses, cars and bicycles. Right, now I''ll pass round this sheet of paper... </p><p><span>That is the end of Part 2. You now have 30 seconds to check your answers to Part 2.</span></p>'),(CAST(N'<p>Part 2. You will hear the leader of a college camping club talking to members about a cycling holiday that they are going to have together. First, you have 