(N'7a9a3eb9-9bea-5e50-90b1-d727161dea8c',N'0d5b0b35-61fe-5121-bae5-de17c2af76d9',0,3,19,N'<h3>Assignment Notes</h3><table border="1"><tbody><tr><td><p><span>Things to do:</span></p> <ul><li><p>check accuracy of the</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ in the last section</p> <ul><li><p>try to give more</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p> <p><span>Karen’s tasks:</span></p> <ul><li><p>she will give her presentation at</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p> <ul><li><p>she must provide explanation of</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ during the presentation</p> <ul><li><p>the abstract due date is on</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p> <ul><li><p>the presentation will be taken place in</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p> <ul><li><p>her presentation will be graded by</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p></td></tr></tbody></table>',N'<p>Đáp án: references. Tutor nói Karen có lỗi khi trích dẫn nhưng ghi thông tin tài liệu không đúng, nên cần kiểm tra độ chính xác của references. Paraphrase: “recorded the information properly at the end” = phần tài liệu tham khảo.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,21,NULL,0,1555),
(N'8a1ac27f-ff58-5e93-9d4b-65cad828c0b4',N'0d5b0b35-61fe-5121-bae5-de17c2af76d9',0,3,19,N'Question number 22',N'<p>Đáp án: examples. Tutor khuyên Karen thêm ví dụ để luận điểm thuyết phục hơn. Từ hay: hammer the point home = làm cho ý trở nên rất rõ, rất thuyết phục.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,22,NULL,0,1555),
(N'c35b9e36-9587-55eb-8920-53a27e706420',N'0d5b0b35-61fe-5121-bae5-de17c2af76d9',0,3,19,N'Question number 23',N'<p>Đáp án: the next seminar. Tutor nhắc lại thỏa thuận trước đó: Karen sẽ thuyết trình ở buổi seminar tiếp theo. Bẫy: Karen hỏi “next term?” =&gt; tutor đính chính lại</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,23,NULL,0,1555),
(N'6a7f4e08-fb6f-53bc-82df-83f11a912be0',N'0d5b0b35-61fe-5121-bae5-de17c2af76d9',0,3,19,N'Question number 24',N'<p>Đáp án: the experiment. Tutor nhấn mạnh đây là phần cốt lõi của bài thuyết trình. Từ khóa mạnh: absolutely essential = cực kỳ quan trọng.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,24,NULL,0,1555),
(N'91a4fffe-2ac6-5d7d-a8c9-dfdb73822eb2',N'0d5b0b35-61fe-5121-bae5-de17c2af76d9',0,3,19,N'Question number 25',N'<p>Đáp án: 26th November. Đây là hạn nộp abstract cho tutor, không phải hạn in handouts. Bẫy: 3rd December là hạn in, không phải hạn nộp abstract.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,25,NULL,0,1555),
(N'bdc3d2d8-89a9-5f21-b68a-299138b209f2',N'0d5b0b35-61fe-5121-bae5-de17c2af76d9',0,3,19,N'Question number 26',N'<p>Đáp án: the chemistry lab. Địa điểm thay đổi do phòng trong khoa không phù hợp. Paraphrase: “go across the road” = sang tòa khác.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,26,NULL,0,1555),
(N'7dddfbc1-307d-5341-b613-89de070b4320',N'0d5b0b35-61fe-5121-bae5-de17c2af76d9',0,3,19,N'Question number 27',N'<p>Đáp án: the professor. Tutor phân biệt rõ: bài đầu do tutor chấm, bài này do professor chấm.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,27,NULL,0,1555),
(N'be90b015-9991-58cc-9387-fdc428d527dc',N'43d9a880-0bf9-542e-bef5-c2892fa858bd',0,2,18,N'<p><em>Choose <span>THREE</span> letters, <span>A–F.</span></em></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',5,0,2,NULL,0,1555),
(N'b112cf28-5cb0-5cd8-b4cf-86393c741b79',N'be90b015-9991-58cc-9387-fdc428d527dc',0,3,19,N'<p>Which <span>THREE</span> modules will Karen study next year?</p>',N'<p>Karen chủ động chọn môn này vì thấy thú vị. Không có câu phủ định hay thay đổi quyết định sau đó =&gt; đáp án chắc chắn.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,28,NULL,0,1555),
(N'0c71a2b2-f175-5dfc-b86d-a8a490b51bc9',N'be90b015-9991-58cc-9387-fdc428d527dc',0,3,19,N'<p>Which <span>THREE</span> modules will Karen study next year?</p>',N'<p>went for = đã quyết định chọn sau khi cân nhắc. Đây là tín hiệu đáp án rất mạnh trong IELTS Listening. Chọn C</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,29,NULL,0,1555),
(N'a196cbd7-460c-5b16-ace2-51057da9cc2c',N'be90b015-9991-58cc-9387-fdc428d527dc',0,3,19,N'<p>Which <span>THREE</span> modules will Karen study next year?</p>',N'<p>Karen so sánh và chọn discourse analysis thay vì methodology =&gt; rõ ràng là môn sẽ học.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,30,NULL,0,1555),
(N'16438cd9-d209-583f-a328-6442621ab4a1',N'c6f1b814-4f27-53b1-ae33-5d64f7d745fd',0,1,15,(CAST(N'<h2>[VOL 2] Extinction of Australian species</h2><p>Good afternoon. From my work as curator at the Brisbane Zoo, it is becoming increasingly obvious to me that the animal world is a highly endangered one. It sometimes seems as though a new species is added to the endangered list every day, and a great deal of this is due to human activity.

You may have read about the orange-bellied parrot colonies in South Australia. These are under threat from wind farms, so even our attempts to save energy can have a negative impact.

A further example is provided by the expansion of our cities here in Australia. Many species of frog are losing their habitat as a direct result of this urban development. What''s more, thanks to the increasing use of pesticides, few insects are surviving. Many species depend upon these as a food source — birds in particular — and so their numbers are declining as well. So even in rural areas, we are having a damaging effect on species.

In fact, when our farmers choose to grow large amounts of one staple crop each year — corn is a perfect example — this often results in the greater need for chemicals and fertilizers, which has a devastating effect on local wildlife.

Clearly, something needs to be done about this. However, very little can be achieved without full public support, and our general attitude is not always a positive one.

Of course, it is easy to get people interested in animals such as the panda, thanks to the attention it is given in the media. People are very aware of its plight and so are willing to give a great deal of support. However, it is not so easy to attract sympathy for those essential smaller species such as insects. They may seem insignificant, but these tiny creatures have an enormous effect on our ecosystem.

And it isn''t only size that is a problem when it comes to our attitude towards animals. There are certain animals that we would prefer to simply ignore for various reasons.

Firstly, we might do this because of fear. That is the normal reaction when people see a shark or a snake, for example.

Another reason might be that we believe that certain animals are rivals when it comes to food. Locusts and even mice could come into this category.

Then there are animals that we view with disgust because of how they look or feel — the many different parasites, for example.

You may well ask, what does it matter if any of these species dies? Extinction is a fact of life, after all.

I would argue that there are seve' AS nvarchar(max))+N'ral reasons to be concerned about the extinction of any species. Each species helps us to understand more about how our ecosystem works. One species can be linked to many others in the food chain, for example, and inevitably they all lead back to us in some way.

We now know that the more complex the ecosystem is, the more stable it is. When this is the case, large numbers of one animal are quickly controlled by outbreaks of its predators.

We''ve also began to realise that the presence or absence of certain plants can alert us to changes in our environment. One type of plant might indicate the presence of rich mineral deposits; another might alert us to toxic water.

And so even seemingly insignificant species can be helpful and beneficial to us. This is especially true in the area of medicine. There are many well-documented cases of the health benefits of pet ownership, especially with the ill or the handicapped. But not many people know that spiders are also being used in medicine. The cobwebs they make can be used to assist with certain blood disorders — it actually helps blood to clot.

Imagine how much more there is for us still to discover from plants and animals. But we can only do this if we can save these creatures from extinction.

Perhaps, in the end, it is our self-interest that will save the animals.</p>'),(CAST(N'<p>Good afternoon. From my work as curator at the Brisbane Zoo, it is becoming increasingly obvious to me that the animal world is a highly endangered one. It sometimes seems as though a new species is added to the endangered list every day, and a great deal of this is due to human activity.

You may have read about the orange-bellied parrot colonies in South Australia. These are under threat from wind farms, so even our attempts to save energy can have a negative impact.

A further example is provided by the expansion of our cities here in Australia. Many species of frog are losing their habitat as a direct result of this urban development. What''s more, thanks to the increasing use of pesticides, few insects are surviving. Many species depend upon these as a food source — birds in particular — and so their numbers are declining as well. So even in rural areas, we are having a damaging effect on species.

In fact, when our farmers choose to grow large amounts of one staple crop each year — corn is a perfect example — this often results in the greater need for chemicals and fertilizers, which has a devastating effect on local wildlife.

Clearly, something needs to be done about this. However, very little can be achieved without full public support, and our general attitude is not always a positive one.

Of course, it is easy to get people interested in animals such as the panda, thanks to the attention it is given in the media. People are very aware of its plight and so are willing to give a great deal of support. However, it is not so easy to attract sympathy for those essential smaller species such as insects. They may seem insignificant, but these tiny creatures have an enormous effect on our ecosystem.

And it isn''t only size that is a problem when it comes to our attitude towards animals. There are certain animals that we would prefer to simply ignore for various reasons.

Firstly, we might do this because of fear. That is the normal reaction when people see a shark or a snake, for example.

Another reason might be that we believe that certain animals are rivals when it comes to food. Locusts and even mice could come into this category.

Then there are animals that we view with disgust because of how they look or feel — the many different parasites, for example.

You may well ask, what does it matter if any of these species dies? Extinction is a fact of life, after all.

I would argue that there are several reasons to be concerned about the extinction ' AS nvarchar(max))+N'of any species. Each species helps us to understand more about how our ecosystem works. One species can be linked to many others in the food chain, for example, and inevitably they all lead back to us in some way.

We now know that the more complex the ecosystem is, the more stable it is. When this is the case, large numbers of one animal are quickly controlled by outbreaks of its predators.

We''ve also began to realise that the presence or absence of certain plants can alert us to changes in our environment. One type of plant might indicate the presence of rich mineral deposits; another might alert us to toxic water.

And so even seemingly insignificant species can be helpful and beneficial to us. This is especially true in the area of medicine. There are many well-documented cases of the health benefits of pet ownership, especially with the ill or the handicapped. But not many people know that spiders are also being used in medicine. The cobwebs they make can be used to assist with certain blood disorders — it actually helps blood to clot.

Imagine how much more there is for us still to discover from plants and animals. But we can only do this if we can save these creatures from extinction.

Perhaps, in the end, it is our self-interest that will save the animals.</p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-2/iL.VOL2.1.S1555.PART4.mp3',NULL,1,0,4,NULL,0,1555),
(N'ae3de30b-00b4-5561-bc44-767baab5913e',N'16438cd9-d209-583f-a328-6442621ab4a1',0,2,18,N'<p><em>Write <span>ONE WORD ONLY</span> in each gap.</em></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'Extinction of Australian species',11,0,1,NULL,0,1555),
(N'a39713e3-4486-570b-b99a-b605482fe51a',N'ae3de30b-00b4-5561-bc44-767baab5913e',0,3,19,N'<h3>Extinction of Australian species</h3><table border="1"><tbody><tr><td><p><span>Recent problems:</span></p> <ul><li><p>several species of</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ are at risk because of increased housing</p> <ul><li><p>many animals, especially</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ are affected by pesticides</p> <ul><li><p>production of single crops like</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ is harming wildlife</p> <p><span>Endangered animals:</span></p> <ul><li><p>can be influenced by the</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ (e.g. the panda)</p> <ul><li><p>people are less concerned about smaller animals, e.g.</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p> <ul><li><p>some animals are ignored because they are viewed: with</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ as our</p>  }{SPACE}{ in terms of food, with disgust</p> <p><span>Reasons for preventing extinction:</span></p> <ul><li><p>the ecosystem needs to be</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ to be stable</p> <ul><li><p>some types of</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ can help to signal environmental issues</p> <ul><li><p>cobwebs help with medical disorders related to</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p></td></tr></tbody></table>',N'<p>Đáp án là frogs. Người nói đang nói về việc mở rộng đô thị làm mất môi trường sống, và ví dụ cụ thể được nêu ra là nhiều loài ếch. Dạng số nhiều là hợp lý vì nói đến several species.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,31,NULL,0,1555),
(N'cb33f5f4-0f43-55ad-9284-9b5d1d160813',N'ae3de30b-00b4-5561-bc44-767baab5913e',0,3,19,N'Question number 32',N'<p>Đáp án là insects. Thuốc trừ sâu ảnh hưởng trực tiếp đến côn trùng, khiến số lượng của chúng giảm mạnh. Câu sau còn nhấn mạnh nhiều loài khác phụ thuộc vào chúng làm nguồn thức ăn. </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,32,NULL,0,1555),
(N'9fc9250d-ffa4-54eb-9fba-6980a0c2d3f0',N'ae3de30b-00b4-5561-bc44-767baab5913e',0,3,19,N'Question number 33',N'<p>Đáp án là corn. Người nói đưa ra ví dụ rất rõ về độc canh, cụ thể là trồng ngô, gây tăng sử dụng hóa chất và làm hại động vật hoang dã.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,33,NULL,0,1555),
(N'8a90affa-1e1d-54cd-8aea-cdb70f5b1aa5',N'ae3de30b-00b4-5561-bc44-767baab5913e',0,3,19,N'Question number 34',N'<p>Đáp án là media. Gấu trúc được dùng làm ví dụ cho những loài nhận được nhiều truyền thông chú ý, nên dễ kêu gọi sự ủng hộ của công chúng.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,34,NULL,0,1555),
(N'714d7e0c-ac84-50b8-a54a-40135174e759',N'ae3de30b-00b4-5561-bc44-767baab5913e',0,3,19,N'Question number 35',N'<p>Đáp án là insects. Người nói nhấn mạnh rằng các loài nhỏ như côn trùng thường không được quan tâm, dù vai trò sinh thái rất lớn.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,35,NULL,0,1555),
(N'4bf8f564-2339-5642-8f10-0be193c43b47',N'ae3de30b-00b4-5561-bc44-767baab5913e',0,3,19,N'Question number 36',N'<p>Đáp án là rivals. Một số loài bị con người phớt lờ vì bị xem là đối thủ cạnh tranh thức ăn, ví dụ như châu chấu hay chuột.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,36,NULL,0,1555),
(N'b20f4c11-e0ce-509d-9e13-e54b2dabae4c',N'ae3de30b-00b4-5561-bc44-767baab5913e',0,3,19,N'Question number 37',N'<p>Đáp án là looked được suy ra từ look trong script. Cụm trong đề là “viewed … with disgust” và lý do là hình dáng, nên từ phù hợp là looked.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,37,NULL,0,1555),
(N'437ab502-b1fd-573e-9507-36024b416032',N'ae3de30b-00b4-5561-bc44-767baab5913e',0,3,19,N'Question number 38',N'<p>Đáp án là complex. Người nói giải thích rằng hệ sinh thái càng phức tạp thì càng ổn định, vì các loài tự kiểm soát lẫn nhau.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,38,NULL,0,1555),
(N'b3192b8a-b560-5d02-92f8-e841f980ad24',N'ae3de30b-00b4-5561-bc44-767baab5913e',0,3,19,N'Question number 39',N'<p>Đáp án là plants. Một số loài thực vật đóng vai trò như chỉ báo môi trường, giúp phát hiện vấn đề về khoáng sản hay nước độc.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,39,NULL,0,1555),
(N'c6ffeab3-5ff5-58d2-9841-38bcbf528bd2',N'ae3de30b-00b4-5561-bc44-767baab5913e',0,3,19,N'Question number 40',N'<p>Đáp án là blood. Tơ nhện được dùng trong y học để hỗ trợ các rối loạn về máu, đặc biệt là quá trình đông máu.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,40,NULL,0,1555),
(N'40d1d7aa-0a2b-5be7-9565-6b75316ea8e0',NULL,0,0,11,NULL,NULL,NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-4/iL.VOL4.8.S1542.mp3',N'Vol 4 LISTENING FULL TEST 8',0,7,1,NULL,1,1542),
(N'38c0b64b-993b-53b9-8e6b-c20899ae49af',N'40d1d7aa-0a2b-5be7-9565-6b75316ea8e0',0,1,13,(CAST(N'<h2>[VOL 4] Person''s Estate Agency</h2><p>Pearsons Estate Agents, Can I help you? Yes. Good morning, I''d like to register with your agency. Oh yes, OK. Did you want to rent a property or buy one? Buy, OK. Right, I''ll just get a registration form. Right. So, in which area are you hoping to find a property? In the Huddersfield area. Fine. I''ll just take some personal details, if I may. You are Mary King, fine. And can I have your present address, please? It''s 59 Franklyn Avenue. Is that spelt L I N at the end? No, it''s F R A N K L Y N. Oh right, OK. And the town? Barnsley, right. And do you happen to know your postcode? It''s TY12 6OS. Is that T for Tango? Yes, it is. Fine. Now, obviously, I''ll put you on our mailing list for property details, but sometimes we might want to contact you quickly, so can you give me a phone number? Yes, my number''s 0194 88 536. And is that daytime or evening or both? No, it''s an office number, so from 8 in the morning to 3:30. Do you need an evening number? No, not really. Thanks. OK, well now I''ll take some details about the kind of property you''re looking for. Was it a house or a flat? House. OK. Any particular kind? Yes, I don''t really like modern houses very much; I''d like something traditional really. Yes. OK. And how big? Three bedrooms, four bedrooms? Yes, that sort of size. I wouldn''t want anything with less than three. </p><p>I got that. Anything else as far as the property itself is concerned? I''d really like to find somewhere with central heating. I know a lot of those cottages still just have fireplaces, but I don''t really want that, and those electric heaters are very expensive too. You''re right, they are. OK, I''ll make a note of that. Anything else? What about outside? Do you need a garden, for example? Well, that''d be nice, but it''s not essential. But one thing I really must have is a garage. I know that a lot of older places don''t have one of those either, but… Well, that''s true, but we''ll do our best. I''ve made a note.  Right. And what about the location? If possible, I''d like something in a village, but not too far away from the town. Right. Now what about the price? What''s your budget? I could go up to £120,000, not more, but if I can get something suitable for less, I''d rather of course. And will you be applying for a loan from the bank to help cover the cost? I''ve already done that and the bank''s approved it. Oh good! Could you just give me a few details? What''s the name of your bank? York. Right. And which ' AS nvarchar(max))+N'branch is that? It''s in Park Square. I used to live in that area, and then when I moved, I kept my account there. That''s excellent! You''ll be able to go straight ahead then. That''s a real advantage when you''re bidding for a property. Now we''ve got a few things in the books already that you might be interested in. Shall I put the details in the post? Well, actually, I can collect them myself. My office is quite near yours. That would probably be easier.</p>'),(CAST(N'<p>Pearsons Estate Agents, Can I help you? Yes. Good morning, I''d like to register with your agency. Oh yes, OK. Did you want to rent a property or buy one? Buy, OK. Right, I''ll just get a registration form. Right. So, in which area are you hoping to find a property? In the Huddersfield area. Fine. I''ll just take some personal details, if I may. You are Mary King, fine. And can I have your present address, please? It''s 59 Franklyn Avenue. Is that spelt L I N at the end? No, it''s F R A N K L Y N. Oh right, OK. And the town? Barnsley, right. And do you happen to know your postcode? It''s TY12 6OS. Is that T for Tango? Yes, it is. Fine. Now, obviously, I''ll put you on our mailing list for property details, but sometimes we might want to contact you quickly, so can you give me a phone number? Yes, my number''s 0194 88 536. And is that daytime or evening or both? No, it''s an office number, so from 8 in the morning to 3:30. Do you need an evening number? No, not really. Thanks. OK, well now I''ll take some details about the kind of property you''re looking for. Was it a house or a flat? House. OK. Any particular kind? Yes, I don''t really like modern houses very much; I''d like something traditional really. Yes. OK. And how big? Three bedrooms, four bedrooms? Yes, that sort of size. I wouldn''t want anything with less than three. </p><p>I got that. Anything else as far as the property itself is concerned? I''d really like to find somewhere with central heating. I know a lot of those cottages still just have fireplaces, but I don''t really want that, and those electric heaters are very expensive too. You''re right, they are. OK, I''ll make a note of that. Anything else? What about outside? Do you need a garden, for example? Well, that''d be nice, but it''s not essential. But one thing I really must have is a garage. I know that a lot of older places don''t have one of those either, but… Well, that''s true, but we''ll do our best. I''ve made a note.  Right. And what about the location? If possible, I''d like something in a village, but not too far away from the town. Right. Now what about the price? What''s your budget? I could go up to £120,000, not more, but if I can get something suitable for less, I''d rather of course. And will you be applying for a loan from the bank to help cover the cost? I''ve already done that and the bank''s approved it. Oh good! Could you just give me a few details? What''s the name of your bank? York. Right. And which branch is that? It''s in Park Square. I ' AS nvarchar(max))+N'used to live in that area, and then when I moved, I kept my account there. That''s excellent! You''ll be able to go straight ahead then. That''s a real advantage when you''re bidding for a property. Now we''ve got a few things in the books already that you might be interested in. Shall I put the details in the post? Well, actually, I can collect them myself. My office is quite near yours. That would probably be easier.</p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-4/iL.VOL4.8.S1542.PART1.mp3',NULL,1,0,1,NULL,0,1542),
(N'e13d0e39-f035-5e9a-ba41-cc1e06c74cbd',N'38c0b64b-993b-53b9-8e6b-c20899ae49af',0,2,18,N'<p>Write <span>NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER</span> for each answer.</p>',N'',N'',N'',N'Pearson''s Estate Agency',11,0,1,NULL,0,1542),
(N'f6dd5e9f-6550-5437-8f9d-3e684037e0cd',N'e13d0e39-f035-5e9a-ba41-cc1e06c74cbd',0,3,19,N'<h3>Pearson''s Estate Agency</h3><table border="1"><tbody><tr><td><p>Registration Form for House Purchase</p></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p><span>Area where property required: Huddersfield</span></p></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p><span>Personal details:</span></p></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p>Name:</p></td><td><p>Mary King</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Address:</p></td><td> }{SPACE}{ Avenue Barnsley</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Postcode:</p></td><td> }{SPACE}{ </td></tr><tr><td><p>Phone no.:</p></td><td> }{SPACE}{ (between 8.00 am and 3.30 pm)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><span>Details of property wanted:</span></p></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p>Type:</p></td><td><p>house( }{SPACE}{ style)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Size:</p></td><td><p>minimum 3 bedrooms</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><span>Other requirement(s):</span></p></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p>Inside:</p></td><td><p>must have }{SPACE}{ </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Outside:</p></td><td><p>must have a }{SPACE}{ </p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Location:</p></td><td><p>in a }{SPACE}{ </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><span>Purchase details:</span></p></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p>Maximum price:</p></td><td> }{SPACE}{ </td></tr><tr><td><p>Finances:</p></td><td><p>Bank loan already approved</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Bank:</p></td><td><p>York Bank</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Branch location:</p></td><td> }{SPACE}{ </td></tr><tr><td><p><span>Other information:</span></p></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p>Customer</p></td><td><p>will }{SPACE}{ the house details</p></td></tr></tbody></table>',N'<p>Câu hỏi: “Address: … Avenue Barnsley.” → Bà King nói rõ địa chỉ 59 Franklyn Avenue, điền 59 Franklyn.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,1,NULL,0,1542),
(N'b3171982-d032-548b-9c9a-f107ddea235f',N'e13d0e39-f035-5e9a-ba41-cc1e06c74cbd',0,3,19,N'Question number 2',N'<p>Câu hỏi: “Postcode: …” → Bà King cho mã bưu điện rõ ràng ⇒ điền TY12 6OS.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,2,NULL,0,1542),
(N'942220a9-bdaf-5775-b1ea-3771d6ddf604',N'e13d0e39-f035-5e9a-ba41-cc1e06c74cbd',0,3,19,N'Question number 3',N'<p>Câu hỏi: “Phone no. … (between 8.00 am and 3.30 pm).” → Bà King cho số điện thoại văn phòng dùng trong khoảng giờ này ⇒ điền 0194 88 536.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,3,NULL,0,1542),
(N'46529771-e6eb-50b3-b70e-08e173a4c3a8',N'e13d0e39-f035-5e9a-ba41-cc1e06c74cbd',0,3,19,N'Question number 4',N'<p>Câu hỏi: “Type: house (… style).” → Bà King muốn kiểu truyền thống ⇒ điền traditional.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,4,NULL,0,1542),
(N'0d6857f7-55ef-5935-b0fe-025d2f214afe',N'e13d0e39-f035-5e9a-ba41-cc1e06c74cbd',0,3,19,N'Question number 5',N'<p>Câu hỏi: “Inside: must have …” → Yêu cầu cụ thể là phải có central heating.

</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,5,NULL,0,1542),
(N'5accb5f3-629a-573d-a085-bc25183b97da',N'e13d0e39-f035-5e9a-ba41-cc1e06c74cbd',0,3,19,N'Question number 6',N'<p>Câu hỏi: “Outside: must have a …” → Rõ ràng là cần garage.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,6,NULL,0,1542),
(N'9d0defea-63ae-5e33-a17c-44adf4e70bf4',N'e13d0e39-f035-5e9a-ba41-cc1e06c74cbd',0,3,19,N'Question number 7',N'<p>Câu hỏi: “Location: in a …” → Bà King muốn ở village- làng</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,7,NULL,0,1542),
(N'4b2a982a-9fbf-5457-8cf1-736b7d161a85',N'e13d0e39-f035-5e9a-ba41-cc1e06c74cbd',0,3,19,N'Question number 8',N'<p>Câu hỏi: “Maximum price: …” → Ngân sách tối đa là £120,000.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,8,NULL,0,1542),
(N'0ddc2095-5f05-50d1-a589-a1873bd99d37',N'e13d0e39-f035-5e9a-ba41-cc1e06c74cbd',0,3,19,N'Question number 9',N'<p>Câu hỏi: “Branch location: …” → Chi nhánh ngân hàng ở Park Square.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,9,NULL,0,1542),
(N'1d325e38-7ee5-5e25-91f4-6f7cef8a3ac1',N'e13d0e39-f035-5e9a-ba41-cc1e06c74cbd',0,3,19,N'Question number 10',N'<p>Câu hỏi: “Customer will … the house details.” → Bà King muốn tự collect- thu thập.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,10,NULL,0,1542),
(N'ee8aa55d-5b6e-58f9-a4e6-ca66439bebe4',N'40d1d7aa-0a2b-5be7-9565-6b75316ea8e0',0,1,14,(CAST(N'<h2>Pennyfield Horse Riding Centre</h2><p>Good morning everyone and welcome to Pennyfield Horse Riding Center. My name''s Maxine and I''m really pleased that you''re interested in having horse riding lessons with us. I''d like to tell you a little about our operation, what we have to offer, and where everything''s located, so later you can find your way around. Now we''ve been in business since 1979, and since then we''ve trained hundreds of children and adults to be confident horse riders. We''re not the biggest riding center in the area, but we do offer a very wide range of services to suit most people''s needs. Because we have a large indoor arena, the center is open in any weather. Our busiest time is the weekend, but we also run sessions every weekday afternoon. We offer lessons for all abilities, from absolute beginners to advanced riders, though prices vary, and jumping lessons, for example, cost a little more than beginners'' classes. We don''t offer one-to-one lessons, but we have so many groups running every day that we''re sure to find a level that''s right for you.  Now, if you do decide to take lessons here, you have to register first. To do this, you''ll need to fill out a form which has questions about your contact details, your general health, and any previous riding experience you have. There''s no need to show certificates or anything like that because we like to assess your ability ourselves. We''ll just assign you provisionally to one of our groups until we get the chance to do that. For registration purposes, you also need to make a one-off payment to use our riding gear. This is refundable. We don''t actually charge you; it''s only to cover us in case anything gets lost or damaged. You can book lessons over the phone or in person. Though we can''t make promises, we''ll offer you a choice of horses to ride, and if you have a particular animal you like, we''ll do our best to accommodate you. Regarding payment, we can''t take credit cards, but we do accept checks with a bank card. If you have to cancel your booking, please do it at least a couple of days ahead, otherwise a 50% cancellation fee will apply. Also, you may want to consider booking lessons in blocks of 10 since it''s cheaper.  Now, many of you are first-time riders, and we know that you may be feeling a little nervous. Don''t worry! All our teachers are specially trained to help you build your confidence. We suggest that you observe one lesson to see what''s going on. There are plenty of other riders' AS nvarchar(max))+N' who feel the same as you. You''ll soon start to relax. We''re very happy for people to look on while you''re having your lessons, but we do ask that you keep talking to a minimum. </p><p>Spectators can take photos, of course, as long as there''s no flash, and please we ask riders not to carry cell phones, even in your pocket. We''ve had quite a few going off, and it frightens the horses. Now you probably want to know what to wear. Most important is what you wear on your feet and legs, and we have a wide selection of boots for sale in our shop. It''s well worth a visit. Younger riders, especially, love our range of stationery with the Pennyfield logo on it. Sadly, we no longer sell clothing like sweatshirts or coats, but don''t worry, just wear any warm, waterproof jacket. And then, I do just want to tell you about a new group we''re starting on Thursday evenings called the Equis Club. This is for riders who are visually impaired or who have another type of handicap. We offer high levels of care and aim to take riders through all the levels, right up to competition standards where appropriate. Now, before I finish, the Riding Centre is pretty large, so I''ll just explain where all the key areas are. Looking at this plan, you can see that we''re standing here in the stable block. Just in front of us, over the way, you can see the shop. Between that and the storeroom is the cafe. Then, as we look to the left of the storeroom, next to the parking lot, there''s the office where you make your bookings. Obviously, that''s where you''ll go to make arrangements for particular classes, to fill in forms, etc. Nobody can go on a ride without going in there first. And looking at the other side of the shop, to the right of it, is the place where you wait to ride. It runs alongside the whole length of the arena. Finally, you''ll need to know where the bathrooms are. As you go out of this stable block, they''re on the left, next to the indoor arena. I hope that''s clear.</p>'),(CAST(N'<p>Good morning everyone and welcome to Pennyfield Horse Riding Center. My name''s Maxine and I''m really pleased that you''re interested in having horse riding lessons with us. I''d like to tell you a little about our operation, what we have to offer, and where everything''s located, so later you can find your way around. Now we''ve been in business since 1979, and since then we''ve trained hundreds of children and adults to be confident horse riders. We''re not the biggest riding center in the area, but we do offer a very wide range of services to suit most people''s needs. Because we have a large indoor arena, the center is open in any weather. Our busiest time is the weekend, but we also run sessions every weekday afternoon. We offer lessons for all abilities, from absolute beginners to advanced riders, though prices vary, and jumping lessons, for example, cost a little more than beginners'' classes. We don''t offer one-to-one lessons, but we have so many groups running every day that we''re sure to find a level that''s right for you.  Now, if you do decide to take lessons here, you have to register first. To do this, you''ll need to fill out a form which has questions about your contact details, your general health, and any previous riding experience you have. There''s no need to show certificates or anything like that because we like to assess your ability ourselves. We''ll just assign you provisionally to one of our groups until we get the chance to do that. For registration purposes, you also need to make a one-off payment to use our riding gear. This is refundable. We don''t actually charge you; it''s only to cover us in case anything gets lost or damaged. You can book lessons over the phone or in person. Though we can''t make promises, we''ll offer you a choice of horses to ride, and if you have a particular animal you like, we''ll do our best to accommodate you. Regarding payment, we can''t take credit cards, but we do accept checks with a bank card. If you have to cancel your booking, please do it at least a couple of days ahead, otherwise a 50% cancellation fee will apply. Also, you may want to consider booking lessons in blocks of 10 since it''s cheaper.  Now, many of you are first-time riders, and we know that you may be feeling a little nervous. Don''t worry! All our teachers are specially trained to help you build your confidence. We suggest that you observe one lesson to see what''s going on. There are plenty of other riders who feel the same as you. You''ll soon ' AS nvarchar(max))+N'start to relax. We''re very happy for people to look on while you''re having your lessons, but we do ask that you keep talking to a minimum. </p><p>Spectators can take photos, of course, as long as there''s no flash, and please we ask riders not to carry cell phones, even in your pocket. We''ve had quite a few going off, and it frightens the horses. Now you probably want to know what to wear. Most important is what you wear on your feet and legs, and we have a wide selection of boots for sale in our shop. It''s well worth a visit. Younger riders, especially, love our range of stationery with the Pennyfield logo on it. Sadly, we no longer sell clothing like sweatshirts or coats, but don''t worry, just wear any warm, waterproof jacket. And then, I do just want to tell you about a new group we''re starting on Thursday evenings called the Equis Club. This is for riders who are visually impaired or who have another type of handicap. We offer high levels of care and aim to take riders through all the levels, right up to competition standards where appropriate. Now, before I finish, the Riding Centre is pretty large, so I''ll just explain where all the key areas are. Looking at this plan, you can see that we''re standing here in the stable block. Just in front of us, over the way, you can see the shop. Between that and the storeroom is the cafe. Then, as we look to the left of the storeroom, next to the parking lot, there''s the office where you make your bookings. Obviously, that''s where you''ll go to make arrangements for particular classes, to fill in forms, etc. Nobody can go on a ride without going in there first. And looking at the other side of the shop, to the right of it, is the place where you wait to ride. It runs alongside the whole length of the arena. Finally, you''ll need to know where the bathrooms are. As you go out of this stable block, they''re on the left, next to the indoor arena. I hope that''s clear.</p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-4/iL.VOL4.8.S1542.PART2.mp3',NULL,1,0,2,NULL,0,1542),
(N'6f9e3922-101c-5906-9f96-7c70588831d6',N'ee8aa55d-5b6e-58f9-a4e6-ca66439bebe4',0,2,18,N'<p>Choose the correct letter,<span> A, B or C.</span></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',1,0,1,NULL,0,1542),
(N'054c5628-083a-5969-8e30-6bbdecbc39d9',N'6f9e3922-101c-5906-9f96-7c70588831d6',0,3,19,N'<p>What does Maxine say about the Pennyfield Horse Riding Centre?</p>',N'<p>Câu hỏi: “What does Maxine say…?” → Đúng: không có individual (one to one) lessons.
 A sai: “open in any weather” → không phải “classes do not run when weather is bad”.
 B sai: “We’re not the biggest riding center in the area.”</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,11,NULL,0,1542),
(N'3e19f0a2-4dab-5b28-a031-2cef9d5a5186',N'6f9e3922-101c-5906-9f96-7c70588831d6',0,3,19,N'<p>What must riders provide when they register at the Riding Centre?</p>',N'<p>Câu hỏi: “What must riders provide…?” → Đúng: deposit for equipment.
 A sai: “no need to show certificates.”
C sai: không nhắc đến
</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,12,NULL,0,1542),
(N'2268beab-7a72-5adf-ab68-cdebb4e2acf8',N'6f9e3922-101c-5906-9f96-7c70588831d6',0,3,19,N'<p>What does Maxine say about booking arrangements?</p>',N'<p>Câu hỏi: “Maxine say about booking…?” → Đúng: có thể hủy 2 days in advance without charge.
 A sai: có nhắc “blocks of 10” nhưng chỉ là gợi ý để rẻ hơn, không bắt buộc.
 B sai: “we can’t take credit cards.”</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,13,NULL,0,1542),
(N'33e5eb7e-cca2-5617-8066-3730fae31b07',N'6f9e3922-101c-5906-9f96-7c70588831d6',0,3,19,N'<p>Maxine advises nervous riders to</p>',N'<p>Câu hỏi: “Maxine advises nervous riders to …” → Đúng: watch a lesson.
  B sai: có nhắc “other riders” nhưng không khuyên nói chuyện.
  C sai: không bảo “discuss with teacher”, chỉ nói teachers được đào tạo giúp đỡ.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,14,NULL,0,1542),
(N'88d369f9-6192-59c2-b986-cf6a9b1bfd5a',N'6f9e3922-101c-5906-9f96-7c70588831d6',0,3,19,N'<p>While riders are having their lesson, they are not allowed to</p>',N'<p>Câu hỏi: “While riders are having their lesson…” → Đúng: không được carry a phone.
  B sai: “Spectators can take photos.” Chỉ khán giả chứ không phải riders.
  C sai: “keep talking to a minimum”, nhưng áp dụng cho spectators, không phải riders.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,15,NULL,0,1542),
(N'0aa9963d-a224-52b9-b53c-8d9559c2d502',N'6f9e3922-101c-5906-9f96-7c70588831d6',0,3,19,N'<p>What can you buy in the Riding Centre shop?</p>',N'<p>Câu hỏi: “What can you buy…?” → Đúng: footwear.
  A sai: “we no longer sell clothing like sweatshirts, coats.”
  C sai: không hề nhắc tới trousers.
</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,16,NULL,0,1542),
(N'4b5d2694-724a-580b-a895-44e778fddcbb',N'6f9e3922-101c-5906-9f96-7c70588831d6',0,3,19,N'<p>The Equus Club is specially for riders</p>',N'<p>Câu hỏi: “The Equus Club is specially for …” → Đúng: riders with a physical disability.
  B sai: có nói “competition standards” nhưng không phải mục đích chính.
  C sai: không nhắc tới chăm sóc ngựa.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,17,NULL,0,1542),
(N'38963f64-338e-5d0d-9411-bf7e2a4de645',N'ee8aa55d-5b6e-58f9-a4e6-ca66439bebe4',0,2,18,N'<p>Label the plan below. </p><p>Write the correct letter, <span>A-G</span>, next to questions <span>18-20.</span></p><p><img src="https://ieltsroom.com/upload/images/ieltsadvancedtest/5e3509d33441861d270c.png" alt="Question diagram"></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'Plan of the Pennyfield Riding Centre',12,0,2,NULL,0,1542),
(N'600b3698-6875-5195-a133-381cda468585',N'38963f64-338e-5d0d-9411-bf7e2a4de645',0,3,19,N'<p>Café:</p>',N'<p>Script: “Just in front of us, over the way, you can see the shop. Between that and the storeroom is the café.”
 Giải thích: Quán café nằm giữa shop và storeroom, tức vị trí D.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,18,NULL,0,1542),
(N'd1ff3844-b6f3-5727-8248-26f25cf6cda1',N'38963f64-338e-5d0d-9411-bf7e2a4de645',0,3,19,N'<p>Booking office:</p>',N'<p>Script: “To the left of the storeroom, next to the parking lot, there’s the office where you make your bookings.”
 Giải thích: Văn phòng booking ở bên trái storeroom, sát bãi xe → C.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,19,NULL,0,1542),
(N'f8be7570-d84e-56c1-ae8b-d91bc55b0528',N'38963f64-338e-5d0d-9411-bf7e2a4de645',0,3,19,N'<p>Waiting area for rides:</p>',N'<p>Script: “And looking at the other side of the shop, to the right of it, is the place where you wait to ride. It runs alongside the whole length of the arena.”
 Giải thích: Khu chờ rides nằm bên phải shop, kéo dài song song arena → E.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,20,NULL,0,1542),
(N'73397126-43e2-5503-b3e3-810460b18876',N'40d1d7aa-0a2b-5be7-9565-6b75316ea8e0',0,1,15,(CAST(N'<h2>Follow-up work</h2><p>Right, Lena. On the whole, your essay on Just Coffee was well-researched and made a much better impression on me than your last assignment. Several of you chose to write about Just Coffee, in fact. So I feel I''ve learned a lot about the company, too. Good. But I was a bit disappointed with the grade I was given. Where did I go wrong? Well, it was an interesting choice of company and it gave you a lot to say, but you could have expressed it better in places. It sounded a bit informal at times. Oh, dear. But I have to say, you obviously put more time into the planning stage this time. Yes, I did. In my last essay, I didn''t really think about how the essay should develop, which meant I ended up repeating a lot of details. Well, you can see how helpful planning is now. However, a couple of other points also let you down. Although your profile covered the five main areas we asked you to research – operation, products, shareholders, objectives, and mission statement – you should have spent more time on layout, just making sure that it looks professional. Sorry about that. I''m still not 100% confident with the graphics software. Okay. It was also handed in after the deadline. That automatically means you''re penalized. However, it was very satisfactory on the whole.  </p><p>Read my notes at the end, but I''d like to run through a few minor points with you, too. Fine. So, just coffee. You cover the company''s operation well, but I think you could have added more about how the company supports the communities where the coffee is produced. They focus on this a lot in their advertising. You mean in practical terms? Yes. I was thinking specifically of the fact that it offers producers up to 60% of the value of the coffee in advance of delivery. Which makes it possible for them to cover startup equipment and employment costs in the field. Precisely. And you mentioned that Just Coffee pays its growers more than the standard global rate, but you didn''t quote any precise figures. It''s double, isn''t it? I know it''s very generous. Triple, in fact. And it''s premium to growers, who produce organic crops, too. I didn''t know that. Well, it''s too late to include that now, but you really ought to have done a bit more research on the impact of the company on its local growers. I did mention how some coffee producers in Haiti are producing enough coffee to sell to other markets, too. Yes, I remember that. But in Peru, the company suggested that farmers experi' AS nvarchar(max))+N'ment with different kinds of coffee at different altitudes. That''s an interesting development, and it would have been good to mention it. I didn''t know about that. Can you give me some information about it? Yes, we''ve got a collection of articles on Just Coffee in a folder here, which I''ll give you in a minute  Now, talking of reference materials... Yes? I think Just Coffee is a very interesting company, so I''d like you to compile a reference document to add to the department''s library file. Oh, okay. What should it include? Well, it would be useful to say something about their range of products. How many are there on the market at the moment? Eight in total. Okay. A quick description of each one. And what about a section on the local profit and how it''s used to help the local community? I thought that was interesting. It''s a bit of a diversion, but why not? If I remember correctly, it''s used to purchase computers, among other things. Yes, that''s right. It''s great that the profit is plowed back like that. Lots of customers buy their products for that reason alone. </p><p>You''re right. Okay. And say something about the most important advantage for producers who work with Just Coffee. Would you say that it''s the trading partnership? In all the literature, the term they use is knowledge sharing. So perhaps I should quote that. It''s called that because the company doesn''t only buy the coffee from the suppliers, it also gives them advice on market conditions and export strategies. Good. I''ll give this some more thought and drop a brief for you to work with. There''s no rush for this, so don''t worry. Okay. Thanks.</p>'),(CAST(N'<p>Right, Lena. On the whole, your essay on Just Coffee was well-researched and made a much better impression on me than your last assignment. Several of you chose to write about Just Coffee, in fact. So I feel I''ve learned a lot about the company, too. Good. But I was a bit disappointed with the grade I was given. Where did I go wrong? Well, it was an interesting choice of company and it gave you a lot to say, but you could have expressed it better in places. It sounded a bit informal at times. Oh, dear. But I have to say, you obviously put more time into the planning stage this time. Yes, I did. In my last essay, I didn''t really think about how the essay should develop, which meant I ended up repeating a lot of details. Well, you can see how helpful planning is now. However, a couple of other points also let you down. Although your profile covered the five main areas we asked you to research – operation, products, shareholders, objectives, and mission statement – you should have spent more time on layout, just making sure that it looks professional. Sorry about that. I''m still not 100% confident with the graphics software. Okay. It was also handed in after the deadline. That automatically means you''re penalized. However, it was very satisfactory on the whole.  </p><p>Read my notes at the end, but I''d like to run through a few minor points with you, too. Fine. So, just coffee. You cover the company''s operation well, but I think you could have added more about how the company supports the communities where the coffee is produced. They focus on this a lot in their advertising. You mean in practical terms? Yes. I was thinking specifically of the fact that it offers producers up to 60% of the value of the coffee in advance of delivery. Which makes it possible for them to cover startup equipment and employment costs in the field. Precisely. And you mentioned that Just Coffee pays its growers more than the standard global rate, but you didn''t quote any precise figures. It''s double, isn''t it? I know it''s very generous. Triple, in fact. And it''s premium to growers, who produce organic crops, too. I didn''t know that. Well, it''s too late to include that now, but you really ought to have done a bit more research on the impact of the company on its local growers. I did mention how some coffee producers in Haiti are producing enough coffee to sell to other markets, too. Yes, I remember that. But in Peru, the company suggested that farmers experiment with different kin' AS nvarchar(max))+N'ds of coffee at different altitudes. That''s an interesting development, and it would have been good to mention it. I didn''t know about that. Can you give me some information about it? Yes, we''ve got a collection of articles on Just Coffee in a folder here, which I''ll give you in a minute  Now, talking of reference materials... Yes? I think Just Coffee is a very interesting company, so I''d like you to compile a reference document to add to the department''s library file. Oh, okay. What should it include? Well, it would be useful to say something about their range of products. How many are there on the market at the moment? Eight in total. Okay. A quick description of each one. And what about a section on the local profit and how it''s used to help the local community? I thought that was interesting. It''s a bit of a diversion, but why not? If I remember correctly, it''s used to purchase computers, among other things. Yes, that''s right. It''s great that the profit is plowed back like that. Lots of customers buy their products for that reason alone. </p><p>You''re right. Okay. And say something about the most important advantage for producers who work with Just Coffee. Would you say that it''s the trading partnership? In all the literature, the term they use is knowledge sharing. So perhaps I should quote that. It''s called that because the company doesn''t only buy the coffee from the suppliers, it also gives them advice on market conditions and export strategies. Good. I''ll give this some more thought and drop a brief for you to work with. There''s no rush for this, so don''t worry. Okay. Thanks.</p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-4/iL.VOL4.8.S1542.PART3.mp3',NULL,1,0,3,NULL,0,1542),
