(N'28ac7cb6-e3c7-52d5-b014-05e451477dea',N'37b9d2e7-2476-5551-9f21-dd94ab381c0a',0,1,13,(CAST(N'<h2>[VOL 4] Family presents</h2><p>Hello, Ramona Toys. You''re through to Tracy. How can I help you?

Good morning! I want to buy birthday presents for my sister''s children. She''s very keen on educational toys. Do you sell that sort of thing?

Yes, actually we specialise in those types of toys. How old are the children?

Well, Peter, he''s the oldest. He''s going to be nine next week. Did you have anything particular in mind for him?

I got him a jigsaw last year, but I''d like to get him something a bit more challenging this time. Perhaps something he could make himself.

How about a model truck? Might that be any good? It''s made of wood; it comes in a kit, so you get all the pieces, and then there are the electrical components.

Oh, it''s not just mechanical then?

Oh no, it''s quite sophisticated. It''s recommended for children over eight, and you also get a sheet of stickers to decorate it.

That sounds just up his street, and I''m sure it''d help him to understand technology even if it''s only basic.

Well, yes. And it is a change from the chemistry sets we used to get.

Oh, you had one of those too, did you?

What about price?

It''s £17.50

It''s not too expensive then. I could get him something else as well. He''s always been interested in animals.

How about a book about jungle animals?

I think he''s already got one.

OK. Well, how about a bird feeder instead? That''s a kit as well. You even get some paints and a brush, so you can decorate it how you like.

Wow!

That sounds just the thing. And it''d give him contact with wildlife.

