(N'df473a3c-8897-51b7-ac86-0e40d56c03e6',N'66f30f54-5c33-568d-8a64-baad80eeedb3',0,2,18,N'<p>Look at the following statements (Questions 14-18) and the list of researchers below.<br>Match each statement with the correct researchers, <span>A, B, C, or D.<br></span>Write the correct letter,<span> A, B, C, or D</span>, in boxes 14-18 on your answer sheet.<br><span>NB </span>You may use any letter more than once.</p>',N'',N'',N'',N'Answer choices',10,0,1,NULL,0,1517),
(N'792c5c16-9a26-552a-b11c-1f3a380e4163',N'df473a3c-8897-51b7-ac86-0e40d56c03e6',0,3,19,N'<p>Memories are stored in various parts of the brain.</p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms:<br>‘various parts’ = ‘one area’, ‘elsewhere’, ‘another place’: Nhiều bộ phận khác nhau.<br>+ Question:<br>Interpretation: Ký ức được lưu trữ ở nhiều bộ phận khác nhau của não bộ.<br>+ Answer: <br>Dựa vào thông tin trong bài và synonyms ta thấy ông Jay Gottfried lấy ví dụ về sóng biển để chỉ ra việc ký ức được lưu trữ ở nhiều bộ phận khác nhau của não.<br>=&gt; Đáp án cần điền là B</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,14,NULL,0,1517),
(N'86a825de-533a-535d-9c56-681c06d9313a',N'df473a3c-8897-51b7-ac86-0e40d56c03e6',0,3,19,N'<p>Memories awakened by smell arouse stronger feelings than memories awakened by other senses.</p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms:<br>‘stronger feelings’ = ‘more emotional’: Cảm xúc mãnh liệt hơn.<br>+ Question: <br>Interpretation: Những ký ức được khơi gợi bởi mùi hương khơi dậy cảm xúc mạnh mẽ hơn so với những ký ức được khơi gợi bởi các giác quan khác. <br>+ Answer:<br>Dựa vào thông tin trong bài và synonyms ta thấy bà Rachel Herz cho rằng ký ức được khơi gợi bởi mùi hương khơi dậy cảm xúc mạnh mẽ hơn so với những ký ức được khơi gợi bởi các giác quan khác =&gt; Hoàn toàn trùng khớp với đề bài.<br>=&gt; Câu trả lời là A </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,15,NULL,0,1517),
(N'6887a3a3-2596-5db6-94a8-3ec6da58dca4',N'df473a3c-8897-51b7-ac86-0e40d56c03e6',0,3,19,N'<p>Smells can be used to assist in recalling past events more accurately.</p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms:<br>‘more accurately’ = ‘more details’: Chính xác hơn.<br>+ Question: <br>Interpretation: Mùi hương có thể được sử dụng để hỗ trợ việc hồi tưởng các sự kiện trong quá khứ một cách chính xác hơn.<br>+ Answer: <br>Dựa vào thông tin trong bài và synonyms ta thấy John Downes và Simon Chu cho rằng mùi hương của những đồ vật trong câu chuyện có thể giúp đối tượng nhớ được nhiều chi tiết trong câu chuyện của họ hơn =&gt; trùng với ý kiến đề đưa ra.<br>=&gt; Đáp án cần điền là C</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,16,NULL,0,1517),
(N'b488d0c7-0029-5ba4-bd3b-c91db760381b',N'df473a3c-8897-51b7-ac86-0e40d56c03e6',0,3,19,N'<p>There need not be a direct link between visual cues and memories of smells.</p>',N'<p>+Synonyms:</p><p>+Question: Interpretation: Không nhất thiết phải có mối liên hệ trực tiếp giữa các tín hiệu thị giác và ký ức về mùi hương.</p><p>+Answer: Dựa vào thông tin trong bài ta thấy ông Jay Gottfried cho ví dụ về việc các tín hiệu thị giác không nhất thiết phải liên kết trực tiếp với các ký ức về mùi hương =&gt; trùng với ý kiến đề đưa ra. </p><p>=&gt; Đáp án cần điền là B</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,17,NULL,0,1517),
(N'7a93ad82-42fa-5364-81b8-70c549bb4d84',N'df473a3c-8897-51b7-ac86-0e40d56c03e6',0,3,19,N'<p>Emotions have a different relationship with smell than with the other senses.</p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms:<br>‘different’ = ‘unique’: Khác biệt.<br>+ Question: <br>Interpretation: Cảm xúc có mối quan hệ với khứu giác khác so với các giác quan khác.<br>+ Answer: <br>Dựa vào thông tin trong bài và synonyms ta thấy bà Rachel Herz cho rằng có một mối liên kết độc nhất giữa khứu giác và phần của não mà xử lí cảm xúc =&gt; mối quan hệ của cảm xúc và khứu giác khác với các giác quan khác.<br>=&gt; Đáp án cần điền là A</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,18,NULL,0,1517),
(N'b4063d77-affb-55d8-b9b6-db0da1d5b778',N'66f30f54-5c33-568d-8a64-baad80eeedb3',0,2,18,N'<p>Choose the correct letter, <span>A, B, C, or D</span>. Write the correct letter in boxes 19-22 on your answer sheet.</p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',1,0,2,NULL,0,1517),
(N'b46cf3de-dd78-5bfe-b538-09ddd65235cd',N'b4063d77-affb-55d8-b9b6-db0da1d5b778',0,3,19,N'<p>The writer uses the example of a newspaper to show that </p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms:</p><p>+ Question: Interpretation: Tác giả sử dụng ví dụ về một tờ báo để cho thấy rằng.</p><p>+ Answer: Tác giả cho rằng người đọc thường chú ý tới một tờ báo bằng mắt của họ hơn là bằng mũi nhưng đưa ra ví dụ cho thấy ngược lại =&gt; Chúng ta có thể không nhận thức được những tác động mạnh mẽ của mùi hương. </p><p>=&gt; đáp án là C</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,19,NULL,0,1517),
(N'7f98e4d9-e3f0-5697-adfc-d9c683b81e46',N'b4063d77-affb-55d8-b9b6-db0da1d5b778',0,3,19,N'<p>According to the passage, memories activated by smells can be more emotional than those recalled by other senses because </p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms:<br>‘go directly to the part of the brain that affects feelings’ = ‘odour molecules activate the brain cells…a part of the brain that helps control emotion.’<br>+ Question: <br>Interpretation: Theo đoạn văn, những ký ức được kích hoạt bởi mùi hương có thể mang tính cảm xúc nhiều hơn so với những ký ức được gợi lại bởi các giác quan khác bởi vì.<br>+ Answer: <br>Dựa vào thông tin trong bài và synonyms ta có thể thấy rằng đoạn trích đã chỉ ra vì những phân tử mùi hương kích hoạt những tế bào não ở trong amiđan-một phần của não mà giúp kiểm soát cảm xúc, nên đó là vì sao những ký ức được kích hoạt bởi mùi hương có thể mang tính cảm xúc nhiều hơn so với những ký ức được gợi lại bởi các giác quan khác =&gt; lời giải thích trùng với câu trả lời C của đề.<br>=&gt; đáp án là C</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,20,NULL,0,1517),
(N'b5b587f7-c9c4-5049-8f41-d7d8d9424805',N'b4063d77-affb-55d8-b9b6-db0da1d5b778',0,3,19,N'<p>Herz''s first study proves that</p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms:</p><p>+ Question: Interpretation: Nghiên cứu đầu tiên của Herz chứng minh rằng.</p><p>+ Answer: Dựa vào thông tin trong bài ta có thể thấy sau cuộc thí nghiệm, Herz phát hiện ra khứu giác kích hoạt não của các tình nguyện viên hơn nhiều so với thị giác của họ. </p><p>=&gt; từ cần điền là B</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,21,NULL,0,1517),
(N'469348e8-7feb-52f8-9e6c-a64967293ea9',N'b4063d77-affb-55d8-b9b6-db0da1d5b778',0,3,19,N'<p>What do we learn about Herz''s second study?</p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms:<br>+ Question:<br>Interpretation: Chúng ta biết được gì về nghiên cứu thứ hai của Herz?<br>+ Answer: <br>Giống như phần nghiên cứu có thí nghiệm sử dụng nước hoa, thông tin trong bài chỉ đang xác nhận nghiên cứu đầu tiên của Herz bằng một thí nghiệm khác.</p><p>=&gt; Đáp án cần điền là B</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,22,NULL,0,1517),
(N'c0363aab-1606-53e8-ad18-2c2c0bb1d5fd',N'66f30f54-5c33-568d-8a64-baad80eeedb3',0,2,18,N'<p>Complete the summary below. </p><p>Choose <span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span> from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 23-26 on your answer sheet.</p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',11,0,3,NULL,0,1517),
(N'd12ef311-edcb-556c-8911-88155d57f0ca',N'c0363aab-1606-53e8-ad18-2c2c0bb1d5fd',0,3,19,N'<p>In one trial, neuroscientists at University College London asked volunteers to make up a }{SPACE}{ which connected a picture and an unrelated smell.</p><p>The researchers then showed the picture to the volunteers again and then monitored their responses by taking }{SPACE}{ .</p><p>The results showed that the part of the brain called the }{SPACE}{ was affected even when no smell was present.</p><p>In another study, evidence was found to show how, in Chinese families, the scent of }{SPACE}{ helped in transmitting oral histories from one generation to another.</p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms: make up = create: tạo ra.</p><p>+ Question: Interpretation: Trong một cuộc thử nghiệm, các nhà thần kinh học tại đại học London đã yêu cầu các tình nguyện viên tạo ra một …...</p><p>+ Answer: Từ cần điền là một danh từ số ít dựa trên mạo từ ‘a’. Theo như thông tin trong bài, các tình nguyện viên đã được yêu cầu tạo nên một câu chuyện liên kết hình ảnh của con vịt và mùi của hoa hồng trong cuộc thử nghiệm. </p><p>=&gt; từ cần điền là story</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,23,NULL,0,1517),
(N'800df56d-e96c-5819-aaa9-76dd2477be10',N'c0363aab-1606-53e8-ad18-2c2c0bb1d5fd',0,3,19,N'Question number 24',N'<p>+ Synonyms: <br>+ Question: <br>Interpretation: Sau đó, các nhà nghiên cứu lại cho các tình nguyện viên xem bức tranh và theo dõi phản ứng của họ bằng cách ……<br>+ Answer: <br>Từ cần điền là danh từ về một thứ dùng để theo dõi phản ứng của tình nguyện viên.<br>Theo như thông tin trong bài ta thấy việc chụp quét não các tình nguyện viên cho các nhà nghiên cứu thấy được hoạt động não của họ =&gt; các nhà nghiên cứu theo dõi phản ứng của các tình nguyện viên bằng cách chụp quét não.<br>=&gt; Từ cần điền là brain scans</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,24,NULL,0,1517),
(N'8a86ebb6-9367-5b08-8ac4-4de4406c5d18',N'c0363aab-1606-53e8-ad18-2c2c0bb1d5fd',0,3,19,N'Question number 25',N'<p>+ Synonyms: ‘no smell was present’ = ‘ without the rose smell’: Không có mùi.<br>+ Question: <br>Interpretation: Kết quả cho thấy phần bị ảnh hưởng của não được gọi là …… dù không có sự hiện diện của mùi.<br>+ Answer:<br>Từ cần tìm là một danh từ chỉ một bộ phận của não.<br>Dựa vào thông tin trong bài kết hợp với synonyms ta có thể thấy trong thí nghiệm, dù không có hoa hồng nhưng phần ‘olfactory cortex’ vẫn hoạt động<br>=&gt; từ cần điền là olfactory cortex</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,25,NULL,0,1517),
(N'aba9f21f-f45e-541b-a9d4-91a1952d730c',N'c0363aab-1606-53e8-ad18-2c2c0bb1d5fd',0,3,19,N'Question number 26',N'<p>+ Synonyms: ‘scent’ = ‘smell’: Mùi hương.<br>+ Question:<br>Interpretation: Trong một nghiên cứu khác, người ta tìm thấy bằng chứng cho thấy trong các gia đình Trung Quốc, mùi hương của …… đã giúp trong việc truyền đạt lịch sử truyền miệng.<br>+ Answers:<br>Từ cần tìm là 1 danh từ dựa theo giới từ “of” có trong câu hỏi.<br>Dựa theo thông tin trong bài kết hợp với synonym ta thấy các gia đình Trung Quốc truyền tay nhau một bình đựng gia vị =&gt; mùi hương của gia vị là thứ giúp các gia đình Trung Quốc trong việc truyền đạt lịch sử truyền miệng.<br>=&gt; Câu trả lời sẽ là spice</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,26,NULL,0,1517),
(N'761d5374-8850-52c0-a16b-22be17d857bf',N'e4b7384d-1dca-5f20-b2ee-10a658972998',0,1,15,(CAST(N'<h2>[VOL 4] The New Zealand writer Margaret Mahy</h2><p><span><span>The New Zealand writer Margaret Mahy</span></span></p><p></p><p>In a career spanning some fifty years, Margaret Mahy has come to occupy a unique place in New Zealand writing with innovative fiction and original characterisation. In our solidly realist tradition, the linguistic fireworks of Mahy''s children''s fiction and the explorations of human behaviour at the heart of her supernatural teenage fiction stand gloriously alone. Mahy''s clearest heir, I have always thought, is Elizabeth Knox - and maybe the true inheritance there is sheer singularity. Just as there is no one else like Knox in New Zealand writing, Mahy, too, has ventured into imaginative territory unknown to other local writers. So it was with great pleasure that I visited Mahy recently at her Governor''s Bay home to talk about her new book. As with all journalists, she is generous to a fault with her time and attention; and, as always - despite her careful consideration of questions and thoughtful answers - I am reminded she is not truly comfortable making herself or her life the heart of any conversation. The author honestly lays out her position at the start of the book when she states that: "But as someone who had avidly avoided science classes in school, I longed to read a straightforward book written for a layperson that could teach me how to taste food without first having to teach myself science. There was not one, so I decided to write this book." Consistent with this objective, complex terms that might prove difficult for a lay audience to understand, such as orthonasal and retronasal olfaction, are simplified as ''nose-smelling'' and ''mouth-smelling'', respectively.</p><p></p><p>Certainly, any consideration of the style of Mahy''s novels and picture books throws up some inspiration from her immediate environment: the writing on the side of a bus; a spelling mistake in a note to herself; the similarity between a cat and a fur hat. But despite these sometimes mundane origins, the settings for her stories are delightfully varied, as these books celebrate the dramatic plot twists and unpredictability of adventures on the high seas or in Antarctica, and also in quite unassuming places like the library or even down the back of a chair at home. Mahy has a lifelong affection for characters who are agents of upheaval and disturbance. Her junior and picture books are peppered with pirates, robbers and lions, though they appear alon' AS nvarchar(max))+N'gside librarians, mothers and children, working against comfortable stereotype. Her fictions often have at their heart a young adult burdened with special powers, such as the ability to cast spells in order to transform their world in supernatural and fantastical ways. Another common feature is that, while the conclusions of her tales are usually predictable, they leave the reader feeling absolutely complete, the moral questions resulting from our hero''s powers having been resolved.</p><p></p><p>Many of these themes can be found in her new novel, The Magician of Hoad. The book was begun more than 15 years ago and envisioned as an entire fantasy - one set in a fully imagined world with detailed history and complex tribal inter-relationships, a classical hero quest at its heart. The story ballooned at one point to 800 pages and has been through at least two substantial rewrites. Now half its original size, it is a fascinating read - an adventure, a romance, and a gold mine of Mahy literary preoccupations.</p><p></p><p>The other splendid Mahy publication this year is a re-issue of Bubble Trouble in a new illustrated edition. This tongue-twister tale first appeared in 1991, was included in 100 New Zealand Poems (1993) and has been recited by Mahy at countless private and public functions. Perhaps more than any other work, Bubble Trouble is the Mahy that New Zealand children and their parents know so well, the rollicking story of a clown who serves up a joyous torrent of word play and unexpected rhyme.</p><p></p><p>Those connections are four or five deep now. I read The Lion in the Meadow in the School Journal in the late 1960s; my stepdaughter listened to The Boy Who Was Followed Home over and over in the 1970s; my own children sat very still mouthing The Great White Man-Eating Shark in the 80s and 90s; now in the 21st century, my grandchildren have read Down the Dragon''s Tongue, A Summery Saturday Morning and Dashing Dandy many times.</p><p></p><p>Of course, readers are important to any working writer, but Mahy''s espousal of the act of reading goes beyond that: a book is not properly finished, she has often said, until it has been read, because a reader brings something important to the book. So, doubtless out of need to build a market - she is not ignorant of her popularity - but also out of genuine care for that other dynamic part of the author-reader relationship, Mahy has, until recently, kept up a punishing schedule of public appearances.</p><p></p><p>Pr'+N'ivate conversation with Mahy has always been a wild ride - marvellous, in the true sense of the word, the product of a hungry head and an infinite capacity to be astonished. She races away at one stage to consult an encyclopaedia for L M Montgomery''s date of death, and speculates about the ''real'' Montgomery, creator of the ever-popular Anne of Green Gables. Although I would come to talk about her new book, I could not help but be captivated by her infectious curiosity.</p><p></p><p>A few years ago, the writer David Hill told a funny story. Though his writing was, he conceded, very different from Mahy''s, he had been affected by her, especially by her way of looking at the world, particularly the mad, slippery life of language. Hill said, in a motel room, a sign on a wardrobe caught his eye: "This door is alarmed." Mahy would like that, thought Hill. She would enjoy the comedy just below the surface of the formal warning; she would leap immediately to the possibilities for story and language play: "Yes, and this window is concerned, this light fitting is irritated." His story was a wonderful comment on Mahy''s vision.</p>'),NULL,NULL,N'',NULL,1,0,3,NULL,0,1517),
(N'0e23e711-5f69-5bb2-aeee-6c61a5c9851e',N'761d5374-8850-52c0-a16b-22be17d857bf',0,2,18,N'<p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 27–31 on your answer sheet, write<span> TRUE/ FALSE/ NOT GIVEN.</span></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',1,0,1,NULL,0,1517),
(N'8b466330-62ff-501c-8d55-ee2bf5ed56ed',N'0e23e711-5f69-5bb2-aeee-6c61a5c9851e',0,3,19,N'<p>Mahy and Knox have sometimes criticised each other''s work.</p>',N'<p>+ Question:<br>Interpretation: Mahy và Knox đôi khi đã chỉ trích tác phẩm của nhau.<br>+ Answer: <br>Đoạn trích không đề cập đến bất kỳ sự bất đồng nào giữa họ =&gt; Không có thông tin về việc Mahy và Knox phê bình nhau.</p><p>=&gt; Đáp án cần điền là NOT GIVEN</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,27,NULL,0,1517),
(N'ca4ede92-6934-5cb6-be1c-0f2fde2a0c14',N'0e23e711-5f69-5bb2-aeee-6c61a5c9851e',0,3,19,N'<p>Mahy explores the traditional themes of New Zealand literature.</p>',N'<p>+ Antonyms:<br>‘explores the traditional themes’: Khám phá những chủ đề truyền thống &gt;&lt; ‘stand gloriously alone’: Tách biệt.<br>+ Question: <br>Interpretation: Mahy khám phá các chủ đề truyền thống trong văn học New Zealand. <br>+ Answer:<br>Dựa vào thông tin trong bài và antonyms ta thấy câu chuyện của Mahi tách hẳn với cái truyền thống, những câu chuyện của bà ‘đứng hiên ngang một mình’ =&gt; bà không khám phá chủ đề truyền thống.<br>=&gt; Câu trả lời là FALSE </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,28,NULL,0,1517),
(N'22a431cd-81dc-5897-96e5-5af35082b285',N'0e23e711-5f69-5bb2-aeee-6c61a5c9851e',0,3,19,N'<p>Mahy''s children''s books have been more popular than her teenage books.</p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms:<br>+ Question: <br>Interpretation: Các cuốn sách thiếu nhi của Mahy phổ biến hơn các cuốn sách dành cho thiếu niên.<br>+ Answer: <br>Đoạn trích đã liệt kê những cuốn sách thiếu nhi và cả sách cho thiếu niên =&gt; không so sánh độ nổi tiếng.<br>=&gt; Đáp án cần điền là NOT GIVEN</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,29,NULL,0,1517),
(N'fbdbb76c-27f2-5111-8a14-b659f2821e58',N'0e23e711-5f69-5bb2-aeee-6c61a5c9851e',0,3,19,N'<p>Mahy is welcoming to interviewers.</p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms:<br>‘welcoming to interviewers.’ = ‘generous to a fault with her time and attention.’: Niềm nở với những người phỏng vấn.<br>+ Question: <br>Interpretation: Mahy cởi mở với những người phỏng vấn.<br>+ Answer: <br>Dựa vào thông tin trong bài và synonyms ta thấy Mahy dành rất nhiều thời gian và sự chú ý của bà cho những người phỏng vấn =&gt; Mahy cởi mở với những người phỏng vấn.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,30,NULL,0,1517),
(N'abfbd366-e166-5e12-88d4-ac35bf7697b9',N'0e23e711-5f69-5bb2-aeee-6c61a5c9851e',0,3,19,N'<p>Mahy is at ease speaking about her experiences</p>',N'<p>+ Antonyms:<br>‘at ease’: Thoải mái &gt;&lt; ‘not truly comfortable’: Không thoải mái.<br>+ Question: <br>Interpretation: Mahy cảm thấy thoải mái khi nói về những trải nghiệm của mình.<br>+ Answer: <br>Dựa vào thông tin trong bài và antonyms ta thấy Mahy không thật sự thoải mái với việc làm bản thân trở thành trung tâm của cuộc trò chuyện =&gt; Mahy không thoải mái khi nói về những trải nghiệm của mình.<br>=&gt; Đáp án cần điền là FALSE</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,31,NULL,0,1517),
(N'97ad9895-05b4-5685-8def-08a237da952a',N'761d5374-8850-52c0-a16b-22be17d857bf',0,2,18,N'<p>Complete the summary using the list of words and phrases below.</p><p>Drag the correct word or phrase from the list into each gap.</p>',N'',N'',N'',N'Theories about Mahy''s style',13,0,2,NULL,0,1517),
(N'b644e2f0-89fa-5972-b3f4-374e10ab0767',N'97ad9895-05b4-5685-8def-08a237da952a',0,3,19,N'<h3>Theories about Mahy''s style</h3><p>Mahy''s determination to earn a living from writing has encouraged her to find the ideas for her work in }{SPACE}{ places.</p><p>The stories themselves are set in locations that are }{SPACE}{ .</p><p>In terms of characterisation, almost all of her books feature unruly people, and very often an adolescent who possesses }{SPACE}{ abilities.</p><p>Finally, the endings of the stories tend to be }{SPACE}{ .</p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms:<br>‘everyday places’ = ‘immediate environment’: Những nơi gần gũi.<br>+ Question: <br>Interpretation: Sự quyết tâm của Mahy trong việc kiếm sống bằng nghề viết đã khuyến khích cô tìm ý tưởng cho các tác phẩm của mình ở những nơi …….<br>+ Answer: <br>Đoạn trích liệt kê những nơi gần gũi, thường ngày với Mahy, vậy nên từ cần điền ở đây là everyday.<br>=&gt; đáp án là B</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,32,NULL,0,1517),
(N'108e2253-3b82-5779-9bff-c75d572f2b18',N'97ad9895-05b4-5685-8def-08a237da952a',0,3,19,N'Question number 33',N'<p>+ Synonyms:<br>‘exotic’ = ‘high seas or in Antarctica’: Những nơi mới mẻ, kỳ lạ.<br>‘ordinary’ = ‘library or even down the back of a chair at home.’: Những nơi bình thường<br>+ Question: <br>Interpretation: Các câu chuyện được đặt trong những địa điểm … về mặt xây dựng nhân vật.<br>+ Answer: <br>Dựa vào thông tin trong bài và synonyms ta có thể thấy tác giả đưa ra những nơi khác thường và thông thường để làm bối cảnh trong những câu chuyện của bà, bao gồm những vùng biển hay Nam cực, thư viện hay ở nhà =&gt; từ cần điền ở đây là exotic and ordinary.<br>=&gt; đáp án là E</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,33,NULL,0,1517),
(N'906046a5-11b1-5167-bcfa-1c355f689ad9',N'97ad9895-05b4-5685-8def-08a237da952a',0,3,19,N'Question number 34',N'<p>+ Question: Interpretation: Hầu hết các cuốn sách của bà đều có những người ngang bướng, và thường là một thiếu niên sở hữu những khả năng …….</p><p>+ Answer: Dựa vào thông tin trong bài và synonyms ta thấy bà viết về một thiếu niên thay đổi thế giới của họ bằng những cách siêu nhiên và kì ảo</p><p>=&gt; vậy ta điền magical ở đây là hợp lí.</p><p>=&gt; từ cần điền là F</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,34,NULL,0,1517),
(N'38f6b588-a33b-5bfa-921a-77a06851f919',N'97ad9895-05b4-5685-8def-08a237da952a',0,3,19,N'Question number 35',N'<p>+ Synonyms:<br>‘unsurprising’ = ‘usually predictable’: Dễ đoán.<br>+ Question:<br>Interpretation: Cuối cùng, kết thúc của các câu chuyện thường có xu hướng ……<br>+ Answer: <br>Dựa vào thông tin trong bài và synonyms ta thấy kết truyện của bà thường dễ đoán, vậy từ cần điền ở đây là unsurprising.<br>=&gt; Đáp án cần điền là H</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,35,NULL,0,1517),
(N'594ad2ad-785b-5ce5-9342-0ed049fa30cb',N'761d5374-8850-52c0-a16b-22be17d857bf',0,2,18,N'<p>Choose the correct letter, <span>A, B, C, or D</span>. Write the correct letter in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.</p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',1,0,3,NULL,0,1517),
(N'3769c3c7-621a-509c-af1c-d094f2c7bd6d',N'594ad2ad-785b-5ce5-9342-0ed049fa30cb',0,3,19,N'<p>What does the writer say about The Magician of Hoad?</p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms:<br>‘restructured’ = ‘two substantial rewrites’: Được viết lại.<br>+ Question: <br>Interpretation: Tác giả nói gì về The Magician of Hoad?<br>+ Answer:<br>Dựa vào thông tin trong bài và synonyms ta có thể thấy câu chuyện đã trải qua ít nhất hai lần viết lại.<br>=&gt; Đáp án cần điền là B</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,36,NULL,0,1517),
(N'6f81a8e0-e6de-56c2-b585-5a897f931069',N'594ad2ad-785b-5ce5-9342-0ed049fa30cb',0,3,19,N'<p>According to the writer, Bubble Trouble</p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms: <br>‘is an old favourite’ = ‘know so well’: Kinh điển<br>+ Question: <br>Interpretation: Theo tác giả, Bubble Trouble.<br>+ Answer: <br>Dựa vào thông tin trong bài và synonyms ta có thể thấy Bubble Trouble là câu chuyện mà trẻ em và phụ huynh New Zealand đều biết.<br>=&gt; Đáp án cần điền là C</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,37,NULL,0,1517),
(N'916465bd-b7df-5e5b-88ce-553398b26138',N'594ad2ad-785b-5ce5-9342-0ed049fa30cb',0,3,19,N'<p>The writer''s purpose in the fifth paragraph is to</p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms:<br>+ Question: <br>Interpretation: Mục đích của tác giả trong đoạn thứ năm là.<br>+ Answer:<br>Dựa vào đoạn trích ta có thể thấy tác giả đang liệt kê ra những tác phẩm của Mahy mà nhiều thế hệ trẻ em đã đọc, tác giả đã đọc vào cuối những năm 1960, tiếp theo đó là con cái của ông và cuối cùng là những đứa cháu =&gt; Mahy rất nổi tiếng với nhiều thế hệ trẻ em.<br>=&gt; Đáp án cần điền là D</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,38,NULL,0,1517),
(N'80782568-19ee-517b-97a7-c7cc675f175f',N'594ad2ad-785b-5ce5-9342-0ed049fa30cb',0,3,19,N'<p>According to the sixth paragraph, which of the following is true?</p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms: <br>‘Readers are necessary‘ = ‘reader brings something important’: Độc giả rất quan trọng.<br>+ Question:<br>Interpretation: Theo đoạn văn thứ sáu, điều nào sau đây là đúng?<br>+Answers:<br>Dựa theo thông tin trong bài kết hợp với synonyms ta thấy tác giả khẳng định một cuốn sách không thể hoàn thiện cho tới khi nó được đọc, độc giả là cần thiết. =&gt; Câu trả lời sẽ là C</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,39,NULL,0,1517),
(N'c8ea3a11-ecc6-5da7-82cf-11e35f9d2e6d',N'594ad2ad-785b-5ce5-9342-0ed049fa30cb',0,3,19,N'<p>What is the writer doing in the final paragraph?</p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms: <br>‘view of the world’ = ‘vision’: Góc nhìn.<br>+ Question:<br>Interpretation: Tác giả đang làm gì ở đoạn văn cuối?<br>+ Answers:<br>Dựa theo đoạn trích ở thông tin trong bài ta thấy được Hill đang miêu tả cách Mahy nhìn nhận thế giới =&gt; trùng với câu trả lời A<br>=&gt; Câu trả lời sẽ là A</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,40,NULL,0,1517),
(N'ff75774c-f2e7-5ded-8750-1543ceb27448',NULL,0,0,11,NULL,NULL,NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-4/iL.VOL4.6.S1505.mp3',N'Vol 4 LISTENING FULL TEST 6',0,7,1,NULL,1,1505),
(N'852df6f9-e93b-5b64-83ab-8bb6e698d3ce',N'ff75774c-f2e7-5ded-8750-1543ceb27448',0,1,13,(CAST(N'<h2>[VOL 4] Gym Membership Form</h2><p>Good morning. Can I help you? Yes, actually, I''m interested in joining your gym, so I thought I''d come and find out about your membership options. Why don''t you take a seat now and I''ll just get the form and a pen. Thanks. Now, your full name, please? It''s Jean Simpson. Right, Jean. Is that Simpson with a P? Yeah. Right, Jean. Date of birth? The 24th of August, 1979. And where do you live? 70 Fox Lane. Is that Fox as in the animal? Yes. And it''s Surfers Paradise, 4167. Do you have a home phone number Jane? Yes, it''s 3378 4150. Great! Now that we have that information, I''ll tell you about the membership plans we offer, and you can select a payment option that suits you. That sounds good. Our two most popular payment options are yearly and monthly. The yearly membership fee works out to about 11$ per week. On the monthly plan, you pay slightly more each week. By the way, this month with both of these options, we''re offering a free gym outfit. That''s great! I think I''ll go for the yearly option. The initial outlay is more, but I''m mostly interested in getting in shape, and that option will help keep me coming. Even if I don''t like it, I should be fit by the end. Fair enough. The yearly option it is then. Have you got any questions or concerns? Yeah, I''m going away for a month, and I won''t be able to come to the gym. During that time, lots of people have this problem when they go on holiday. We can just suspend your gym membership for that month. That''s it. It won''t be until July, and it''s for work, actually, but next year I''m going overseas to my friend''s wedding, so can I suspend my membership for a couple of weeks then as well? No problem. Just tell us about that closer to the date of your departure. I''ll tell you about the facilities we offer here. We offer a range of group fitness classes such as Body Step, Body Tone, and Body Balance. They all sound very interesting. But I can''t see myself ever going to a class. Well, if that''s not an option, perhaps you should try some general weight training exercises in the gym. Our instructors are fully trained and very good at helping new members to feel comfortable. Everybody''s encouraged to go at their own pace. I like the sound of that. I wouldn''t have to get fit first, would I? I could just start straight away. That''s right. Let me tell you about the other services we offer. Are you interested in doing any water-based training? Hmmmmmm. Well, we have an Olympic-sized swimmi' AS nvarchar(max))+N'ng pool where you can do aqua aerobics classes. That''s group exercise in the swimming pool. Or we can develop a personal swimming plan to suit your needs. Aqua aerobics doesn''t really appeal to me; I''m really not very keen on fixed classes, but working on my own swimming regime would be okay in a few months when I''m a bit fitter I suppose. Fine, We also have a sauna where you can relax after a strong workout. That''s not my idea of relaxing; saunas are just too hot for me. Many people feel that way, I must say. One other facility we offer is our child-minding service. It''s available to our members at 5$ per child. Well, my husband will be working at home for the first few months, so he''ll be able to look after the baby when I''m exercising. But once he goes back to work, I''ll probably be using that service. Right? If you don''t have any questions, let''s finalise things. We can arrange payment and make an entry key for you to use whenever you come to the gym.</p>'),(CAST(N'<p>Good morning. Can I help you? Yes, actually, I''m interested in joining your gym, so I thought I''d come and find out about your membership options. Why don''t you take a seat now and I''ll just get the form and a pen. Thanks. Now, your full name, please? It''s Jean Simpson. Right, Jean. Is that Simpson with a P? Yeah. Right, Jean. Date of birth? The 24th of August, 1979. And where do you live? 70 Fox Lane. Is that Fox as in the animal? Yes. And it''s Surfers Paradise, 4167. Do you have a home phone number Jane? Yes, it''s 3378 4150. Great! Now that we have that information, I''ll tell you about the membership plans we offer, and you can select a payment option that suits you. That sounds good. Our two most popular payment options are yearly and monthly. The yearly membership fee works out to about 11$ per week. On the monthly plan, you pay slightly more each week. By the way, this month with both of these options, we''re offering a free gym outfit. That''s great! I think I''ll go for the yearly option. The initial outlay is more, but I''m mostly interested in getting in shape, and that option will help keep me coming. Even if I don''t like it, I should be fit by the end. Fair enough. The yearly option it is then. Have you got any questions or concerns? Yeah, I''m going away for a month, and I won''t be able to come to the gym. During that time, lots of people have this problem when they go on holiday. We can just suspend your gym membership for that month. That''s it. It won''t be until July, and it''s for work, actually, but next year I''m going overseas to my friend''s wedding, so can I suspend my membership for a couple of weeks then as well? No problem. Just tell us about that closer to the date of your departure. I''ll tell you about the facilities we offer here. We offer a range of group fitness classes such as Body Step, Body Tone, and Body Balance. They all sound very interesting. But I can''t see myself ever going to a class. Well, if that''s not an option, perhaps you should try some general weight training exercises in the gym. Our instructors are fully trained and very good at helping new members to feel comfortable. Everybody''s encouraged to go at their own pace. I like the sound of that. I wouldn''t have to get fit first, would I? I could just start straight away. That''s right. Let me tell you about the other services we offer. Are you interested in doing any water-based training? Hmmmmmm. Well, we have an Olympic-sized swimming pool where you can do aqua aerobi' AS nvarchar(max))+N'cs classes. That''s group exercise in the swimming pool. Or we can develop a personal swimming plan to suit your needs. Aqua aerobics doesn''t really appeal to me; I''m really not very keen on fixed classes, but working on my own swimming regime would be okay in a few months when I''m a bit fitter I suppose. Fine, We also have a sauna where you can relax after a strong workout. That''s not my idea of relaxing; saunas are just too hot for me. Many people feel that way, I must say. One other facility we offer is our child-minding service. It''s available to our members at 5$ per child. Well, my husband will be working at home for the first few months, so he''ll be able to look after the baby when I''m exercising. But once he goes back to work, I''ll probably be using that service. Right? If you don''t have any questions, let''s finalise things. We can arrange payment and make an entry key for you to use whenever you come to the gym.</p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-4/iL.VOL4.6.S1505.PART1.mp3',NULL,1,0,1,NULL,0,1505),
(N'7866f7b5-6247-5531-a66b-2e1af9978a43',N'852df6f9-e93b-5b64-83ab-8bb6e698d3ce',0,2,18,N'<p><em>Write <span>ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER </span>for each answer.</em></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',11,0,1,NULL,0,1505),
(N'6adfaa3f-6bbe-5ee4-834a-6b72a1598b3d',N'7866f7b5-6247-5531-a66b-2e1af9978a43',0,3,19,N'<table border="1"><tbody><tr><td></td><td><p><span><span>Gym Membership Form</span></span></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><span>Personal Details</span></p></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p><span>Name:</span></p></td><td><p>Jean Simpson</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><span>Date of birth:</span></p></td><td> }{SPACE}{ </td></tr><tr><td><p><span>Address:</span></p></td><td><p>70, }{SPACE}{ Lane Surfers Paradise, 4167</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><span>Home phone:</span></p></td><td><p>33784150</p></td></tr></tbody></table>',N'<p>Question: “Ngày sinh của Jean Simpson là gì?” → Cần ngày/tháng/năm. Answer: Người nói khẳng định rõ “the 24th of August, 1979” → điền đáp án 24th August</p><p>Key vocab: date of birth = ngày sinh.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,1,NULL,0,1505),
(N'8f50110b-73db-50ee-abd3-a661c4c7a620',N'7866f7b5-6247-5531-a66b-2e1af9978a43',0,3,19,N'Question number 2',N'<p>Question: “Jean sống  đâu? (hoàn thành số nhà và tên đường)” → Cần danh từ chỉ đường. Answer: Người nói nhấn mạnh “70 Fox Lane” → từ còn thiếu là Fox. Key vocab: Lane = ngõ/đường nhỏ. </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,2,NULL,0,1505),
(N'9f0071e3-5188-527c-9a4c-6c91c5eb6187',N'852df6f9-e93b-5b64-83ab-8bb6e698d3ce',0,2,18,N'<p><em>Choose the correct letter,<span> A, B </span>or<span> C.</span></em></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',1,0,2,NULL,0,1505),
(N'65202717-6b3d-5ed1-b200-afd85d35cacc',N'9f0071e3-5188-527c-9a4c-6c91c5eb6187',0,3,19,N'<p>What is Jean’s reason for choosing the yearly payment option</p>',N'<p>Question: “Lý do Jean chọn trả phí theo năm là gì?” → Cần động cơ cá nhân. Answer: Jean nói “interested in getting in shape” = mục tiêu là trở nên khỏe/fit → C đúng. Key vocab: get in shape = trở nên khỏe mạnh, become fitter.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,3,NULL,0,1505),
(N'62821d4d-a89c-5ff6-a7a5-1e828e5b4555',N'9f0071e3-5188-527c-9a4c-6c91c5eb6187',0,3,19,N'<p>What is Jean doing in July this year?</p>',N'<p>Question: “Jean sẽ làm gì vào tháng 7 năm nay?” → Cần hoạt động chính.
Answer: Jean nói rõ “for work” → tức traveling for business. -&gt; B
Key vocab: for work = công tác, traveling for business.
</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,4,NULL,0,1505),
(N'7f9e2741-962d-5e46-bbe8-e617000ef25e',N'852df6f9-e93b-5b64-83ab-8bb6e698d3ce',0,2,18,N'<p><em>Choose the correct letter, <span>A, B </span>or <span>C.</span></em></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'Answer choices',15,0,3,NULL,0,1505),
(N'4a102ec0-7c45-5e81-b1c9-fc8acb14ff99',N'7f9e2741-962d-5e46-bbe8-e617000ef25e',0,3,19,N'<p>group fitness class</p>',N'<p>Answer: Jean phủ định hoàn toàn → đáp án C.
Key vocab: ever going = không bao giờ định đi.
</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,5,NULL,0,1505),
(N'61d4379b-bf0d-5278-aec9-bfec81385f55',N'7f9e2741-962d-5e46-bbe8-e617000ef25e',0,3,19,N'<p>general weight training</p>',N'<p>Answer: Jean nói “I like the sound of that” = hứng thú ngay bây giờ → B.
Key vocab: like the sound of = thích ngay, quan tâm.
</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,6,NULL,0,1505),
(N'5b72edd1-c978-5e41-845b-f74a9566926e',N'7f9e2741-962d-5e46-bbe8-e617000ef25e',0,3,19,N'<p>group fitness in the pool</p>',N'<p>Answer: Jean nói “doesn’t appeal” → hoàn toàn không hứng thú. → C.
Key vocab: doesn’t appeal = không hứng thú.
</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,7,NULL,0,1505),
(N'688607e7-f885-53d7-a997-c85f1bf24d8f',N'7f9e2741-962d-5e46-bbe8-e617000ef25e',0,3,19,N'<p>swimming</p>',N'<p>Answer: Jean nói chỉ trong tương lai khi khỏe hơn → A. Key vocab: in a few months = trong tương lai gần.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,8,NULL,0,1505),
(N'36024b25-2a70-570d-8738-f989d058336a',N'7f9e2741-962d-5e46-bbe8-e617000ef25e',0,3,19,N'<p>sauna</p>',N'<p>Answer: Jean từ chối rõ ràng → không quan tâm. → C.
Key vocab: too hot for me = không thích.
</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,9,NULL,0,1505),
(N'16a2ed5d-d34a-537f-9c6d-c2edd67e65c6',N'7f9e2741-962d-5e46-bbe8-e617000ef25e',0,3,19,N'<p>child minding</p>',N'<p>Answer: Jean nói sẽ dùng sau này khi chồng đi làm lại → A. Key vocab: probably be using = có khả năng dùng trong tương lai.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,10,NULL,0,1505),
(N'a6c5de85-7568-57c2-90b4-9cd7d294b3fe',N'ff75774c-f2e7-5ded-8750-1543ceb27448',0,1,14,(CAST(N'<h2>[VOL 4] Test 6 - Section 2</h2><p>Welcome to the Global Museum, located at the heart of this truly multicultural city, which is home to more than 60 different nationalities. The museum has a number of exciting displays and exhibitions, and this audio guide is designed to help you make the most of your visit. Altogether, the museum has 18 different galleries, and this season sees the opening of three new exhibitions. We recommend that you begin your tour by visiting this season''s highlights. The Heritage Clothes exhibition is located in Gallery 5 of the museum. People who live in the area have spent two years preparing this exhibition, which brings together some of the fascinating garments traditionally worn in their own communities. They research the history of their community''s clothing traditions and the customs and rituals associated with them.

Altogether, 16 countries are represented, from Ghana to Korea, from Turkey to Nepal. The photographs that accompany each display case were taken by some of the city college students who are studying design and show the clothes being. modelled by the real people who wear them in the course of their everyday lives. Another highlight this season is the exhibition called Toys from the Past, which can be found in Gallery 9. The exhibition, which will appeal to people of all ages, is on tour throughout the country and will be here for 10 weeks only. The exhibits include dolls made over 100 years ago with beautiful porcelain faces and, in some cases, real hair. The collection covers the favourite toys, such as wooden train sets from many different generations, and provides plenty of interest for children and adults: the gigantic board games which are laid out on the gallery floor.

Flooring is one of the most popular activities in the exhibition and should not be neast. This exhibition concludes with a special display of miniature toys. These small objects are on loan from countries all over the world and in some cases measure no more than a few centimetres. There''s a tiny car made from matchsticks, a toy aeroplane complete with pilot and passengers made out of seashells, and some exquisite little buildings no higher than four centimetres.

The Final gallery highlight of the season is. the Biscuit Gallery number 15. Many years ago, this city was famous for its biscuits; although today the factory no longer exists. Did you know, for example, that before, biscuits were packed in paper or cardboard boxes, biscuit tins' AS nvarchar(max))+N' were fashion items. The factory made tins – round, square, triangular, hexagonal – for a whole range of different occasions to celebrate national events, festivals, famous faces, and so on. One fascinating display deals with people''s favourite biscuits. There are sweet biscuits and savoury ones, biscuits filled with jam and biscuits filled with currants, biscuits with pink, yellow, and white sugar icing. or coloured sugar flowers. When the factory finally closed, it announced that people''s favourite biscuit was not, as you might expect, a chocolate biscuit or one filled with jam and cream, but a plain savoury one which was eaten with cheese.

When you get to the end of the exhibition, there''s an entertaining hands-on activity – to fill your own biscuit tin. All the biscuits ever produced by the company are piled up on a table along with various tins. The biscuits are made out of thin pieces of wood, but the weight, colours, and shapes replicate the original biscuits. Your job is to fill a tin with biscuits so that when the lid is taken. Off, they sit there as neatly as they did when the job was done by machine. It''s not as easy as it looks. If you would like to buy a memento of your visit, there is a museum gift shop selling postcards, souvenirs, and handmade pottery next to the information desk on the ground floor. And finally, if you don''t want to carry your coats and bags around with you during your visit, please make use of the free lockers provided by the museum! Enjoy your visit.</p>'),(CAST(N'<p>Welcome to the Global Museum, located at the heart of this truly multicultural city, which is home to more than 60 different nationalities. The museum has a number of exciting displays and exhibitions, and this audio guide is designed to help you make the most of your visit. Altogether, the museum has 18 different galleries, and this season sees the opening of three new exhibitions. We recommend that you begin your tour by visiting this season''s highlights. The Heritage Clothes exhibition is located in Gallery 5 of the museum. People who live in the area have spent two years preparing this exhibition, which brings together some of the fascinating garments traditionally worn in their own communities. They research the history of their community''s clothing traditions and the customs and rituals associated with them.

Altogether, 16 countries are represented, from Ghana to Korea, from Turkey to Nepal. The photographs that accompany each display case were taken by some of the city college students who are studying design and show the clothes being. modelled by the real people who wear them in the course of their everyday lives. Another highlight this season is the exhibition called Toys from the Past, which can be found in Gallery 9. The exhibition, which will appeal to people of all ages, is on tour throughout the country and will be here for 10 weeks only. The exhibits include dolls made over 100 years ago with beautiful porcelain faces and, in some cases, real hair. The collection covers the favourite toys, such as wooden train sets from many different generations, and provides plenty of interest for children and adults: the gigantic board games which are laid out on the gallery floor.

Flooring is one of the most popular activities in the exhibition and should not be neast. This exhibition concludes with a special display of miniature toys. These small objects are on loan from countries all over the world and in some cases measure no more than a few centimetres. There''s a tiny car made from matchsticks, a toy aeroplane complete with pilot and passengers made out of seashells, and some exquisite little buildings no higher than four centimetres.

The Final gallery highlight of the season is. the Biscuit Gallery number 15. Many years ago, this city was famous for its biscuits; although today the factory no longer exists. Did you know, for example, that before, biscuits were packed in paper or cardboard boxes, biscuit tins were fashion items. The factory ma' AS nvarchar(max))+N'de tins – round, square, triangular, hexagonal – for a whole range of different occasions to celebrate national events, festivals, famous faces, and so on. One fascinating display deals with people''s favourite biscuits. There are sweet biscuits and savoury ones, biscuits filled with jam and biscuits filled with currants, biscuits with pink, yellow, and white sugar icing. or coloured sugar flowers. When the factory finally closed, it announced that people''s favourite biscuit was not, as you might expect, a chocolate biscuit or one filled with jam and cream, but a plain savoury one which was eaten with cheese.

When you get to the end of the exhibition, there''s an entertaining hands-on activity – to fill your own biscuit tin. All the biscuits ever produced by the company are piled up on a table along with various tins. The biscuits are made out of thin pieces of wood, but the weight, colours, and shapes replicate the original biscuits. Your job is to fill a tin with biscuits so that when the lid is taken. Off, they sit there as neatly as they did when the job was done by machine. It''s not as easy as it looks. If you would like to buy a memento of your visit, there is a museum gift shop selling postcards, souvenirs, and handmade pottery next to the information desk on the ground floor. And finally, if you don''t want to carry your coats and bags around with you during your visit, please make use of the free lockers provided by the museum! Enjoy your visit.</p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-4/iL.VOL4.6.S1505.PART2.mp3',NULL,1,0,2,NULL,0,1505),
(N'c0f1606a-3190-5717-a3a1-e972b3cc1182',N'a6c5de85-7568-57c2-90b4-9cd7d294b3fe',0,2,18,N'<p><em>Choose the correct letter,<span> A, B </span>or <span>C.</span></em></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',1,0,1,NULL,0,1505),
(N'd63d6261-2cc7-5364-97da-cff0048fcff4',N'c0f1606a-3190-5717-a3a1-e972b3cc1182',0,3,19,N'<p>The Heritage Clothes exhibition was put together by</p>',N'<p>- Câu hỏi: “The Heritage Clothes exhibition was put together by …” - Đúng: local residents, vì chính cư dân địa phương chuẩn bị.
- Sai A (museum staff): chỉ cung cấp không gian, không chuẩn bị.
- Sai C (clothing manufacturers): không được nhắc.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,11,NULL,0,1505),
(N'dc4a2a33-abf5-5c8c-8c53-b2e3acfd9330',N'c0f1606a-3190-5717-a3a1-e972b3cc1182',0,3,19,N'<p>The photographs show the clothes worn by</p>',N'<p>- Câu hỏi: “The photographs show the clothes worn by …” - Đúng: their owners (người thật mặc hằng ngày).
- Sai B (professional models): không đề cập.
- Sai C (design students): họ chỉ chụp ảnh, không mặc</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,12,NULL,0,1505),
(N'4306b5bb-e4ee-5e48-ac07-c8c32b713a46',N'c0f1606a-3190-5717-a3a1-e972b3cc1182',0,3,19,N'<p>The exhibition called Toys from the Past is</p>',N'<p>- Câu hỏi: “The exhibition called Toys from the Past is …” - Đúng: on show for a limited time (10 tuần). - Sai A (displayed in a new gallery): không nhắc “new gallery”. - Sai C (aimed specially at children): nói “appeal to people of all ages”.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,13,NULL,0,1505),
(N'17b0103c-4905-505b-94c3-a8dc90e200d3',N'c0f1606a-3190-5717-a3a1-e972b3cc1182',0,3,19,N'<p>Visitors to Toys from the Past are recommended to</p>',N'<p>- Câu hỏi: “Visitors… are recommended to …” - Đúng: see the board games, vì được khuyên không nên bỏ lỡ. - Sai A (play with toy trains): chỉ trưng bày, không cho chơi. - Sai B (look at all the dolls): có búp bê nhưng không khuyến nghị đặc biệt.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,14,NULL,0,1505),
(N'1a2ced41-e485-530e-b541-af8a8fa61eaf',N'c0f1606a-3190-5717-a3a1-e972b3cc1182',0,3,19,N'<p>The miniature toys have been</p>',N'<p>- Câu hỏi: “The miniature toys have been …” - Đúng: borrowed by the museum. - Sai A (made by the museum): không nhắc. - Sai B (bought by the museum): không nhắc.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,15,NULL,0,1505),
(N'37d69f90-1d6d-576e-b14a-2e370b880e86',N'c0f1606a-3190-5717-a3a1-e972b3cc1182',0,3,19,N'<p>The biscuit factory made tins</p>',N'<p>- Câu hỏi: “The biscuit factory made tins …” - Đúng: of different shapes. - Sai A (for people all over the world): là đối tượng, không phải mô tả “made tins”. - Sai C (for many famous people): không nhắc.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,16,NULL,0,1505),
(N'41c175e8-8411-558d-8e68-53f4e79ba7ff',N'c0f1606a-3190-5717-a3a1-e972b3cc1182',0,3,19,N'<p>People’s favourite biscuit used to be</p>',N'<p>- Câu hỏi: “People’s favourite biscuit used to be …” - Đúng: one filled with cream. - Sai C và B: Không như mọi người nghĩ, thứ được yêu thích nhất là bánh nhạt ăn cùng phô mai.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,17,NULL,0,1505),
(N'708ead2d-6589-5495-833f-a9373d90746b',N'c0f1606a-3190-5717-a3a1-e972b3cc1182',0,3,19,N'<p>The hands-on activity allows people to</p>',N'<p>- Câu hỏi: “The hands-on activity allows people to …” - Đúng: C pack a biscuit tin. - Sai A (make some biscuits): không đề cập. - B taste some of the biscuits: không có.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,18,NULL,0,1505),
(N'81f1b187-8432-5abc-a87c-0633a721b549',N'a6c5de85-7568-57c2-90b4-9cd7d294b3fe',0,2,18,N'<p><em>Write <span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span> for each answer.</em></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',11,0,2,NULL,0,1505),
(N'b71e3962-7ce9-5a7e-b829-94681c1188d0',N'81f1b187-8432-5abc-a87c-0633a721b549',0,3,19,N'<p>The gift shop is located beside the }{SPACE}{ on the ground floor</p><p>Free }{SPACE}{ are available for visitors’ belongings.</p>',N'<p>Câu hỏi: “Cửa hàng quà tặng nằm bên cạnh cái gì?” → Cần danh từ địa điểm.
Đáp án: Người nói chỉ rõ là information desk. Key vocab: beside = next to.
</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,19,NULL,0,1505),
(N'865d6968-9891-5e0b-8af0-7f5c216c0778',N'81f1b187-8432-5abc-a87c-0633a721b549',0,3,19,N'Question number 20',N'<p>Câu hỏi: “Những gì miễn phí được cung cấp để cất đồ cho khách tham quan?” → Cần danh từ chỉ đồ vật.
Đáp án: Người nói nhấn mạnh là free lockers. Key vocab: provided = available.
</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,20,NULL,0,1505),
(N'ee1ce174-321d-5eda-a3b5-33e8f531f95e',N'ff75774c-f2e7-5ded-8750-1543ceb27448',0,1,15,(CAST(N'<h2>[VOL 4] Seminar Outline</h2><p>Hi Sue, sorry I''m late. That''s okay, but we really do need to get started on planning this seminar presentation. We''ve only got a week before we present it to the rest of the class. Are you still happy with the original topic? You mean aircraft engine design? Yes, it''s fine with me. I''m afraid I haven''t had a chance to finish the reading yet, but I have been thinking about the structure of the presentation, and I thought we could begin by looking at the problems associated with current aircraft engines. Sounds reasonable. We could get the other students to suggest the problems. What do you think? It might be better to ask questions; otherwise, they may not suggest all the relevant ones. You''re right.

Then there has to be some direct input from us. But we should keep the lecture part brief and then do something different to stop people falling asleep. What? Oh, maybe an activity they have to do in threes or fours toward the end of the seminar. Yes, they could discuss the alternatives. Or, even better, why not get the groups to actually draw the engine designs? Great idea. Discussions can be a bit boring. What else do we need to do? Well, we also have to think about what we need to help us to get the main ideas across. What do you mean? Well, will we have all of the information on slides?

So, we''d better start jotting down the order we''re going to present the information in. Got any paper? Yes, hang on. Now let''s think. Well, first we need to establish what''s wrong with the way things are at the moment with regard to aircraft engine design. And we should bring the focus specifically onto the environment. issues Yes, because that''s really the whole purpose of looking at the new designs. So after that, why don''t we talk about the future situation? We need to stress that even when petrol production begins to slow down in a few years, it won''t be the end of our problem because there are alternatives like tar sands and what''s the other stuff? Oil shale. Right, oil shale.

And we really don''t ever need to worry about either of those in terms of supply there are huge amounts available. Using them would mean that we could just go on using the same engines as we are now and producing just as much pollution. Exactly, so CO2 levels won''t change. Right. So then we need to put forward the safer alternative energy sources. And these need to be related to the two designs we''re going to present later on. Yes, so there''s the idea of using' AS nvarchar(max))+N' batteries instead of fuel-based engines. Yes, and then there''s hydrogen fuels. Right. What else do we need to add? The next thing is probably to look at the problems we think will be identified with those alternatives. Yes, people are always worried about changing to totally new forms of energy.

Well, I suppose that the first protest will be how expensive they are. That''s number one. We don''t need to spend too much time on that because it''s not too hard to. What other problems are there? I guess I''d have to say the next difficulty would be how to generate and store the power from those sources. Sure. No one''s really come up with a way to do that effectively or cheaply yet. And of course, finally, our topic: engine design. Because current engines are only designed to run on petroleum-based fuels. Perfect.</p>'),(CAST(N'<p>Hi Sue, sorry I''m late. That''s okay, but we really do need to get started on planning this seminar presentation. We''ve only got a week before we present it to the rest of the class. Are you still happy with the original topic? You mean aircraft engine design? Yes, it''s fine with me. I''m afraid I haven''t had a chance to finish the reading yet, but I have been thinking about the structure of the presentation, and I thought we could begin by looking at the problems associated with current aircraft engines. Sounds reasonable. We could get the other students to suggest the problems. What do you think? It might be better to ask questions; otherwise, they may not suggest all the relevant ones. You''re right.

Then there has to be some direct input from us. But we should keep the lecture part brief and then do something different to stop people falling asleep. What? Oh, maybe an activity they have to do in threes or fours toward the end of the seminar. Yes, they could discuss the alternatives. Or, even better, why not get the groups to actually draw the engine designs? Great idea. Discussions can be a bit boring. What else do we need to do? Well, we also have to think about what we need to help us to get the main ideas across. What do you mean? Well, will we have all of the information on slides?

So, we''d better start jotting down the order we''re going to present the information in. Got any paper? Yes, hang on. Now let''s think. Well, first we need to establish what''s wrong with the way things are at the moment with regard to aircraft engine design. And we should bring the focus specifically onto the environment. issues Yes, because that''s really the whole purpose of looking at the new designs. So after that, why don''t we talk about the future situation? We need to stress that even when petrol production begins to slow down in a few years, it won''t be the end of our problem because there are alternatives like tar sands and what''s the other stuff? Oil shale. Right, oil shale.

And we really don''t ever need to worry about either of those in terms of supply there are huge amounts available. Using them would mean that we could just go on using the same engines as we are now and producing just as much pollution. Exactly, so CO2 levels won''t change. Right. So then we need to put forward the safer alternative energy sources. And these need to be related to the two designs we''re going to present later on. Yes, so there''s the idea of using batteries instead of fuel-based' AS nvarchar(max))+N' engines. Yes, and then there''s hydrogen fuels. Right. What else do we need to add? The next thing is probably to look at the problems we think will be identified with those alternatives. Yes, people are always worried about changing to totally new forms of energy.

Well, I suppose that the first protest will be how expensive they are. That''s number one. We don''t need to spend too much time on that because it''s not too hard to. What other problems are there? I guess I''d have to say the next difficulty would be how to generate and store the power from those sources. Sure. No one''s really come up with a way to do that effectively or cheaply yet. And of course, finally, our topic: engine design. Because current engines are only designed to run on petroleum-based fuels. Perfect.</p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-4/iL.VOL4.6.S1505.PART3.mp3',NULL,1,0,3,NULL,0,1505),
(N'121dcd10-17b7-53c7-a338-f62c4bb2b2a9',N'ee1ce174-321d-5eda-a3b5-33e8f531f95e',0,2,18,N'<p><em>Choose <span>THREE</span> letters, <span>A-G.</span></em></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',5,0,1,NULL,0,1505),
(N'3739d234-b238-53a5-99b2-a04fa06c020b',N'121dcd10-17b7-53c7-a338-f62c4bb2b2a9',0,3,19,N'<p><em>Which <span>THREE</span> things do the students decide to include in their seminar presentation?</em></p>',N'<p>Question: “Which three things do the students decide to include in their seminar presentation?” → Yêu cầu chọn các hoạt động cụ thể. Answer: Họ quyết định đặt câu hỏi cho sinh viên để khởi động thảo luận. Key vocab: suggest = gợi ý; ask questions = đặt câu hỏi.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,21,NULL,0,1505),
(N'bc8df59a-cceb-5614-a40f-229de5bec6bb',N'121dcd10-17b7-53c7-a338-f62c4bb2b2a9',0,3,19,N'<p><em>Which <span>THREE</span> things do the students decide to include in their seminar presentation?</em></p>',N'<p>Question: “Which activities are được chọn để đưa vào seminar?” Answer: Họ chọn nhiệm vụ nhóm nhỏ (3-4 người) để vẽ thiết kế động cơ theo nhóm. Key vocab: in threes or fours = nhóm nhỏ; draw designs = nhiệm vụ.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,22,NULL,0,1505),
(N'2b0abdf7-b785-588c-9ea2-a2845e156d01',N'121dcd10-17b7-53c7-a338-f62c4bb2b2a9',0,3,19,N'<p><em>Which <span>THREE</span> things do the students decide to include in their seminar presentation?</em></p>',N'<p>Question: “Các hoạt động nào được đưa vào seminar?” Answer: Họ đồng ý sẽ dùng slide presentation để hỗ trợ trình bày. Key vocab: slides = bài trình chiếu; information = nội dung.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,23,NULL,0,1505),
(N'7a40c79f-1aea-5fb1-97b4-6377626b4820',N'ee1ce174-321d-5eda-a3b5-33e8f531f95e',0,2,18,N'<p><em>Write <span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span> for each answer.</em></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',11,0,2,NULL,0,1505),
(N'8523766e-9c72-554b-920d-53658d303472',N'7a40c79f-1aea-5fb1-97b4-6377626b4820',0,3,19,N'<p><span>Seminar Outline</span></p><p>Establish problems</p><p>Concentrate on the }{SPACE}{ problems</p><p><span>Future situation</span></p><ul><li><p>Production of</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ will decline.</p><ul><li><p>Tar sands and oil shale-no</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ problems, but produce pollution.</p><p><span>Alternative energy sources</span></p><ul><li><p></p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p><ul><li><p>Hydrogen</p></li></ul><p><span>Objections</span></p><ul><li><p>too</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p><ul><li><p>difficult to generate power and to</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ it.</p><ul><li><p>not suited to the design of present-day</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p>',N'<p>Câu hỏi: “Concentrate on the 24 … problems.” → Đáp án: environmental, vì họ nhấn mạnh tập trung vào vấn đề môi trường.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,24,NULL,0,1505),
(N'96cf4fc8-fa73-5eaf-ada7-2c8fea47e15c',N'7a40c79f-1aea-5fb1-97b4-6377626b4820',0,3,19,N'Question number 25',N'<p>Câu hỏi: “Production of 25 … will decline.” → Đáp án: petrol, vì script nói “petrol production will slow down.”</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,25,NULL,0,1505),
(N'5beaac75-c57d-581b-98af-32c70e965d09',N'7a40c79f-1aea-5fb1-97b4-6377626b4820',0,3,19,N'Question number 26',N'<p>Câu hỏi: “Tar sands and oil shale—no 26 … problems.” → Đáp án: supply, vì nhấn mạnh có “huge amounts available,” tức không lo thiếu nguồn cung.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,26,NULL,0,1505),
(N'24138fad-2a25-5815-bf66-daa4ecf53762',N'7a40c79f-1aea-5fb1-97b4-6377626b4820',0,3,19,N'Question number 27',N'<p>Câu hỏi: “Alternative energy sources …” → Đáp án: batteries, vì nhắc đến batteries + hydrogen.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,27,NULL,0,1505),
