(N'0746a23a-eba3-569b-9cf8-e2282de8b997',N'a044fdfd-aa60-5da5-af89-67a7c12122c7',0,3,19,N'<h3>International Student Travel Agency Enquiry Form</h3><table border="1"><tbody><tr><td><p>Name: Sarah Brown</p> <p>Date of birth: }{SPACE}{ </p> <p>Address: 21 Waverley Road, Radstone, RD4 6WV</p> <p>Contact tel. no: }{SPACE}{ </p> <p>Notes:</p> <p>• wants to travel in }{SPACE}{ Europe</p> <p>• hopes to travel by }{SPACE}{ </p> <p>• interested in working in a }{SPACE}{ </p> <p>• recommended to consider an alternative e.g. }{SPACE}{ work</p> <p>• advised to buy a European }{SPACE}{ for travelling</p> <p>• given a }{SPACE}{ with accommodation details</p> <p>• agreed to take out }{SPACE}{ from the Agency</p> <p>• told to use an }{SPACE}{ for contacting people</p></td></tr></tbody></table>',N'<p>Question: “Ngày sinh của Sarah Brown?”<br>→ Cần ngày/tháng/năm.</p><p>Script (dịch): “Ngày sinh của bạn là? 30/3.</p><p>Answer: Đáp án chính xác là 30. </p><p>Key vocab: date of birth = ngày sinh.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,1,NULL,0,1504),
(N'ceabcf73-1820-56f3-867f-eb480f7d92c6',N'a044fdfd-aa60-5da5-af89-67a7c12122c7',0,3,19,N'Question number 2',N'<p>Question: “Số điện thoại liên lạc?” </p><p>Answer: 0903 775 115. </p><p>Key vocab: contact number = số liên lạc; mobile = di động.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,2,NULL,0,1504),
(N'7c590b93-113e-59be-9996-2d6f342341e3',N'a044fdfd-aa60-5da5-af89-67a7c12122c7',0,3,19,N'Question number 3',N'<p>Question: “Cô ấy muốn đi tới ... Europe.” Script (dịch): “Tôi muốn đi tới Bắc Âu nhưng chưa từng đi trước đây. Tôi biết Nam Âu khá rõ...” </p><p>Answer: Đáp án là Northern- Bắc Âu Key </p><p>vocab: Northern Europe = Bắc Âu; Southern Europe = Nam Âu.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,3,NULL,0,1504),
(N'f48b4d73-37ad-5a6a-9449-52a772ab9470',N'a044fdfd-aa60-5da5-af89-67a7c12122c7',0,3,19,N'Question number 4',N'<p>Question: “Cô ấy hy vọng được đi bằng phương tiện gì?” → Cần danh từ chỉ phương tiện.  </p><p>Script (dịch): “Gia đình tôi luôn đi máy bay, nhưng giờ tôi muốn đi bằng tàu hỏa để có thể dừng lại bất cứ lúc nào (kiểu đi ngắm cảnh/du lịch).”</p><p>Answer: train. </p><p>Key vocab: go by plane = đi bằng máy bay; go by train = đi bằng  tàu.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,4,NULL,0,1504),
(N'f7d4ac54-a876-5989-a53c-6715ebbf3984',N'a044fdfd-aa60-5da5-af89-67a7c12122c7',0,3,19,N'Question number 5',N'<p>Question: “Sarah quan tâm làm việc ở lĩnh vực nào?” → Cần danh từ.</p><p>Script (dịch): “Bạn định làm việc gì? Tôi nghĩ tới công việc khách sạn vì có thể có  chỗ ở.”  </p><p>Answer: hotel. </p><p>Key vocab: hotel work = công việc khách sạn; accommodation =  chỗ ở.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,5,NULL,0,1504),
(N'ed99f950-3ff8-5070-90c6-1e4bf79cd478',N'a044fdfd-aa60-5da5-af89-67a7c12122c7',0,3,19,N'Question number 6',N'<p>Question: “Được khuyên xem xét công việc khác ngoài khách sạn, ví dụ ...” → Cần danh từ.  </p><p>Script (dịch): “Có lẽ bạn nên nghĩ tới lựa chọn khác. Ví dụ? Nhiều sinh viên thích làm việc ở nông trại.”-farm </p><p>Answer: farm. </p><p>Key vocab: alternative = lựa chọn khác; farm = nông trại.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,6,NULL,0,1504),
(N'802e4aeb-e568-5380-9c6c-72a2a97a43e3',N'a044fdfd-aa60-5da5-af89-67a7c12122c7',0,3,19,N'Question number 7',N'<p>Question: “Được khuyên mua ... để đi lại.” → Cần danh từ. </p><p>Script (dịch): “Mua vé lẻ sẽ tốn kém, nên lựa chọn tốt nhất là có một thẻ châu Âu (European pass), cho phép đi tàu không giới hạn vào giờ thấp điểm (off-peak  time).”  </p><p>Answer: Đáp án là pass. </p><p>Key vocab: pass = thẻ đi lại; unlimited rail travel = đi tàu  không giới hạn.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,7,NULL,0,1504),
(N'd50b6509-cd1c-561d-b760-b21a0be5f41e',N'a044fdfd-aa60-5da5-af89-67a7c12122c7',0,3,19,N'Question number 8',N'<p>Question: “Được phát ... với thông tin chỗ ở.” → Cần danh từ. </p><p>Script (dịch): “Bạn có thông tin về nhà trọ sinh viên không? – Vâng, tôi sẽ đưa bạn một cuốn booklet-kiểu quyển sổ chứa thông tin về một địa điểm/ nơi chốn, dùng để hướng dẫn. Nhưng bạn phải tự đặt  phòng ở.” </p><p>Answer: booklet. </p><p>Key vocab: booklet = sổ nhỏ/tờ rơi; accommodation = chỗ ở.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,8,NULL,0,1504),
(N'938c76cc-aad9-5228-84dd-cc1dd6d04d5f',N'a044fdfd-aa60-5da5-af89-67a7c12122c7',0,3,19,N'Question number 9',N'<p>Question: “Đồng ý mua ... từ công ty.” → Cần danh từ. </p><p>Script (dịch): “Trước khi sắp xếp, bạn cần có bảo hiểm cho toàn bộ chuyến đi. Chúng tôi có thể sắp xếp lo cho bạn nếu muốn. Nó bao gồm bảo hiểm những vật sau: đồ quý giá, tiền, điện thoại,  tính mạng...” </p><p>Answer: insurance. </p><p>Key vocab: insurance = bảo hiểm; cover = bảo vệ.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,9,NULL,0,1504),
(N'698d25c5-5d6a-58ba-84e5-55989d38ee5f',N'a044fdfd-aa60-5da5-af89-67a7c12122c7',0,3,19,N'Question number 10',N'<p>Question: “Đồng ý mua ... từ công ty.” → Cần danh từ.</p><p>Script (dịch): “Trước khi sắp xếp, bạn cần có bảo hiểm cho toàn bộ chuyến đi. Chúng tôi có thể sắp xếp lo cho bạn nếu muốn. Nó bao gồm bảo hiểm những vật sau: đồ quý giá, tiền, điện thoại, tính mạng...”</p><p>Answer: insurance cafe</p><p>Key vocab: insurance = bảo hiểm; cover = bảo vệ.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,10,NULL,0,1504),
(N'4753880b-0300-5487-98d9-f8c1cb620cc2',N'03c3bf9b-8545-5de7-b42f-5ba532c9409d',0,1,14,(CAST(N'<h2>[VOL 4] Afternoon tea</h2><p>(11-14) The special guest today is Claire Benetal, the restaurant manager of the Emperor Hotel here in town. She is here to tell us about their famous afternoon teas in the restaurant. Welcome! Thanks, Peter. Tell us about what makes afternoon tea so special. Well, it''s been a time-honored tradition for over a century. At the Emperor Hotel, we''ve been serving tea to royalty, dignitaries, and movie stars in the grandest tradition. A lot Of people come to see the expensive fabrics, antique carpets, and beautiful handmade furniture we have here. Our waiters serve tea against the picturesque backdrop of the boats on the habour. We''re busy, so we strongly recommend making reservations. However, we rarely turn guests away. Tea is always an event here. 00:01:50 Of course, we serve the Emperor Tea Blend, which is created exclusively for the hotel by the Metropolitan Tea Company. This famous blend comes from more than six different places all over the world. That''s why the taste is so special. I also have some interesting facts about our tea tables during our dining room renovation. We kept the wood from the original floor and used it to make our tea tables. You can now say you were eating off the floor. They always have white tablecloths on them, which is, of course, normal in the better hotels. We''ll finish renovating next year by covering the chairs in a shade of red to match the walls. These days, we serve about half a million cups of tea every year. Our waiting staff have over 42 years of combined service with us. The Original cups and saucers were first used by the hotel back in 1939 for a visit by the king and queen of england. Today, the pattern is still made by the Midland China Company exclusively for us and is available for sale in the hotel''s store. and online. (15-20) Would You describe your afternoon tea parties for our listeners?. Sure, the hotel has several different kinds of tea parties. We have a special afternoon tea for children known as the playtime tea. Children can enjoy bubblegum tea and cookies inside a little children''s castle. We give them crowns and dress-up clothes to wear. This gives them the experience of being kings and queens. Our bridal tea can be customized for any upcoming marriage. It''s a traditional afternoon where women, friends, and family get together and shower. the bride with gifts. our photographer will be there to take many pictures of the best moments of the day to remind the bride and h' AS nvarchar(max))+N'er friends of something special that they can look back at. The summer tea is served out in the lovely hotel grounds. We spread a souvenir blanket for you under a tree. A basket is prepared for you. Inside it has four local Salt Spring Island cheeses with fresh honey that''s made from the cheft own beehives. Our Canadian tea is the most popular one with our international visitors. It includes strawberries and peaches grown in the neighborhood, which we serve with special sandwiches and jam made with raspberries from Our own backyard. the farmer''s tea is our most famous party. Guests love having a satisfying tea where our famous drink is served with a variety of meat and egg pies, hot from the oven, along with our homemade bread. And don''t forget the farm-style fruit pies for dessert. Finally, back by popular demand is our seniors'' tea. If you''re 60 or older, you can enjoy afternoon tea in our cozy library. While there, you can look at the photos of famous actors and musicians that have visited our hotel and read what they said about the hotel. our chef and restaurant staff serve handmade scones, delicious pastries, and sweets freshly baked in our restaurant daily. It''s wonderful.</p>'),(CAST(N'<p>(11-14) The special guest today is Claire Benetal, the restaurant manager of the Emperor Hotel here in town. She is here to tell us about their famous afternoon teas in the restaurant. Welcome! Thanks, Peter. Tell us about what makes afternoon tea so special. Well, it''s been a time-honored tradition for over a century. At the Emperor Hotel, we''ve been serving tea to royalty, dignitaries, and movie stars in the grandest tradition. A lot Of people come to see the expensive fabrics, antique carpets, and beautiful handmade furniture we have here. Our waiters serve tea against the picturesque backdrop of the boats on the habour. We''re busy, so we strongly recommend making reservations. However, we rarely turn guests away. Tea is always an event here. 00:01:50 Of course, we serve the Emperor Tea Blend, which is created exclusively for the hotel by the Metropolitan Tea Company. This famous blend comes from more than six different places all over the world. That''s why the taste is so special. I also have some interesting facts about our tea tables during our dining room renovation. We kept the wood from the original floor and used it to make our tea tables. You can now say you were eating off the floor. They always have white tablecloths on them, which is, of course, normal in the better hotels. We''ll finish renovating next year by covering the chairs in a shade of red to match the walls. These days, we serve about half a million cups of tea every year. Our waiting staff have over 42 years of combined service with us. The Original cups and saucers were first used by the hotel back in 1939 for a visit by the king and queen of england. Today, the pattern is still made by the Midland China Company exclusively for us and is available for sale in the hotel''s store. and online. (15-20) Would You describe your afternoon tea parties for our listeners?. Sure, the hotel has several different kinds of tea parties. We have a special afternoon tea for children known as the playtime tea. Children can enjoy bubblegum tea and cookies inside a little children''s castle. We give them crowns and dress-up clothes to wear. This gives them the experience of being kings and queens. Our bridal tea can be customized for any upcoming marriage. It''s a traditional afternoon where women, friends, and family get together and shower. the bride with gifts. our photographer will be there to take many pictures of the best moments of the day to remind the bride and her friends of something specia' AS nvarchar(max))+N'l that they can look back at. The summer tea is served out in the lovely hotel grounds. We spread a souvenir blanket for you under a tree. A basket is prepared for you. Inside it has four local Salt Spring Island cheeses with fresh honey that''s made from the cheft own beehives. Our Canadian tea is the most popular one with our international visitors. It includes strawberries and peaches grown in the neighborhood, which we serve with special sandwiches and jam made with raspberries from Our own backyard. the farmer''s tea is our most famous party. Guests love having a satisfying tea where our famous drink is served with a variety of meat and egg pies, hot from the oven, along with our homemade bread. And don''t forget the farm-style fruit pies for dessert. Finally, back by popular demand is our seniors'' tea. If you''re 60 or older, you can enjoy afternoon tea in our cozy library. While there, you can look at the photos of famous actors and musicians that have visited our hotel and read what they said about the hotel. our chef and restaurant staff serve handmade scones, delicious pastries, and sweets freshly baked in our restaurant daily. It''s wonderful.</p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-4/iL.VOL4.2.S1504.PART2.mp3',NULL,1,0,2,NULL,0,1504),
(N'557900f8-e79e-54ab-a3f0-eb34fdd4210c',N'4753880b-0300-5487-98d9-f8c1cb620cc2',0,2,18,N'<p>Choose the correct letter, <span>A</span>, <span>B</span> or <span>C</span>.</p>',N'',N'',N'',N'Afternoon tea',1,0,1,NULL,0,1504),
(N'e342b6de-15ce-5daa-b3c8-35970cc62bcf',N'557900f8-e79e-54ab-a3f0-eb34fdd4210c',0,3,19,N'<p>According to Claire, what makes the Emperor Hotel attractive to people?</p>',N'<p>Question: “Theo Claire, điều gì khiến khách thích ở khách sạn Emperor?”</p><p>Script (dịch): “Nhiều người đến để xem những tấm vải đắt tiền, thảm, đồ gỗ thủ công. Nhân viên của chúng tôi phục vụ trà trong khung cảnh bến cảng thơ mộng.”</p><p>Answer: Đây là mô tả sự sang trọng, xa<br>hoa của không gian → đáp án C. </p><p>Key vocab: expensive fabrics = vải đắt tiền;<br>surroundings = khung cảnh.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,11,NULL,0,1504),
(N'b2365586-0b5e-5712-9ab3-f1310714faed',N'557900f8-e79e-54ab-a3f0-eb34fdd4210c',0,3,19,N'<p>The Emperor blend of tea is</p>',N'<p>Question: “Trà Emperor Blend là gì?”</p><p>Script (dịch): “Chúng tôi phục vụ trà Emperor Blend, được tạo riêng cho khách sạn bởi Metropolitan Tea Company.” </p><p>Answer: Nhấn mạnh “exclusively for the hotel” → đáp án B. </p><p>Key vocab: created exclusively = làm riêng cho; blend = pha  trộn.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,12,NULL,0,1504),
(N'ccde0dca-3b48-53e3-b490-d0bb468f6d85',N'557900f8-e79e-54ab-a3f0-eb34fdd4210c',0,3,19,N'<p>Why are the tea tables special?</p>',N'<p>Question: “Tại sao bàn uống trà đặc biệt?”</p><p>Script (dịch): “Trong khi cải tạo, chúng tôi giữ gỗ từ sàn cũ và dùng để làm bàn.” </p><p>Answer: Rõ ràng là làm từ sàn tái sử dụng → đáp án C. </p><p>Key vocab: original floor = sàn gốc; used to make = dùng để làm.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,13,NULL,0,1504),
(N'c5b70238-a2d2-5539-a47c-1d0bf6bcffad',N'557900f8-e79e-54ab-a3f0-eb34fdd4210c',0,3,19,N'<p>The cups and saucers that are used at the hotel</p>',N'<p>Question: “Bộ tách đĩa ở khách sạn có đặc điểm gì?”  </p><p>Script (dịch): “Bộ tách đĩa gốc lần đầu dùng năm 1939... Ngày nay mẫu vẫn được sản xuất riêng cho khách sạn và bán trong cửa hàng cùng trực tuyến.” </p><p>Answer: Có thể mua bởi khách → đáp án B. </p><p>Key vocab: available for sale = có bán; cups and saucers = tách và đĩa.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,14,NULL,0,1504),
(N'b172e721-0c43-5b36-b5b9-3df150907498',N'4753880b-0300-5487-98d9-f8c1cb620cc2',0,2,18,N'<p>Choose six answers from the box and write the correct letter, <span>A–H</span>.</p>',N'',N'',N'',N'What is the highlight of each of the following tea parties?',15,0,2,NULL,0,1504),
(N'9ad157aa-7558-5932-9046-2efe8e0431f5',N'b172e721-0c43-5b36-b5b9-3df150907498',0,3,19,N'<p>Playtime Tea</p>',N'<p>Question: “Điểm đặc biệt của Playtime Tea là gì?”
Script (dịch): “Trà chiều đặc biệt cho trẻ em gọi là Playtime Tea. Trẻ em uống trà kẹo cao su, ăn bánh quy trong lâu đài nhỏ. Chúng tôi cho đội vương miện, mặc trang phục → cảm giác làm vua và hoàng hậu.”
Answer: Trải nghiệm cảm giác hoàng gia → C. Key vocab: crowns = vương miện; kings and queens = vua và hoàng hậu.
</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,15,NULL,0,1504),
(N'193c6dfc-3581-5385-8a17-8c5cb6bc2ed8',N'b172e721-0c43-5b36-b5b9-3df150907498',0,3,19,N'<p>Bridal Tea</p>',N'<p>Question: “Điểm đặc biệt của Bridal Tea?”
Script (dịch): “Bridal Tea có thể điều chỉnh cho lễ cưới. Nhiếp ảnh gia chụp nhiều khoảnh khắc đẹp nhất để cô dâu và bạn bè nhớ lại sau này.”
Answer: Chụp hình kỷ niệm → H. </p><p>Key vocab: photographer = nhiếp ảnh gia; pictures = ảnh
</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,16,NULL,0,1504),
(N'48751a43-97dc-586d-91b5-97d5207a8999',N'b172e721-0c43-5b36-b5b9-3df150907498',0,3,19,N'<p>Summer Tea</p>',N'<p>Question: “Điểm nổi bật của Summer Tea?”
Script (dịch): “Summer Tea được phục vụ ngoài khuôn viên khách sạn. Chúng tôi trải chăn dưới gốc cây và chuẩn bị giỏ đồ.”
Answer: Điểm nhấn là thưởng thức trong vườn → D. </p><p>Key vocab: hotel grounds = khuôn viên; under a tree = dưới cây.
</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,17,NULL,0,1504),
(N'7527f099-c3a8-507c-b62d-5fffb4149b1e',N'b172e721-0c43-5b36-b5b9-3df150907498',0,3,19,N'<p>Canadian Tea</p>',N'<p>Question: “Điểm đặc biệt của Canadian Tea?”
Script (dịch): “Canadian Tea phổ biến nhất… có dâu tây, đào trồng gần đó, mứt từ mâm xôi sau vườn.”
Answer: Thưởng thức trái cây địa phương → A. </p><p>Key vocab: strawberries, peaches, raspberries = dâu, đào, mâm xôi.
</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,18,NULL,0,1504),
(N'1d1d8ca3-4624-50cc-af2a-ba76ef3cb117',N'b172e721-0c43-5b36-b5b9-3df150907498',0,3,19,N'<p>Farmers’ Tea</p>',N'<p>Question: “Điểm nổi bật của Farmers’ Tea?”
Script (dịch): “Farmers’ Tea nổi tiếng nhất. Khách thích uống kèm bánh thịt, trứng nóng hổi, bánh mì tự làm, bánh trái cây nông trại.”
Answer: Thưởng thức đồ ăn nóng → B. </p><p>Key vocab: hot from the oven = nóng hổi; pies = bánh nướng.
</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,19,NULL,0,1504),
(N'2f442ce5-0895-50e7-91ef-18a6f706ad3d',N'b172e721-0c43-5b36-b5b9-3df150907498',0,3,19,N'<p>Seniors’ Tea</p>',N'<p>Question: “Điểm đặc biệt của Seniors’ Tea?”
Script (dịch): “Seniors’ Tea cho người trên 60. Trong thư viện, bạn có thể xem ảnh diễn viên, nhạc sĩ nổi tiếng từng ghé và đọc nhận xét của họ.”
Answer: Tìm hiểu về khách trước đây → F. </p><p>Key vocab: photos = ảnh; previous guests = khách trước đây.
</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,20,NULL,0,1504),
(N'abde80c0-efe7-50c3-bad7-e99a93865ba6',N'03c3bf9b-8545-5de7-b42f-5ba532c9409d',0,1,15,(CAST(N'<h2>[VOL 4] Report on Geography Field Trip</h2><p>(21-26) Hello Charlotte. Come in. I just wanted to go through the first draft of your report on the field trip to the coastal sand dunes. Thank you. I''d really like some feedback. I found it quite hard to do. Yes, but these reports are really important. You did a great presentation on the planning of the trip before you went, and we''ve already decided to include that in your portfolio. But Writing up the report''s equally important because if you can identify an area that''s caught your interest you may decide to choose that as your specialty for next term. OK, so what do you think of this first draft? Well, there''s one problem, but it''s something that can be easily remedied. Did you download the template for reports from the website? I didn''t know there was one. Look on the course site under Report Writing; the home page is a bit confusing, but once you''ve got that template, you''ll see what we''re expecting from a report. Other than that, I think you''ll easily meet the word count, as you collected lots of data. Now, first tell me, how did your group go about choosing the exact location? It''s important to explain that in the report We didn''t want to influence our results in any way, so instead of studying a map and choosing an area that looked as if it would provide useful data, we listed six possible locations, and then we just tossed a dice. We ended up with an area just south of the jetty, nice and easy to get to. And what did you personally see as your main aim during the field trip? Well, we were looking at coastal sand dunes and analysing whether there''s any marked change in vegetation type and coverage as you go inland. And although we''d been told that one of the main objectives was to use the fieldwork techniques we''d learnt about, I wanted to look. at soil structure. The others were focusing on things like the range of species and the density of the vegetation. Interesting! And in the group I was working in, there were people from another college. Can I include their data in my report? Well, what are the advantages of doing that? Well, we all looked at the same area of land, so they didn''t collect any different data. But by adding theirs, it gives me a bigger sample, and that must make the results more reliable. That''s how you can really test a hypothesis so I think. good point! So include it. Now let''s look at the introduction in a bit more detail. Your reasons for carrying out the study are fully de' AS nvarchar(max))+N'scribed as are the ways you collected your information. Then you go on to the measurements you took. Was that easy to do? Some of them took longer than others, for example getting the proportion of sand to vegetation. But I soon got used to the equipment and could get the elevation of the sand dunes quite quickly. It was funny to see some people trying to measure how high plants were as the plants waved about in the wind. I can imagine. </p><p>(27-30) OK now we''d like to have your feedback on the trip as we''re keen to make any necessary improvements for future trips. OK. so first, the equipment. Was it easy to use. It was, once you got used to it. It would have been good if we could have found out how to use it at college before we went, though. It''s not exactly simple to use. I''ve noted that down. Now, the data collection sheets you used, I wonder if they could be made more user-friendly by cutting down the number of columns on each page. Yes, I think the information would still be clearly organised. And what did you think of the reference materials? Well, we had problems identifying some vegetation. Was that because you didn''t get a full picture from the books you were using? Yes, I think so. And finally, how did you feel about working with people you didn''t know in your group? Well, you probably need to discuss this with everyone, but for me, it meant I learnt a lot from others too, so I think that''s a pattern you should stick to.</p>'),(CAST(N'<p>(21-26) Hello Charlotte. Come in. I just wanted to go through the first draft of your report on the field trip to the coastal sand dunes. Thank you. I''d really like some feedback. I found it quite hard to do. Yes, but these reports are really important. You did a great presentation on the planning of the trip before you went, and we''ve already decided to include that in your portfolio. But Writing up the report''s equally important because if you can identify an area that''s caught your interest you may decide to choose that as your specialty for next term. OK, so what do you think of this first draft? Well, there''s one problem, but it''s something that can be easily remedied. Did you download the template for reports from the website? I didn''t know there was one. Look on the course site under Report Writing; the home page is a bit confusing, but once you''ve got that template, you''ll see what we''re expecting from a report. Other than that, I think you''ll easily meet the word count, as you collected lots of data. Now, first tell me, how did your group go about choosing the exact location? It''s important to explain that in the report We didn''t want to influence our results in any way, so instead of studying a map and choosing an area that looked as if it would provide useful data, we listed six possible locations, and then we just tossed a dice. We ended up with an area just south of the jetty, nice and easy to get to. And what did you personally see as your main aim during the field trip? Well, we were looking at coastal sand dunes and analysing whether there''s any marked change in vegetation type and coverage as you go inland. And although we''d been told that one of the main objectives was to use the fieldwork techniques we''d learnt about, I wanted to look. at soil structure. The others were focusing on things like the range of species and the density of the vegetation. Interesting! And in the group I was working in, there were people from another college. Can I include their data in my report? Well, what are the advantages of doing that? Well, we all looked at the same area of land, so they didn''t collect any different data. But by adding theirs, it gives me a bigger sample, and that must make the results more reliable. That''s how you can really test a hypothesis so I think. good point! So include it. Now let''s look at the introduction in a bit more detail. Your reasons for carrying out the study are fully described as are the ways you collected your info' AS nvarchar(max))+N'rmation. Then you go on to the measurements you took. Was that easy to do? Some of them took longer than others, for example getting the proportion of sand to vegetation. But I soon got used to the equipment and could get the elevation of the sand dunes quite quickly. It was funny to see some people trying to measure how high plants were as the plants waved about in the wind. I can imagine. </p><p>(27-30) OK now we''d like to have your feedback on the trip as we''re keen to make any necessary improvements for future trips. OK. so first, the equipment. Was it easy to use. It was, once you got used to it. It would have been good if we could have found out how to use it at college before we went, though. It''s not exactly simple to use. I''ve noted that down. Now, the data collection sheets you used, I wonder if they could be made more user-friendly by cutting down the number of columns on each page. Yes, I think the information would still be clearly organised. And what did you think of the reference materials? Well, we had problems identifying some vegetation. Was that because you didn''t get a full picture from the books you were using? Yes, I think so. And finally, how did you feel about working with people you didn''t know in your group? Well, you probably need to discuss this with everyone, but for me, it meant I learnt a lot from others too, so I think that''s a pattern you should stick to.</p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-4/iL.VOL4.2.S1504.PART3.mp3',NULL,1,0,3,NULL,0,1504),
