(N'cb3153a9-c345-5847-9bba-4f6febe7c99a',N'f24f244d-5fb2-522a-aa5f-64c5876eb899',0,1,13,(CAST(N'<h2> [VOL 1] People Central New Potential Staff</h2><p>Sarah: Hi there. Welcome to People Central. I''m Sarah. How can I help you?</p><p>Mark: Hi Sarah, I''m Mark. I''m out of work right now and I''d like to find a job.</p><p>Sarah: I''m sure we can ind something for you. We have lots of companies searching for people in different industries. What job are you looking for?</p><p>Mark: I''m looking for a job in a countancy.</p><p>Sarah: Fine, I''m sure we can help you out with that. To begin with, I need to take some personal details for our files. You said your first name is Mark. What''s your surname? - Mark: It''s Castle. C-A-S-T-L-E.</p><p>Sarah: Thank you and I need your address.</p><p>Mark: 13 Wellington Street, South Brisbane, Queensland.</p><p>Sarah: And the postcode?</p><p>Mark: It''s 4101.</p><p>Sarah: Now I need your date of birth. - Mark: It''s 30th of May 1988.</p><p>Sarah: Thank you. Let me just write that down. What was the month again?</p><p>Mark: May, the 30th of May 1988.</p><p>Sarah: Got it. Do you have an email address we can have?</p><p>Mark: Let me think for a second which is best.</p><p>Sarah: Do you have more than one?</p><p>Mark: Yes, I''ve got three.</p><p>Sarah: Really? Okay.</p><p>Mark: I think I know. The address you can use is markc@AustraliaNow.com.</p><p>Sarah: Okay, just a minute. I have to write that all down. Did you say the provider is AustraliaNow.com?</p><p>Mark: That''s right.</p><p>Sarah: Good. Now what contact phone numbers do you want to give me?</p><p>Mark: My home number is 07-355-4-7671.</p><p>Sarah: Do you have a mobile phone number as well? That''s often the easiest way to get hold of people.</p><p>Mark: Of course, my mobile number is 046-9153-443.</p><p>Sarah: Thanks. Now let me look at the form. Yes. There''s just one more initial question left. And that is whether you have any preferred areas where you''d like to work.</p><p>Mark: I don''t really want to travel too far from home. So the area of Brisbane, of course. I suppose anywhere within a drive of about two hours.</p><p>Sarah: Now, do you have your professional certificates?</p><p>Mark: Yes, here you are. They''re all in this file.</p><p>Sarah: I''ll need to make some copies, but our copy is down. Do you mind if I keep them for a day?</p><p>Mark: I have scans on the list of questions. I''ll have them checked. I''ll do that in a second.</p><p>Sarah: Now we''ve got a selection of different companies looking for an accountant right now. Let''s have a look at this first one. It''s a' AS nvarchar(max))+N' big printing company down there called Gold Coast Printing. It''s about an hour away and you can drive there quite easily.</p><p>Mark: I know that company. I can also get a train there quite easily, which I prefer, as it takes away the stress of the drive. I hate driving too far and buses are always too slow for me.</p><p>Sarah: Well, that''s handy then. So Gold Coast Printing needs someone four times starting as soon as possible. The working hours are 9 to 5 Monday to Friday. For details about what exactly you''d be doing and the benefits package. You''ll need to talk with the company itself. We just get you together.</p><p>Mark: It''s certainly a possibility.</p><p>Sarah: I have another company here that needs a part-time accountant starting next month. They''re an import export company and they have a Brisbane City Centre location. Parking might be a problem but the bus or tram would get you there easily. - Mark: Yes, the trouble is no headache and it''d be fun to work in the City Centre. But I''m not sure about a part-time job. I''ll probably need to earn more than that can provide.</p><p>Sarah: Yes, that might be a problem. Let''s look at the next one then. It''s a fishing company called Baracuda down on the dock to the Brisbane River. There is more family foam and they need a full-time accountant to help them with their expansion.</p><p>Mark: That would be very interesting, but I usually prefer larger companies. When it''s a small company, there can often be problems with personal relationships.</p><p>Sarah: Well, that''s the three possibilities that we have right now. Though I know we might be getting some more next week.</p><p>Mark: Well, I was quite interested in Gold Coast printing. I can get in contact with them and then see what comes in next week.</p><p>Sarah: Okay, I''ll set up a meeting for you with them.</p><p>Mark: By the way, do I need to pay you anything for placing me?</p><p>Sarah: The company who we place you with will pay us, but you aren''t charged any commission at all. - Mark: Oh good, that''s great for me.</p>'),(CAST(N'<p>Sarah: Hi there. Welcome to People Central. I''m Sarah. How can I help you?</p><p>Mark: Hi Sarah, I''m Mark. I''m out of work right now and I''d like to find a job.</p><p>Sarah: I''m sure we can ind something for you. We have lots of companies searching for people in different industries. What job are you looking for?</p><p>Mark: I''m looking for a job in a countancy.</p><p>Sarah: Fine, I''m sure we can help you out with that. To begin with, I need to take some personal details for our files. You said your first name is Mark. What''s your surname? - Mark: It''s Castle. C-A-S-T-L-E.</p><p>Sarah: Thank you and I need your address.</p><p>Mark: 13 Wellington Street, South Brisbane, Queensland.</p><p>Sarah: And the postcode?</p><p>Mark: It''s 4101.</p><p>Sarah: Now I need your date of birth. - Mark: It''s 30th of May 1988.</p><p>Sarah: Thank you. Let me just write that down. What was the month again?</p><p>Mark: May, the 30th of May 1988.</p><p>Sarah: Got it. Do you have an email address we can have?</p><p>Mark: Let me think for a second which is best.</p><p>Sarah: Do you have more than one?</p><p>Mark: Yes, I''ve got three.</p><p>Sarah: Really? Okay.</p><p>Mark: I think I know. The address you can use is markc@AustraliaNow.com.</p><p>Sarah: Okay, just a mi