(N'd02c2068-cc9e-563a-b48e-a3313510bcc1',N'77494ca7-4e2f-5854-9d56-e102adf977bb',0,3,19,N'Question number 18',N'<p>- Đáp án là 2:30. - Suất diễn matinee vào thứ Bảy được xác định chính xác là lúc 2.30. - Key word: + matinee (n) suất diễn ban ngày + performance (n) buổi biểu diễn</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,18,NULL,0,1439),
(N'7e09d782-570b-5409-8cea-d9f476ef92dc',N'fd79c4ba-106c-5e94-bdfe-8b3a4f55f3a2',0,2,18,N'<p>Choose the correct letter,<span> A, B or C.</span></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',1,0,2,NULL,0,1439),
(N'1d552f95-37a2-5b50-b5b7-a8a8833fa092',N'7e09d782-570b-5409-8cea-d9f476ef92dc',0,3,19,N'<p>In the Spring Festival competition, you can win</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là C. 
- Giải thưởng là một chuyến bay khinh khí cầu miễn phí, không phải tiền mặt hay vé gia đình. 
- Các phương án khác sai vì không được nhắc là giải thưởng.
 - Key word: 
+ prize (n) giải thưởng 
+ hot air balloon (n) khinh khí cầu
</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,19,NULL,0,1439),
(N'3b0ed9e4-9d02-508d-9917-2aacd97c4755',N'7e09d782-570b-5409-8cea-d9f476ef92dc',0,3,19,N'<p>You can get anentry form for the competition from</p>',N'<p> Đáp án là B. 
- Phiếu dự thi được lấy từ báo Yorktown News, không phải radio hay website. 
- Các phương án khác chỉ được nhắc ở ngữ cảnh khác. 
- Key word: 
+ entry form (n) đơn dự thi 
+ newspaper (n) báo
</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,20,NULL,0,1439),
(N'4070dce3-9712-5a35-b9e3-63e69d0e88a6',N'1645e211-48f1-5e8f-9aa3-0ed66b5a481a',0,1,15,(CAST(N'<h2>SUVs (Sports Utility Vehicles)</h2><p>So guys, have you got all your notes on four-wheel-drive vehicles? Shall we go through what we''ve each found and think about how we''ll put it together for next week''s marketing seminar? Yeah, sure. Let''s start with what these cars were originally designed for. Oh, I''ve got something on that here. Well, four-wheel-drives or sports utility vehicles, as they are officially known SUVs for short, were originally designed for off-road use by people who need to get to remote areas out in the bush, for instance. But the interesting thing is that they''re actually sold now to a lot of people who just use them in cities, so they make quite different use of them. </p><p>Okay, then maybe we should make a list of their advantages, shall we? So one thing is that they''re good for commercial use, okay? How about also saying utilitarian rather than luxurious? So you''re not paying out for unnecessary luxuries? Okay, what else? Well, they have increased engine capacity and they''re also heavier, so suitable for towing large loads. So is this why so many people buy them then? Well, no, they seem to have become fashionable now for rather different reasons. Research carried out by automobile clubs shows that people buy them for business because of the sort of image they project, and mums like to drive their kids to school in them because they think they''re safe. So that''s another reason. And you can get about seven people into one of these, so we could say seating capacity is another factor. Okay, another thing that came out of my research is that people also like the higher seats. They say it means they can get a better view of the traffic ahead of them. Before you hear the rest of the discussion, you have some time to look at questions 26 to 30 on page 6. Now listen and answer questions 26 to 30. But, you know, some of these reasons just don''t work. I mean, the safety thing is just a misconception because generally in a collision they can do terrible damage to a smaller car. That''s right. That''s one of the disadvantages I have here. Shall we go through those now? Good idea. So let''s say that potentially they are harmful in built-up areas. Generally, the damage they cause is due to their weight. That''s right, isn''t it? Yes, it is. I''ve got a note here about their chassis. The bodywork on an SUV is stiffer and doesn''t crumple to absorb impact in a collision the way it does in smaller cars. </p><p>And there''s another reason why they''re not' AS nvarchar(max))+N' safe. It''s quite easy for them to roll over more so than an ordinary car because they''ve got a high center of gravity. So these are all the disadvantages. How are we going to round this up? Well, I think maybe we could round up with a few ideas of how we can limit the use of these SUVs. One thing that could be done is to limit them to people like farmers who can prove that they need them. That''s good, but it might be hard to enforce. Companies could also increase the insurance for SUVs since they cause more damage when there''s an accident. That''s a good idea, too. I''ll tell you what, guys. I''ll write up these notes onto an OHT so that everyone can see them when we talk through our notes in the seminar. But I think we need to put together a list of our sources, too. Can you do that?</p>'),(CAST(N'<p>So guys, have you got all your notes on four-wheel-drive vehicles? Shall we go through what we''ve each found and think about how we''ll put it together for next week''s marketing seminar? Yeah, sure. Let''s start with what these cars were originally designed for. Oh, I''ve got something on that here. Well, four-wheel-drives or sports utility vehicles, as they are officially known SUVs for short, were originally designed for off-road use by people who need to get to remote areas out in the bush, for instance. But the interesting thing is that they''re actually sold now to a lot of people who just use them in cities, so they make quite different use of them. </p><p>Okay, then maybe we should make a list of their advantages, shall we? So one thing is that they''re good for commercial use, okay? How about also saying utilitarian rather than luxurious? So you''re not paying out for unnecessary luxuries? Okay, what else? Well, they have increased engine capacity and they''re also heavier, so suitable for towing large loads. So is this why so many people buy them then? Well, no, they seem to have become fashionable now for rather different reasons. Research carried out by automobile clubs shows that people buy them for business because of the sort of image they project, and mums like to drive their kids to school in them because they think they''re safe. So that''s another reason. And you can get about seven people into one of these, so we could say seating capacity is another factor. Okay, another thing that came out of my research is that people also like the higher seats. They say it means they can get a better view of the traffic ahead of them. Before you hear the rest of the discussion, you have some time to look at questions 26 to 30 on page 6. Now listen and answer questions 26 to 30. But, you know, some of these reasons just don''t work. I mean, the safety thing is just a misconception because generally in a collision they can do terrible damage to a smaller car. That''s right. That''s one of the disadvantages I have here. Shall we go through those now? Good idea. So let''s say that potentially they are harmful in built-up areas. Generally, the damage they cause is due to their weight. That''s right, isn''t it? Yes, it is. I''ve got a note here about their chassis. The bodywork on an SUV is stiffer and doesn''t crumple to absorb impact in a collision the way it does in smaller cars. </p><p>And there''s another reason why they''re not safe. It''s quite easy for them to roll' AS nvarchar(max))+N' over more so than an ordinary car because they''ve got a high center of gravity. So these are all the disadvantages. How are we going to round this up? Well, I think maybe we could round up with a few ideas of how we can limit the use of these SUVs. One thing that could be done is to limit them to people like farmers who can prove that they need them. That''s good, but it might be hard to enforce. Companies could also increase the insurance for SUVs since they cause more damage when there''s an accident. That''s a good idea, too. I''ll tell you what, guys. I''ll write up these notes onto an OHT so that everyone can see them when we talk through our notes in the seminar. But I think we need to put together a list of our sources, too. Can you do that?</p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-1/iL.VOL1.3.S1439.PART3.mp3',NULL,1,0,3,NULL,0,1439),
(N'f22e7f0d-7b13-5bf1-ba96-015c8cf0c9bd',N'4070dce3-9712-5a35-b9e3-63e69d0e88a6',0,2,18,N'<p>Complete the notes below.
Write<span> NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS</span> for each answer.</p>',N'',N'',N'',N'SUVs (Sports Utility Vehicles)',11,0,1,NULL,0,1439),
(N'3f221138-a487-53cf-a728-ab5b54f48b76',N'f22e7f0d-7b13-5bf1-ba96-015c8cf0c9bd',0,3,19,N'<h3>SUVs (Sports Utility Vehicles)</h3><ul><li><p>Originally made for off-road driving (e.g. in remote areas)</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Now widely used in</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p><p><span>Advantages</span></p><ul><li><p>Useful for</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ purposes</p><ul><li><p>Larger</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ capacity</p><ul><li><p>Suitable for towing large loads</p></li></ul><p><span>Why popular in a wider market?</span></p><ul><li><p>Because of their image</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Seen as</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ by mothers</p><ul><li><p>Larger seating capacity</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Drivers prefer the</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p><p><span>Disadvantages</span></p><ul><li><p>SUVs can be</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ </p><p>in urban centers because of their }{SPACE}{ </p><ul><li><p>Bodywork doesn’t crumple in an accident</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Liable to</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ easily</p><p><span>How to limit use of SUVs</span></p><ul><li><p>Limit use to those people who need them (e.g.</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ )</p><ul><li><p>Raise cost of</p></li></ul> }{SPACE}{ paid by SUV drivers</p>',N'<p> Đáp án là cities. 
- Script nói rõ SUVs hiện nay được sử dụng chủ yếu trong các thành phố, trái với mục đích ban đầu là off-road. 
- Key word: 
+ cities (n) thành phố 
+ use (v) sử dụng
</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,21,NULL,0,1439),
(N'7a85b5aa-1f4c-5d8c-a05f-58f7218c3a07',N'f22e7f0d-7b13-5bf1-ba96-015c8cf0c9bd',0,3,19,N'Question number 22',N'<p>- Đáp án là commercial. 
- Lợi thế đầu tiên được nêu rõ là dùng cho mục đích thương mại. 
- Key word: 
+ commercial (adj) thương mại 
+ use (n) việc sử dụng
</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,22,NULL,0,1439),
(N'f6e76bde-823f-5c80-b331-bbbe930118c6',N'f22e7f0d-7b13-5bf1-ba96-015c8cf0c9bd',0,3,19,N'Question number 23',N'<p>- Đáp án là engine. 
- Cụm “engine capacity” xuất hiện nguyên văn, nên chỗ trống là engine. 
- Key word: 
+ engine (n) động cơ 
+ capacity (n) dung tích
</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,23,NULL,0,1439),
(N'62c3819b-3a7a-5624-8c64-8c317b37709a',N'f22e7f0d-7b13-5bf1-ba96-015c8cf0c9bd',0,3,19,N'Question number 24',N'<p>- Đáp án là safe. 
- Các bà mẹ coi SUVs là an toàn cho việc chở con đi học. 
- Key word: 
+ safe (adj) an toàn 
+ mums (n) các bà mẹ
</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,24,NULL,0,1439),
(N'e3febce8-4233-52a4-b9cc-e861e2068558',N'f22e7f0d-7b13-5bf1-ba96-015c8cf0c9bd',0,3,19,N'Question number 25',N'<p>- Đáp án là view. 
- Người lái thích ghế cao vì có tầm nhìn tốt hơn. 
- Key word: 
+ view (n) tầm nhìn 
+ traffic (n) giao thông
</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,25,NULL,0,1439),
(N'428373fa-d905-5225-9902-ac16751c3acc',N'f22e7f0d-7b13-5bf1-ba96-015c8cf0c9bd',0,3,19,N'Question number 26',N'<p> Đáp án là harmful. 
- SUVs được cho là gây hại trong khu vực đô thị đông đúc. 
- Key word: 
+ harmful (adj) gây hại 
+ built-up areas (n) khu đô thị
</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,26,NULL,0,1439),
(N'baa8bcf4-3d9f-5fa7-9d83-f1710abe877b',N'f22e7f0d-7b13-5bf1-ba96-015c8cf0c9bd',0,3,19,N'Question number 27',N'<p>- Đáp án là weight. 
- Nguyên nhân chính gây thiệt hại là do trọng lượng lớn của xe. 
- Key word: 
+ damage (n) thiệt hại 
+ weight (n) trọng lượng
</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,27,NULL,0,1439),
(N'826fd21c-1ad5-5293-b34f-590d07be8424',N'f22e7f0d-7b13-5bf1-ba96-015c8cf0c9bd',0,3,19,N'Question number 28',N'<p>- Đáp án là roll over. 
- SUVs dễ bị lật do trọng tâm cao. - Key word: 
+ roll over (v) lật xe 
