</p>',N'<p>+ Synonym: rapid=faster=nhanh chóng capuchins, spider monkeys=native monkey species=các loài khỉ bản địa</p><p>+ Interpretation: tỉ lệ… của khỉ howler nhanh hơn các loài khỉ bản địa -&gt; tìm danh từ chỉ khái niệm mà ở khỉ howler nhanh chóng hơn các loài khác</p><p>+ Answer: Dựa vào phần synonym và thông tin trong bài: khỉ howler có tỉ lệ sinh sản nhanh hơn các loài khỉ kia </p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là reproduction</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,18,NULL,0,1416),
(N'b2395eb7-7014-50f8-b842-a1e26f79b541',N'aaca6d0c-6671-5679-9472-a3cf10590bcb',0,3,19,N'Question number 19',N'<p>●      Synonym: do not depend on large areas on fruiting trees = can survive without eating fruit (ko cần phụ thuộc vào hoa quả vẫn sống đc)<br>●      Interpretation: khỉ howler có thể sống sót mà ko cần ăn… -&gt; tìm danh từ chỉ đồ ăn của khỉ </p><p>●      Answer: eat fruit when it is available = có hoa quả thì ăn do not depend on large areas: ko cần phụ thuộc (như trên phần synonym) -&gt; Đáp án là fruit  </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,19,NULL,0,1416),
(N'bba93675-6c99-54b8-a8b7-aa01f89a8146',N'aaca6d0c-6671-5679-9472-a3cf10590bcb',0,3,19,N'Question number 20',N'<p>+Synonym: tolerate (chịu đựng được) = thrive on leaves with high amounts of toxin = loaded with toxin</p><p>+Interpretation: khỉ howler có thể chịu đựng được lá với lượng…cao</p><p>+Answer: dựa vào synonym và thông tin trong bài -&gt; Đáp án là toxins</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,20,NULL,0,1416),
(N'88e538a1-a2c9-5100-93a3-ca69c8104ec7',N'aaca6d0c-6671-5679-9472-a3cf10590bcb',0,3,19,N'Question number 21',N'<p>+ Synonym: real advantage (lợi thế) in droughts = survive in droughts capuchin and spider monkeys = other</p><p>+ Interpretation: khỉ howler có thể sống sót vào thời kỳ … tốt hơn các loài khỉ khác -&gt;</p><p>+ Answer: dựa vào synonym và thông tin trong bài: - leaves howlers eat hold plenty of water = ăn lá có nhiều nước -&gt; survive away from open streams and water holes=ko cần suối/nguồn nước </p><p>- howlers: real advantage &gt;&lt; other monkeys: suffered during the long ongoing drought (chịu khổ trong thời kỳ hạn hán kéo dài) </p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là drought</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,21,NULL,0,1416),
(N'b2db1e1d-57a0-529a-94f4-1a60d48bda34',N'38ea1904-742e-5456-a5f4-4f56f762a303',0,2,18,N'<p>Look at the following statements (Questions 22-26) and the list of locations below. </p><p>Match each feature with the correct location, <span>A, B or C. </span></p><p>Write the correct letter, <span>A, B or C</span>, in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet. </p><p><span>NB</span> You may use any letter more than once. </p>',N'',N'',N'',N'List of Locations',10,0,3,NULL,0,1416),
(N'e79a3dbc-134e-51c0-b2a0-6e5cc2b805db',N'b2db1e1d-57a0-529a-94f4-1a60d48bda34',0,3,19,N'<p>It has seen the return of native tree species.</p>',N'<p>+ Synonym: native=indigenous</p><p>+ Interpretation: địa điểm này đã có nhiều loài cây bản địa trở lại </p><p>+ Answer: - large areas have been burnt=nhiều nơi bị đốt cháy </p><p>- absent for decades=biến mất trong nhiều thập kỷ &gt;&lt; began to invade the abandoned pastures=bắt đầu xâm chiếm những đồng cỏ bỏ hoang=những loài cây này đã quay trở lại (return) </p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là B</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,22,NULL,0,1416),
(N'402d7489-84c3-590c-bc65-4506d1e6c47e',N'b2db1e1d-57a0-529a-94f4-1a60d48bda34',0,3,19,N'<p>It supports only one species of native monkey.</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: địa điểm này chỉ có 1 loài khỉ sinh sống</p><p>+ Answer: - been home to a community of mantled howler monkeys=từ lâu đã là nơi khỉ howler sinh sống - other native primates were once common=trước kia từng sinh sống&gt;&lt;vanished (biến mất) </p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là A</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,23,NULL,0,1416),
(N'315a24b4-e137-5e5f-a87e-1597c5940a21',N'b2db1e1d-57a0-529a-94f4-1a60d48bda34',0,3,19,N'<p>Its monkey population helps the agriculture of the area.</p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms: benefits=helps (lợi ích)</p><p>+ Interpretation: địa điểm này là nơi mà loài khỉ howler đã giúp đỡ nhiều cho nông nghiệp</p><p>+ Answer: - howlers moved in -&gt; địa điểm này có khỉ howler - underappreciated benefits to such plantations -&gt; lợi ích cho nơi trồng trọt này </p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là C</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,24,NULL,0,1416),
(N'c22479d8-07fd-5250-aaf6-242b51df4619',N'b2db1e1d-57a0-529a-94f4-1a60d48bda34',0,3,19,N'<p>It is home to populations of all three local monkey species.</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: địa điểm này là nơi có cả 3 loài khỉ sinh sống</p><p>+ Answer: - Capuchins were the first -&gt; howlers -&gt; spider monkeys </p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là B</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,25,NULL,0,1416),
(N'b6406c28-19db-5b66-9720-b092ec3fe17f',N'b2db1e1d-57a0-529a-94f4-1a60d48bda34',0,3,19,N'<p>Its landscape was altered by the construction of a transport link.</p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms: Pan-American Highway = transport link</p><p>+ Interpretation: địa điểm này là nơi phong cảnh mà 1 tuyến đường vận chuyển làm cho thay đổi</p><p>+ Answer: vanished after the Pan-American Highway was built -&gt; biến mất sau khi đường sắt được xây dựng </p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là A</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,26,NULL,0,1416),
(N'd7b41115-daec-5659-ad48-ce89d6965128',N'5ccf79f0-9974-5baa-9b80-8bf16225b0a2',0,1,15,(CAST(N'<p><span><span>INNOVATION IN BUSINESS</span></span></p><p></p><p>Innovation describes the way that we develop new ideas, products and approaches, and it is one of the most vital human endeavours. Over the history of humanity, innovation has made life better in so many different ways. It is a part of human nature to recognize the benefits of innovation; however, the majority of us have little comprehension of the processes that actually lead to innovation occurring. It is a frequent topic for discussion in journals and university lecture theatres. However, in company boardrooms across New Zealand, the term is heard far too frequently and more caution should be applied. Certainly, a recent international survey showed that the idea of innovation is so broad as to appear almost meaningless, with different sectors of the business world – or different divisions inside the same business – often defining innovation in their own way.</p><p></p><p>While there is an obvious attraction to the new, innovation is not always about large scale research and development projects or revolutionary business models; it can be on a small, highly localized scale and involve a step-by-step approach. The famous case study of the drinks company Lucozade shows it can be as simple as adding a screw top to a bottle. This carefully managed change in packaging shifted the public perception of the product from a medicine to a sports drink and Lucozade profited handsomely, clearly showing their approach was successful. So, what steps can businesses take to keep ahead in the innovation game?</p><p></p><p>There seems to be a widespread belief that the world’s best ideas are sudden and intuitive. Thomas Edison supposedly invented the light bulb with a sudden moment of clarity but in fact the book Edison: His Life and Inventions shows that Edison’s own inspiration usually resulted from laborious experimentation, rather than a single moment of genius. Many of his inventions were the result of overestimating the piece of work needed, and then underestimating the amount of perseverance needed. This is why we must reject the false assumption that innovation is just a moment of brilliance waiting to strike.</p><p></p><p>No exploration of innovation is complete without mention of Steve Job, the late chief executive officer (CEO) of Apple. No-one encapsulated the critical essence of Silicon Valley, the home of many global tech companies, better than Jobs but he has also accused of arrogance. Jobs’ ma' AS nvarchar(max))+N'nagerial approach often irritated his co workers but, in part, it was the fuel for his visionary innovations. He felt it his duty to make society a better place but his egotistical behaviour could have undesirable consequences, too. Jobs’ former employees have suggested this type of demanding behaviour affects sickness rates and group morale, which in turn may squash creativity and innovation.</p><p></p><p>In his 2011 TED (Technology, Entertainment, Design) Talk, economist Tim Harford has made statement: ‘Show me a successful complex system and I will show you a system that has evolved through trial and error.’ It sounds like common sense and some commentators have claimed Harford’s TED Talk was not persuasive, because it was stating the obvious. But he responds that a trial and error approach is not all that obvious, because it was starting the obvious. But the problems to have a quick and simple solution. Harford is right to point out that both consumers and investors expect consistent and clear breakthroughs. But the value of step-by-step innovation is often underrated and failure may in fact be crucial to eventual success.</p><p></p><p>Former chief solutions officer at Yahoo, Tim Sanders, believes that innovation is only ‘little ideas that combine with other little ideas that improve themselves into game-changing ideas’. This snowballing effect has similarities to the phenomenon that author and broadcaster Steven Johnson calls the ‘hummingbird effect’ of innovation. This points out that progress in a specific area or discipline can end up triggering small but significant developments elsewhere entirely. A good case to cite in support of this universal truth would be Gutenberg’s printing press, which was revolutionary in itself for making books accessible to the masses. However, the press also affected an unrelated industry by causing a rise in demand for reading glasses.</p><p></p><p>This highlights the wider idea of connectivity, which is an essential component of innovation. When Kode Biotech won a recent innovation award, CEO Steve Henry had this to say: ‘Most people think innovation is invention, but they don’t understand that innovation is the conversion of invention into something useful’. This is particularly true when it comes to Kode’s highly specialised use of nano technology. Henry says that Kode cannot chase all the opportunities it has created. Instead, Kode’s approach is to collaborate with similar nanotechnology businesses, which take it'+N's innovations and develop them into commodities that can be sold in the marketplace. Innovation can be hectic and disorganised, but that is the way that radical new ideas sometimes are. But, for established businesses, the disorderly nature of innovation can seem discouraging. Previously Unavailable, a specialist innovation consultancy, says that while 84% of businesses consider innovation critical to their future, only 6% are satisfied with their innovation efforts. Previously Unavailable uses a process called Black Box, which was developed through a study at Harvard Business School. Black Box was formed to overcome the barriers that prevent innovation in larger organisations. Using this unique system, Previously Unavailable will lease a team of innovation experts on a short-term basis to its client organisations to assist with consultancy and teaching and launching new product lines. The innovation seems probable that this sort of innovation consultancy will become increasingly common, as businesses already employ specialist consultants for legal, financial or marketing services.</p>'),NULL,NULL,N'',NULL,1,0,3,NULL,0,1416),
(N'f4ca194a-b434-5086-90d8-951b1117f04c',N'd7b41115-daec-5659-ad48-ce89d6965128',0,2,18,N'<p><span>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3? </span></p><p><span>In boxes 27–30 of your answer sheet, write </span></p><p><span><span>YES</span> if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer </span></p><p><span><span>NO </span>if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer </span></p><p><span><span>NOT GIVEN</span> if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this </span></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',1,0,1,NULL,0,1416),
(N'05f9d8cf-1f57-5fa9-9e7c-a037f6ceedbc',N'f4ca194a-b434-5086-90d8-951b1117f04c',0,3,19,N'<p>Most people naturally understand how innovation happens.
</p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms: "naturally understand" = "recognize"; "how innovation happens" = "processes that lead to innovation occurring"</p><p>+ Interpretation: Hầu hết mọi người tự nhiên hiểu được sự phát minh diễn ra như thế nào</p><p>+ Answer: phần lớn mọi người đều ko hiểu quá trình phát minh thực sự xảy ra ntn </p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là No</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,27,NULL,0,1416),
(N'1fab7f3d-c952-5b33-9341-0a619fa57516',N'f4ca194a-b434-5086-90d8-951b1117f04c',0,3,19,N'<p>The word ‘innovation’ is overused in business in New Zealand. </p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms: "overused" = "heard far too frequently"; "in business" = "in company boardrooms"</p><p>+ Interpretation: Từ ''đổi mới'' được sử dụng quá nhiều trong kinh doanh ở New Zealand</p><p>+ Answer: cho dù từ “innovation” thường xuyên được sử dụng nhưng nó được dùng quá nhiều ở New Zealand </p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là YES</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,28,NULL,0,1416),
(N'f65b5f8a-ab7f-5cf5-9812-736f804c019b',N'f4ca194a-b434-5086-90d8-951b1117f04c',0,3,19,N'<p>There are many interpretations of what innovation means in business,  according to one global study.</p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms: "many interpretations" = "so broad as to appear almost meaningless" . "defining innovation in their own way" (tự định nghĩa); "global study" = "international survey</p><p>+ Interpretation: "Có nhiều cách giải thích khác nhau về ý nghĩa của đổi mới trong kinh doanh, theo một nghiên cứu toàn cầu." </p><p>+ Answer: những ngành kinh doanh khác nhau (different sectors) định nghĩa về “innovation” theo một cách khác nhau theo 1 nghiên cứu quốc tế. </p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là YES</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,29,NULL,0,1416),
