(N'b154e893-3852-5eb0-b032-15619037839d',N'787bceef-90e6-570e-996e-b3c32717c76d',0,3,19,N'What did Provine conclude from his ''closed nose yawn1 experiment?',N'<p>+Interpretation: Provine kết luận gì từ thí nghiệm ngáp khi bịt mũi?</p><p>+Answer: Thí nghiệm cho thấy rằng một cái ngáp không cần đến mũi khi hít vào và thở ra ở giai đoạn đầu và cuối</p><p>-&gt; đáp án B: Bạn có thể ngáp mà không cần thở bằng mũi.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,33,NULL,0,1094),
(N'005435b6-9392-5cfa-8489-b93c8ac6ff1a',N'787bceef-90e6-570e-996e-b3c32717c76d',0,3,19,N'Provine''s clenched teeth yawn''s experiment shows that',N'<p>+Interpretation: Thí nghiệm ngáp với răng cắn chặt của Provine cho thấy...</p><p>+Answer: Thí nghiệm đã chứng minh rằng việc mở rộng hàm một yếu tố cần thiết của một cái ngáp</p><p>-&gt; đáp án C: Bạn phải có khả năng mở rộng miệng để ngáp.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,34,NULL,0,1094),
(N'5e19da0d-9373-51a0-93f4-b41c76e92d37',N'787bceef-90e6-570e-996e-b3c32717c76d',0,3,19,N'The nose yawn experiment was used to test weather yawning',N'<p>+Synonym: nasal airway = nose</p><p>+Interpretation: Thí nghiệm ngáp bằng mũi được sử dụng để kiểm tra xem liệu ngáp...</p><p>+Answer: Thí nghiệm là để thử xem rằng đường thở bằng mũi có thể duy trì một cái ngáp được không -&gt; đáp án D: có thể được thực hiện chỉ thông qua mũi hay không.</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là D</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,35,NULL,0,1094),
(N'efac9d7d-802c-5ecc-9512-3d157b97e81a',N'787bceef-90e6-570e-996e-b3c32717c76d',0,3,19,N'In people paralyzed on one side because of brain damage',N'<p>+Interpretation: Ở những người bị liệt một bên do tổn thương não...</p><p>+Explanation: Đoạn văn nói rằng khi ngáp thì cánh tay bị tê liệt sẽ nâng lên và duỗi ra tự động</p><p>-&gt; đáp án C: cử động ở cánh tay bị liệt được kích thích bởi ngáp.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,36,NULL,0,1094),
(N'228140a9-3831-54ac-aae7-24ba4ee8f789',N'787bceef-90e6-570e-996e-b3c32717c76d',0,3,19,N'In the last paragraph, the writer concludes that',N'<p>+Interpretation: Trong đoạn cuối, người viết kết luận rằng...</p><p>+Answer: Đoạn văn nói rằng việc ngáp là một hành vi cổ xưa và vô thức nhắc nhở chúng ta về thế giới động vật ở dưới bề ngoài của văn hóa, lý trí và ngôn ngữ</p><p>-&gt; đáp án B: chúng ta ngáp bất chấp sự phát triển của loài người chúng ta.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,37,NULL,0,1094),
(N'de66050f-9f43-5486-bcc1-77ca9cd0accd',N'adcfea11-bfcb-5ffc-ad7c-ff9d29c9d476',0,2,18,N'<p>Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in Reading Passage 3? </p><p>In boxes 3 8-40 on your answer sheet, write  </p><p><span>YES </span>                If the statement agrees with the claims of the writer </p><p><span>NO  </span>                lf the statement contradicts the claims of the writer </p><p><span>NOT GIVEN </span>   it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this </p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',1,0,3,NULL,0,1094),
(N'0b6169dc-01b1-550c-b928-1adedd16147e',N'de66050f-9f43-5486-bcc1-77ca9cd0accd',0,3,19,N'Research students were initially reluctant to appreciate the value of Provine''s studies.',N'<p>+Interpretation: Các nghiên cứu sinh ban đầu miễn cưỡng đánh giá cao giá trị các nghiên cứu của Provine.</p><p>+Answer: Đoạn văn nói rằng khi Provine bắt đầu nghiên cứu về ngáp, ông gặp khó khăn trong việc thuyết phục học viên rằng “khoa học ngáp” có giá trị</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là Yes</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,38,NULL,0,1094),
(N'444945d3-b826-5fa6-be90-12e33f4453b5',N'de66050f-9f43-5486-bcc1-77ca9cd0accd',0,3,19,N'When foetuses yawn and stretch they are learning how to control movement.',N'<p>+Interpretation: Khi bào thai ngáp và duỗi người, chúng đang học cách kiểm soát cử động.</p><p>+Answer: Đoạn văn chỉ nói rằng sự liên kết giữa việc ngáp và duỗi được quan sát ở bào thai, ko nói gì đến việc học cử động</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là Not given</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,39,NULL,0,1094),
(N'883fd1d1-2fbc-5ea3-ba7b-d44360f655ee',N'de66050f-9f43-5486-bcc1-77ca9cd0accd',0,3,19,N'According to Provine, referring to only one function is probably inadequate to explain why people yawn.',N'<p>+Interpretation: Theo Provine, việc chỉ đề cập đến một chức năng có lẽ là không đủ để giải thích tại sao mọi người ngáp.</p><p>+Answer: Đoạn văn nói rằng việc ngáp có nhiều chức năng và việc chọn ra 1 chức năng trong số đó là ko thực tế</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là Yes</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,40,NULL,0,1094),
(N'11dd7601-eadf-5288-9ccb-e41c75d1c8c7',NULL,0,0,11,NULL,NULL,NULL,N'',N'Vol 2 READING FULL TEST 10',0,7,1,NULL,1,1070),
(N'86b41f35-41fe-5282-ae4e-92a5cb48d67e',N'11dd7601-eadf-5288-9ccb-e41c75d1c8c7',0,1,13,(CAST(N'<p><span><span><span>Rubber</span></span></span></p><p><em>T and W Musgrove discuss the origins and early uses of rubber</em></p><p></p><p>The plants that produce rubber are spread right across the globe, and grow in many different habitats. One might think it likely, therefore, that humankind has known about rubber for thousands of years. Yet, unlike other crops of economic importance, rubber led a relatively anonymous life until the last 150 years or so. The Indians of South America ''appear to be the first people to have understood the properties of rubber, and the Aztecs of what is now Mexico were the first to be recorded using the substance; a wall painting dating back to the sixth century depicts a scene of a tributary offering of crude rubber.</p><p></p><p>With the arrival of Columbus in the Americas and the resulting Spanish influx, further evidence starts to appear concerning the Native American use of rubber Antonio de Herrera y Tordesillas describes a ritual game played with a rubber ball at the court of the Aztec Emperor Montezuma II, and the Mayan and Toltec people are known to have taken part in similar activities Rubber was also used to make raincoats, shoes, jars, torches and ''musical instruments, all of which must have been made from the indigenous Castilla elastica, as the Para plant now favoured for rubber cultivation does not grow in the Mexican region.</p><p></p><p>''The first description of latex (liquid rubber) extraction is made by Juan de Torquemada, who noted that if a receptacle was not at hand the Native Americans would place the latex on their bodies to allow it to solidify. However, no real interest in rubber was shown by any European until Charles de la Condamine, a French mathematician, published an ''account of his journey to South America in 1735. The journey was undertaken on behalf of the Paris Academy of Sciences to measure an arc of the meridian line on the equator, but the journey home was to turn out to be more significant than the true purpose of the trip. Condamine explored Brazil and Peru and discovered how the local people used one single piece of coagulated latex to make boots. The boots were impervious to water and, when smoked, looked like real leather. In 1747 the first description of the rubber tree and latex tapping was made by a military engineer and amateur botanist, Francois Fresneau, who was posted to French Guiana, The publications of Condamine and Fresneau created considerable excitement among French sci' AS nvarchar(max))+N'entists, and an attempt was made to discover a solvent that could turn the crude rubber into a substance for commercial exploitation.</p><p></p><p>In 1818 a British medical student named James Syme first used rubber to make waterproof cloth. Another early use of the substance was as an eraser of pencil marks, hence the name "rubber. This was complemented by balloons, rubber bands, braces, boots for the army and other ideas that met with varying degrees of success. In 1820 Thomas Hancock, an English manufacturer of rubber goods such as driving belts, industrial rollers and rubber hoses, invented a machine he called the ''piokle'', which chewed up waste strips for re-use. It was discovered that the masticated rubber was more malleable, while maintaining much of its elasticity. In Scotland at the same time Charles Mackintosh had discovered a way of using rubber as waterproofing material, by a process he patented in 1823. Hancock and Mackintosh joined forces in 1834, and three years later Hancock invented a machine for spreading rubber onto material.</p><p></p><p>Despite their beneficial qualities, such as waterproofing, rubber goods were still not particularly popular as they had some major flaws, including the fact that they dissolved malodorously. They also became pliant when warm and rigid when cold. Then in 1839 the American Charles Goodyear discovered that it was possible to stabilize rubber by mixing it with sulphur while exposing it to heat, a process he called vulcanisation and the full versatility of this extraordinary substance became apparent.</p><p></p><p>Rubber goods could now be manufactured which had all the beneficial qualities of the material, such as durability, elasticity and variability, but which were not sticky, soluble or governed by the vagaries of the weather. The economic potential of rubber was now clearly evident. It played an important role in the Industrial Revolution, being employed in the steam engines found in factories, mills, mines and railways. It made a triumphant entrance as a new and innovative material at the Great Exhibition of 1851, where shoes, airbeds, furniture and clothing made out of newly improved rubber were proudly displayed.</p><p></p><p>One of the most important rubber inventions was made in 1888, when an Irishman called John Boyd Dunlop produced the first pneumatic tyre. Solid rubber tyres had been used for the previous 18 years, but Dunlop''s new design, which he updated in 1890, immediately became popular. I'+N'n 1895 Dunlop''s tyres were first used in motor cars, and with the mass production of cars just over the horizon the rubber industry had never looked healthier. The import levels of rubber over the nineteenth century bear witness to it''s irrepressible rise. In 1830 Britain had imported just 211 kg of crude rubber. This had risen to 10,000kg in 1857, and by 1874 levels were just under six times as much again.</p>'),NULL,NULL,N'',NULL,1,0,1,NULL,0,1070),
(N'4a2aa38a-fb53-5b97-9a52-6f6b69fee66c',N'86b41f35-41fe-5282-ae4e-92a5cb48d67e',0,2,18,N'<p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? </span></p><p><span>In boxes 1–6 on your answer sheet, write </span></p><p><span><span>TRUE</span> if the statement agrees with the information </span></p><p><span><span>FALSE</span> if the statement contradicts the information </span></p><p><span><span>NOT GIVEN</span> if there is no information on this </span></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',1,0,1,NULL,0,1070),
(N'c3ae545b-548e-57bd-bef3-270f3e486e9d',N'4a2aa38a-fb53-5b97-9a52-6f6b69fee66c',0,3,19,N'<p>Rubber plants grow only in certain regions of the world.</p>',N'<p>-Synonyms: </p><p>regions = habitats </p><p>-Question: </p><p>Interpretation: Cây cao su chỉ mọc ở một số khu vực trên thế giới. </p><p>-Answer: </p><p>Thông tin trong bài nói cây cao su phân bố khắp toàn cầu và nhiều môi trường, tức là không chỉ một số khu vực </p><p>⇒ FALSE </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,1,NULL,0,1070),
(N'25fa7860-1201-5207-8b41-8e9084a19ab8',N'4a2aa38a-fb53-5b97-9a52-6f6b69fee66c',0,3,19,N'<p>Rubber was extracted in Mexico as early as the sixth century.</p>',N'<p>-Synonyms: </p><p>offering = was extracted </p><p>-Question: </p><p>Interpretation: Ở Mexico, cao su được khai thác từ sớm vào thế kỷ 6.  </p><p>-Answer: </p><p>Bức tranh từ thế kỷ 6 vẻ lại một cảnh dâng cao su thô, bằng chứng rõ ràng cho thấy có cao su từ thế kỷ 6 </p><p>⇒ TRUE </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,2,NULL,0,1070),
(N'eb69f0c8-9730-5e53-a4ea-e7488fb89704',N'4a2aa38a-fb53-5b97-9a52-6f6b69fee66c',0,3,19,N'<p>Rubber from the Castilla elastica plant is of poorer quality than that from the Para plant.</p>',N'<p>-Question: </p><p>Interpretation: Cao su từ Castilla elastica chất lượng kém hơn Para.  </p><p>-Answer: </p><p>Thông tin trong bài chỉ nói về vị trí trồng, không so sánh chất lượng giữa hai loại cao su này </p><p>⇒ NOT GIVEN </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,3,NULL,0,1070),
(N'17f941a8-194e-5889-a1cd-fa7ecd360aef',N'4a2aa38a-fb53-5b97-9a52-6f6b69fee66c',0,3,19,N'<p>A French mathematician inspired real interest in rubber amongst Europeans.</p>',N'<p>-Synonyms: </p><p>inspired real interest = no real interest in rubber was shown until </p><p>-Question: </p><p>Interpretation: Nhà toán học Pháp tạo cảm hứng khiến châu Âu quan tâm đến cao su.  </p><p>-Answer: </p><p>Thông tin trong bài đọc có nói rằng trước khi ông kể về câu chuyện về chuyến hành trình của ông thì không có ai quan tâm tới cao su, tức là ông chính là người làm nhiều người quan tâm tới cao su </p><p>⇒ TRUE </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,4,NULL,0,1070),
(N'c8a059a0-c556-57ae-813b-6bb64604297b',N'4a2aa38a-fb53-5b97-9a52-6f6b69fee66c',0,3,19,N'<p>The process of vulcanisation was discovered by accident.</p>',N'<p>-Question: </p><p>Interpretation: Quá trình lưu hóa được phát hiện tình cờ. </p><p>-Answer: </p><p>Thông tin trong bài có kể về việc Charles phát hiện ra quá trình lưu hoá nhưng chỉ nói về cách thức của quá trình, không nói tới việc phát hiện vô tình hay không </p><p>⇒ NOT GIVEN   </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,5,NULL,0,1070),
(N'4751a04b-981f-5b99-bf5c-4a7534c45d0e',N'4a2aa38a-fb53-5b97-9a52-6f6b69fee66c',0,3,19,N'<p>Imports of crude rubber into Britain fell during the nineteenth century</p>',N'<p>-Question: </p><p>Interpretation: Nhập khẩu cao su thô vào Anh giảm trong thế kỷ 19. </p><p>-Answer: </p><p>Thông tin trong bài đề cập là nước Anh nhập khẩu 211kg cao su năm 1830, sau đó tăng mạnh lên 10000 kg vào 1857 và lại tăng gấp 6 lần nữa vào 1874, tức là tăng theo thời gian, trái với thông tin đề bài </p><p>⇒ FALSE </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,6,NULL,0,1070),
(N'923539ef-40af-5ec5-8497-f5cb89d1762e',N'86b41f35-41fe-5282-ae4e-92a5cb48d67e',0,2,18,N'<p>Complete the summary below. </p><p>Choose <span>NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS </span>from the passage for each answer. </p><p>Write your answers in boxes 7–13 on your answer sheet. </p>',N'',N'',N'',N'The Commercial Development of Rubber',11,0,2,NULL,0,1070),
(N'9baf1487-ec3e-5ce8-b87e-3a58d79293dc',N'923539ef-40af-5ec5-8497-f5cb89d1762e',0,3,19,N'<h3>The Commercial Development of Rubber</h3><p>Early European travellers gave accounts of various rubber objects in use in Central and South America, and these accounts created interest in the commercial exploitation of rubber. In 1818, }{SPACE}{ </p><p>was produced using rubber, and in 1820 a machine was invented for recycling }{SPACE}{ of rubber. Over the next few years, other attempts were made to improve rubber, but some problems remained.</p><p>Over the next few years, other attempts were made to improve rubber, but some problems remained. For example, rubber products smelt bad when they were dissolved, and could turn either soft or }{SPACE}{ depending on the temperature.</p><p>However, in 1839, a new process to }{SPACE}{ the substance greatly increased its potential.</p><p>For example, rubber was used in the creation of the }{SPACE}{ industry during the industrial revolution.</p><p>Then in 1888, the }{SPACE}{ </p><p>was developed, and a few years later, the }{SPACE}{ of the motor car began</p>',N'<p>-Synonyms: </p><p>produced = make. </p><p>-Question: </p><p>Interpretation: Năm 1818, … được tạo ra bằng cao su. </p><p>-Answer: </p><p>Từ cần điền là danh từ chỉ một vật làm từ cao su, thông tin trong bài chỉ ra là James dùng cao su để tạo ra quần áo chống nước </p><p>⇒ Đáp án: waterproof cloth </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,7,NULL,0,1070),
(N'a9748960-3a7e-5488-9957-ce342bfa6d02',N'923539ef-40af-5ec5-8497-f5cb89d1762e',0,3,19,N'Question number 8',N'<p>-Synonyms: </p><p>recycling = re-use. </p><p>-Question: </p><p>Interpretation: Năm 1820, có một máy được chế tạo dùng để tái chế ...  </p><p>-Answer: </p><p>Từ cần điền là một danh từ. Thông tin trong bài nói rằng Thomas đã chế tạo một máy gọi là piokle để nghiền các dải cao su nhằm tái sử dụng, tức là để tái chế dải cao su </p><p>⇒ Đáp án là waste strips </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,8,NULL,0,1070),
(N'22c7f11b-a9b2-5174-beeb-c150a2b41f4d',N'923539ef-40af-5ec5-8497-f5cb89d1762e',0,3,19,N'Question number 9',N'<p>-Synonyms: </p><p>depending on the temperature = pliant when warm and rigid when cold.  </p><p>-Question: </p><p>Interpretation: Cao su có thể trở nên mềm hoặc … theo nhiệt độ. </p><p>-Answer: </p><p>Từ phải điền là một tính từ, thông tin trong bài có nói là cao su sẽ trở nên mềm dẻo lúc nóng và cứng lại khi lạnh. Trong đề có thông tin là cao su sẽ mềm hoặc… tuỳ theo nhiệt độ, vì đã có mềm rồi nên chỗ trống sẽ là cứng. </p><p>⇒ Đáp án là rigid </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,9,NULL,0,1070),
(N'8ad36e5d-e4bf-5019-88e9-a01221d0f521',N'923539ef-40af-5ec5-8497-f5cb89d1762e',0,3,19,N'Question number 10',N'<p>-Synonyms: </p><p>increased its potential = stabilize rubber. </p><p>-Question: </p><p>Interpretation: Vào năm 1839, một quy trình mới để (10)… chất này đã làm tăng đáng kể tiềm năng của nó. </p><p>-Answer: </p><p>Từ cần điền là một động từ. Thông tin trong bài có nói rằng năm 1839, Charles phát hiện có thể làm cao su ổn định hơn bằng một quy trình ông mới phát hiện </p><p>=&gt; Đáp án là stabilize. </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,10,NULL,0,1070),
(N'ca21fa18-ff73-5d9c-8bc8-c6491047acdc',N'923539ef-40af-5ec5-8497-f5cb89d1762e',0,3,19,N'Question number 11',N'<p>Synonyms: </p><p>used = employed </p><p>Question: </p><p>Interpretation: Cao su được dùng trong việc tạo nên ngành công nghiệp…thời Cách mạng Công nghiệp. </p><p>Answer: </p><p>Từ cần điền là một danh từ thuộc ngành công nghiệp. Thông tin trong bài có nói rằng cao su được ứng dụng trong đầu máy hơi nước. </p><p>⇒ Đáp án là steam engines </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,11,NULL,0,1070),
(N'a0d380e0-5bdb-5d3f-8617-6a4a2a9350b5',N'923539ef-40af-5ec5-8497-f5cb89d1762e',0,3,19,N'Question number 12',N'<p>-Synonyms: developed = produced.</p><p>-Question:</p><p>Interpretation: Năm 1888, … được phát triển.</p><p>-Answer: Thông tin trong bài nhắc đến mốc thời gian 1888 có lốp hơi được ra đời, tức là thời điểm đó lốp hơi được phát triển.</p><p>⇒ Đáp án là first pneumatic tyre</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,12,NULL,0,1070),
(N'c15c4a67-7696-5884-aa3e-7c053eb4e17f',N'923539ef-40af-5ec5-8497-f5cb89d1762e',0,3,19,N'Question number 13',N'<p>-Synonyms: </p><p>began = over the horizon </p><p>-Question: </p><p>Interpretation: Một vài năm sau, .. của ô tô bắt đầu diễn ra.  </p><p>-Answer: </p><p>Từ cần điền là một danh từ. Thông tin trong bài có nói rằng năm 1895, tức là một vài năm sau năm 1888, thì việc ô tô được sản xuất hàng loạt ở ngay trước mặt, tức là việc sản xuất hàng loạt ô tô diễn ra trong năm đó </p><p>→ Đáp án là mass production </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,13,NULL,0,1070),
(N'0a75e929-2bb6-58d4-873e-a7a0aa455fc7',N'11dd7601-eadf-5288-9ccb-e41c75d1c8c7',0,1,14,(CAST(N'<p><span><span><span>STRESS LESS</span></span></span></p><p></p><p>How busy is too busy? For some, it means sometimes having to have a short lunch; for others, it may mean missing lunch altogether. For a few, it is not being able to take a day off once a month. Then there is a group of people for whom working every evening and weekend is normal, and feeling stressed is taken for granted. For most senior executives, workloads swing between extremely busy and frenzied. Neil Plumridge, vice-president of a management consultancy company, says that his weeks vary from a ''manageable 45 hours to 80 hours, but average 60 hours.''</p><p></p><p>Three signs warn Plumridge about his workload: sleep, scheduling, and family. He knows he is doing too much when he gets less than six hours'' sleep for three consecutive nights, when he is constantly having to reschedule appointments, and when he misses a family birthday or anniversary. Then, he says, "I know things are out of control." Plumridge states that stress is often caused by his having unrealistic expectations of himself. "I''ll promise a client that I''ll do something tomorrow, and then I''ll promise another client that I''ll do the same thing when I know it''s not going to happen. I could have said: ''Why don''t I give that to you in 48 hours?'' The client wouldn''t care."</p><p></p><p>Over-committing is something people experience as an individual problem. However, new research indicates that people may be designed to over-commit. A study in the Journal of Experimental Psychology shows that people always believe that they will be less busy in the future. This is a misapprehension, according to the authors of the report, Gal Zauberman of the University of North Carolina and John Lynch of Duke University. On average, an individual will be just as busy two weeks or a month from now as he or she is today. But that is not how it appears in everyday life, they say. "People make commitments long in advance that they would never make if the same commitments required immediate action. They discount future time investments relatively steeply."</p><p></p><p>Being too busy is highly subjective, but for any individual, there are some concrete signs of stress—disturbed sleep and declining mental and physical health are the most common examples. Figures for National Workers'' Compensation (insurance against injury caused by work) show that stress causes the most lost time of any workplace injury: employees suffering stress are absent from ' AS nvarchar(max))+N'work for an average of 16.6 weeks. The effects of stress are also expensive. The Australian Government insurer reports that in 2003-2004, claims for stress-related psychological injury accounted for 7% of insurance claims but almost 27% of the amount paid out in claim payments.</p><p></p><p>Experts say the key to dealing with stress is not to focus on relief—a game of golf or a massage—but to reassess workloads. Neil Plumridge says he makes it a priority to work out what has to change: that might mean allocating extra staff to a job, allowing more time, or changing expectations. He also relies on the advice of colleagues, saying that his peers coach each other on business problems: "Just a fresh pair of eyes over an issue can help," he states.</p><p></p><p>Executive stress is not confined to big organisations. Vanessa Stoykov has been running her own advertising agency and public relations business for seven years. Her company has grown so fast that it appeared on the Business Review Weekly ''Fast 100'' list of fastest-growing small enterprises in 2004, just after Stoykov had her first child. In 2005, revenue was projected to double to $2.4 million. She had just had her second child. With a fast-growing business and two small children, Stoykov says she has mastered the art of caring for children, typing, and talking on the phone at the same time. But, unlike many others, she appears to thrive on the mental stimulation of running her own business, despite the stress.</p><p></p><p>Jan Elsner, a psychologist who specialises in executive coaching, says that doing well on a demanding workload is typical of senior executives. Some people work best with high-adrenaline periods followed by quieter times, while others thrive under sustained pressure. Elsner''s practice is based on a movement known as positive psychology, a school of thought that argues that positive experiences—feeling engaged and challenged, for example—do not balance out negative experiences such as stress; instead, they help people increase their resilience over time. Elsner says that many of the senior business people she coaches are increasingly relying more on regulating stress through methods such as meditation. She points to research showing that meditation can alter the biochemistry of the brain and the way that brains and bodies react to stress.</p><p></p><p>Some experts believe there is too much emphasis on treating job stress as an individual problem. Tony LaMontagne, of the University of '+N'Melbourne, says that while personality traits do have some effect on stress, it is systemic stressors—qualities of job roles and organisations themselves—that have a far greater effect. His recent research shows that the major predictor of stress is the level of job control a person has. The best type of job combines challenging work with high autonomy. The worst jobs combine challenging work and low control. People with demanding jobs but little autonomy have up to four times the probability of depression and more than double the risk of heart attack</p>'),NULL,NULL,N'',NULL,1,0,2,NULL,0,1070),
(N'4c87024a-d0ec-5d82-a2b3-16dcbc961a6c',N'0a75e929-2bb6-58d4-873e-a7a0aa455fc7',0,2,18,N'<p>Look at the following statements (questions 14-18) and the list of people below. </p><p>Match each statement with the correct person, <span>A-D. </span></p><p>Write the correct letter, <span>A-D</span>, in boxes 19-22 on your answer sheet. </p>',N'',N'',N'',N'Answer choices',10,0,1,NULL,0,1070),
(N'f7e0002d-6869-5b2f-8e77-5e56cea9f945',N'4c87024a-d0ec-5d82-a2b3-16dcbc961a6c',0,3,19,N'<p>High-level workers tend to react positively to stress</p>',N'<p>- Synonyms:</p><p>react positively to stress = thrive under sustained pressure</p><p>- Question:</p><p>Interpretation: Những người làm việc ở vị trí cao thường phản ứng tích cực với căng thẳng.</p><p>- Answer:</p><p>Thông tin trong bài có nói rằng Jan Elsner cho rằng một số người làm việc tốt nhất trong giai đoạn căng thẳng cao và thậm chí còn phát triển khi chịu áp lực liên tục. Điều đó cho thấy họ phản ứng tích cực với stress</p><p>⇒ Đáp án C.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,14,NULL,0,1070),
(N'47a57bb1-3ec6-5f5a-990d-7b96badd6ad5',N'4c87024a-d0ec-5d82-a2b3-16dcbc961a6c',0,3,19,N'<p>Stress levels are increased by trying to please customers</p>',N'<p>- Synonyms:</p><p>customers = client.</p><p>- Question:</p><p>Interpretation: Mức độ căng thẳng tăng lên do cố gắng làm hài lòng khách hàng.</p><p>- Answer:</p><p>Neil Plumridge nói rằng căng thẳng của ông thường do tự đặt ra kỳ vọng thiếu thực tế, cố gắng hứa hẹn với nhiều khách hàng hơn khả năng của bản thân, tức là cố làm hài lòng khách hàng</p><p>⇒ Đáp án A.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,15,NULL,0,1070),
(N'5aeacdde-94ad-5ad9-9437-beaffc51b11d',N'4c87024a-d0ec-5d82-a2b3-16dcbc961a6c',0,3,19,N'<p>Support from other workers may relieve stress</p>',N'<p>- Synonyms:</p><p>support from other workers = advice of colleagues</p><p>- Question:</p><p>Interpretation: Sự hỗ trợ từ đồng nghiệp có thể giúp giảm căng thẳng.</p><p>- Answer:</p><p>Neil Plumridge cho biết ông dựa dẫm vào lời khuyên của đồng nghiệp, các đồng nghiệp giúp nhau giải quyết vấn đề kinh doanh và từ đó giúp giảm bớt căng thẳng</p><p>⇒ Đáp án A.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,16,NULL,0,1070),
(N'f942b34c-73cf-5972-b731-055011b892bd',N'4c87024a-d0ec-5d82-a2b3-16dcbc961a6c',0,3,19,N'<p>Lack of independence at work is often responsible for stress</p>',N'<p>- Synonyms:</p><p>lack of independence at work = low control</p><p>- Question:</p><p>Interpretation: Thiếu sự tự chủ trong công việc thường là nguyên nhân gây ra căng thẳng.</p><p>- Answer:</p><p>Tony LaMontagne cho rằng yếu tố dự đoán chính của stress là mức độ kiểm soát công việc. Công việc có ít quyền kiểm soát sẽ gây nhiều stress hơn, tức là loại công việc thiếu sự tự chủ, tự quyết định từ bản chất</p><p>⇒ Đáp án D.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,17,NULL,0,1070),
(N'59810260-7fc3-5692-b2f1-ae099bcc29d6',N'4c87024a-d0ec-5d82-a2b3-16dcbc961a6c',0,3,19,N'<p>Workers commonly expect their workloads to lessen over time</p>',N'<p>- Synonyms:</p><p>expect their workloads to lessen = believe that they will be less busy</p><p>- Question:</p><p>Interpretation: Người lao động thường mong rằng khối lượng công việc của họ sẽ giảm dần theo thời gian.</p><p>- Answer:</p><p>Trong bài, Gal Zauberman và John Lynch phát hiện rằng con người luôn tin rằng họ sẽ ít bận hơn trong tương lai, tức họ kỳ vọng khối lượng công việc sẽ giảm</p><p>⇒ Đáp án B.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,18,NULL,0,1070),
(N'fbf67d14-4234-54ca-8479-fae4eb4f67dd',N'0a75e929-2bb6-58d4-873e-a7a0aa455fc7',0,2,18,N'<p>For questions 19-21, choose the correct letter <span>A, B, C, or D. </span></p><p>Write the correct letter A-D on your answer sheet. </p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',1,0,2,NULL,0,1070);
