(N'cb25f634-f809-53e9-b5b3-bf5923501f78',N'7a996a80-fbda-5666-87b1-c03e2cfad62d',0,3,19,N'<h3>Polyethylene</h3><p>In 1933, two organic chemists applied extreme }{SPACE}{ </p><p>to ethylene and benzaldehyde, to discover what }{SPACE}{ would occur.</p><p>The experiment was spoiled by a minor   }{SPACE}{ during the test process, but the scientists found that polyethylene had been created. </p><p>A }{SPACE}{ was built to manufacture polyethylene on a large scale. </p><p>The material was later used as a  }{SPACE}{ for submarine cables and</p><p>to provide  }{SPACE}{ in radar systems,</p><p>allowing them to be carried on }{SPACE}{ </p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: ...áp dụng cực kỳ... lên ethylene và benzaldehyde.</p><p>+ Answer: Thí nghiệm để kích hoạt phản ứng giữa 2 chất trên được thực hiện dưới áp suất cao</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là pressure</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,7,NULL,0,1043),
(N'35b403a4-31fb-587f-b2ab-e72281fdf2a0',N'7a996a80-fbda-5666-87b1-c03e2cfad62d',0,3,19,N'Question number 8',N'<p>+ Interpretation: ...để khám phá xem... nào sẽ xảy ra. </p><p>+ Answer: Mục đích của nghiên cứu là để kích hoạt một phản ứng hóa học </p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là reaction</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,8,NULL,0,1043),
(N'dea4fc54-2642-5b46-8728-c4af4023ffa2',N'7a996a80-fbda-5666-87b1-c03e2cfad62d',0,3,19,N'Question number 9',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Thí nghiệm bị làm hỏng bởi một... nhỏ.</p><p>+ Answer: Thí nghiệm gặp sự cố khi có một chỗ rò rỉ (leak)</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là leak</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,9,NULL,0,1043),
(N'81799ad4-c1b8-5e5e-b273-a185e9a149ce',N'7a996a80-fbda-5666-87b1-c03e2cfad62d',0,3,19,N'Question number 10',N'<p>+ Synonyms: production of vast quantities (sản xuất số lượng lớn) = manufacture on large scale (sản xuất quy mô lớn)</p><p>+ Interpretation: Một... đã được chế tạo để sản xuất polyethylene trên quy mô lớn.</p><p>+ Answer: ICI đã phát triển một máy nén để sản xuất polyethylene số lượng lớn</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là compressor</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,10,NULL,0,1043),
(N'669f04fb-583b-57c5-8af7-d159b48c76d2',N'7a996a80-fbda-5666-87b1-c03e2cfad62d',0,3,19,N'Question number 11',N'<p>+ Synonyms: submarine = underwater (ngầm dưới mặt nước)</p><p>+ Interpretation: Vật liệu này sau đó được sử dụng làm... cho cáp ngầm.</p><p>+ Answer: Polyethylene được dùng làm lớp phủ (coating) cho cáp dưới nước</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là coating</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,11,NULL,0,1043),
(N'4fee02e9-66ba-5c47-9d2d-fab1ea08634e',N'7a996a80-fbda-5666-87b1-c03e2cfad62d',0,3,19,N'Question number 12',N'<p>+ Interpretation: ...và để cung cấp... trong các hệ thống radar.</p><p>+ Answer: Polyethylene được dùng làm vật liệu cách điện (insulation) cho radar</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là insulation</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,12,NULL,0,1043),
(N'5af054a0-2cf4-5e29-b7a4-0dfd233c537e',N'7a996a80-fbda-5666-87b1-c03e2cfad62d',0,3,19,N'Question number 13',N'<p>+ Interpretation: ...cho phép chúng được mang trên...</p><p>+ Answer: Vì polyethylene nhẹ hơn các vật liệu khác, radar có thể lần đầu được lắp đặt trên máy bay</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là planes</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,13,NULL,0,1043),
(N'b1ff5a32-a834-5483-b49a-5e5a34afed9b',N'd9fba187-0ca8-5afa-882e-0a8b70197462',0,1,14,(CAST(N'<p><span><span><span>Urban Revitalization: Transforming Talbot Park in Auckland</span></span></span></p><p><span><span>A. }{HEADING}{ </span></span> Transformation is underway at Talbot Park, nestled in the heart of Auckland''s Glen Innes. Once plagued by crime and social issues, the area is undergoing a remarkable renewal. Following a $48 million investment in urban revitalization, the site now accommodates 700 residents - an increase of 200 from its previous population. The renovated brick and weatherboard apartments and townhouses defy the stereotype of social housing, prompting inquiries from prospective buyers and renters. Dene Busby, Housing New Zealand housing services manager, notes that the revitalized architecture no longer resembles typical public housing. Similarly, Design Group architect Neil emphasizes the importance of dignified design, asserting that public housing need not convey a sense of cheapness.<br><br><span><span>B }{HEADING}{ </span></span>. Talbot Park is a triangle of government-owned land bounded by Apirana Ave Pilkington Rd and Point England Rd. in the early 1960s, it was developed for state housing built around a linear park that ran through the middle. Initially, there was a strong sense of a family-friendly community. Former residents recall how the Talbot Park reserve played a big part in their childhoods - a place where the kids in the block came together to play softball, cricket, tiggy, leapfrog and bullrush. Sometimes they''d play "Maoris against Pakehas" but without any animosity. "It was all just good fun", says Georgie Thompson in Ben Schrader''s We Call it Home: A History of State Housing in New Zealand. "We had respect for our neighbours and addressed them by title Mr. and Mrs. so-and-so," she recalls.<br><br><span><span>C. }{HEADING}{ </span></span> Quite what went wrong with Talbot Park is not clear. We call it Home Records that the community began to change in the late 1970s as more Pacific Islanders and Europeans moved in. The new arrivals didn''t readily integrate with the community, a "them and us" mentality developed, and residents interact with their neighbours less What was clear was the buildings were deteriorating and becoming dilapidated, petty crime was on the rise and the reserve - the focus of fond childhood memories - had become a wasteland and was considered unsafe.<br><br><span><span>D. }{HEADING}{ </span></span> But it wasn''t until 2002 that Housing New Zealand decided the properties needed upgrading' AS nvarchar(max))+N'. The master renewal plan didn''t take advantage of the maximum accommodation density allowable (one unit per 100 sq metres) but did increase density to one unit per 180 sq m by refurbishing all 108 star flat units, removing the multis and building 111 new home. The Talbot strategy can be summed up as mix, match and manage. Mix up the housing with various plans from a mix of architects, match house styles to what''s built by the private sector, match tenants to the mix, and manage their occupancy. Inevitably cost comes into the equation. "If you''re going to build low-cost homes, you''ve got to keep them simple and you can''t afford a fancy bit on them." Says Michael Thompson of Architectus which designed the innovative three-level Atrium apartments lining two sides of a covered courtyard. At $300,000 per two-bedroom unit, the building is more expensive but provides for independent disabled accommodation as well as offering solar hot water heating and rainwater collection for toilet cisterns and outside taps.<br><br><span><span>E. }{HEADING}{ </span></span> The renewal project budget at $1.5 million which will provide park pathways. planting, playgrounds, drinking fountains, seating, skateboard rails, a half-size basketball hard court, and a pavilion. But if there was any doubt this is a low socioeconomic area, the demographics for the surrounding Tamaki area are sobering. Of the 5000 households there, 55 per cent are statehouses, 28 per cent privately owned (compared to about 65 per cent nationally) and 17 per cent are private rental. The area has a high concentration of households with incomes in the $5000 to $15,000 range and very few with an income of over $70,000. That''s in sharp contrast to the more affluent suburbs like Kohimarama and St John''s that surround the area.</p><p></p><p><span><span>F. }{HEADING}{ </span></span> "The design is for people with different culture background," says architect James Lunday of Common Ground which designed the 21 large family homes. "Architecturally we decided to be relatively conservative — a nice house in its own garden with a bit of space and good indoor-outdoor flow." There''s a slight reflection of the whare and a Pacific fale, but not overplayed "The private sector is way behind in urban design and sustainable futures," says Bracey. "Redesigning streets and parks is a big deal and very difficult to do. The private sector won''t do it, because it''s so hard.</p><p></p><p><span><span>G. }{HEADING}{ </span></span> Ther'+N'e''s no doubt good urban design and good architecture play a significant part in the scheme. But probably more important is a new standard of social control. Housing New Zealand calls it "intensive tenancy management". Others view it as social engineering. "It''s a model that we are looking at going forward, according to Housing New Zealand''s central Auckland regional manager Graham Bodman. "The focus is on frequent inspections, helping tenants to get to know each other and trying to create an environment of respect for neighbours, says Bodman. That includes some strict rules - no loud parties after 10 pm, no dogs, no cats in the apartments, no washing hung over balcony rails and a requirement to mow lawns and keep the property tidy. Housing New Zealand has also been active in organising morning teas and street barbecues for residents to meet their neighbours. "It''s all based on the intensification," says Community Renewal project manager Stuart Bracey. "We acknowledge if you are going to put more people living closer together, you have to actually help them to live closer together because it creates tension - especially for people that aren''t used to it."</p>'),NULL,NULL,N'',NULL,4,0,2,NULL,0,1043),
(N'5e45ad7b-f10c-5014-94fe-b7709f60c9ef',N'b1ff5a32-a834-5483-b49a-5e5a34afed9b',0,2,18,N'<p>Choose the correct heading for paragraphs, <span><span>A-G,</span></span> from the list below. Write the correct number, <span>i-x</span>, in boxes 14-20 on your answer sheet.</p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',4,0,1,NULL,0,1043),
(N'ed9cffd3-95c7-50ca-b268-9187413634b0',N'5e45ad7b-f10c-5014-94fe-b7709f60c9ef',0,3,19,N'Paragraph A',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Giới thiệu một cộng đồng nhà ở xã hội với tiêu chuẩn cao bất ngờ. </p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn A mô tả khu nhà được tân trang không giống với nhà ở công cộng thông thường và có thiết kế đẹp, khẳng định rằng nhà ở công cộng không cần phải thể hiện sự rẻ tiền </p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là vi </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,14,NULL,0,1043),
(N'fb5ef48a-2447-5f29-a27d-3f3b8e447906',N'5e45ad7b-f10c-5014-94fe-b7709f60c9ef',0,3,19,N'Paragraph B',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Mối quan hệ thân thiết giữa hàng xóm tại khu vực nguyên bản.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn B hồi tưởng về những ngày đầu, khi cộng đồng thân thiện, trẻ con chơi cùng nhau và mọi người tôn trọng láng giềng </p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là viii</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,15,NULL,0,1043),
