echnical side if I were you. If you start describing mechanical stuff, people will switch off. I think it''s more interesting to look at the impact Stone Point had on the people''s lives at the time. I mean, for example, there were about 25 years when they used local prisoners to build the tunnels and the underground rooms. They lived there too. Yeah, I guess if we can find some firsthand accounts. (25-30) OK, so let''s make a checklist of things to do. For the Early Maori Inhabitation section, we' AS nvarchar(max))+N' have to look at the material we''ve used again and make sure we know who the writers were and when they wrote it. Yes, that needs work. And for the part about Stone Point being used as a lookout point, I''m sure we can locate some drawings of how Stone Point looked then and the kind of ships coming in. Nice. And what else? We haven''t got a lot of detail for the reconstruction of the fouth. We. should add some more information about what it was the prisoners were adding to it. OK, I''ll do that bit too. I''ll deal with the section regarding the modernisation that happened in the 1930s and 40s. 00:05:06 I mean, that''s the bit where we have the most visible evidence of historic buildings. I''ll ring the Department of Conservation and see if they''ll agree to let me film the sight, maybe allow me access to some of the tunnels the public don''t see. OK, for the 1950s onwards, could you also arrange a meeting with someone from the Department of Conservation to ask them about their restoration work? I could try. Oh, and just about its use as a public. park today. Where is aboundary it exactly? Does it go all the way to the Not sure; I''ll check that out. Great! I suppose it would finish off the presentation nicely if we explain the future plans for the site.</p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-4/iL.VOL4.3.S1024.PART3.mp3',NULL,1,0,3,NULL,0,1024),
(N'003e7e5b-d148-57d5-8a99-edd197c7eb6a',N'97c8d32d-36ad-59d7-8007-e9fbc7338e55',0,2,18,N'<p>Choose the correct letter, <span>A</span>, <span>B</span> or <span>C</span>.</p>',N'',N'',N'',N'Stone Point: A New Zealand historical site',1,0,1,NULL,0,1024),
(N'cfd5b9a9-b8ff-5e37-8e09-12a987dd3529',N'003e7e5b-d148-57d5-8a99-edd197c7eb6a',0,3,19,N'<p>According to Liz, Stone Point played a key role in local history because</p>',N'<p>Câu hỏi: Theo Liz, Stone Point quan trọng vì lý do gì? → Đáp án đúng A. Defence or attack purposes. </p><p>- Giải thích: Stone Point đóng vai trò quân sự phòng thủ và tấn công. </p><ul><li><p>Đáp án B sai vì không có thông tin “điểm hạ cánh đầu tiên”. </p></li><li><p>Đáp án C sai vì không nhắc đến “commercial port”. </p><p>Key vocab: shelter from attack, launch an attack.</p></li></ul>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,21,NULL,0,1024),
(N'3b3fa699-cc03-5f73-80fb-4506c35f28d3',N'003e7e5b-d148-57d5-8a99-edd197c7eb6a',0,3,19,N'<p>Scott and Liz agree that Maori originally chose to inhabit Stone Point because of</p>',N'<p>Câu hỏi: Người Māori ban đầu chọn Stone Point vì lý do nào?→ Đáp án đúng B. the supply of fish. -Soil chỉ được công nhận sau vài mùa vụ. -&gt; no rich soil - Không có bằng chứng về building materials. </p><p>Key vocab: initially, fishing opportunities.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,22,NULL,0,1024),
(N'1f6ef77b-895d-5ca6-b2e0-fc221f37d7e7',N'003e7e5b-d148-57d5-8a99-edd197c7eb6a',0,3,19,N'<p>Scott and Liz agree that using Maori terminology in their presentation</p>',N'<p>Câu hỏi: Về việc dùng từ Māori trong thuyết trình, họ đồng ý điều gì? → Đáp án đúng C. would be best avoided.</p><p>- Họ thấy thú vị nhưng không đủ thời gian giải thích, sinh viên quốc tế khó theo dõi.</p><p>Đáp án A sai vì không dùng cho international students ở đây. Đáp án B sai vì không bắt buộc cho nghiên cứu.</p><p>- Key vocab: keep ... terminology out, won’t be able to follow.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,23,NULL,0,1024),
(N'4f270481-46b8-5a58-bce4-9376d02ad3f2',N'003e7e5b-d148-57d5-8a99-edd197c7eb6a',0,3,19,N'<p>When Scott mentions the engines at Stone Point, Liz advises him to</p>',N'<p>Câu hỏi: Khi Scott nhắc tới động cơ ở Stone Point, Liz khuyên gì? → Đáp án đúng A. focus on the human aspect instead. - Đáp án B sai vì không nói “check accuracy of dates”. - Đáp án C sai vì không đề cập “explain complex technical language”. </p><p>Key vocab: impact on people’s lives, switch off.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,24,NULL,0,1024),
(N'fedf1d92-9355-5646-86bd-e4ad5c12f19e',N'97c8d32d-36ad-59d7-8007-e9fbc7338e55',0,2,18,N'<p>Choose <span>SIX</span> answers from the box and write the correct letter, <span>A–H</span>, next to questions 25–30.</p>',N'',N'',N'',N'What do Liz and Scott agree they must do for each of the following sections of their presentation on Stone Point?',15,0,2,NULL,0,1024),
(N'fb5c8680-372a-57c4-884a-9fb5e2937d49',N'fedf1d92-9355-5646-86bd-e4ad5c12f19e',0,3,19,N'<p>Early Maori inhabitation of Stone Point</p>',N'<p>- Nói rõ cần make sure who the writers were and when they wrote it → phải check authors’ details.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,25,NULL,0,1024),
(N'0557e286-8aa4-58a7-916d-9371762b1425',N'fedf1d92-9355-5646-86bd-e4ad5c12f19e',0,3,19,N'<p>The use of Stone Point as a lookout point</p>',N'<p>- Nhắc đến drawings (hình vẽ) → tức là cần find images.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,26,NULL,0,1024),
(N'0e78fe2c-4a30-5f2b-b43d-a4f93f101759',N'fedf1d92-9355-5646-86bd-e4ad5c12f19e',0,3,19,N'<p>The reconstruction of the fort</p>',N'<p>- Nói rõ haven’t got a lot of detailvà should add more information → phải provide further description.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,27,NULL,0,1024),
(N'b2b164bc-71db-5e9d-ae16-b4057c57762c',N'fedf1d92-9355-5646-86bd-e4ad5c12f19e',0,3,19,N'<p>Modernisation of the fort in the 1930s–40s</p>',N'<p>Nhắc đến agree to let me film và allow me access → cần obtain official permission.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,28,NULL,0,1024),
(N'6a04c53e-6ed9-5503-aaa5-8f90b19ac056',N'fedf1d92-9355-5646-86bd-e4ad5c12f19e',0,3,19,N'<p>Uses of Stone Point from 1950s to the present day</p>',N'<p>Arrange a meeting with someone → chính là set up an interview.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,29,NULL,0,1024),
(N'820561ec-449f-588c-8c82-89ed690688d8',N'fedf1d92-9355-5646-86bd-e4ad5c12f19e',0,3,19,N'<p>The use of Stone Point as a public park</p>',N'<p>- Nhắc đến boundary và check that out → cần check the exact location.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,30,NULL,0,1024),
(N'6e916c84-7751-5a85-86d3-c1b0e2e2a29f',N'6e3fb186-c29c-5dbb-b888-512eb1cb6485',0,1,15,(CAST(N'<h2>[VOL 4] Jatropha - a new biofuel</h2><p>(31-40) Good afternoon. As you know, the world is running out of fossil fuels; that is, crude oil, coal, and natural gas. As an alternative, certain plants are now being considered as biofuels, which are fuels made from organic plant material. These are possible sources of energy once the fossil fuels have gone forever. Well, one such plant goes by the name of Jatropha. It was first a native of Central America, and it''s now found across the world. A few things that make this plant especially attractive are that it can survive in very poor quality, infertile soil, as it does, for example, alongside train tracks in India on the line between Mumbai and Deli. And for up to three years, it''s resistant to drought. 00:01:58 That''s right, it can do without rain for that long. And even if it''s not actually a plant that people can eat, it''s still worth having it on your land as it prevents erosion. And we looked at the dangerous consequences of that in a previous lecture. Furthermore, Jatropha seeds can be slowly distilled to produce diesel oil, and it''s this kind of fuel of that''s of interest to scientists. and power companies. After processing, the seeds can yield up to four times the oil that soybean can and ten times the amount compared to corn. So you can see why it''s causing such interest. And not much is wasted in the processing procedure either. After the oil has been extracted from seeds, the residue is processed into biomass, which can run power stations, which in turn can provide electricity for thousands of local homes. Also, whereas our fossil fuels cannot be replaced, the energy produced by biofuels such as Jatropha is renewable. It''s not going to run out because the plants just go on growing. 00:03:09 There''s no doubt that it is remarkable plant and one that has been very beneficial to man. In various African communities, it''s been used to operate water pumps and refrigerate medicines. It can be used to produce candles or as a fencing plant to keep some animals enclosed and some animals out. It can also treat a number of health problems; for example, the boiled leaves can do much to relieve the suffering of people with malaria, and some jatropha species have seeds which are used to treat digestion problems. Anyway, that''s not what the European corporations who are buying vast amounts of land for jatropha plantations are focusing on. They claim that people who are dependent on rural economies, will benefit fr' AS nvarchar(max))+N'om growing jatropha, and that it will help them bring an end to poverty by providing a long-term local industry. They Also, point out that few or no modifications would be necessary in modern diesel engines since they were originally designed to run on biofuels such as peanut oil and ethanol anyway. Of course, when the plants are burnt, they release carbon dioxide, but they absorb great amounts when they''re growing, making them a considerably greener alternative to fossil fuels. But Not everyone shares the excitement over jatropha nor other biofuels. In Western Australia, jatropha. has in fact been banned since the seeds of some species are toxic, and it only takes three or four to kill a person. and Animals are also very vulnerable. Furthermore, sceptics also point out that as there are many species of jatropha, its oil productivity is unreliable. Beside From this, critics of jatropha and other biofuels claim that farmers now have a strong economic incentive to grow them rather than food crops. 00:05:05 Poor countries would be particularly affected because they would have to rely on imported foods to survive, and people would end up having to pay greatly inflated prices for basic foods. There''s also the concern over Environmental damage in order to provide land for palm oil or sugarcane plantations, for instance, companies are cutting down vast areas of rainforest, which can never be replaced, and this in turn results in the disappearance of wildlife which depended on that habitat. You can also imagine that such deforestation makes a considerable contribution to global warming. Furthermore, opponents also reject the idea that biofuels are a carbon-neutral source of energy.</p>'),(CAST(N'<p>(31-40) Good afternoon. As you know, the world is running out of fossil fuels; that is, crude oil, coal, and natural gas. As an alternative, certain plants are now being considered as biofuels, which are fuels made from organic plant material. These are possible sources of energy once the fossil fuels have gone forever. Well, one such plant goes by the name of Jatropha. It was first a native of Central America, and it''s now found across the world. A few things that make this plant especially attractive are that it can survive in very poor quality, infertile soil, as it does, for example, alongside train tracks in India on the line between Mumbai and Deli. And for up to three years, it''s resistant to drought. 00:01:58 That''s right, it can do without rain for that long. And even if it''s not actually a plant that people can eat, it''s still worth having it on your land as it prevents erosion. And we looked at the dangerous consequences of that in a previous lecture. Furthermore, Jatropha seeds can be slowly distilled to produce diesel oil, and it''s this kind of fuel of that''s of interest to scientists. and power companies. After processing, the seeds can yield up to four times the oil that soybean can and ten times the amount compared to corn. So you can see why it''s causing such interest. And not much is wasted in the processing procedure either. After the oil has been extracted from seeds, the residue is processed into biomass, which can run power stations, which in turn can provide electricity for thousands of local homes. Also, whereas our fossil fuels cannot be replaced, the energy produced by biofuels such as Jatropha is renewable. It''s not going to run out because the plants just go on growing. 00:03:09 There''s no doubt that it is remarkable plant and one that has been very beneficial to man. In various African communities, it''s been used to operate water pumps and refrigerate medicines. It can be used to produce candles or as a fencing plant to keep some animals enclosed and some animals out. It can also treat a number of health problems; for example, the boiled leaves can do much to relieve the suffering of people with malaria, and some jatropha species have seeds which are used to treat digestion problems. Anyway, that''s not what the European corporations who are buying vast amounts of land for jatropha plantations are focusing on. They claim that people who are dependent on rural economies, will benefit from growing jatropha, and that it will hel' AS nvarchar(max))+N'p them bring an end to poverty by providing a long-term local industry. They Also, point out that few or no modifications would be necessary in modern diesel engines since they were originally designed to run on biofuels such as peanut oil and ethanol anyway. Of course, when the plants are burnt, they release carbon dioxide, but they absorb great amounts when they''re growing, making them a considerably greener alternative to fossil fuels. But Not everyone shares the excitement over jatropha nor other biofuels. In Western Australia, jatropha. has in fact been banned since the seeds of some species are toxic, and it only takes three or four to kill a person. and Animals are also very vulnerable. Furthermore, sceptics also point out that as there are many species of jatropha, its oil productivity is unreliable. Beside From this, critics of jatropha and other biofuels claim that farmers now have a strong economic incentive to grow them rather than food crops. 00:05:05 Poor countries would be particularly affected because they would have to rely on imported foods to survive, and people would end up having to pay greatly inflated prices for basic foods. There''s also the concern over Environmental damage in order to provide land for palm oil or sugarcane plantations, for instance, companies are cutting down vast areas of rainforest, which can never be replaced, and this in turn results in the disappearance of wildlife which depended on that habitat. You can also imagine that such deforestation makes a considerable contribution to global warming. Furthermore, opponents also reject the idea that biofuels are a carbon-neutral source of energy.</p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-4/iL.VOL4.3.S1024.PART4.mp3',NULL,1,0,4,NULL,0,1024),
(N'2448b1ea-51dd-52e4-8aaf-ac6d088a1bcf',N'6e916c84-7751-5a85-86d3-c1b0e2e2a29f',0,2,18,N'<p>Complete the notes below.
Write <span>NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS</span> for each answer.</p>',N'',N'',N'',N'Jatropha – a new biofuel',11,0,1,NULL,0,1024),
(N'be7570a1-0003-5cdd-92f2-665d588b1406',N'2448b1ea-51dd-52e4-8aaf-ac6d088a1bcf',0,3,19,N'<h3>Jatropha – a new biofuel</h3><table border="1"><tbody><tr><td><p><span>Plant facts</span></p> <p>The plant jatropha</p> <p>• is originally from Central America</p> <p>• can grow in poor }{SPACE}{ </p> <p>• can survive }{SPACE}{ for several years</p> <p>• can stop }{SPACE}{ of land</p> <p><span>Its seeds</span></p> <p>• can be used to produce diesel oil</p> <p>• produce far more fuel than soybean or }{SPACE}{ </p> <p>• leave a residue after processing – used to make electricity</p> <p>• produce energy which is renewable, unlike fossil fuels</p> <p><span>Uses of jatropha in Africa</span></p> <p>• for water pumps and fridges</p> <p>• made into }{SPACE}{ </p> <p>• used as fencing</p> <p>• the }{SPACE}{ are boiled and used to treat malaria</p> <p>• for problems with }{SPACE}{ </p> <p><span>European companies’ claims about Jatropha</span></p> <p>• It could help stop poverty among rural populations</p> <p>• It could be used in current diesel engines</p> <p>• The plants use up lots of }{SPACE}{ </p> <p><span>Problems with jatropha</span></p> <p>• some seeds are toxic to people and animals</p> <p>• unreliable oil productivity</p> <p><span>Other criticisms of biofuels</span></p> <p>Widespread production of biofuels could result in:</p> <p>• high food prices in poor countries</p> <p>• environmental damage caused by loss of rainforest and }{SPACE}{ </p> <p>• adding to the problem of }{SPACE}{ </p></td></tr></tbody></table>',N'<p>- Câu hỏi: “Jatropha can grow in poor ...” → cần danh từ chỉ môi trường đất. </p><p>- Script nhắc rõ poor quality, infertile soil → điền soil.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,31,NULL,0,1024),
(N'f2660727-9d1f-5e4d-a9a7-d74d1020b670',N'2448b1ea-51dd-52e4-8aaf-ac6d088a1bcf',0,3,19,N'Question number 32',N'<p>Câu hỏi: “Jatropha can survive ... for several years.” → cần chỉ điều kiện khắc nghiệt.</p><p>Script: resistant to drought ... do without rain → đáp án là drought.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,32,NULL,0,1024),
(N'eb25b0bd-411a-5f92-b492-fd85b2c110d1',N'2448b1ea-51dd-52e4-8aaf-ac6d088a1bcf',0,3,19,N'Question number 33',N'<p>- Câu hỏi: “Jatropha can stop ... of land.” </p><p>- Script nhắc prevents erosion → điền erosion.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,33,NULL,0,1024),
(N'c2af9c44-9552-54a1-8faf-e9881bcba01b',N'2448b1ea-51dd-52e4-8aaf-ac6d088a1bcf',0,3,19,N'Question number 34',N'<p>- Câu hỏi: “Produce more fuel than soybean or ...” </p><p>- Script so sánh với corn → đáp án corn.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,34,NULL,0,1024),
(N'860c05c5-accf-5501-9aed-382ad44bb1bf',N'2448b1ea-51dd-52e4-8aaf-ac6d088a1bcf',0,3,19,N'Question number 35',N'<p>- Câu hỏi: “Made into ...” </p><p>- Script nêu rõ produce candles → đáp án candles.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,35,NULL,0,1024),
(N'ddf1859f-d826-5d39-a95f-3be691b4cfa0',N'2448b1ea-51dd-52e4-8aaf-ac6d088a1bcf',0,3,19,N'Question number 36',N'<p>- Câu hỏi: “The ... are boiled and used to treat malaria.” </p><p>- Script khẳng định boiled leaves treat malaria → điền leaves.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,36,NULL,0,1024),
(N'b4ec954f-cac3-5eea-bf96-95ef06e0741e',N'2448b1ea-51dd-52e4-8aaf-ac6d088a1bcf',0,3,19,N'Question number 37',N'<p>- Câu hỏi: “For problems with ...” </p><p>- Script nhắc seeds treat digestion problems → điền digestion.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,37,NULL,0,1024),
(N'a889a931-8fef-58d7-ba61-959ebabee491',N'2448b1ea-51dd-52e4-8aaf-ac6d088a1bcf',0,3,19,N'Question number 38',N'<p>- Câu hỏi: “The plants use up lots of ...” </p><p>- Script: absorb great amounts of carbon dioxide → điền carbon dioxide.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,38,NULL,0,1024),
(N'c20a1714-7e5e-5594-b375-1f4dfb55d687',N'2448b1ea-51dd-52e4-8aaf-ac6d088a1bcf',0,3,19,N'Question number 39',N'<p>- Câu hỏi: “Environmental damage caused by loss of rainforest and ...” </p><p>- Script: disappearance of wildlife → đáp án wildlife.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,39,NULL,0,1024),
(N'c109768e-e960-561d-8f24-b75a55bb3483',N'2448b1ea-51dd-52e4-8aaf-ac6d088a1bcf',0,3,19,N'Question number 40',N'<p>- Câu hỏi: “Adding to the problem of ...” </p><p>- Script: contribution to global warming→ điền global warming.</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,40,NULL,0,1024),
(N'9fffd850-a933-505c-9eb5-96ff08f8a192',NULL,0,0,11,NULL,NULL,NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-5/iL.VOL5.7.S1018.mp3',N'Vol 5 LISTENING FULL TEST 7',0,7,1,NULL,1,1018),
(N'b16fd13f-cce5-5266-9cd4-576f1beb867b',N'9fffd850-a933-505c-9eb5-96ff08f8a192',0,1,13,(CAST(N'<h2>Medical Helpline Enquiry Customer Information Sheet</h2><p><span><span>Now turn to section 1. Section 1, you will hear a telephone conversation between a doctor at a medical advice helpline and a man who has a problem. First, you have some time to look at questions 1 to 6. You will see that there is an example that has been done for you. On this occasion only, the conversation relating to this will be played first.</span></span></p><p>Hello, this is Medical Help Direct. How can I help you? Oh, hello. I''ve got a problem with my back. And with it being the middle of the night, I can''t go to the doctor. And I wonder if you can give me some advice. Certainly. But first, can I have your telephone number, please? It''s 03786-439-251. The man''s telephone number is 03786-439-251. So, 03786-439-251 has been written in the space.</p><p><span><span>Now we shall begin. You should answer the questions as you listen because you will not hear the recording a second time. Listen carefully and answer questions 1 to 6.</span></span></p><p>Hello, this is Medical Help Direct. How can I help you? Oh, hello. I''ve got a problem with my back. And with it being the middle of the night, I can''t go to the doctor. And I wonder if you can give me some advice. Certainly. But first, can I have your telephone number, please? It''s 03786-439-251. Okay. And if you could give me your first name, please. Right. And your surname. It''s Rydyard. That''s R-I-D-Y-A-R-D. And now your address, please. It''s 27 Station Road. Okay. Moortown. And do you need the postcode? Yes, please. D-P-1-7-5-H-J. And your date of birth. The 25th of February, 1975. Fine. Now I just need to take details of your doctor. </p><p>She''s called Dr. Craven. And the surgery? It''s Moortown Health Center. Thanks. Now, can you tell me a bit more about what the problem is? Well, like I said, it''s my back. Okay. Can you tell me which part of the back? Lower. And have you had any problems with your back before? Yes. I had a bit of trouble last year, in June, I think. Or was it July? No. We went on holiday the beginning of July, and it had cleared up by then. And when did it start this time? Has it just come on? No. I''ve had it, let''s see, since Monday. So that''s three days now. But it wasn''t too bad at first. I mean, I could just about get around, though I couldn''t drive the car or anything. Then this afternoon, the pain suddenly got so bad that I went to bed. I''ve been there ever since, but that hasn''t helped. And do you have any' AS nvarchar(max))+N' pain elsewhere? In your stomach or abdomen, for example? No.</p><p><span><span>Before you hear the rest of the conversation, you have some time to look at questions 7 to 10. Now listen and answer questions 7 to 10.</span></span></p><p>OK. Now, have you any idea what caused the problem? Well, I was tidying up my office, and I lifted a box up from the floor that was heavier than I thought. And I think that''s what did it. Yes, it''s easily done, isn''t it? So, you''re in bed now. Yes. Have you tried applying heat to the back? Yes, I''ve got a hot water bottle. That''s usually the first thing I try. And have you taken any painkillers? Yes. And other than that, you feel quite well? I do, yes. Right. Now, I cannot diagnose or prescribe any medication, but I can offer you some advice. One thing you could do now is to see if ice makes any difference. That sometimes helps. But don''t put it directly onto your skin. Wrap it up in a towel or something, and don''t leave it on for longer than 20 minutes. </p><p>Oh, right. I haven''t tried that before. It can be useful sometimes. Now, have you seen your doctor about this? No. I just thought, well, everyone has back pain, but I''ve never had it as bad as this before. I think you should go and see your doctor tomorrow, and she may be able to give you something to help. Okay, I''ll do that. I''m actually feeling a bit better now. Good. And you might get some advice from her about exercise. That''s often the best way of dealing with this sort of problem. Okay, I''ll ask her. Right. Now, if you''re worried about anything before tomorrow, you can always phone back. Our lines are open 24 hours.</p>'),(CAST(N'<p><span><span>Now turn to section 1. Section 1, you will hear a telephone conversation between a doctor at a medical advice helpline and a man who has a problem. First, you have some time to look at questions 1 to 6. You will see that there is an example that has been done for you. On this occasion only, the conversation relating to this will be played first.</span></span></p><p>Hello, this is Medical Help Direct. How can I help you? Oh, hello. I''ve got a problem with my back. And with it being the middle of the night, I can''t go to the doctor. And I wonder if you can give me some advice. Certainly. But first, can I have your telephone number, please? It''s 03786-439-251. The man''s telephone number is 03786-439-251. So, 03786-439-251 has been written in the space.</p><p><span><span>Now we shall begin. You should answer the questions as you listen because you will not hear the recording a second time. Listen carefully and answer questions 1 to 6.</span></span></p><p>Hello, this is Medical Help Direct. How can I help you? Oh, hello. I''ve got a problem with my back. And with it being the middle of the night, I can''t go to the doctor. And I wonder if you can give me some advice. Certainly. But first, can I have your telephone number, please? It''s 03786-439-251. Okay. And if you could give me your first name, please. Right. And your surname. It''s Rydyard. That''s R-I-D-Y-A-R-D. And now your address, please. It''s 27 Station Road. Okay. Moortown. And do you need the postcode? Yes, please. D-P-1-7-5-H-J. And your date of birth. The 25th of February, 1975. Fine. Now I just need to take details of your doctor. </p><p>She''s called Dr. Craven. And the surgery? It''s Moortown Health Center. Thanks. Now, can you tell me a bit more about what the problem is? Well, like I said, it''s my back. Okay. Can you tell me which part of the back? Lower. And have you had any problems with your back before? Yes. I had a bit of trouble last year, in June, I think. Or was it July? No. We went on holiday the beginning of July, and it had cleared up by then. And when did it start this time? Has it just come on? No. I''ve had it, let''s see, since Monday. So that''s three days now. But it wasn''t too bad at first. I mean, I could just about get around, though I couldn''t drive the car or anything. Then this afternoon, the pain suddenly got so bad that I went to bed. I''ve been there ever since, but that hasn''t helped. And do you have any pain elsewhere? In your stomach or abdomen, for example? No' AS nvarchar(max))+N'.</p><p><span><span>Before you hear the rest of the conversation, you have some time to look at questions 7 to 10. Now listen and answer questions 7 to 10.</span></span></p><p>OK. Now, have you any idea what caused the problem? Well, I was tidying up my office, and I lifted a box up from the floor that was heavier than I thought. And I think that''s what did it. Yes, it''s easily done, isn''t it? So, you''re in bed now. Yes. Have you tried applying heat to the back? Yes, I''ve got a hot water bottle. That''s usually the first thing I try. And have you taken any painkillers? Yes. And other than that, you feel quite well? I do, yes. Right. Now, I cannot diagnose or prescribe any medication, but I can offer you some advice. One thing you could do now is to see if ice makes any difference. That sometimes helps. But don''t put it directly onto your skin. Wrap it up in a towel or something, and don''t leave it on for longer than 20 minutes. </p><p>Oh, right. I haven''t tried that before. It can be useful sometimes. Now, have you seen your doctor about this? No. I just thought, well, everyone has back pain, but I''ve never had it as bad as this before. I think you should go and see your doctor tomorrow, and she may be able to give you something to help. Okay, I''ll do that. I''m actually feeling a bit better now. Good. And you might get some advice from her about exercise. That''s often the best way of dealing with this sort of problem. Okay, I''ll ask her. Right. Now, if you''re worried about anything before tomorrow, you can always phone back. Our lines are open 24 hours.</p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-5/iL.VOL5.7.S1018.PART1.mp3',NULL,1,0,1,NULL,0,1018),
(N'92e91bab-6753-5bba-b285-425abe26a755',N'b16fd13f-cce5-5266-9cd4-576f1beb867b',0,2,18,N'<p>Complete the notes below.
Write <span>ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER</span> for each answer.</p>',N'',N'',N'',N'Medical Helpline Enquiry Customer Information Sheet',11,0,1,NULL,0,1018),
(N'ebb4f23d-3bae-5c11-9a3b-717d9e1c8407',N'92e91bab-6753-5bba-b285-425abe26a755',0,3,19,N'<h3>Medical Helpline Enquiry Customer Information Sheet</h3><table border="1"><tbody><tr><td><p><span>Example:</span> telephone: 03786 439 251</p> <p><span>Full Name:</span> Wright }{SPACE}{ </p> <p><span>Address:</span> }{SPACE}{ Road, Mortown, DP175HJ</p> <p><span>Date of Birth:</span> }{SPACE}{ 1975</p> <p><span>Current position of pain:</span> }{SPACE}{ back</p> <p>The pain started to hurt since }{SPACE}{ ago</p> <p><span>Time the pain got worse:</span> today''s }{SPACE}{ </p> <p><span>Why got hurt:</span> lifting a heavy }{SPACE}{ </p> <p><span>Methods applied to ease the pain:</span></p> <p>- put water bottle on the back</p> <p>- took some }{SPACE}{ </p> <p><span>Suggestion for the patient: </span>use }{SPACE}{ to see if it works.</p> <p>The doctor will give him some advice on }{SPACE}{ </p> <p>The line is open 24 hours.</p></td></tr></tbody></table>',N'<p>- Đáp án là Ridyard. Trong form đã cho sẵn “Wright”, đây là first name, nên chỗ trống cần điền surname. </p><p>- Người đàn ông đánh vần rất rõ họ của mình để tránh nhầm lẫn. </p><p>- Key words: surname; Ridyard</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,1,NULL,0,1018),
(N'7b1515f3-82bc-51a5-9800-673efda4c44b',N'92e91bab-6753-5bba-b285-425abe26a755',0,3,19,N'Question number 2',N'<p>- Đáp án là Station. Đề đã cho sẵn từ “Road”, nên chỉ cần điền tên đường. </p><p>- Người nói cung cấp địa chỉ đầy đủ ngay sau khi được hỏi. </p><p>- Key words: address; Station Road</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,2,NULL,0,1018),
(N'd08d33d3-2040-5a32-86b0-2bd9fb48b40a',N'92e91bab-6753-5bba-b285-425abe26a755',0,3,19,N'Question number 3',N'<p>- Đáp án là 25th February. Câu hỏi chỉ yêu cầu ngày sinh, vì năm 1975 đã có sẵn trong form. </p><p>- Người nói nêu rõ ngày - tháng - năm theo thứ tự. </p><p>- Key words: </p><p>+ date of birth</p><p>+ 25th</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,3,NULL,0,1018),
(N'c5b03a8f-a2bb-5b27-b11b-4ef8fb30e778',N'92e91bab-6753-5bba-b285-425abe26a755',0,3,19,N'Question number 4',N'<p>- Đáp án là lower. </p><p>- Bác sĩ hỏi cụ thể vị trí đau trên lưng và người đàn ông trả lời ngắn gọn “Lower”, tức là lưng dưới. </p><p>- Key words: which part; lower back</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,4,NULL,0,1018),
(N'b39c4eae-99ba-558c-8890-397bbb9efded',N'92e91bab-6753-5bba-b285-425abe26a755',0,3,19,N'Question number 5',N'<p>- Đáp án là three. </p><p>- Người đàn ông quy đổi trực tiếp từ “since Monday” sang khoảng thời gian là three days. </p><p>- Đề hỏi “how long ago”, nên đáp án là số ngày. </p><p>- Key words: since Monday; three days</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,5,NULL,0,1018),
(N'f78b36b0-6a9d-5e6b-86f6-164bc1978aec',N'92e91bab-6753-5bba-b285-425abe26a755',0,3,19,N'Question number 6',N'<p>- Đáp án là afternoon. Người nói chỉ rõ thời điểm trong ngày khi cơn đau trở nên nghiêm trọng hơn. </p><p>- Từ “today’s” trong đề giúp xác định rõ mốc thời gian. </p><p>- Key words: this afternoon; pain got worse</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,6,NULL,0,1018),
(N'574c0d5e-3bc9-5471-839e-47939ebbd343',N'92e91bab-6753-5bba-b285-425abe26a755',0,3,19,N'Question number 7',N'<p>- Đáp án là box. Nguyên nhân chấn thương được xác định là do nâng một chiếc hộp nặng. </p><p>- Danh từ “box” xuất hiện trực tiếp sau động từ lifted. </p><p>- Key words: lifting; heavy box</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,7,NULL,0,1018),
(N'9ba9854f-2860-5f56-94fb-41d797f85900',N'92e91bab-6753-5bba-b285-425abe26a755',0,3,19,N'Question number 8',N'<p>- Đáp án là painkillers. </p><p>- Bác sĩ hỏi trực tiếp về việc dùng thuốc giảm đau và người đàn ông xác nhận đã dùng. Đề yêu cầu ONE WORD nên giữ nguyên dạng số nhiều. </p><p>- Key words: taken; painkillers</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,8,NULL,0,1018),
(N'8025c61b-1aac-589b-8c5b-e07f7bbfda42',N'92e91bab-6753-5bba-b285-425abe26a755',0,3,19,N'Question number 9',N'<p>- Đáp án là ice. Bác sĩ đưa ra lời khuyên cụ thể là thử dùng đá lạnh để giảm đau. </p><p>- Đây là phương pháp mới mà bệnh nhân chưa thử trước đó. </p><p>- Key words: advice; ice</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,9,NULL,0,1018),
(N'da5054f4-bac8-517f-aa35-e76524db3ab8',N'92e91bab-6753-5bba-b285-425abe26a755',0,3,19,N'Question number 10',N'<p>- Đáp án là exercise. </p><p>- Bác sĩ cho biết khi gặp bác sĩ riêng, bệnh nhân có thể được tư vấn về tập luyện, được xem là cách điều trị lâu dài hiệu quả. - Key words: advice; exercise</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,10,NULL,0,1018),
(N'49a82ec0-a146-58c0-9856-3385986e3f9b',N'9fffd850-a933-505c-9eb5-96ff08f8a192',0,1,14,(CAST(N'<h2>[VOL 5] Test 7 - Section 2</h2><p><span><span>Listen and answer questions 11 to 15.</span></span></p><p>Welcome to the Global Museum, located at the heart of this truly multicultural city, which is home to more than 60 different nationalities. The museum has a number of exciting displays and exhibitions, and this audio guide is designed to help you make the most of your visit. Altogether, the museum has 18 different galleries, and this season sees the opening of three new exhibitions. We recommend that you begin your tour by visiting this season''s highlights. The Heritage Clothes exhibition is located in Gallery 5 of the museum. People who live in the area have spent two years preparing this exhibition, which brings together some of the fascinating garments traditionally worn in their own communities. </p><p>They research the history of their community''s clothing traditions and the customs and rituals associated with them. Altogether, 16 countries are represented from Ghana to Korea, from Turkey to Nepal. The photographs that accompany each display case were taken by some of the city''s college students who are studying design and show the clothes being modelled by the real people who wear them in the course of their everyday lives. Another highlight of the season is the exhibition called Toys from the Past, which can be found This exhibition, which will appeal to people of all ages, is on tour throughout the country and will be here for 10 weeks only. </p><p>The exhibits include dolls made over 100 years ago with beautiful porcelain faces and, in some cases, real hair. The collection covers the favourite toys, such as wooden train sets from many different generations, and provides plenty of interests for children and adults. The gigantic board games, which are laid out on the gallery floor, are one of the most popular activities in the exhibition and should not be missed. This exhibition concludes with the special display of miniature toys. These small objects are on loan from countries all over the world and, in some cases, measure no more than a few centimetres. There is a tiny car made from matchsticks, a toy aeroplane completed with pilot and passengers made out of seashells, and some exquisite little buildings no higher than 4 centimetres.</p><p><span><span>Before you hear the rest of the conversation, you have some time to look at questions 16 to 20. Now listen and answer questions 16 to 20.</span></span></p><p>The final gallery highlight of the ' AS nvarchar(max))+N'season is the Biscuit Gallery, number 15. Many years ago, this city was famous for its biscuits, although today the factory no longer exists. Did you know, for example, that before biscuits were packed in paper or cardboard boxes, biscuit tins were fashion items? The factory made tins round, square, triangular, hexagonal for a whole range of different occasions to celebrate national events, festivals, famous phases and so on. One fascinating display deals with people''s favourite biscuits. There are sweet biscuits and savoury ones, biscuits filled with jam and biscuits filled with currants, biscuits with pink, yellow and white sugar icing or coloured sugar flowers. When the factory finally closed, it announced that people''s favourite biscuit was not, as you might expect, a chocolate biscuit or one filled with jam and cream, but a plain savoury one which was eaten with cheese. </p><p>When you get to the end of the exhibition, there is an entertaining hands-on activity to fill your own biscuit tin. All the biscuits ever produced by the company are piled up on the table along with various tins. The biscuits are made out of thin pieces of wood, but the weight, colours and shapes replicate the original biscuits. Your job is to fill a tin with biscuits so that when the lid is taken off, they sit there as neatly as they did when the job was done by machine. It is not as easy as it looks. If you would like to buy a moment of your visit, there is a museum gift shop selling postcards, souvenirs and handmade pottery next to the information desk on the ground floor. And finally, if you don''t want to carry your coats and bags around with you during your visit, please make use of the free lockers provided by the museum. Enjoy your visit.</p><p><span><span>That is the end of part 2. You now have half a minute to check your answers.</span></span></p>'),(CAST(N'<p><span><span>Listen and answer questions 11 to 15.</span></span></p><p>Welcome to the Global Museum, located at the heart of this truly multicultural city, which is home to more than 60 different nationalities. The museum has a number of exciting displays and exhibitions, and this audio guide is designed to help you make the most of your visit. Altogether, the museum has 18 different galleries, and this season sees the opening of three new exhibitions. We recommend that you begin your tour by visiting this season''s highlights. The Heritage Clothes exhibition is located in Gallery 5 of the museum. People who live in the area have spent two years preparing this exhibition, which brings together some of the fascinating garments traditionally worn in their own communities. </p><p>They research the history of their community''s clothing traditions and the customs and rituals associated with them. Altogether, 16 countries are represented from Ghana to Korea, from Turkey to Nepal. The photographs that accompany each display case were taken by some of the city''s college students who are studying design and show the clothes being modelled by the real people who wear them in the course of their everyday lives. Another highlight of the season is the exhibition called Toys from the Past, which can be found This exhibition, which will appeal to people of all ages, is on tour throughout the country and will be here for 10 weeks only. </p><p>The exhibits include dolls made over 100 year