 with?</span></span></p><p><span>Helen:</span> Well, we have a son, a teenager, who will be coming with us, so we''ll need to find a school for him.</p><p><span>Jason:</span> Sure. What grade will he be in?</p><p><span>Helen:</span> He''s just turned 13, so he should be going into grade 9, but we''ve decided it would be better if he repeats grade 8. <span>Jason:</span> Right, so you''ll need a high school. Now, do you have any preferences regarding the school?</p><p><span>Helen:</span> Well, he''s at a state school at the moment, but the company is prepared to pay his school fees, so we would probably go for a private school if possible. It doesn''t matter if it''s mixed or single sex.</p><p><span>Jason:</span> Sure, I''ll make some enquiries and I''ll send you a short list of possibilities.</p><p><span>Helen:</span> That would be wonderful.</p><p><span>Jason:</span> Oh, can you send me a copy of your son''s report? The latest one, if possible. The schools will want to know something about him as a student. You can fax or scan it to me.</p><p><span>Helen:</span> OK, fine. Jason: Now, is there anything else I can help you with today?</p><p><span>Helen:</span> Yes, there is one other thing. We''d like some information to help us settle into the community and make friends. My son isn''t really into sport, but he''s a keen chess player. He''d like to continue playing when we move to Brisbane. Could you find out about a club for him?</p><p><span>Jason:</span> Certainly, I''ll make enquiries for you.</p><p><span>Helen:</span> And I play the flute, so I''d like to find a band that I could join, if possible.</p><p><span>Jason:</span> Music is very popular here, so that should be easy. </p><p><span>Helen:</span> Thank you for all your help, Jason. </p><p><span>Jason:</span> My pleasure. I''ll be in touch soon.</p><p><span>That is the end of part one. You now have one minute to check your answers to part one.</span></p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-5/iL.VOL5.5.S1016.PART1.mp3',NULL,1,0,1,NULL,0,1016),
