ilt much later. He seems to be emphasising the difference between them. </p><p><span>Tina:</span> Hard to say, but you might be right.</p><p><span>Dave:</span> And then there''s Still Life.</p><p><span>Tina:</span> Right. Do you think that''s the kind of thing he''d have sold or exhibited? </p><p><span>Dave:</span> I don''t know. Maybe not. It was in all likelihood just done to showcase his technique to one of his pupils.</p><p><span>Tina:</span> Ah, right. He worked as an art tutor, did he? </p><p><span>Dave:</span> Yeah. What about the cricketers? It makes living in a village seem really idyllic. - <span>Tina:</span> Right. I imagine things weren''t quite as perfect as they look there. </p><p><span>Dave:</span> No. One of my favourite de wints is The Burning '+N'of the Houses of Parliament.</p><p><span>Tina:</span> Oh, yes. Because that fire actually happened, didn''t it, in 18... </p><p><span>Dave:</span> 34.</p><p><span>Tina:</span> Yes. But unlikely to have been done on site. I mean, it''s quite plausible that he actually witnessed the event and then went back and did it in his studio later.</p><p><span>Dave:</span> Yeah, I guess you''re right. So, what do you think to the... </p><p><span>That is the end of Part 3. You now have 30 seconds to check your answers to Part 3.</span></p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-5/iL.VOL5.4.S1015.PART3.mp3',NULL,1,0,3,NULL,0,1015),
