(N'9bf78c71-b81b-5d21-8ba0-82b809041206',N'1585379a-d36b-5391-9d92-1f5f3c548d8a',0,2,18,N'<p>Choose the correct letter, <span>A</span>, <span>B </span>or <span>C</span></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',1,0,1,NULL,0,1014),
(N'098deae9-0d4e-5950-afbb-38f83061054a',N'9bf78c71-b81b-5d21-8ba0-82b809041206',0,3,19,N'<p>What is the topic of the project?</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là C.
- Ngay từ đầu, Rosie nói rõ dự
án tập trung vào cách sinh viên
sử dụng các cơ sở giải trí, không
chỉ mô tả chung về địa điểm.
- Cụm “how much they use it”
và “how well students use” cho
thấy trọng tâm là mức độ sử
dụng, đúng với lựa chọn C.</p><p>- Key words:
+ how much they use it
+ how well students use</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,21,NULL,0,1014),
(N'34abc3a7-1ab2-5d5f-9708-3fffb95eb336',N'9bf78c71-b81b-5d21-8ba0-82b809041206',0,3,19,N'<p>What is the main aim of the project?</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là A.
- Nhóm nghiên cứu cố ý loại bỏ
giải trí trong khuôn viên trường,
để tập trung vào giải trí bên
ngoài trường đại học.
- Điều này trực tiếp phù hợp với
phương án “entertainment away
from the university”.
- Key words:
+ omitted campus facilities
+ outside entertainment</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,22,NULL,0,1014),
(N'1312a2a9-3180-5b43-81ee-e4612dcb8c32',N'9bf78c71-b81b-5d21-8ba0-82b809041206',0,3,19,N'<p>How about the percentage of cinema seats provided by different cinema
houses?</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là B.</p><p> - Rosie đưa ra số liệu chính xác về tỷ lệ ghế ngồi của từng rạp.</p><p> - Thứ tự và tỷ lệ 75% - 20% </p><p>- 5% khớp hoàn toàn với lựa chọn B. </p><p>- Lựa chọn C là phương án bẫy, lưu ý note ra khi làm bài liên quan tới con số.</p><p> - Key words: </p><p>+ 75% Complex </p><p>+ 20% Park </p><p>+ 5% Odeon</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,23,NULL,0,1014),
(N'f93ac384-57fc-56a2-adcb-c81b0217b3ff',N'9bf78c71-b81b-5d21-8ba0-82b809041206',0,3,19,N'<p>What is the most popular among different cinemas?</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là C.</p><p> - Mike nhấn mạnh yếu tố bất ngờ, cho thấy Odeon mới là rạp được sinh viên chọn nhiều nhất. </p><p>- Đây là thông tin về mức độ phổ biến, không phải quy mô hay số ghế. </p><p>- Key words: </p><p>+ surprisingly </p><p>+ most popular </p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,24,NULL,0,1014),
(N'ce1c026c-a5b1-5b8e-8beb-b76cab67f160',N'9bf78c71-b81b-5d21-8ba0-82b809041206',0,3,19,N'<p>What did Rosie and Mike realise about the two theatres?</p>',N'<p>Đáp án là B.
- Khi so sánh hai nhà hát, họ
nhận ra sinh viên mua vé ở cả
nhà hát và rạp phim
- Thông tin về giá là thông tin
đánh lừa.
- Key words:
+ variety of seat prices
+ buy seats at both</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,25,NULL,0,1014),
(N'14d4733f-8d4f-55bf-a800-79dcfabc7948',N'9bf78c71-b81b-5d21-8ba0-82b809041206',0,3,19,N'<p>What is the comparative attendance for cinema and theatre?</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là A.
- Rosie mô tả rõ sự thay đổi theo
mùa, trong đó theatre đông vào
tháng 11, 12 cinema đông khách
vào tháng 6, 7.
- Điều này trùng khớp với
phương án A.</p><p>- Key words:
+ cinema becomes quite popular
+ June, July</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,26,NULL,0,1014),
(N'ebc8bcf3-0f13-5a2b-8e5f-084d1745f6bc',N'1585379a-d36b-5391-9d92-1f5f3c548d8a',0,2,18,N'<p>What information was given by each writer?
Choose your answers from the box, <span>A, B or C.</span> Write it next to Questions<span> 27-30</span>.</p>',N'',N'',N'',N'Answer choices',15,0,2,NULL,0,1014),
(N'bbbafd9a-46c9-503e-bf29-40e318a34931',N'ebc8bcf3-0f13-5a2b-8e5f-084d1745f6bc',0,3,19,N'<p>The Blues</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là A.
- Blues Club bị đánh giá thấp do
không gian nhỏ và chỗ ngồi hạn
chế.
- Cụm “not a very good rating”
tương ứng với mức poor.
- Key words:
+ didn’t give a very good rating
+ seating was minimal</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,27,NULL,0,1014),
(N'4d05161f-835b-5fa2-9cc3-82eee6d32edc',N'ebc8bcf3-0f13-5a2b-8e5f-084d1745f6bc',0,3,19,N'<p>The Sansue</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là C.
- Sansu được đánh giá cao nhất
với hai dấu tick, tương ứng với
mức excellent.
- Các yếu tố hỗ trợ gồm không
gian lớn, không khí sôi động và
nghệ sĩ tốt.
- Key words:
+ two ticks
+ good performers</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,28,NULL,0,1014),
(N'787ef7b0-fc2e-5e10-a9c6-978e70aaacfd',N'ebc8bcf3-0f13-5a2b-8e5f-084d1745f6bc',0,3,19,N'<p>Pier Hotel</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là B.<br>
- Pier Hotel không quá xuất sắc<br> nhưng cũng không tệ, được đánh giá ở mức trung bình / fine. </p><p>- Từ “reasonable” và “average” là tín hiệu rõ ràng. </p><p>- Key words: </p><p>+ reasonable </p><p>+ average rating</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,29,NULL,0,1014),
(N'b47c1661-7542-52b1-b260-015005c8aa08',N'ebc8bcf3-0f13-5a2b-8e5f-084d1745f6bc',0,3,19,N'<p>Baldrock Café</p>',N'<p>- Đáp án là C.
- Baldrock Café được cho điểm
cao nhất, tương ứng với mức
excellent.
- “Top marks” là paraphrase trực
tiếp của “excellent”.
- Key words:
+ top marks
+ enjoyed ourselves</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,30,NULL,0,1014),
(N'f62c3efe-7153-5cc3-a946-3e5877ac1e3a',N'830d3479-3bb2-5c71-8f82-4c927bad150b',0,1,15,(CAST(N'<h2>Certified Green Buildings</h2><p>Good morning everyone, today I am here to talk about the construction of green buildings. Given the current state of the global environment, new types of architecture, design and construction techniques are absolutely necessary. My brief lecture today will cover two topics. What qualifies a building to receive a green certification and also how widespread such sustainable buildings currently are. There is a growing demand for so-called green buildings. And agencies and corporations around the world understand the sustainable workplaces are quite cost effective in the long run.  </p><p>Though initial outlays for construction are  usually more expensive, the savings in maintenance and energy costs make up for it. Here at the Ministry of Environmental Stewardship we have created a detailed set of requirements that a building must pass in order to be certified as green. For buildings that have already been constructed, we offer two levels of certification, bronze and silver, depending on the number of guidelines implemented. These include reducing or recycling waste products as well as in-storing efficient heating and cooling systems.</p><p> For a gold certification, a building must have had sustainable and environmentally friendly practices from the beginning of this construction. Measures such as using local materials would grow from well-managed forests or reducing the use of toxic chemicals or contribute to all this prestigious distinction. It''s pleasing to see how mainstream-going green is now. Here at the Ministry however, we know and understand that this cannot be just some passing fad. We created these guidelines that institutions could not merely greenwash their buildings, claiming that they are environmentally friendly when in fact they aren''t.  I would now like to talk about some buildings that have received these special certifications. In the 60s there was a great number of public housing projects built. Over the years, many of them have fallen into gross disrepair. As part of an urban revitalization project, construction companies have consulted with Ministry experts to make those council estates a greener and healthier place to live. At Cabrini Fields, lead pipes and lead paint were removed, improving the health of children living there. A system of rooftop and community gardens also helped residents to support themselves. It was one of the first buildings we awarded at Bronze Certification 2. One building wi' AS nvarchar(max))+N'th a silver certification is the Milocture Tower, built over centuries ago and located in the downtown area. </p><p>The insides of the building were completely scooped out, allowing the construction company to implement innovative new ways of saving energy. The utility bill of the entire building is now 40% down, only 60% of its previous level, despite rising energy costs. Lastly, I would like to talk about the latest building to receive a goal certification from the Ministry. Arcadia Arbor''s is a really great example of green engineering and construction. From the very beginning, the project heads made a really unique plan and held to it. Many of the Ministry''s guidelines were followed and we even got ideas for other ways to make buildings sustainable. The centerpiece of this skyscraper is a multi-story hanging garden that serves both an aesthetic and practical purpose.</p>'),(CAST(N'<p>Good morning everyone, today I am here to talk about the construction of green buildings. Given the current state of the global environment, new types of architecture, design and construction techniques are absolutely necessary. My brief lecture today will cover two topics. What qualifies a building to receive a green certification and also how widespread such sustainable buildings currently are. There is a growing demand for so-called green buildings. And agencies and corporations around the world understand the sustainable workplaces are quite cost effective in the long run.  </p><p>Though initial outlays for construction are  usually more expensive, the savings in maintenance and energy costs make up for it. Here at the Ministry of Environmental Stewardship we have created a detailed set of requirements that a building must pass in order to be certified as green. For buildings that have already been constructed, we offer two levels of certification, bronze and silver, depending on the number of guidelines implemented. These include reducing or recycling waste products as well as in-storing efficient heating and cooling systems.</p><p> For a gold certification, a building must have had sustainable and environmentally friendly practices from the beginning of this construction. Measures such as using local materials would grow from well-managed forests or reducing the use of toxic chemicals or contribute to all this prestigious distinction. It''s pleasing to see how mainstream-going green is now. Here at the Ministry however, we know and understand that this cannot be just some passing fad. We created these guidelines that institutions could not merely greenwash their buildings, claiming that they are environmentally friendly when in fact they aren''t.  I would now like to talk about some buildings that have received these special certifications. In the 60s there was a great number of public housing projects built. Over the years, many of them have fallen into gross disrepair. As part of an urban revitalization project, construction companies have consulted with Ministry experts to make those council estates a greener and healthier place to live. At Cabrini Fields, lead pipes and lead paint were removed, improving the health of children living there. A system of rooftop and community gardens also helped residents to support themselves. It was one of the first buildings we awarded at Bronze Certification 2. One building with a silver certification is the M' AS nvarchar(max))+N'ilocture Tower, built over centuries ago and located in the downtown area. </p><p>The insides of the building were completely scooped out, allowing the construction company to implement innovative new ways of saving energy. The utility bill of the entire building is now 40% down, only 60% of its previous level, despite rising energy costs. Lastly, I would like to talk about the latest building to receive a goal certification from the Ministry. Arcadia Arbor''s is a really great example of green engineering and construction. From the very beginning, the project heads made a really unique plan and held to it. Many of the Ministry''s guidelines were followed and we even got ideas for other ways to make buildings sustainable. The centerpiece of this skyscraper is a multi-story hanging garden that serves both an aesthetic and practical purpose.</p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/vol-5/iL.VOL5.3.S1014.PART4.mp3',NULL,1,0,4,NULL,0,1014),
