(N'cd785ea7-f17f-5200-a677-a03b2a607507',N'da971f0a-2f2e-5163-b076-e7760794f89e',0,3,19,N'Question number 10',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Trước hệ thống đường mới, nhiều khu vực của Socotra chỉ có thể tiếp cận bằng cách đi bộ, bằng…., hoặc bằng xe bốn bánh.</p><p>+ Answer: "Donkey" (con lừa) được liệt kê như một phương tiện cùng với đi bộ.</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là donkey</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,10,NULL,0,1000),
(N'e70126d6-244f-54b5-bfc8-5780aa0a8fbd',N'da971f0a-2f2e-5163-b076-e7760794f89e',0,3,19,N'Question number 11',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Người dân địa phương sẽ duy trì ít …. hơn vì tốc độ phát triển.</p><p>+ Answer: Bài đọc nói rằng sẽ khó khăn để duy trì các truyền thống vì sự phát triển quá nhanh</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là traditions</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,11,NULL,0,1000),
(N'a6173ff2-b2a7-5d2f-a2fc-d0b9e2d317f2',N'da971f0a-2f2e-5163-b076-e7760794f89e',0,3,19,N'Question number 12',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Các cán bộ đa dạng sinh học đảm bảo con đường mới không đi qua những nơi có …. quý hiếm.</p><p>+ Answer: Những cán bộ đa dạng sinh học được tham vấn trong quá trình thiết kế đường để tránh các khu vực có loài thực vật chỉ có ở một số ít địa điểm</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là plants</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,12,NULL,0,1000),
(N'ae2f98b1-3a9e-50c8-b4b3-10cedacf0db7',N'da971f0a-2f2e-5163-b076-e7760794f89e',0,3,19,N'Question number 13',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Trong tương lai, thiệt hại môi trường do xây dựng đường sẽ được đánh giá trong một …..</p><p>+ Answer: Tác động môi trường của những con đường sẽ được đánh giá bằng báo cáo trước khi xây dựng</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là report</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,13,NULL,0,1000),
(N'4c0f7322-f8c4-5a00-ab8a-c8cf661cf069',N'09f4ab8e-600e-5083-b1af-0e2bddbc5b5b',0,1,14,(CAST(N'<p><span><span>Australian Society Before European Settlement</span></span></p><p><em>The Aboriginal people of Australia came to that continent between 40,000 and 60,000 years ago. In some areas enough of the basic structures of their society remain to show how they used to live.</em></p><p></p><p><span><span>A</span></span> Traditionally, Australian Aboriginal people used to live in family groups, a few of which would join together to form larger groups known to sociologists as bands or hordes. To take part in important ceremonies or gatherings such as initiations, these bands came together as a single tribe, making a group of a hundred to several hundred people. In turn, these tribes sometimes met in still larger groups of a thousand or more. Aboriginal society was organised in three different ways: according to geographical structuring, religious/totemic structuring, and kinship structuring.</p><p></p><p><span><span>B</span></span> Firstly, there was the geographical structuring of society, in which tribes of perhaps 500 people were made up of a number of bands of up to 20 people, each of which occupied a specific area. These bands were economic groups which would join together for day-to-day hunting and other food gathering. However, the term ‘band’ is given to this type of group by non-Aboriginal observers, and is not a distinct group in the minds of Aboriginal people, who regard themselves rather as belonging to a particular tribe or totemic group.</p><p></p><p><span><span>C</span></span> In Aboriginal Australia, tribes are groups made up of people sharing the same language, customs, and general laws. The people of a tribe share a common bond and, in their own language, the word for ‘man’ is often the word used for the name of the tribe. Some tribal groups now also use the English term ‘nation’ to describe themselves, as, for example, the Larrakeyah tribe around Darwin in Australia’s Northern Territory who call themselves the ‘Larrakeyah nation’. Tribes were generally not groups concerned with making war, and were not led by a chief. When Europeans first settled in Australia at the end of the 18th century there were an estimated 500 Aboriginal tribes. Of these, around 400 still have people representing them in the centre and north of Australia, where the tribal structure is still largely intact.</p><p></p><p><span><span>D</span></span> The second way in which Aboriginal society was organised is religious and totemic. On a religious level, Aboriginal s' AS nvarchar(max))+N'ociety in Australia was divided into two ‘moieties’ (a term used by European anthropologists) or halves. Within each moiety are significant animals, plants or places connected to the time of creation, which Aboriginal people call the ‘Dreamtime’. For example, in the northern Kimberley area of Western Australia, the two moieties are represented by the two birds, Wodoi, the spotted nightjar, and Djungun, the owlet nightjar, who are said to have fought in the Dreamtime. Wodoi is associated with certain plants such as the edible cabbage palm, while Djungun is connected to a fish called the rock cod and a bird, the corella.</p><p></p><p><span><span>E</span></span> Each person, as well as belonging to one or the other moiety, also belongs to a totemic group. A totem is an animal, plant, or other object which is believed to be ancestrally related to a person. In the Kimberley example given above, people belonging to the Wodoi moiety call the spotted nightjar their father, but they also have other animal and plant associates. For example, Jack Kararlada, a Kimberley elder, is named after his totem, the butcher bird, or kararlada in the local language. A totem can be represented by a large rock, a tree, hill, river, or other land form, and may also have a man-made emblem such as a wooden pole or other decorated object. Much of Aboriginal art is connected with the imagery of totems. A person is born into one or the other moiety, with their own totems, and that does not change throughout their life. A person belonging to one moiety must marry a person of the opposite moiety, a custom which has the effect of increasing genetic variation in the group.</p><p></p><p><span><span>F</span></span> The third way that the society is structured is through the kinship system, which regulates relations between people. The kinship system is complex, needing up to 70 relationship terms to describe it. It structures obligations and behaviour among families and between members of society in general, and defines such matters as who will look after children if a parent dies, who can marry whom, who is responsible for another person’s misdeeds, and who will care for the sick and the elderly. Under kinship laws, Aboriginal people may have similar family obligations to their aunts and uncles as they would to their mother or father.</p><p></p><p><span><span>G</span></span> A family group can be quite large, consisting of a man and his wives, the children from each wife, and sometimes his p'+N'arents or in-laws. A man used to have from one to ten wives, but nowadays most men have just one. Interestingly, Aboriginal custom all over Australia bans a person from speaking directly to their mother-in-law. So, in traditional society, if you wanted your mother-in-law to do something for you, you would have to ask another person to ask her. When food was divided and shared around the camp fire, a mother-in-law would have her own small fire, and her son or daughter would take her some of the meat and stay to chat, or a grandchild would sit with her and act as a messenger.</p>'),NULL,NULL,N'',NULL,1,0,2,NULL,0,1000),
(N'9a2e044b-20c5-5407-b1c2-71d44f31befa',N'4c0f7322-f8c4-5a00-ab8a-c8cf661cf069',0,2,18,N'<p>Reading Passage 2 has seven paragraphs, <span>A–G. </span></p><p>Which paragraph contains the following information? </p><p>Write the correct letter, <span>A–G</span>, in boxes 14–19 on your answer sheet. </p><p><span>NB</span> You may use any letter more than once. </p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',12,0,1,NULL,0,1000),
(N'3f432847-71be-5640-8313-fae8491c295c',N'9a2e044b-20c5-5407-b1c2-71d44f31befa',0,3,19,N'<p>a description of the way Aboriginal society was organised for survival activities</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Mô tả cách thức xã hội thổ dân được tổ chức cho các hoạt động sinh tồn.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn B mô tả các nhóm kinh tế, cùng nhau thực hiện săn bắn và hái lượm hàng ngày, là những hoạt động sinh tồn cơ bản</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là B</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,14,NULL,0,1000),
(N'750a51c8-a854-5965-8e80-9a36d78323c3',N'9a2e044b-20c5-5407-b1c2-71d44f31befa',0,3,19,N'<p> an example of a person’s name taken from that of a totem   </p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Ví dụ về tên một người được lấy từ tên của một vật tổ.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn E đưa ra ví dụ cụ thể: Jack Kararlada được đặt tên theo vật tổ của ông là 1 loài chim</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là E</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,15,NULL,0,1000),
(N'b7475997-4844-5cf4-a0d9-431d5f066333',N'9a2e044b-20c5-5407-b1c2-71d44f31befa',0,3,19,N'<p>examples of special occasions when bands came together as tribes</p>',N'<p>+ Synonyms: special occasions = important ceremonies or gatherings Interpretation: Ví dụ về những dịp đặc biệt khi các nhóm tập hợp lại thành bộ lạc.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn A liệt kê các nghi lễ quan trọng hoặc tụ họp như lễ thành đạo (initiations) là những dịp các nhóm hợp lại thành một bộ lạc.</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là A</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,16,NULL,0,1000),
(N'62130120-e0fa-5ac6-93d1-fc8716a91dfa',N'9a2e044b-20c5-5407-b1c2-71d44f31befa',0,3,19,N'<p>a mention of a change in Aboriginal marriage customs</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Đề cập đến một sự thay đổi trong phong tục hôn nhân của thổ dân.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn G nêu rõ trước đây một người đàn ông có thể có nhiều vợ, nhưng ngày nay hầu hết chỉ có một vợ</p><p>-&gt; là một sự thay đổi trong phong tục hôn nhân</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là G</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,17,NULL,0,1000),
(N'814f0c28-bc68-5307-ad0b-b80463fd08be',N'9a2e044b-20c5-5407-b1c2-71d44f31befa',0,3,19,N'<p> a reference to the approximate number of Aboriginal tribes in existence at the time of colonisation   </p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Đề cập đến số lượng gần đúng các bộ lạc thổ dân tồn tại vào thời điểm thuộc địa hóa.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn C cung cấp con số ước tính 500 bộ lạc vào thời điểm người châu Âu định cư cuối thế kỷ 18</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là C</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,18,NULL,0,1000),
(N'1d3e0e1f-b1d0-51f8-9a04-3b3eedc4b3d4',N'9a2e044b-20c5-5407-b1c2-71d44f31befa',0,3,19,N'<p>a mention of a biological outcome of the moiety system</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Đề cập đến một kết quả sinh học của hệ thống moiety.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn E giải thích phong tục hôn nhân khác moiety có tác dụng làm tăng biến dị di truyền trong nhóm</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là E</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,19,NULL,0,1000),
(N'087d4b95-d02e-5d0a-8d89-7f4e5bc6e587',N'4c0f7322-f8c4-5a00-ab8a-c8cf661cf069',0,2,18,N'<p>Choose <span>TWO</span> letters, A–E. </p><p>Write the correct letters in boxes 20 and 21 on your answer sheet. </p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',5,0,2,NULL,0,1000),
(N'2587b72d-cdbe-5625-a6df-1f2d9377c837',N'087d4b95-d02e-5d0a-8d89-7f4e5bc6e587',0,3,19,N'<p>Which TWO of the following statements are made about a totem?</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Nó có thể được đại diện bởi một đặc điểm của cảnh quan.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn E nói rõ vật tổ có thể được đại diện bởi các yếu tố địa hình như đá, cây, đồi, sông.</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là B</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,20,NULL,0,1000),
(N'055a64c3-fd12-51b0-a9f7-7969489c5335',N'087d4b95-d02e-5d0a-8d89-7f4e5bc6e587',0,3,19,N'<p>Which TWO of the following statements are made about a totem?</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Nó được cho là một tổ tiên.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn E định nghĩa vật tổ là một con vật, cây cối hay vật thể được tin là có liên hệ tổ tiên với một người.</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là E</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,21,NULL,0,1000),
(N'8d4f6bd5-5017-581d-93ef-cf2f80737e8d',N'4c0f7322-f8c4-5a00-ab8a-c8cf661cf069',0,2,18,N'<p>Complete the sentences below. </p><p>Choose <span>ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER</span> from the passage for each answer. </p><p>Write your answers in boxes 22–26 on your answer sheet. </p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',11,0,3,NULL,0,1000),
(N'f9714a7c-112d-5870-91a5-246350303149',N'8d4f6bd5-5017-581d-93ef-cf2f80737e8d',0,3,19,N'<p>The tribal system still exists in the north and }{SPACE}{ of Australia.  </p><p>Aboriginal people refer to the beginning of the world as the }{SPACE}{ </p><p>A }{SPACE}{  made of wood is sometimes used to represent a totem.  </p><p>Aboriginal languages have as many as  }{SPACE}{ words to describe family relationships.  </p><p>The social system of an Aboriginal tribe controls matters such as who should look after children, the old and the  }{SPACE}{ </p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Hệ thống bộ lạc vẫn tồn tại ở phía bắc và ….. của Úc.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn văn cho biết cấu trúc bộ lạc phần lớn vẫn còn nguyên vẹn ở miền trung và bắc nước Úc</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là centre</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,22,NULL,0,1000),
(N'95820f1c-5daf-5dda-b131-1cde8bbe76b4',N'8d4f6bd5-5017-581d-93ef-cf2f80737e8d',0,3,19,N'Question number 23',N'<p>+ Synonyms: "the beginning of the world" (sự khởi đầu của thế giới) ↔ "time of creation" (thời gian sáng thế).</p><p>+ Interpretation: Thổ dân gọi thời kỳ khởi nguyên của thế giới là …..</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn D nói rõ thời kỳ sáng thế được thổ dân gọi là "Dreamtime".</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là Dreamtime</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,23,NULL,0,1000),
(N'87358749-0367-53e3-89b5-b8aca3a6fe78',N'8d4f6bd5-5017-581d-93ef-cf2f80737e8d',0,3,19,N'Question number 24',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Một …. làm bằng gỗ đôi khi được dùng để đại diện cho vật tổ.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn E đề cập đến biểu tượng nhân tạo như một cây cột gỗ có thể đại diện cho vật tổ -</p><p>&gt; Đáp án là pole</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,24,NULL,0,1000),
(N'5e992a2b-4a19-5aec-bc31-c19f10234e9a',N'8d4f6bd5-5017-581d-93ef-cf2f80737e8d',0,3,19,N'Question number 25',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Ngôn ngữ thổ dân có tới … từ để mô tả các mối quan hệ gia đình.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn F nói hệ thống thân tộc cần tới 70 thuật ngữ quan hệ để mô tả</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là 70</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,25,NULL,0,1000),
(N'41b43227-88cb-54eb-bcca-3109224a20a2',N'8d4f6bd5-5017-581d-93ef-cf2f80737e8d',0,3,19,N'Question number 26',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Hệ thống xã hội của bộ lạc thổ dân kiểm soát các vấn đề như ai sẽ chăm sóc trẻ em, người già và …..</p><p>+ Answer: - Đoạn F liệt kê việc quản lý chăm sóc người bệnh và người già</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là sick</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,26,NULL,0,1000),
(N'67a1d1e2-de34-5e75-b298-a67d273e3b8b',N'09f4ab8e-600e-5083-b1af-0e2bddbc5b5b',0,1,15,(CAST(N'<p><span>The Exploration of Mars  </span></p><p></p><p><span>A.</span> In 1877, Giovanni Schiaparelli, an Italian astronomer, made drawings and maps of the Martian surface that suggested strange features. The images from telescopes at that time were not as sharp as today’s. Schiaparelli said he could see a network of lines, or canali. In 1894, an American astronomer, Percival Lowell, made a series of observations of Mars from his own observatory at Flagstaff, Arizona, U.S.A. Lowell was convinced a great network of canals had been dug to irrigate crops for the Martian race. He suggested that each canal had fertile vegetation on either side, making them noticeable from Earth. Drawings and globes he made show a network of canals and oases all over the planet. </p><p></p><p><span>B.</span> The idea that there was intelligent life on Mars gained strength in the late 19th century. In 1898, H. G. Wells wrote the science-fiction classic The War of the Worlds about an invading force of Martians who try to conquer Earth. They use highly advanced technology (advanced for 1898) to crush human resistance. In 1917, Edgar Rice Burroughs wrote the first in a series of 11 novels about Mars. Strange beings and rampaging Martian monsters gripped the public’s imagination. A radio broadcast by Orson Welles on Halloween night in 1938 of The War of the Worlds caused widespread panic across America; people ran into the streets in their pyjamas—millions believed the dramatic reports of a Martian invasion. </p><p></p><p><span>C.</span> Probes are very important to our understanding of other planets. Much of our recent knowledge comes from these robotic missions into space. The first images sent back from Mars came from Mariner 4 in July 1965. They showed a cratered and barren landscape, more like the surface of our Moon than Earth. In 1969, Mariners 6 and 7 were launched and took 200 photographs of Mars’s southern hemisphere and pole on fly-by missions, but these revealed little more information. In 1971, Mariner 9 became the first spacecraft to orbit the planet, circling every 12 hours. In 1975, the U.S.A. sent two Viking probes, each with an orbiter and a lander. The landers had sampler arms to scoop up Martian rocks and carried out experiments to try to find signs of life. Although no life was found, they sent back the first colour pictures of the planet’s surface and atmosphere from pivoting cameras. </p><p></p><p><span>D.</span> A Martian meteorite found on Earth raised fresh ' AS nvarchar(max))+N'doubts about the above analysis. Meteorite ALH 84001 was discovered in December 1984 in Antarctica by members of the ANSMET project. The sample was ejected from Mars about 17 million years ago and spent 11,000 years in, or on, Antarctic ice sheets. NASA’s compositional analysis revealed a kind of magnetite that on Earth is only found in association with certain micro-organisms. Some structures resemble the mineralised casts of terrestrial bacteria and their appendages, fibrils or by-products occurring in the rims of carbonate globules and pre-terrestrial aqueous-alteration regions. The size and shape of the objects are consistent with Earthly fossilised nanobacteria, but the very existence of nanobacteria is still controversial. </p><p></p><p><span>E.</span> In 1965, the Mariner 4 probe discovered that Mars had no global magnetic field to protect the planet from potentially life-threatening cosmic and solar radiation; observations made in the late 1990s by Mars Global Surveyor confirmed this discovery. Scientists speculate that the lack of magnetic shielding helped the solar wind blow  away much of Mars’s atmosphere over several billion years. After mapping cosmic- radiation levels at various depths on Mars, researchers concluded that any life within  the first several metres of the planet’s surface would be killed by lethal doses of radiation. In 2007 it was calculated that DNA and RNA damage would limit life on Mars to depths greater than 7.5 metres below the surface. Therefore, the best places to look for life may be subsurface environments that have not yet been studied. The disappearance of the magnetic field may have played a significant role in Martian climate change. According to scientists’ evaluation, Mars’s climate gradually transitioned from warm and wet to cold and dry after the magnetic field vanished. </p><p></p><p><span>F.</span> NASA’s recent missions have focused on another question: whether Mars had lakes or oceans of liquid water on its surface in the ancient past. Scientists have found hematite, a mineral that forms only in the presence of water. Thus, the 2004 Mars Exploration Rovers were designed not to look for present or past life, but for evidence of ancient liquid water. Because of Mars’s current low atmospheric pressure and temperature, liquid water cannot persist at the surface except, briefly, at the lowest shaded elevations. In March 2004, NASA announced that its rover Opportunity had discovered evidence that Mars was once a '+N'wet planet. This raised hopes that evidence of past life might still be found. Later, the Mars Express orbiter detected huge reserves of water-ice at Mars’s south pole in January 2004. </p><p></p><p><span>G.</span> Researchers from the Center for Astrobiology (Spain) and the Catholic University of the North in Chile have found an oasis of micro-organisms two metres below the surface of the Atacama Desert. SOLID, a life-detection instrument, could be used in environments similar to Martian sub-soil. “We have named it a microbial oasis because we found micro-organisms developing in a habitat rich in rock salt and other highly hygroscopic compounds that absorb water,” explained Victor Parro of the Center for Astrobiology. “If similar microbes, or their remains, exist on Mars under comparable conditions, we could detect them with instruments like SOLID,” Parro added. </p><p></p><p><span>H.</span> Even more intriguing is an alternative scenario proposed by the Spanish scientists. If samples on Mars were found to use DNA—as Earthly life does—it would be extremely unlikely that such a specialised, complex molecule could have evolved independently on two planets. This would indicate a common origin for Martian and Earth life. Life based on DNA might have appeared first on Mars and then spread to Earth, where it evolved into the myriad plants and creatures alive today. If that proved true, we would face a startling conclusion: we are all Martians. If not, we must continue the search for other signs of life. </p>'),NULL,NULL,N'',NULL,1,0,3,NULL,0,1000),
(N'9f6692ce-528f-5cd1-8bf5-32459ceff4b0',N'67a1d1e2-de34-5e75-b298-a67d273e3b8b',0,2,18,N'<p>The reading passage has eight paragraphs, <span>A–H. </span></p><p>Which paragraph contains the following information? </p><p>Write the correct letter,<span> A–H</span>, in boxes 27–32 on your answer sheet. </p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',12,0,1,NULL,0,1000),
(N'26522732-5809-54d7-9718-3826f8716c3d',N'9f6692ce-528f-5cd1-8bf5-32459ceff4b0',0,3,19,N'<p>Martian evidence found on Earth</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Bằng chứng về Sao Hỏa được tìm thấy trên Trái Đất.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn D thảo luận về một thiên thạch từ Sao Hỏa (ALH 84001) được tìm thấy ở Nam Cực</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là D</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,27,NULL,0,1000),
(N'6848a6ad-94df-5781-80bd-de0d90ac533d',N'9f6692ce-528f-5cd1-8bf5-32459ceff4b0',0,3,19,N'<p>Mars and Earth may share the same origin of life</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Sao Hỏa và Trái Đất có thể có cùng nguồn gốc sự sống.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn H nói rằng nếu mẫu vật trên Sao Hỏa được phát hiện ra là có DNA như sự sống trên Trái Đất, nó có thể chỉ ra nguồn gốc chung cho sự sống trên cả hai hành tinh</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là H</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,28,NULL,0,1000),
(N'ca226ecc-6ebe-5bf5-adc2-c1b37c008dfa',N'9f6692ce-528f-5cd1-8bf5-32459ceff4b0',0,3,19,N'<p>Detailed depiction of large-scale agricultural constructions</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Miêu tả chi tiết về các công trình nông nghiệp quy mô lớn.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn A mô tả chi tiết quan điểm của Lowell về một mạng lưới kênh đào rộng lớn được đào để tưới tiêu cho cây trồng trên sao Hỏa</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là A</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,29,NULL,0,1000),
(N'c36d6b54-ec57-563f-b92b-0ed0ccd9bc49',N'9f6692ce-528f-5cd1-8bf5-32459ceff4b0',0,3,19,N'<p>A project that aims to detect life under conditions similar to those on Mars</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Một dự án nhằm phát hiện sự sống trong điều kiện tương tự Sao Hỏa. </p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn G giới thiệu công cụ SOLID được phát triển để phát hiện vi sinh vật trong môi trường dưới bề mặt, tương tự như đất dưới bề mặt Sao Hỏa</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là G</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,30,NULL,0,1000),
(N'0e53e3a8-87d0-5248-99c2-3b9b9f7a8e10',N'9f6692ce-528f-5cd1-8bf5-32459ceff4b0',0,3,19,N'<p>Mars has undergone drastic climatic transformation</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Sao Hỏa đã trải qua sự biến đổi khí hậu mạnh mẽ.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn E giải thích rằng từ trường biến mất dẫn đến sự thay đổi khí hậu lớn từ nóng ẩm sang lạnh khô</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là E</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,31,NULL,0,1000),
(N'97b30d61-f5b8-57f9-93b7-c8128ddaedd4',N'9f6692ce-528f-5cd1-8bf5-32459ceff4b0',0,3,19,N'<p>Scientific attempts to locate liquid water on Mars</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Các nỗ lực khoa học để xác định vị trí nước dạng lỏng trên Sao Hỏa.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn F nói rằng các nhiệm vụ gần đây của NASA tập trung vào câu hỏi sao Hỏa đã từng có hồ hay biển nước lỏng hay không</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là F</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,32,NULL,0,1000),
(N'86c928e0-e285-5dc5-80d1-b1d946516951',N'67a1d1e2-de34-5e75-b298-a67d273e3b8b',0,2,18,N'<p>Choose the correct letter, <span>A, B, C or D.</span> </p><p>Write your answers in boxes 33–36 on your answer sheet. </p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',1,0,2,NULL,0,1000),
(N'6c045595-45c1-5177-b81a-5b7a25f7dd82',N'86c928e0-e285-5dc5-80d1-b1d946516951',0,3,19,N'<p>How did Percival Lowell describe Mars in this passage?</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Percival Lowell miêu tả Sao Hỏa thế nào trong đoạn văn?</p><p>+ Answer: Lowell nghĩ rằng trên Sao Hỏa có một mạng lưới kênh đào lớn để tưới tiêu và mỗi kênh đào có cây trồng màu mỡ ở hai bên bờ</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là C</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,33,NULL,0,1000),
(N'ba77dbc0-b28d-557a-bbaa-e2d07b404dd6',N'86c928e0-e285-5dc5-80d1-b1d946516951',0,3,19,N'<p>How did people change their view of Mars from the 19th century onwards?</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Quan điểm của mọi người về Sao Hỏa thay đổi thế nào từ thế kỷ 19 trở đi?</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn văn nói rằng ý tưởng về việc có sự sống trên sao Hỏa bắt đầu trở nên phổ biến từ cuối thế kỉ 19</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là B</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,34,NULL,0,1000),
(N'a3a365a3-780e-5729-b6ee-2b2930cecf77',N'86c928e0-e285-5dc5-80d1-b1d946516951',0,3,19,N'<p>According to the probes sent in the 1960s, which statement about Mars is correct?</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Theo các tàu thăm dò gửi đi những năm 1960, câu nào về Sao Hỏa là đúng?</p><p>+ Answer: Hình ảnh từ Mariner 4 cho thấy một cảnh quan cằn cỗi, nhiều hố va chạm, giống Mặt Trăng hơn là Trái Đất, cho thấy nó kém "sống động" (dynamic) hơn Trái Đất.</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là B</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,35,NULL,0,1000),
(N'ad1262b8-c585-5644-a265-c47c20a73756',N'86c928e0-e285-5dc5-80d1-b1d946516951',0,3,19,N'<p> What is the implication of the project using the technology called SOLID in the Atacama Desert?</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Hàm ý của dự án sử dụng công nghệ SOLID ở sa mạc Atacama là gì?</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn G nói rõ công cụ SOLID có thể được sử dụng trong các môi trường tương tự như đất dưới bề mặt Sao Hỏa để tìm kiếm vi sinh vật</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là A</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,36,NULL,0,1000),
(N'ab52d8c6-8cea-529f-af77-9010166164dd',N'67a1d1e2-de34-5e75-b298-a67d273e3b8b',0,2,18,N'<p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 3? </span></p><p><span>In boxes 37–40, write: </span></p><p><span><span>TRUE</span> if the statement agrees with the information </span></p><p><span><span>FALSE</span> if the statement contradicts the information </span></p><p><span><span>NOT GIVEN</span> if there is no information on this </span></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',1,0,3,NULL,0,1000),
(N'93b61633-acdf-51a9-bbb9-1ffd945f1a27',N'ab52d8c6-8cea-529f-af77-9010166164dd',0,3,19,N'<p>According to The War of the Worlds, Martian technology surpassed that of humans in every field at the time.</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Theo "The War of the Worlds", công nghệ của người Sao Hỏa vượt trội hơn của con người trong mọi lĩnh vực vào thời điểm đó.</p><p>+ Answer: Bài đọc chỉ nói công nghệ của người Sao Hỏa là tiên tiến vào năm 1898, nhưng không khẳng định nó vượt trội trong mọi lĩnh vực -</p><p>&gt; Đáp án là Not given</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,37,NULL,0,1000),
(N'6545b7d9-111c-523d-8334-b73ce66067be',N'ab52d8c6-8cea-529f-af77-9010166164dd',0,3,19,N'<p>The evidence supplied by the Viking probes has never been challenged.</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Bằng chứng do tàu Viking cung cấp chưa bao giờ bị thách thức.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn D nói rằng việc phát hiện ra thiên thạch Sao Hỏa đã làm dấy lên nghi ngờ mới về các phân tích của tàu Viking ở đoạn trước</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là False</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,38,NULL,0,1000),
(N'540c76cc-fe01-5972-b7da-70fa40c6b671',N'ab52d8c6-8cea-529f-af77-9010166164dd',0,3,19,N'<p>

Analysis of a meteorite from Mars discovered a substance associated with certain germs.
</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Phân tích một thiên thạch từ Sao Hỏa đã phát hiện ra một chất liên quan đến một số vi trùng nhất định.</p><p>+ Answer Phân tích thiên thạch tìm thấy magnetite, một chất mà trên Trái Đất chỉ được tìm thấy liên quan đến một số vi sinh vật</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là True</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,39,NULL,0,1000),
(N'7189c154-6ed7-534a-9626-c674d2d6576c',N'ab52d8c6-8cea-529f-af77-9010166164dd',0,3,19,N'<p>According to Victor Parro, their project will be sent to Mars once DNA-based life has been identified on Earth.</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Theo Victor Parro, dự án của họ sẽ được gửi lên Sao Hỏa một khi sự sống dựa trên DNA đã được xác định trên Trái Đất.</p><p>+ Answer: Parro nói rằng công cụ như SOLID có thể được sử dụng để phát hiện sự sống trên Sao Hỏa nếu nó tồn tại</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là Not given</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,40,NULL,0,1000),
(N'4f84567c-3208-5b5d-976e-eb239fa1f1f6',NULL,0,0,11,NULL,NULL,NULL,N'',N'Vol 1 READING FULL TEST 1',0,7,1,NULL,1,977),
(N'1e92596b-d2ae-56a4-8d91-4499dadf08e3',N'4f84567c-3208-5b5d-976e-eb239fa1f1f6',0,1,13,(CAST(N'<p><span><span>Think Small</span></span></p><p><em>Izon is a New Zealand company specialising in nanoscience - the study of atoms, molecules and other very small pieces of matter</em></p><p></p><p>The new US headquarters of Izon are situated in Cambridge, Massachusetts, one of the most important global centres of scientific research and technology. Half the other offices in the building Izon shares have scientific names like Stemgent, or the word ''pharmaceutical" in the name. In the past three years, Izon has expanded to 17 times its previous size. It''s done so selling only one product that it''s been developing since 2004, the qNano. This is an adjustable tool for the measurement and analysis of tiny particles in scientific research, which comes with a $27,000 price tag. Izon''s success results from the fact that the qNano machine provides precise measurements, while similar machines of the same price only offer averaging techniques. In effect, researchers using the q Nano are able to gather information about very small things, and it has many possible applications from drug delivery analysis through to environmental research.</p><p></p><p>Kristoffer Bolen is Izon''s US head of sales. Alongside his full-time role with the company, he''s just finished the fifth semester of six for his High Tech Masters of Business Administration at Northeastern University, which will be his second Masters degree alongside a Masters of Science. These soon to be twin Masters degrees provide Bolen with the perfect combination of skills for his job, which depends on him being able to manage the sales process and also comprehend in depth a very complicated piece of technology. When a customer buys a gNano device, an Izon representative will fly anywhere in America to train them how to use the instrument. The representative then checks in with the client on an ongoing basis to be completely informed about how each qNano is being used, and then liaises with technicians back in New Zealand.</p><p></p><p>The Izon story started 8 years ago in New Zealand. Hans van der Voorn was aimless, having sold his own company, and was looking for something more taxing to set his mind to, Van der Voor was introduced to three scientists with an idea that involved simply a small plastic membrane with a tiny adjustable hole to measure a range of very small particles. Initially he put up an investment of $1.5 million to move the process forwards to the development of a prototype, and this led to the fou' AS nvarchar(max))+N'nding of Izon and the production of the qNano. Van der Voor believes that the worlds of science and business sometimes don’t understand each other very well. However, he thinks that engineering can be a bridge between the two, and his long experience in that field has been crucial to the company''s success. He soon realised that 1zon was going to need people on the ground overseas if it was going to grow, so the US office was opened. For now Izon trades in the US as a foreign company, so avoids the high level of compliance that comes with being an American registered company. But he sees that one day soon this will change, as Izon''s current position disallows it from entering into partnerships locally.</p><p></p><p>Marketing the gNano is complicated. Izon needs scientists both to buy and advertise the product. The science world may seem like a big playing field, but it''s actually a small group. As a result, the critical part of the company''s marketing is articles that clients publish describing work they have performed with the qNano. So for on the sale isn''t enough in itself, it also has a stake in how customers are using the qNano. That''s where Yaniv Gaynor comes in. As development and training manager, he''s involved throughout the sales process and manages most of the customer''s post-sale experience. The sales process is new for Gavnor, who shifted cities and switched from a role as teacher at the University of Minnesota to his first private sector role with Izon, ''It''s tricky, it''s challenging and it''s net in my comfort zone, he concedes. But nine out of ten times, if there''s an unhappy ci torner he''s able to turn their experience around. And there''s another part to this, because sitting with customers as they learn about the qNano, Gaynor gets to see how they are using the product. ''People ask very good questions and these are great triggers for future development,'' he says.</p><p></p><p>"Our business Is selling research tools.'' van der Voorn says. But he knows that the application range of this tool is wide. For instance, Izon is engaged in a project with Harvard University, looking for a particular type of particle of blood that is a symptom of the medical condition of thrombosis. If in the future they can identify this particle, they can design a simple test for it. This would make it easier for doctors to diagnose thrombosis. Another planned development is eventually to shift the US base to more spacious offices on the other side of town. With larg'+N'er headquarters, the company will be able to bring clients into the Izon building for training with its product, rather than travelling to them, which will hopefully result in an even closer relationship between the company and its customers.</p>'),NULL,NULL,N'',NULL,1,0,1,NULL,0,977),
(N'ad028e6c-c681-545a-9924-6e87b760f5b5',N'1e92596b-d2ae-56a4-8d91-4499dadf08e3',0,2,18,N'<p><span>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage? </span></p><p><span>In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write </span></p><p><span><span>TRUE</span> if the statement is true </span></p><p><span><span>FALSE</span> if the statement is false </span></p><p><span><span>NOT GIVEN</span> if the information is not given in the passage </span></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',1,0,1,NULL,0,977),
(N'32452ac9-7a17-5044-8dd3-0c04686770b5',N'ad028e6c-c681-545a-9924-6e87b760f5b5',0,3,19,N'<p> Ion''s new US headquarters are located in an area popular with other science businesses</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Trụ sở mới của Izon tại Mỹ nằm ở khu vực phổ biến với các doanh nghiệp khoa học khác.</p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn văn mô tả Cambridge là trung tâm nghiên cứu khoa học và công nghệ toàn cầu, và Nhiều văn phòng khác trong tòa nhà có tên liên quan đến khoa học</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là True</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,1,NULL,0,977),
(N'd4018fd3-9191-5415-9992-3f3cb3f03183',N'ad028e6c-c681-545a-9924-6e87b760f5b5',0,3,19,N'<p> Ion''s growth in the last three years has been faster than the company predicted.</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Sự phát triển của Izon trong 3 năm vừa qua nhanh hơn dự kiến </p><p>+ Answer: Đoạn văn không nói gì về tốc độ tăng trưởng hay dự kiến của công ty</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là Not given</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,2,NULL,0,977),
(N'b24f27de-2cd6-5a6c-885e-72f72ecb283f',N'ad028e6c-c681-545a-9924-6e87b760f5b5',0,3,19,N'<p>Since 2004, Izon has developed a range of equipment for use in scientific research.</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Kể từ năm 2004, Izon đã phát triển một loạt thiết bị cho nghiên cứu khoa học.</p><p>+ Answer: Thông tin trong bài nêu rõ Izon chỉ bán một sản phẩm duy nhất được phát triển từ năm 2004.</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là False</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,3,NULL,0,977),
(N'11213ed1-7723-58f5-adca-71687f193fad',N'ad028e6c-c681-545a-9924-6e87b760f5b5',0,3,19,N'<p>One advantage of the qNano is that it is cheaper than its competitors.</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Một lợi thế của qNano là nó rẻ hơn các đối thủ cạnh tranh.</p><p>+ Answer: Bài đọc nói các máy tương tự có cùng mức giá ($27,000) </p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là False</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,4,NULL,0,977),
(N'64ee5f61-1c8f-55b4-b8d8-e16951890d00',N'ad028e6c-c681-545a-9924-6e87b760f5b5',0,3,19,N'<p> Drug delivery analysis will be the most profitable application of the qNano.</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Phân tích phân phối thuốc sẽ là ứng dụng có lợi nhuận nhất của qNano. </p><p>+ Answer: Bài đọc liệt kê nhiều ứng dụng của qNano, nhưng không so sánh lợi nhuận của chúng với nhau</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là Not given</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,5,NULL,0,977),
(N'8c49dbb9-c47e-5189-9623-197d79410901',N'ad028e6c-c681-545a-9924-6e87b760f5b5',0,3,19,N'<p>Kristoffer Bolen is still completing his studies.</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Kristoffer Bolen vẫn đang hoàn thành việc học của mình.</p><p>+ Answer: Anh ấy đã hoàn thành học kỳ thứ năm trong tổng số sáu học kỳ, nghĩa là vẫn còn một học kỳ nữa</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là True</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,6,NULL,0,977),
(N'cd4edc36-300f-5fc7-9c7c-ed127203ad02',N'ad028e6c-c681-545a-9924-6e87b760f5b5',0,3,19,N'<p>Bolen''s job requires him to fully understand how the gNano works.</p>',N'<p>+ Interpretation: Công việc của Bolen yêu cầu anh ấy hiểu đầy đủ cách hoạt động của qNano.</p><p>+ Answer: Bài đọc nói rằng công việc của anh ấy phụ thuộc vào khả năng hiểu sâu về công nghệ phức tạp (tức là qNano).</p><p>-&gt; Đáp án là True</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,7,NULL,0,977),
(N'36b7603b-98e4-55b9-a8d7-6d0cbe938443',N'1e92596b-d2ae-56a4-8d91-4499dadf08e3',0,2,18,N'<p>Complete the notes below. </p><p>Choose<span> ONE WORD ONLY</span> from the passage for each answer. </p><p>Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet. </p>',N'',N'',N'',N'',11,0,2,NULL,0,977),
