(N'30259ece-91e0-5030-80f8-0d94592bcc82',N'3243153a-b67b-55f8-9fe2-2efb7de363b1',0,3,19,N'Question number 6',N'Cô mang hầu hết đồ, chỉ cần tủ lạnh.',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,6,NULL,0,484),
(N'bfc56851-dc2d-5b87-bf06-3a4c1db0043d',N'3243153a-b67b-55f8-9fe2-2efb7de363b1',0,3,19,N'Question number 7',N'Agent khẳng định không cần trả quá $400; Susan cũng xác nhận không thể hơn mức đó.',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,7,NULL,0,484),
(N'2e9617b0-1745-56e7-8f94-5477ed193d7b',N'3243153a-b67b-55f8-9fe2-2efb7de363b1',0,3,19,N'Question number 8',N'Susan là người mê lướt sóng → cần gần bãi biển.',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,8,NULL,0,484),
(N'88d0b5a3-1dbc-5611-a800-c9e291beb3e5',N'3243153a-b67b-55f8-9fe2-2efb7de363b1',0,3,19,N'Question number 9',N'Vì làm ca đêm, cần chỗ đậu xe gần cửa.',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,9,NULL,0,484),
(N'6e0aa4cf-ebc1-5637-b614-135437914b38',N'3243153a-b67b-55f8-9fe2-2efb7de363b1',0,3,19,N'Question number 10',N'Susan muốn điện được tính gộp trong tiền thuê vì hóa đơn mùa đông đắt.',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,10,NULL,0,484),
(N'd17bb011-f24b-581a-ae09-4e45bb0d2f8e',N'1725fc1d-3025-5312-a83a-abb6e10a24dc',0,1,14,(CAST(N'<h2>The pre-school family centre</h2><p>Good evening everyone, and welcome to the Preschool Family Centre. It''s really good to see so many parents here, and I hope this talk will help you to find out more about what we do here and how the centre works, so you can decide if this sounds the right sort of place for your child.</p><p>Okay, so first of all, what is the Preschool Family Centre? Well, basically it''s a childhood education centre for children from 3 months up to 5 years old. But we''re different from a lot of other organisations for preschool children. We believe that the first educators of a child are their parents, and so the Preschool Family Centre is organised as a cooperative by the parents, which means it is the parents themselves who are responsible for running the centre and also for running each session.</p><p>So this means that we ask parents to attend the centre with their children on a regular basis. In order to make this work, we offer training for parents, teaching them the skills they need to work with children and run the sessions. The children do all sorts of different activities – art, music, singing and games. And these are all done in groups of mixed ages because we believe that by learning to play together, children learn how to make choices and how to respect people and things.</p><p>Before you hear the rest of the talk, you have some time to look at questions 15 to 20 on page 3.</p><p>Now, listen and answer questions 15 to 20.</p><p>Now, some factual information. Sessions run each morning from 9.30 to 12.30, and we have an extra session on Thursday afternoons which is solely for older children, where we do some activities to help prepare them for reading before they start school. We feel this is really important and can make a big difference when they get to school.</p><p>And now, before you enrol your child in the centre, you need to make at least five visits with your child. This is so you are fully aware of how the centre works before you enrol.</p><p>The centres are recognised as official pre-schools, and so each centre is entitled to funding from the Government. The centre is a really wonderful experience but does require some work. So I’d just like to talk about some of the commitments you will need to make if you decide to go ahead and enrol your child.</p><p>A couple of points first. Once you and your child have settled into the centre and are familiar with how things work, you will be asked to choose a particular job ' AS nvarchar(max))+N'— like secretary, gardener, librarian, or something to be responsible for. And we have a meeting which we use to plan the programme, and each parent is expected to attend this.</p><p>Now, just before we move on to answer any questions you have, I’d just quickly like to mention some of the ways you and your child are able to get the most out of the centre. It’s important that you attend regularly. This way you will get to know other parents well and your child will develop confidence while he or she is here.</p><p>Younger children might need to leave early. It’s better to leave early than to go home with an overtired child. We do provide drinks for the children, but we ask you to make sure your child has a snack to eat during the morning. No crisps or chocolate, please.</p><p>Right, I think I’ll stop there and ask if anyone’s got any questions.</p>'),(CAST(N'<p>Good evening everyone, and welcome to the Preschool Family Centre. It''s really good to see so many parents here, and I hope this talk will help you to find out more about what we do here and how the centre works, so you can decide if this sounds the right sort of place for your child.</p><p>Okay, so first of all, what is the Preschool Family Centre? Well, basically it''s a childhood education centre for children from 3 months up to 5 years old. But we''re different from a lot of other organisations for preschool children. We believe that the first educators of a child are their parents, and so the Preschool Family Centre is organised as a cooperative by the parents, which means it is the parents themselves who are responsible for running the centre and also for running each session.</p><p>So this means that we ask parents to attend the centre with their children on a regular basis. In order to make this work, we offer training for parents, teaching them the skills they need to work with children and run the sessions. The children do all sorts of different activities – art, music, singing and games. And these are all done in groups of mixed ages because we believe that by learning to play together, children learn how to make choices and how to respect people and things.</p><p>Before you hear the rest of the talk, you have some time to look at questions 15 to 20 on page 3.</p><p>Now, listen and answer questions 15 to 20.</p><p>Now, some factual information. Sessions run each morning from 9.30 to 12.30, and we have an extra session on Thursday afternoons which is solely for older children, where we do some activities to help prepare them for reading before they start school. We feel this is really important and can make a big difference when they get to school.</p><p>And now, before you enrol your child in the centre, you need to make at least five visits with your child. This is so you are fully aware of how the centre works before you enrol.</p><p>The centres are recognised as official pre-schools, and so each centre is entitled to funding from the Government. The centre is a really wonderful experience but does require some work. So I’d just like to talk about some of the commitments you will need to make if you decide to go ahead and enrol your child.</p><p>A couple of points first. Once you and your child have settled into the centre and are familiar with how things work, you will be asked to choose a particular job — like secretary, gardener, librarian' AS nvarchar(max))+N', or something to be responsible for. And we have a meeting which we use to plan the programme, and each parent is expected to attend this.</p><p>Now, just before we move on to answer any questions you have, I’d just quickly like to mention some of the ways you and your child are able to get the most out of the centre. It’s important that you attend regularly. This way you will get to know other parents well and your child will develop confidence while he or she is here.</p><p>Younger children might need to leave early. It’s better to leave early than to go home with an overtired child. We do provide drinks for the children, but we ask you to make sure your child has a snack to eat during the morning. No crisps or chocolate, please.</p><p>Right, I think I’ll stop there and ask if anyone’s got any questions.</p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/real-tests/iL.REAL.2.S484.S484.PART2.mp3',NULL,1,0,2,NULL,0,484),
(N'0862634d-73c9-5164-8173-92393204b099',N'd17bb011-f24b-581a-ae09-4e45bb0d2f8e',0,2,18,N'<p><span><span>Complete the notes below.</span></span></p><p><span><span>Write <span>NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER </span>for each answer.</span></span></p>',N'',N'',N'',N'The pre-school family centre',11,0,1,NULL,0,484),
(N'a8da5c76-f005-55f2-8b03-57f9326fcbef',N'0862634d-73c9-5164-8173-92393204b099',0,3,19,N'<h3>The pre-school family centre</h3><table border="1"><tbody><tr><td><p><span><span>Features of the pre-school family centre</span></span></p> •	For children from  }{SPACE}{ to 5 years old •	Run as a  }{SPACE}{ by parents, who attend with their children •	Parents received special  }{SPACE}{ from the centre •	Children’s activities organised in  }{SPACE}{ age groups <p><span><span>Facts about the centre</span></span></p><p>•	Sessions from 9.30 – 12.30 each morning</p> •	One afternoon session to help prepare older children for  }{SPACE}{ at school •	Parents must make several  }{SPACE}{ before they enroll their child •	Each centre is officially recoginised and received  }{SPACE}{ funding <p><span>Parents’ commitments</span></p> •	Take on responsibility for a special  }{SPACE}{  •	Attend one  }{SPACE}{  <p><span>Practical advice</span></p> •	Attend regularly to help your children gain  }{SPACE}{  <p><span><span>•	Younger children may need to leave early</span></span></p><p><span><span>•	Provide a snack for your child</span></span></p></td></tr></tbody></table>',N'Người nói nêu thẳng độ tuổi tiếp nhận.',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,11,NULL,0,484),
