retching is later on combined with balance exercises which stretch and also strengthen the muscles. Okay then</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>SPEAKER_02: Before you hear the rest of the discussion you have some time to look</p><p>at questions 27 to 30 on page 5. Now listen and answer questions 27 to 30.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>SPEAKER_01: It''s always useful to have some information on case studies at the end</p><p>in case we''re sure of a material. Did you manage to find anything? Yes. A female</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>SPEAKER_00: runner in her 30s talking about her treatment for a swollen heel.</p><p>Initially she rested the injury. This did help to reduce the swelling although it was still a little bit uncomfortable. Then she applied an ice pack to the injury twice a day. Did that work? Well she persisted with this treatment for the first month but decided it wasn''t helping. After this period she was shown how to use deep tissue massage techniques and was surprised at how much freedom of movement this created in her foot. Wasn''t she having ultrasound treatment? Yes she was having sessions at the hospital but she remained unconvinced about its value. Felt the same about the balancing exercises She she was prescribed.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>SPEAKER 01: Okay. that''s interesting. I looked at the aftercare program of a male sprinter who was allowed to do some sports activity as part of his rehabilitation. After four months of treatment he did some light running on Crass wear the shoes that gave plenty of support to his injured heel. the heel was sore afterwards and the so it didn''t hurt. well he found same happened with some jumping exercises he was asked to try. Did he go to the gym and use weights? Yes after a few weeks and this benet hat as has foot was not making contact when ise greed l expended und similar result with swimming but found the repetitive kicking motion was actually aggravating the injury.</p><p></p><p>SPEAKER_00: Well both these case studies have failed.</p><p></p><p>SPEAKER_02: That is the end of section three. You now have half a minute to check</p><p>your answers. Now turn to section four on page six.</p><p></p>'),NULL,N'https://ieltsroom.com/upload/audio/iL-full-test/ieltsadvancedtest/real-tests/iL.REAL.2.S484.S484.PART3.mp3',NULL,1,0,3,NULL,0,484),
